<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Machine Learning for Industrial Manufacturing: A Case Study on Injection Molding Machine Selection Support">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning for Industrial Manufacturing: A Case Study on Injection Molding Machine Selection Support</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, published in DATA 2024 proceedings (LNISO 71, pp. 283–291, Springer Nature Switzerland, 2024). It applies Support Vector Machine and Random Forest to real automotive plastics industry data to support injection molding machine selection, finding that Random Forest outperforms SVM (Accuracy 81%, F1 78%, Precision 85%, Recall 81% vs. SVM Accuracy 67%, F1 66%, Precision 66%, Recall 67%).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">978-3-031-75329-9_31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791420960</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Faouzi Tayalati">
  <data key="d0">Faouzi Tayalati</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Faouzi Tayalati is an engineer and researcher affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMed Genomics Laboratory (also written BioMedGenomics) at the Faculty of Sciences and Techniques (FST) of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University (also spelled Essaadi), where he is a Ph.D. candidate. He graduated as an engineer from the National School of Mechanics and Microtechnics in Besançon in 2011 and holds a master's degree in Electrical Engineering from the Faculty of Applied Sciences in Bethune, France. He has more than twelve years of industrial engineering experience, mostly in the automotive industry. His work focuses on applying artificial intelligence in manufacturing, optimizing production systems, and using AI for maintenance management.

Tayalati has published several works on injection molding and industrial decision-making. He is first author of three cited works on machine learning, AI, and decision models for injection molding, published between 2022 and 2024. These include a paper on a digital twin for injection molding and a study on selecting injection molding machines, for which he is both first and corresponding author. He also wrote an article on machine learning-assisted decision support in industrial settings. Its full title appears in truncated form, as "Machine Learning-Assisted Decision Support in Industrial ...", and the descriptions characterize its focus in several ways: machine selection, machine allocation, manufacturing, plastic molding, and machine selection for injection molding. These descriptions most likely refer to a single article on machine learning-supported machine selection for injection molding.

Tayalati also co-authored a paper presenting a supplier selection framework, also produced under his Abdelmalek Essaâdi University affiliation.&lt;SEP&gt;First author and corresponding author of the hybrid LSTM-AE and SPC anomaly detection article. Affiliated with Abdelmalek Essaâdi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead author of the article being read. An engineer with more than twelve years of industrial engineering experience, mainly in the automotive industry. Works on integrating AI into manufacturing processes, production system optimization, and AI in maintenance management.&lt;SEP&gt;Second author of the hybrid overstock risk paper. Affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory, Abdelmalek Essaadi University.&lt;SEP&gt;First author of the article, affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and Biomed Genomics Laboratory, FST of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaadi University; also author of references [1] and [2].&lt;SEP&gt;First author of the paper; affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMed Genomics Laboratory, FST of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaadi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of the article on accurate AI assistance in contract law using RAG, affiliated with Abdelmalek Essaadi University.</data>
