<node id="Ikhlass Boukrouh">
  <data key="d0">Ikhlass Boukrouh</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Ikhlass Boukrouh is a researcher at Abdelmalek Essaâdi University (also spelled Abdelmalek Essaadi University) in Morocco. She graduated as a Statistical Engineer from the Faculty of Sciences and Technologies (FST) of Tangier in 2021. She is pursuing a Ph.D. in artificial intelligence and data science applied to e-commerce. Her research interests include machine learning, predictive analytics, customer behavior modeling, and risk assessment. Her contact email, ikhlass.boukrouh@etu.uae.ac.ma, uses the university's student domain. Some sources infer her name from this address and describe her as either pursuing or holding the doctorate, but the other descriptions consistently indicate that her Ph.D. is still in progress.

Her institutional affiliations vary across publications. In most of her work she is affiliated with the Laboratory of Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics (also written as BioMed Genomics) at FST Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University. For her ICRAMCS 2022 paper, which compares SARIMA and LSTM models for sales forecasting, she is affiliated with the Computer, Science, Systems and Telecommunications Laboratory at the same university.

Ikhlass Boukrouh is the first and corresponding author of "Explainable Machine Learning Models Applied to Predicting Customer Churn." Only her name appears in that paper's running page header, which is consistent with her role as first author of a multi-author work. She is also the lead, first, and corresponding author of a paper proposing a supplier selection framework.

She has also contributed to research on injection molding. She co-authored a 2024 study that combines the AHP and TOPSIS methods to select injection molding machines. She is the second author of a paper on digital twins for injection molding. She is also credited as a co-author of a work cited as reference [45].

Overall, her publications apply machine learning, forecasting, and data-driven multi-criteria decision-making to business and industrial problems. These include customer retention, sales forecasting, supplier evaluation, and equipment selection.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the ICRAMCS 2025 paper on recurrent ticket prediction. Also first author of the cited paper on explainable machine learning for customer churn. Affiliated with IABL at Abdelmalek Essaâdi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the hybrid LSTM-AE and SPC anomaly detection article.&lt;SEP&gt;Statistical Engineer and co-author with a biography in the article. Pursuing a Ph.D. in artificial intelligence and data science applied to e-commerce. Research interests include machine learning, predictive analytics, customer behavior modeling and risk assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;First author of the hybrid overstock risk paper. Affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory, Faculty of Sciences and Technique of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaadi University, Tetouan, Morocco. Also co-author of a bibliometric study on AI applications in e-commerce.&lt;SEP&gt;Second author of the article, affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and Biomed Genomics Laboratory, Abdelmalek Essaadi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the paper; affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMed Genomics Laboratory, Abdelmalek Essaadi University.</data>
