<node id="Abdellah Azmani">
  <data key="d0">Abdellah Azmani</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Abdellah Azmani, also cited as "A. Azmani" and occasionally spelled "Abdelah Azmani," is a Moroccan computer science academic and researcher (ORCID 0000-0003-4975-3807). In 1991 he received a Ph.D. in Industrial Computing, Dynamic Systems Modelling and Artificial Intelligence from the University of Sciences and Technologies of Lille (Université des Sciences et Technologies de Lille), France. He was formerly a professor at the École Centrale de Lille and at the Institute of Computer and Industrial Engineering in Lens. He is now a professor in the Computer Science Department of the Faculty of Sciences and Technologies (FST) of Tangier, which is part of Abdelmalek Essaâdi University (also written Abdelmalek Essaadi University) in Morocco. Author biographies note that he has contributed to many scientific research projects.

Azmani is a founding member and Director of the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory (IABL) at Abdelmalek Essaâdi University. The laboratory also appears under other names, including the Laboratory of Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics, the Intelligent Automation and BioMed Genomics Laboratory, and simply the Intelligent Automation Laboratory. He has also been affiliated with LIST, the Computer, Science, Systems and Telecommunications Laboratory at the same university, and is described as the creator and coordinator of the Intelligent Automation team. These varying names and affiliations most likely reflect how his research group has changed over time. His research interests include artificial intelligence, dynamic systems modeling, and digital transformation, with an emphasis on IT solutions that support decision-making.

Azmani has authored and co-authored numerous publications in applied AI and related fields. His fuzzy-Bayesian work includes papers on predicting QoS in VANET, on predictive analysis of delivery delay risk, and on vehicle accident risk. He co-authored studies on injection molding machine selection, a supplier selection framework, and, with Faouzi Tayalati, three cited works on injection molding. Other papers address configuration-driven performance analysis of Hyperledger Fabric, the FSMicroGenerator, and a K-means clustering study of professional drivers' susceptibility to musculoskeletal disorders. He also co-authored a cited paper on explainable machine learning for customer churn prediction and "The Potential of Artificial Intelligence in Human Resource Management." In addition, he authored an article on accurate AI assistance in contract law using retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and co-authored a poster on blockchain-based vehicle management.

His conference work includes an ICRAMCS 2022 paper comparing SARIMA and LSTM models for sales forecasting and an ICRAMCS 2025 paper on recurrent ticket prediction. He co-authored articles on hybrid LSTM-AE and statistical process control (SPC) anomaly detection, and he was third author of a paper on hybrid overstock risk assessment. He also co-authored several bibliometric analyses covering feature selection techniques, AI-driven oncology, AI in market analysis, and AI applications in e-commerce.

His authorship position varies across publications: he appears as second author in some works and third author in others, and in at least one article he is credited as a co-author of cited references [1] and [2]. In one article, his credited contributions were conceptualization, validation, resources, review and editing, and supervision.</data>
