<node id="Monir Azmani">
  <data key="d0">Monir Azmani</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Monir Azmani is an academic researcher and authorized professor at the Faculty of Sciences and Technology of Tangier, part of Abdelmalek Essaadi University. His areas of specialization are computer science, industrial computing, signal processing, and artificial intelligence. He holds a Doctorate (Ph.D.) in Computer Engineering, Automation and Signal Processing from the University of Littoral Côte d'Opale (University of the Littoral Opal Coast). He has more than 12 years of experience in teaching and pedagogical supervision.

The descriptions give two laboratory affiliations. Several sources attach him to the Intelligent Automation and BioMed Genomics Laboratory (IABL) at Abdelmalek Essaadi University. Another source attaches him to the Laboratory of Computer Science, Systems, and Telecommunications. This may reflect an earlier and a later affiliation, or concurrent memberships, but the sources do not specify which.

Azmani has co-authored a range of applied research papers, many focused on injection molding:

- **Injection molding with Faouzi Tayalati:** He is a co-author of three cited works on injection molding with Faouzi Tayalati.
- **Machine selection:** He co-authored a study on the selection of injection molding machines.
- **Digital twin:** He is the fourth author of a paper on an injection molding digital twin, listed with his IABL affiliation.
- **Anomaly detection:** He co-authored an article proposing a hybrid anomaly detection approach that combines LSTM autoencoders (LSTM-AE) with Statistical Process Control (SPC).
- **Healthcare and ergonomics:** He co-authored a paper that uses K-means clustering to assess susceptibility to musculoskeletal disorders among professional drivers, also listed with his IABL affiliation at Abdelmalek Essaadi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the paper; affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMed Genomics Laboratory, Abdelmalek Essaadi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of the article on accurate AI assistance in contract law using RAG, affiliated with Abdelmalek Essaadi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the fuzzy-Bayesian vehicle accident risk paper, affiliated with Abdelmalek Essaadi University.</data>
