<node id="Abdelmalek Essaadi University">
  <data key="d0">Abdelmalek Essaadi University</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Abdelmalek Essaadi University is a Moroccan university located in Tetouan, Morocco. It is the parent institution for several academic and research units, most notably the Faculty of Science and Technology of Tangier (FST of Tangier). Sources refer to this faculty by several names, including the Faculty of Science and Technologies, the Faculty of Sciences and Technologies of Tangier, and the Faculty of Sciences and Technique of Tangier. It operates as one of the university's constituent faculties.

The Faculty of Science and Technology of Tangier hosts the Intelligent Automation and BioMed Genomics Laboratory (IABL). The laboratory's name also appears as the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory and the Intelligent Automation and Biomed Genomics Laboratory, and in at least one source in shortened form as the Intelligent Automation Laboratory. These variants most likely refer to the same research unit. Both the faculty and the laboratory belong to Abdelmalek Essaadi University, which provides the broader institutional affiliation for the research carried out there.

Researchers affiliated with the university through the FST of Tangier and the IABL include Wissal El Habti and Abdellah Azmani, both authors of the associated study. Abdelmalek Essaadi University is their institutional home and is credited as the affiliation for their scholarly work. The university is also identified as the institution where Lechhab Ouadrassi and Boukhryss study, reflecting its role in both research and education.</data>
