<node id="Support Vector Machine">
  <data key="d0">Support Vector Machine</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Support Vector Machine (SVM) is a supervised machine learning method used for both classification and regression. It finds a hyperplane that separates classes by maximizing the margin between them, and it uses kernel functions to model non-linear relationships. It is grounded in statistical principles, needs relatively little tuning, and works well with high-dimensional data. SVM is covered in a dedicated "Support Vector Machines" chapter of the Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery Handbook. It is also considered a foundational topic in feature selection research, an area that is still developing and needs further attention.

SVM has been applied in many domains. It has been used with Softmax and K-NN classifiers to classify brain MRI features, and with an electronic tongue for bladder cancer detection. Patre et al. compared it with other models for predicting e-commerce product sales. Matos et al. [11] included it in the time series forecasting module of a musculoskeletal disorder (MSD) risk monitoring system. The literature has frequently compared its predictive performance with Random Forest (RF), for example in Reference 12.

In injection molding machine selection research, SVM was one of six classification algorithms used to predict the clamping force machine. It was described as one of the preferred and best-performing models. Reported results vary by configuration and source:
- **Linear kernel:** 67% accuracy, 66% F1-score, 66% precision and 67% recall.
- **Polynomial kernel:** performance fell to 52% accuracy and a 50% F1-score.
- **Table 3 of one evaluation:** 87% accuracy and 90% precision, recall and F1-score.
- **Narrative text of the same evaluation:** 87% weighted-average precision, recall and F1-score, which differs from Table 3.

These figures probably reflect different experimental setups or reporting inconsistencies. In the same work, SVM correctly predicted classes 1, 2 and 5 and misclassified one machine each in classes 3 and 4. It correctly predicted the 250 t machine for the first new part. Its learning curve resembled RF's and plateaued at larger training sizes. Reported values included 0.32 for class 3 and 0.42 for class 4, with mold weight at 0.21 and material density at 0.06.

In customer churn prediction, SVM was one of seven classification models evaluated. Earlier work by Xiahou and Harada had found SVM better than Logistic Regression for this task. In this evaluation, SVM reached about 83% accuracy (0.8330). Its confusion matrix showed 469 true negatives, 0 false positives, 95 false negatives and 5 true positives. For the non-churn class, it achieved 83% precision, 100% recall and a 91% F1-score. For the churn class, precision was 100%, but recall was only 5% and the F1-score 10%. The headline accuracy therefore hides a serious weakness caused by class imbalance: the model mostly predicts the majority non-churn class and almost entirely fails to identify customers who churn.&lt;SEP&gt;Traditional classification method outperformed by the knowledge reuse CNN approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine learning model applied in reference [16] to analyze crash injury severity.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine learning model that reference [16] applies to crash injury severity analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;SVM classifier used to detect false data injection in intelligent transportation systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">978-3-031-75329-9_31.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;25293-55764-1-PB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
