<node id="Correlation Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Correlation Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis used to verify machine behavior; revealed correlations of machine size with mold width (0.98), mold weight (0.79), mold height (0.76), mold length (0.75), and part weight (0.61).&lt;SEP&gt;Statistical analysis technique whose principles are explained in reference 14.&lt;SEP&gt;Correlation study between the classes and their features. It found strong positive correlations between clamping force and mold dimensions: mold weight 0.788, height 0.737, length 0.741 and width 0.761. It found moderate correlations with total part weight (0.591) and part weight (0.4), and lower correlations with material features.</data>
