<node id="Confusion Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Confusion Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">The Confusion Matrix, also known as an error matrix, is a performance assessment tool for classification tasks. It presents predicted values against actual values in tabular form and sorts the results into four categories: true positives (TP), true negatives (TN), false positives (FP), and false negatives (FN). In this structure, actual values are labeled true or false, and predicted outcomes are labeled positive or negative. By showing these counts directly, the Confusion Matrix gives a comprehensive overview of a classification model's effectiveness, a detailed picture of its classification capabilities, and a way to see both correct and erroneous predictions.

The Confusion Matrix is the foundation for several other evaluation metrics. Accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score are all derived from its TP, TN, FP, and FN counts. In a study on churn prediction, it was one of five evaluation metrics, used alongside accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score, and it reported the TN, FP, FN, and TP values for each of seven models. In that work it also served as a visualization as a binary classification confusion matrix. Figure 3 showed results for models trained on all features, and Figure 4 showed results for models trained on selected features, allowing a direct comparison of the two feature configurations.

The Confusion Matrix has been applied in a variety of other evaluation settings:
- It was used to assess the performance of six classifiers.
- In a multi-class scenario, it showed how well each model classified 15 predicted machines across five machine classes, visualizing each model's true and erroneous predictions.
- It was used to compare a model without and with the Canny filter (Fig 8).

Beyond its role as an evaluation instrument, the Confusion Matrix has been a subject of research. Marom, Rokach and Shmilovici used it to improve ensemble classifiers. It was studied in reference [21], and reference [22] extended it to a multi-label classification setting.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-008</data>
