  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Unit">
  <data key="d0">Injection Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanical structure of the injection molding machine that uses a screw mechanism to drive molten material through a heated barrel into the mold under high pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine component that injects molten material into the mold cavity using a screw mechanism pushing material through a heated barrel under high pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;A primary component of the injection machine. It converts plastic from a solid state to a plasticized state and injects it into the mold.&lt;SEP&gt;Unit using a screw mechanism to push molten material through a heated barrel into the mold under high pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">978-3-031-75329-9_31.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Morocco">
  <data key="d0">Morocco</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Morocco is the country that served as both the source of the study's industrial data and the home of the institutions that supported the research. The dataset came from an automotive industry workshop, operated by an automotive company located in the north of Morocco.

Several Moroccan public bodies supported and funded the research project. These were the Ministry of Higher Education, Scientific Research and Innovation, the Digital Development Agency (DDA), and the National Centre for Scientific and Technical Research (CNRST). Their support was provided through the Smart DLSP Project and the AL KHAWARIZMI IA-PROGRAM. Morocco is also the country whose Law No. 09-08 governs the protection of personal data, which is relevant to how the research handled data.

In addition, Morocco was one of three countries that appeared in the international collaboration analysis of research on human resources (HR) and artificial intelligence (AI), which indicates the country's participation in cross-border scholarly work in this field.&lt;SEP&gt;Country whose contract law is the Code of Obligations and Contracts (COC), promulgated by the Dahir of August 12, 1913. The legal dataset used in the paper comes from Moroccan legal texts.&lt;SEP&gt;Country whose Ministry of Higher Education, Scientific Research and Innovation, Digital Development Agency (DDA) and National Center for Scientific and Technical Research (CNRST) support the research.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">978-3-031-75329-9_31.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_AIapplicationinmarketanalysis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accuracy">
  <data key="d0">Accuracy</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Accuracy is a widely used classification performance metric that measures the overall correctness of a model's predictions. It is the proportion of correct predictions among all predictions made. Derived from the confusion matrix, it is calculated as (TP + TN) / (TP + TN + FP + FN), where TP, TN, FP and FN denote true positives, true negatives, false positives and false negatives. One study presents this formula as Equation (1), although the preceding text says "calculate the MAE," which appears to be a mislabel for accuracy. Accuracy is often the main metric for assessing, comparing and ranking machine learning and deep learning models, including Random Forest classifiers and CNN classification models. It also serves as the optimization criterion in grid search for hyperparameter tuning and is used to evaluate training and validation performance in learning curves. However, accuracy is not always the most reliable measure, particularly when data features are diverse.

In customer churn prediction research, accuracy is the central metric for comparing classification models, including a comparison of seven machine learning models. In one study it is used to rank churn models, and the two most accurate are then explained with SHAP and LIME. Baghla and Gupta [5] are cited as reporting 99.35% accuracy for Random Forest (RF). Another evaluation reports 92.09% for an Artificial Neural Network (ANN), 91.21% for RF and 75.04% for Naive Bayes (NB). A further comparison reports Decision Tree at 89%, Logistic Regression (LR) at 86%, K-Nearest Neighbors at 84%, Support Vector Machine at 83% and NB at 75%. Other studies report RF reaching 93%, with one noting LR at only 53% and Stochastic Gradient Descent at 27%.

Accuracy is also applied as an image-level metric in deep learning. VGG16 reached a validation accuracy of 0.9909 and VGG19 reached 0.9136. In a CNN-based study, accuracy was 99.57% with a Canny filter applied and 95.31% without it, showing the filter's benefit. In another model comparison, prior baselines achieved 96.94% (Lee et al.) and around 93% (Ha et al.).

Beyond these applications, accuracy was used to compare three ticket recurrence prediction methods: Jaccard similarity scored 0.7419, Cosine similarity 0.8710 and the hybrid SBERT-Cosine approach 0.9355. It is also reported as an evaluation metric improved by a cGAN-based fraud detection approach, and it serves as a general performance metric in various performance comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7ef486f441df72175f968e398ffdd23d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-006</data>
