<node id="Digital Development Agency">
  <data key="d0">Digital Development Agency</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Digital Development Agency, also known by its acronym DDA, is a Moroccan government agency. It is consistently identified as an institutional supporter of research activities. Descriptions refer to the research it backs as "the research," "the work," "the project," the review's research, and the study presented in "This Paper" or the article being read.

The DDA's support is tied to research carried out under the Smart DLSP Project, which forms part of the AL KHAWARIZMI Program. This research focuses notably on burnout and includes a review study. One description states that the agency "partly supported" the work, which suggests the DDA was one of possibly several funding or supporting bodies rather than the sole sponsor.

In the knowledge graph, the Digital Development Agency's role is that of a Moroccan institutional backer whose support, through the Smart DLSP Project within the AL KHAWARIZMI Program, helped enable the research effort and its published findings.&lt;SEP&gt;Moroccan agency (DDA) that supports the research.&lt;SEP&gt;Moroccan agency (DDA) supporting the research.&lt;SEP&gt;DDA of Morocco that supported the research.</data>
