<node id="Overfitting">
  <data key="d0">Overfitting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Overfitting is a model failure in which a model fits its training data too closely and consequently struggles to generalize to new, unseen data. An overview of overfitting and its solutions is given in reference [29]. In the analyzed models, overfitting showed up as high variance, with cross-validation scores lower than the corresponding training scores. Learning curves were used to check for this possible bias, since models that appear to predict well may still be overfitting.

Several factors increase the risk of overfitting. High-dimensional data is one of them, and adding features can disperse the data and make generalization harder. The limited size of the dataset was a particular concern. The conclusion names overfitting, together with underfitting, as a consequence of the small dataset, warning that both issues could undermine the generalizability and robustness of the model's predictions.

Multiple strategies were used to mitigate overfitting:

- **Feature selection** removes irrelevant features, reducing both noise and overfitting, especially in high-dimensional settings.
- **Random Forest** reduces overfitting by averaging the outputs of multiple decision trees.
- **An 80/20 train-test split** helps detect and prevent overfitting by evaluating model performance on unseen data.
- **Data augmentation** was applied to counter overfitting given the limited size of the dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;Occurs when GANs memorize specific patterns in historical financial data rather than learning generalizable features, particularly in small or highly correlated datasets.&lt;SEP&gt;Phenomenon prevented by regularization techniques such as dropout to enhance generalization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
