<node id="National Center for Scientific and Technical Research">
  <data key="d0">National Center for Scientific and Technical Research</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Center for Scientific and Technical Research (CNRST, Centre National pour la Recherche Scientifique et Technique) is a Moroccan national research institution that provides institutional and financial support for scientific work. Several research papers and articles cite it as a supporter, including a study on burnout and a review article.

The CNRST supported this research mainly through the Smart Digital Logistic Services Provider (Smart DLSP) Project. The project belongs to the AL KHAWARIZMI Program, Morocco's national artificial intelligence initiative. Sources call the program both the "AL KHAWARIZMI IA-PROGRAM" and the "AL Khawarizmi AI Program." Because "IA" is the French abbreviation for artificial intelligence, both names refer to the same program.

The CNRST also funded research through its PhD-Associate Scholarship (PASS) program, which supports doctoral researchers. At least one study was funded under this scholarship. Through the Smart DLSP Project and the PASS program, the CNRST serves as a key funding and supporting body for Moroccan scientific research.&lt;SEP&gt;CNRST of Morocco, supporting the research through the Smart DLSP Project - AL KHAWARIZMI IA-PROGRAM.&lt;SEP&gt;Moroccan research center (CNRST) that supports the research.&lt;SEP&gt;CNRST of Morocco that supported the research via the Smart DLSP Project (AL KHAWARIZMI IA-PROGRAM).</data>
