<node id="Progress in Artificial Intelligence">
  <data key="d0">Progress in Artificial Intelligence</data>
  <data key="d1">venue</data>
  <data key="d2">Progress in Artificial Intelligence, abbreviated as Prog. Artif. Intell. (also written Prog Artif Intell), is a scientific journal that publishes research in artificial intelligence. It appears across several reference lists as the source of multiple cited works, showing its relevance to research involving AI methods and their applications.

Its earliest cited publication is "A Survey on Bayesian Network Structure Learning from Data," published in 2019. This review covers methods for learning Bayesian network structures from data, reflecting the journal's coverage of probabilistic modeling and machine learning.

Most of the cited works appeared in 2024. In various reference lists these are identified as reference 1 (or [1]), reference 3, reference 5, and reference [11]. Among them is the study by Tayalati et al. (2024) on cooling time prediction, which applies artificial intelligence techniques to estimate cooling times, likely in manufacturing or industrial process contexts. Some of these numbered references may point to the same 2024 cooling time prediction study, cited under different numbers in different documents, though the descriptions do not confirm this.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal (Prog Artif Intell) where reference [1] was published in 2024.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal (Prog. Artif. Intell.) that published the 2019 survey on Bayesian network structure learning from data.</data>
