<node id="I. Boukrouh">
  <data key="d0">I. Boukrouh</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">I. Boukrouh, whose full name appears as Ikhlass Boukrouh based on the corresponding email address (ikhlass.boukrouh@etu.uae.ac.ma), is a researcher affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory at the Faculty of Sciences and Techniques (FST) of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University. Boukrouh has contributed to research across several applied artificial intelligence and industrial engineering domains, appearing as both a lead and a contributing author.

Boukrouh is the first and corresponding author of a paper on hybrid sales forecasting published in IJE Transactions A: Basics, Vol. 38, No. 04, April 2025, pages 859-870. Boukrouh is also the first author of the 2024 bibliometric study on artificial intelligence applications in e-commerce, which drew on merged data sources. In addition, Boukrouh is the first and lead author of "Comprehensive Framework for Supplier Selection" (2024).

Beyond these first-author works, Boukrouh co-authored a study on anomaly detection in injection molding that combines a hybrid deep learning autoencoder with statistical process control (SPC). Boukrouh also co-authored a paper on a road detection pipeline, again listed under the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory at Abdelmalek Essaâdi University. Taken together, the work spans sales forecasting, e-commerce, supply chain decision-making, manufacturing quality control, and computer vision.&lt;SEP&gt;First author of reference [1].&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of reference [3], on the combined AHP-TOPSIS model.&lt;SEP&gt;First author of "Modeling and managing product unavailability risk in inventory through a fuzzy Bayesian network" (2024).&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of reference [19], the combined AHP-TOPSIS model for selecting injection molding machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the AHP-TOPSIS injection molding machine selection paper.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of reference [2].</data>
