<node id="L. Bouhsaien">
  <data key="d0">L. Bouhsaien</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">L. Bouhsaien is a researcher whose published work spans organizational behavior, industrial engineering, and data analytics. L. Bouhsaien is affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory at Abdelmalek Essaadi University. The body of work includes research on workplace well-being, manufacturing decision-making, anomaly detection, sales forecasting, and data resources.

In organizational behavior, L. Bouhsaien is the lead (first) author of the 2024 article "Burnout: A Pervasive Challenge Threatening Workplace Well-Being and Organizational Success," published in the International Journal of Professional Business Review. The paper was co-authored with A. Azmani. It presents burnout as a pervasive challenge that threatens both employee well-being and organizational success. L. Bouhsaien is also credited as the author of "Database BA" (2024).

In industrial and manufacturing research, L. Bouhsaien co-authored a paper proposing a combined AHP-TOPSIS model for selecting injection molding machines. This multi-criteria decision-making work is cited in several reference lists, including as references [3], [19], and [45]. L. Bouhsaien also co-authored a work cited as reference 2, which addresses anomaly detection in injection molding using a hybrid approach that combines a deep learning autoencoder with statistical process control (SPC). In addition, L. Bouhsaien co-authored a hybrid sales forecasting paper.

The technical, manufacturing-oriented topics differ markedly from the burnout research, which earlier raised the possibility that two different individuals share the name L. Bouhsaien. However, the range of applied analytics and decision-support work is consistent with the shared institutional affiliation and the overlapping 2024 publications. This makes it plausible that a single researcher works across organizational management and industrial machine learning. The available information does not definitively confirm whether this is the case.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of reference [2].&lt;SEP&gt;First author of the 2024 burnout paper in J Professional Business Review.</data>
