<node id="Springer">
  <data key="d0">Springer</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Springer is an academic and scientific publisher with regional offices in Singapore; New York, United States; Berlin, Germany; and Cham, Switzerland. It also publishes under the imprint Springer International Publishing. Springer publishes books, conference proceedings, encyclopedias, and book series in computer science, engineering, information systems, cryptography and security, statistics, logistics, transportation, decision science, economics, and social research. It is the publisher of the Lecture Notes in Computer Science series. Across various source documents, it is cited as the publisher of works referenced as [2], [4], [25], [31], and [33].

From Cham, Switzerland, Springer published the ECCV 2014 conference proceedings and Advanced Information Systems Engineering (Lecture Notes in Computer Science, vol. 12127). It also published the proceedings of the 2022 International Conference on Smart Applications and Data Analysis as Smart Applications and Data Analysis (Communications in Computer and Information Science, vol. 1677), which contains cited works including reference [2] and reference 6. From the same office it published the 2019 book "Development of Transport by Telematics," which contains a chapter by Harantová et al., and "Effective Investments on Capital Markets" (2019) in the Springer Proceedings in Business and Economics series. Under the Springer International Publishing name, it published the Encyclopedia of Quality of Life and Well-Being Research.

Through its Singapore office, Springer published Innovations in Computer Science and Engineering (2019), cited as reference 9, and Advances in Communication Systems and Networks (2020). The same office published Advances on Smart and Soft Computing (2022) and Green Connected Automated Transportation and Safety. Springer also published the book "Vehicular Ad-Hoc Networks for Smart Cities" (vol. 306, 2015).

From New York, Springer published the second edition of The Elements of Statistical Learning (2009) and a 2013 book on the R software. Its Berlin office published Hwang and Yoon's 1981 survey on multiple attribute decision making.

In decision science, Springer published Triantaphyllou's 2000 book on multi-criteria decision making methods and "Topsis" by Papathanasiou and Ploskas (2018). In logistics, it published "Dynamics in Logistics" (2017) in its Lecture Notes in Logistics series.

In cryptography and network security, Springer published several Lecture Notes in Computer Science volumes. These include the SAC 2016 proceedings (vol. 10532, 2017), the PQCrypto 2020 proceedings, and the NSS 2025 proceedings.</data>
