<node id="XGBoost">
  <data key="d0">XGBoost</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Gradient boosting machine learning model. Reference 13 uses it as the example model interpreted with SHAP.&lt;SEP&gt;Gradient boosting model used with XAI by Saitoh to identify potential online customers.&lt;SEP&gt;Gradient boosting classifier used as a comparison method.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine learning model used as an example with SHAP to extract spatial effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Gradient boosting ensemble learning algorithm that can be integrated with Boruta.&lt;SEP&gt;Ensemble learning algorithm that can be integrated with Boruta.&lt;SEP&gt;A gradient boosting algorithm combined with Boruta in an improved XGBoost-Boruta algorithm for PEMFC control system feature susceptibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-007</data>
