<node id="Autoencoder">
  <data key="d0">Autoencoder</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">An Autoencoder (AE) is an unsupervised deep learning neural network architecture designed to reconstruct its own input. It consists of three main parts: an encoder, a latent layer, and a decoder. The encoder compresses input sequences into encoded features, and the decoder reconstructs the original input from them. The model learns by predicting its input data and minimizing reconstruction loss. This makes it useful for building data-driven models when labeled data is unavailable, and it provides strong reconstruction-based representation learning and feature extraction.

Autoencoders are widely used for anomaly detection, where reconstruction errors are calculated and used to derive anomaly thresholds. In manufacturing, they are also applied to quality prediction, feature extraction, and input reconstruction. In the hybrid anomaly detection approach described in the source article, the Autoencoder supplies the feature extraction power and is integrated with statistical process control (SPC) charts, an approach also taken in Reference 2. The article implements the Autoencoder with LSTM layers, producing an LSTM-based Autoencoder (LSTM-AE). A prepared sequence array of dimensions [2974 × 5] is fed into the model, and its reconstruction loss is used to set anomaly thresholds.

Conventional autoencoders are noted to have limitations when applied to time series data, which motivates the use of LSTM-based designs. Variants of the architecture include deep, variational, and convolutional LSTM autoencoders, which are used in References [32], [33], [34], and [36]. Cited works apply autoencoders to triggers at the Large Hadron Collider (LHC), quality control of wastewater sensors, and energy forecasting. Table 7 of the article compares Autoencoder applications across these contexts, and the authors state that this comparison confirms the effectiveness of their proposed model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-019</data>
