<node id="Anomaly Detection">
  <data key="d0">Anomaly Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anomaly Detection is the identification of observations, events, or process behaviors that deviate significantly from normal operating conditions or from the majority of the data. In industrial and manufacturing settings, including smart factory environments, it allows deviations to be found early. This supports timely interventions, process optimization, and cost reduction. Whether an observation counts as anomalous is usually decided against a threshold reference point, so detection results depend strongly on the thresholds chosen.

Within the reviewed work, Anomaly Detection is the core problem, applied to the injection molding process. It is regarded as a promising concept for reducing costs in injection molding. It is applied specifically to the melt cushion parameter of an injection molding machine to detect process irregularities. The research area covered includes injection molding processes, Statistical Process Control (SPC) in injection molding, and Long Short-Term Memory Autoencoder (LSTM-AE) techniques. The problem is addressed both by SPC and by deep learning methods. A key approach captures normal process occurrences as time-based sequences on which the LSTM-AE is trained. The resulting hybrid SPC/LSTM-AE model identified four distinct anomaly types, including trend anomalies.

Anomaly Detection is also discussed in the related literature. Reference 2 addresses it for injection molding. References [14], [24], [25], and [34] deal with detecting abnormal behavior in manufacturing and injection molding data. LSTM-based anomaly detection for key performance indicators (KPIs) is also cited as relevant prior work.&lt;SEP&gt;Detection of process deviations and defects, enhanced by predictive control charts.&lt;SEP&gt;Downstream task proposed for future work to assess the impact of generated data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-56015fdaac28ae50466d3ddc4439d39b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-010</data>
