<node id="Using a Fuzzy-Bayesian Approach for Predicting the QoS in VANET">
  <data key="d0">Using a Fuzzy-Bayesian Approach for Predicting the QoS in VANET</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Article by Hafida Khalfaoui, Abdellah Azmani, Abderrazak Farchane and Said Safi, published in Applied Computer Systems, December 2022, vol. 27, no. 2, pp. 101–109. It uses a Fuzzy-Bayesian approach combining Bayesian Networks and Fuzzy Logic to predict risks affecting the quality of service in VANET, analysing the influence of routing, security and data processing on QoS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hafida Khalfaoui">
  <data key="d0">Hafida Khalfaoui</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Hafida Khalfaoui is a researcher in computer science, networking, and network security, affiliated with the LIMATI Laboratory at Sultan Moulay Slimane University. She completed all of her higher education at this university. She earned a B.Sc. in Electronic and Telecommunication Engineering in 2017 and an M.Sc. in Telecommunication Systems and Computer Networks in 2019.

Some descriptions present her as a Ph.D. student in Mathematics and Computer Science at Sultan Moulay Slimane University. A later description states that she obtained a Doctorate in Computer Networks and Security in 2024 from the Polydisciplinary Faculty of Beni Mellal, which belongs to the same university. These accounts likely reflect different stages of her career: the earlier descriptions date from her doctoral studies, and the later one records their completion in 2024.

Her research focuses on network security and on the performance of wireless and mobile networks, especially Mobile Ad hoc Networks (MANETs) and Vehicular Ad hoc Networks (VANETs). Her publications include the following:

- She is first and corresponding author of "Using a Fuzzy-Bayesian Approach for Predicting the QoS in VANET," which addresses quality-of-service prediction in vehicular networks.
- She is first and corresponding author of "Decentralized Authentication Mechanism for Mobile Ad hoc Networks," which proposes a decentralized authentication scheme for MANETs.
- She authored a paper on improving MANET security using artificial intelligence.
- She co-authored the FSMicroGenerator paper.

All of these works were produced under her affiliation with the LIMATI Laboratory at Sultan Moulay Slimane University.&lt;SEP&gt;Corresponding first author of the article, from the Department of Mathematics and Informatics, Sultan Moulay Slimane University.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-000</data>
