<node id="Sultan Moulay Slimane University">
  <data key="d0">Sultan Moulay Slimane University</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Sultan Moulay Slimane University is a university located in Beni Mellal, Morocco. It includes the Polydisciplinary Faculty and hosts the LIMATI Laboratory, which serve as the institutional base for academic research activities at the university.

The university is the institutional affiliation of the three authors of the article under consideration, Khalfaoui, Farchane, and Safi, who are connected to it through its Polydisciplinary Faculty. Hafida Khalfaoui, one of these authors, also received her academic training there, earning both her B.Sc. and M.Sc. degrees from Sultan Moulay Slimane University.&lt;SEP&gt;University in Beni Mellal, Morocco, hosting the Polydisciplinary Faculty and the authors' laboratory.&lt;SEP&gt;University in Beni Mellal, Morocco, hosting the Department of Mathematics and Informatics.</data>
