<node id="Ref [3]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [3]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Ref [3] is a citation label that appears across several distinct documents. Each use points to a different source work, so the descriptions below represent separate references that share the same bracketed number rather than one publication.

In vehicular and mobile networking, Ref [3] is cited for describing smart vehicles as the mobile nodes of Vehicular Ad Hoc Networks (VANETs). A related networking citation labeled [3] describes how nodes in Mobile Ad Hoc Networks (MANETs) operate, forwarding packets to the next hop through intermediate nodes. These two citations may come from the same networking-focused paper or from separate ones; the descriptions do not establish which.

In road safety, Ref [3] is cited for the multitude of factors that contribute to accidents. It is also cited for the link between alcohol consumption while driving and fatal accidents. These two traffic-safety citations may refer to the same source. In a separate occupational health context, Ref [3] is cited for the prevalence of low back pain among bus, car, and truck drivers.

In business and marketing, Ref [3] is cited for the role of customer loyalty in a company's economic success and in generating continuous revenue.

In manufacturing and industrial engineering, Ref [3] appears in two contexts. One work treats machine selection as a multi-criteria decision problem. Another addresses the challenges that quality defects create in injection molding.

In artificial intelligence, Ref [3] is cited for the observation that AI improves the accuracy and consistency of routine tasks.

Overall, Ref [3] is a generic reference identifier rather than a single work. Its meaning depends on the document in which it appears, spanning networking, transportation safety, occupational health, marketing, manufacturing, and AI applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [3]; a work describing Hyperledger Fabric's permissioned architecture, modular components, private data exchange and fine-grained identity management.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work (reference [3]) on vehicular networks improving delivery efficiency, economic factors and service level.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26549e3ff493405b55b221c1d804516e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-000</data>
