<node id="Ref [6]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [6]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Ref [6] is a citation label that appears in several unrelated documents. Each document uses it to point to a different source, so the descriptions below are distinct cited works that share the same in-text reference number rather than a single publication.

In the context of vehicular ad hoc networks (VANETs), Ref [6] covers how vehicles carry out the routing mechanism. It explains how intermediate nodes relay packets between vehicles that are too far apart to communicate directly. The same reference also discusses selfish nodes, which refuse to take part in routing in order to save their own resources.

In the context of mobile ad hoc networks (MANETs), Ref [6] describes a MANET as an infrastructure-less network of mobile nodes. It identifies two communication modes: direct communication between nodes within range, and multi-hop communication, in which messages are relayed through intermediate nodes. This MANET citation is closely related to the VANET citation in subject matter, but it is used in a separate citing context.

In occupational health research, Ref [6] is cited on long-term exposure to whole-body vibration.

In business and customer analytics, Ref [6] is cited on customer churn. It presents churn as a challenge that affects many industries because it leads to missed profit opportunities.

In machine learning, Ref [6] is cited on feature selection. It describes how removing irrelevant and redundant features helps prevent overfitting and improves model accuracy.

In decision-making and operations research, Ref [6] refers to a work that applies the TOPSIS (Technique for Order of Preference by Similarity to Ideal Solution) multi-criteria method to machine selection.

In probabilistic modeling, Ref [6] is cited on the quantitative aspect of Bayesian Networks (BNs). Specifically, it addresses how conditional probability tables express the probabilistic relationships between variables.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [6] regarding shortcomings of traditional inspection methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [6]; reference on Template-Based Code Generation, its popularity, effectiveness and limitations.&lt;SEP&gt;Work cited as [6] for chatbots being promising tools to address challenges in understanding legal documentation and drafting contracts.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited study aiming to detect risk factors related to geometric road design where crashes might happen.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work defining QoS as prioritizing applications under service constraints.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
