<node id="Dynamic Topology">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Topology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frequent changes in VANET topology caused by high vehicle mobility and variable network density.&lt;SEP&gt;VANET network topology that changes constantly because of high vehicle mobility and variable network density. Vehicles join and leave the network rapidly, which causes frequent path disruption and complicates routing.&lt;SEP&gt;MANET characteristic in which the network topology changes quickly and unpredictably as nodes freely join and leave. This makes it hard to distinguish regular topology changes from malicious behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Characteristic of MANET caused by node mobility. Along with the lack of centralized management, it makes MANETs more vulnerable to attacks than wired networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VANET Security">
  <data key="d0">VANET Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security in VANET, one of the input parameters, alongside routing and data processing, whose influence on QoS the Fuzzy-Bayesian approach studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Security of vehicular ad-hoc networks, covering attacks, authentication, privacy and cryptographic solutions. Many of the cited works address this topic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-010</data>
