</node>
<node id="Ref [8]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [8]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Ref [8] is a citation label that appears across multiple distinct scholarly documents. It therefore refers to different cited works depending on the source document, not to a single publication. The descriptions are grouped below by thematic context.

In the context of vehicular ad hoc networks (VANETs), Ref [8] addresses routing challenges, particularly scalability and limited bandwidth, which cause network congestion and interference. Ref [8] is also described as a comparative study of existing VANET routing protocols and algorithms. That study aims to select an efficient protocol that improves QoS parameters such as delay, jitter, throughput, and packet loss ratio across different network scenarios. A related description presents Ref [8] as work evaluating routing protocols using packet loss, end-to-end delay, and packet overhead. These networking descriptions may refer to the same or closely related works. In the context of mobile ad hoc networks (MANETs), Ref [8] provides classifications of attacks targeting these networks.

In transportation, logistics, and road-safety contexts, Ref [8] appears in several roles:
- It is cited as a study using a fuzzy-Bayesian approach for predictive analysis of delivery delay risk, including prediction of accident occurrence.
- It is cited for adopting the three-axiom Bayesian network (BN) validation approach.
- It is cited as work on events that interrupt traffic and on how delivery periods affect traffic.
- It is cited for its treatment of cleaning accident sites and the resulting skidding hazards.

Some of these logistics descriptions may point to the same source, though this cannot be confirmed. In an ergonomics or health-related context, Ref [8] supports the finding that long journeys without regular stops increase muscle tension, presumably among drivers or travelers.

In other domains, Ref [8] denotes further unrelated works:
- In business and customer relationship management, it supports the claim that companies spend six times more to acquire new customers than to retain existing ones, underscoring the value of customer retention strategies.
- In machine learning and data analysis, it is cited for the effectiveness of the Boruta feature selection algorithm.
- In manufacturing, it is a reference on the principle of the injection molding process.
- In software development, it covers Low-Code/No-Code platforms and the role of citizen developers, who build applications with little or no traditional programming expertise.
- In the legal and conversational AI domain, it is cited for the view that chatbots providing precise answers to complex questions are valuable tools for legal clarification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;25293-55764-1-PB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
