<node id="Reference [10]">
  <data key="d0">Reference [10]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference [10] is a citation label that appears across several distinct source documents. Because each document numbers its references independently, the descriptions refer to multiple different cited works rather than a single publication. Each is summarized separately below.

In the context of smart city and transportation security, Reference [10] is cited for the threat of attackers reprogramming traffic signals to cause traffic jams or block streets. This highlights the vulnerability of connected urban infrastructure to malicious manipulation.

In a business and management context, Reference [10] is a cited work on the proactive understanding and management of customer relations. It supports discussion of anticipatory approaches to customer relationship management.

In the medical and data science domain, Reference [10] is cited for feature selection in oncology and cancer detection. It supports the use of feature selection techniques to improve diagnostic and analytical models in cancer research.

In supply chain and decision-making literature, Reference [10] is cited for TOPSIS (Technique for Order of Preference by Similarity to Ideal Solution), a multi-criteria decision-making method used to rank suppliers.

In the field of industrial digitalization, Reference [10] supports the role of the Digital Twin in the Fourth Industrial Revolution (Industry 4.0). It emphasizes how Digital Twins integrate information technology (IT) with operational technology (OT).

In blockchain literature, Reference [10] is a cited work describing Hyperledger Fabric as an enterprise-grade permissioned blockchain platform developed under the Linux Foundation.

In distributed computing literature, Reference [10] is cited for the three-layer architecture of fog computing. This architecture consists of end devices at the bottom layer, fog nodes in the intermediate layer, and cloud servers at the top layer. Two descriptions refer to this same contribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
