<node id="Reference [11]">
  <data key="d0">Reference [11]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference [11] is a citation label that appears across several distinct documents, so it refers to multiple unrelated works rather than a single source. Each cited work is described separately below according to its subject area.

In the context of vehicular networks, Reference [11] is cited for security issues in Vehicular Ad Hoc Networks (VANETs). It attributes these issues to the open network environment and the dynamic topology of such networks.

In a business and management context, Reference [11] is a cited work on implementing customer relationship strategies that fit a particular business.

In the field of multi-criteria decision-making, Reference [11] is cited for Complex Proportional Assessment (COPRAS), a technique used to rank alternatives.

In the domain of Digital Twin research, Reference [11] describes the three-component Digital Twin concept model. The model consists of physical products, virtual products, and the data connections linking them.

In a manufacturing context, Reference [11] supports the claim that the molding adjuster allocates machines based on part design, mold design, material specifications, and customer demand.

In the blockchain domain, Reference [11] is cited for Hyperledger Fabric's modular architecture and its efficient consensus mechanisms, such as Raft and Kafka. According to this work, these features allow tailored networks to be built.

In post-quantum cryptography, Reference [11] is a source on the Module-LWE (Module Learning With Errors) and Module-SIS (Module Short Integer Solution) hardness assumptions. These assumptions underlie the security of ML-DSA (Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Algorithm).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-008</data>
