<node id="Reference [18]">
  <data key="d0">Reference [18]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference [18] is a citation label that appears in several distinct documents. Each use points to a different cited work, so each is described separately below.

In the context of vehicular ad hoc networks (VANETs), Reference [18] is cited for the security property of availability. This property ensures that the VANET network remains operational and that information is always accessible.

In a different context, Reference [18] is cited in connection with elliptic curve cryptography (ECC). It supports the claim that ECC consumes less power than RSA while offering the same level of security.

In the domain of machine learning, Reference [18] is a cited work on metrics for evaluating classification models.

In the field of Industry 4.0, Reference [18] discusses AI-based decision-making algorithms, IoT sensing networks and sustainable cyber-physical management systems within big data-driven cognitive manufacturing.

In the context of blockchain platforms, Reference [18] refers to a work describing Hyperledger Fabric's use of CouchDB as its state database.

Also in blockchain research, Reference [18] is cited for the role of signatures in public blockchains. Signatures authorize asset transfers and bind transactions to their signing keys.

In manufacturing process literature, Reference [18] is a cited work describing the injection molding cycle.</data>
