<node id="Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication is a fundamental security requirement, objective, and process that confirms the identity of users and network nodes. It is the essential step in controlling access to network resources and a core requirement for access control, because it ensures that only legitimate nodes can use network services. It is counted among five fundamental security concepts and is regarded as the first line of defense against attacks. By verifying nodes, authentication enables reliable communication over untrusted networks, keeps malicious users out, and preserves node legitimacy and overall network safety. This protection continues even when nodes move between groups.

In Mobile Ad Hoc Networks (MANET), Authentication is a central security issue and the main concern in reviews of ad hoc network security. It has drawn considerable attention from the scientific community, and research is trending toward decentralized authentication systems. It is the central research problem of the associated work, which proposes an authentication mechanism for MANET. That mechanism supports reliable node-to-node communication over untrusted networks and blocks malicious users, including when nodes move between groups. Related cited works include SIP registration authentication in MANETs, the biometric BSAP protocol, and blockchain-based access authentication in VANETs.

In Vehicular Ad Hoc Networks (VANET), Authentication has two components: identity authentication and message authentication. It is threatened by impersonation, ID disclosure, and spoofing attacks, and secure, anonymous authentication is considered critical in this setting. More broadly, authentication aims to defeat identity or role impersonation attacks. Authentication also appears as a security input parameter in a causal graph, where it is defined as the mechanism that guarantees the authenticity of a message's origin and verifies its sender.

In a separate, software-engineering context, Authentication refers to a pre-configured service built into generated solutions to reduce developers' workload. This usage is distinct from the network-security concept described above.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001</data>
