<node id="Artificial Intelligence">
  <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Artificial Intelligence (AI) is the development of computer systems that replicate human intelligence, including natural language processing, visual perception, speech recognition, and decision-making. The term is attributed to John McCarthy in connection with the Dartmouth conference. One source dates this to 1955, the year of the original proposal, while the conference itself is commonly dated to 1956. AI is regarded as a transformative, emerging technology and a key driver of the fourth industrial revolution. It is now applied in almost every field of activity and has revolutionized industries such as marketing, manufacturing, logistics, and healthcare. AI models are often called "black boxes" because their internal reasoning is opaque. As a search term family, AI also covers Machine Learning, Deep Learning, and Natural Language Processing. Text generation is a crucial domain within the field, and advances in AI have increased the development and deployment of chatbots.

AI is a central research field shared by the authors of the article in question. Their work includes AI for digital ecosystems and the integration of AI with digital transformation. AI is a research interest of Abdellah Azmani and part of the field of his Ph.D., and it is an area of specialization of Monir Azmani. It is also the field of the Ph.D. studies of Ikhlass Boukrouh and Loubna Bouhsaien. Nihad Lechhab Ouadrassi's Ph.D. specializes in AI, and AI for digital ecosystems is one of her research interests. Related doctoral work covers AI applied to e-commerce, as well as AI in manufacturing and maintenance management. AI keywords have been collected from the titles, keywords, and abstracts of scientific papers for bibliometric analysis. One such study examines AI's application in market analysis. Another traces the development and impact of feature selection techniques across AI and machine learning domains. Reference literature covers AI's time scale and social effects (Solomonoff, 1985) and its use in digital marketing (Ziakis and Vlachopoulou, 2023).

AI also serves as a complementary technology that enhances processes across many fields:
- Time series forecasting is one of its important applications.
- In Vehicular Ad Hoc Networks (VANETs), it helps optimize data processing and decision-making.
- In supplier selection, it is suggested for integration with Multi-Criteria Decision-Making (MCDM) methods to enable predictive analysis and dynamic supplier selection.
- In healthcare, it drives P4 medicine and is applied to oncology problems.
- In plastic injection molding, it predicts and alerts on process quality issues, which increases productivity and reduces the production of non-compliant parts.

AI is particularly significant in Human Resources (HR) and Human Resource Management (HRM), where it is described as revolutionizing HR practices. It is used to streamline processes, improve decision-making, automate operations, and support risk management. Research examines its implications for HR practices, organizational dynamics, productivity, employment, and business investment. In co-word network analysis, AI appears as a central theme alongside HRM. Its term frequency rose from 2 occurrences in 2019 to 33 in 2023, reflecting rapidly growing research interest in integrating AI with HR.&lt;SEP&gt;Research field active since the 1950s, now used to improve security and efficiency in networking and to tackle MANET security issues.&lt;SEP&gt;A system's ability to interpret external data, learn from it and use those learnings to achieve goals, applied here to MANET security.&lt;SEP&gt;AI offers dependable solutions for MANET security. Examples include self-manageable network administration, reduced error rates and increasing resilience as systems learn from experience.&lt;SEP&gt;AI; one of the information technologies, along with sensors and edge computing, that Ecodid integrates to enable vehicles to exchange information with their environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-000</data>
