<node id="Impersonation Attack">
  <data key="d0">Impersonation Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An authentication attack in which malicious nodes act as legitimate vehicles, for example by pretending to be an emergency vehicle. It is also enabled by exposed private vehicle data.&lt;SEP&gt;Attacks based on identity or role impersonation, which a robust MANET authentication scheme permitting only legitimate nodes is meant to defeat.&lt;SEP&gt;Attack based on identity or role impersonation. The authentication objective of the paper aims to defeat it.&lt;SEP&gt;An active attack in MANETs that BAODV detects.&lt;SEP&gt;Attack in which an attacker impersonates another node's identity; prevented because each node has one identity and key pair, its private key signs all transactions, and the cluster admin approves identities.&lt;SEP&gt;An attack the model resists. Each node has one identity and one key pair approved by the cluster admin, so an attacker cannot impersonate a node without the node's private key.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spoofing Attack">
  <data key="d0">Spoofing Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of authentication attack in VANET in which malicious nodes create false identities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
