<node id="Quality of Service (QoS)">
  <data key="d0">Quality of Service (QoS)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Measures the degree of service satisfaction as presented to the end user. In telecommunication networks it aims at better communication behaviour by routing packets correctly and using resources optimally.&lt;SEP&gt;Network performance guarantees in vehicular networks, addressed by references [22]–[29].&lt;SEP&gt;Ability to provide different priorities to applications satisfying service constraints in terms of time, bandwidth, packet loss and security; improving QoS in VANETs is a complex research area.&lt;SEP&gt;Network quality of service in ad hoc and vehicular networks, addressed by many of the referenced works.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [22]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [22]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work describing QoS in telecommunication networks as achieving better communication behaviour through correct packet routing and optimal resource use.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [22] for Boruta's wrapper method comparing features to random noise features.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work (in-text [22]) on Bayesian Networks as probabilistic graphical models combining probability and graph theory.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [22] for the statement that the cushion parameter optimizes material flow within the mold cavity.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work ([22]) on chatbots automating tasks across industries.&lt;SEP&gt;Paper cited as [22] on the limitations of normal-mode Internet communication in special conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [23]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [23]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work on the QoS requirements of VANET applications, notably that safety applications require minimum end-to-end delay and packet loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work (in-text [23]) on the formal DAG representation of Bayesian Networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work ([23]) on chatbots as virtual assistants.&lt;SEP&gt;Paper cited as [23] on RSUs providing Internet connectivity through base stations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [24]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [24]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work proposing QMM-VANET, a QoS- and mobility-aware clustering routing protocol for VANET.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work (in-text [24]) on independence relations enabling variable elimination and belief propagation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work ([24]) on chatbots as virtual assistants.&lt;SEP&gt;Paper cited as [24] on VANET applications such as traffic management and platooning.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [25]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [25]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work conducting a brief analysis of QoS and of routing protocols that minimize delay and increase overall QoS in VANET.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work (in-text [25]) on constructing BNs via literature reviews, expert interviews, brainstorming, or data analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work ([25]) on chatbots reshaping human-technology interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [25] in support of chatbots reshaping human-technology interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791500933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [26]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [26]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work conducting a brief analysis of QoS and of routing protocols that minimize delay and increase overall QoS in VANET.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work (in-text [26]) referencing the GeNIe Academic software.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [26] regarding natural language understanding and retrieval models for chatbot response selection.&lt;SEP&gt;Work cited as [26], supporting the statement that AI can help with data selection and security.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [27]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [27]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work improving QoS parameters such as delay, jitter, throughput and packet loss ratio using various routing algorithms, mobility patterns, MIMO and adaptive modulation and coding techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work (in-text [27]) on the impracticality of relying solely on expert knowledge for many CPTs.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [27] regarding NLU context understanding and chatbots remembering previous exchanges.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791500933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [28]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [28]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work that exploits Road Side Units to accumulate and transmit traffic data and finds shortest routes using the DDSRC algorithm.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work (in-text [28]) on fuzzy logic enabling automatic CPT generation and improved modeling precision.&lt;SEP&gt;Work cited as [28] for the definition of Event Tree Analysis as a probabilistic tree-structured technique.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [28] regarding retrieval models that select existing responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-002</data>
