</node>
<node id="Ref [49]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [49]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work [49] on implementing Fuzzy Logic for generating conditional probabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [49] for LSTM's ability to capture long-term memory in time series data.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work on integrating retrieval-based response generation into chatbots, which outperformed purely retrieval or generation models.&lt;SEP&gt;Study on passenger vehicle drivers involved in fatal crashes by speeding, alcohol-impaired driving and restraint use; reports 2819 of 41144 drivers in 2020 fatal crashes were speeding (6.9%).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integrity ensures messages reach destination unaltered">
  <data key="d0">Integrity ensures messages reach destination unaltered</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">It represents the mechanism used to ensure that a sent message should reach the destination on the chosen path without any alteration [32].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confidentiality failure compromises data security and user privacy">
  <data key="d0">Confidentiality failure compromises data security and user privacy</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The mechanism ensures that only authorized users can access the data. Failure to meet this requirement compromises the security of the exchanged data and the privacy of users [33].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Privacy mechanisms guarantee driver anonymity">
  <data key="d0">Privacy mechanisms guarantee driver anonymity</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This mechanism guarantees the anonymity of drivers and prevents an unauthorized party from knowing the combination between the sender's real identity and private information related to traffic messages, such as vehicle identity, direction and location [34].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Selfish nodes refuse to cooperate in forwarding messages">
  <data key="d0">Selfish nodes refuse to cooperate in forwarding messages</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">It refers to selfish nodes in the network that may refuse to cooperate in forwarding messages in order to increase their own resources [35].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Density is the number of vehicles driving concurrently on the road">
  <data key="d0">Density is the number of vehicles driving concurrently on the road</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">It is the number of vehicles driving concurrently on the road [36].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Choosing an effective VANET routing protocol is difficult">
  <data key="d0">Choosing an effective VANET routing protocol is difficult</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Choosing an effective one is very difficult because it depends on various parameters, such as mobility model, environment and others [37].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="High frequency yields short-range communication and poor connectivity">
  <data key="d0">High frequency yields short-range communication and poor connectivity</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">If the frequency is high, we get short-range communication, which results in poor connectivity [39].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obstacles diffract or block road signals">
  <data key="d0">Obstacles diffract or block road signals</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Things that can diffract or block the signals in the road, such as buildings, trees, hills and bridges [40].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adverse weather attenuates vehicular signal transmission">
  <data key="d0">Adverse weather attenuates vehicular signal transmission</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Therefore, they will negatively influence the connectivity of high-speed data links in the vehicle communication range [41].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vehicle sensors collect data on vehicle state and environment">
  <data key="d0">Vehicle sensors collect data on vehicle state and environment</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Amount of data collected from sensor systems related to state of vehicle or the external environment (based on radar systems, video cameras, image processing, etc.) [42].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vehicles can act as mobile service providers">
  <data key="d0">Vehicles can act as mobile service providers</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">These are resources/components that allow vehicle to act as a mobile service provider of sensing, data storage, data relaying, computing, infotainment and localization services [43].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congestion increases transmission delay and decreases throughput">
  <data key="d0">Congestion increases transmission delay and decreases throughput</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This variable describes the state of the network when there is an overload of the links, which progressively affects the network performance with an increase in the transmission delay and a decrease in throughput [44].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Connectivity improves with more active vehicles">
  <data key="d0">Connectivity improves with more active vehicles</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">It can be obtained if the number of active vehicles is increased in the network [45].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="E2ED is the time to send a packet from origin to destination">
  <data key="d0">E2ED is the time to send a packet from origin to destination</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The time required to send a packet from its origin to its destination [46].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy Logic generation of CPs is implemented in three principal steps">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Logic generation of CPs is implemented in three principal steps</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The implementation of the FL for generating CPs is done in three principal steps [48], [49]</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bandwidth is the maximum throughput between nodes without disrupting existing flows">
  <data key="d0">Bandwidth is the maximum throughput between nodes without disrupting existing flows</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">It is the maximum throughput at which packets can be transmitted between nodes without disrupting any existing network flow [38].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integrity">
  <data key="d0">Integrity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security input parameter of the causal graph. It is the mechanism that ensures a sent message reaches its destination on the chosen path without alteration.&lt;SEP&gt;Security goal satisfied by the proposed authentication method.&lt;SEP&gt;Security requirement satisfied through node signatures on request messages, ECDSA-signed transactions and hashed node identifiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Privacy">
  <data key="d0">Privacy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security input parameter of the causal graph. It guarantees driver anonymity and protects the link between a sender's real identity and traffic-related private information.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inadvertence">
  <data key="d0">Inadvertence</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security input parameter of the causal graph. It covers threats from trusted insiders who mean no harm but fail to manage security responsibly, which lets malicious outsiders exploit their privileges.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Selfish Behaviour">
  <data key="d0">Selfish Behaviour</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security input parameter of the causal graph. It describes selfish nodes that may refuse to forward messages in order to increase their own resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Density">
  <data key="d0">Density</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing input parameter of the causal graph. It is the number of vehicles driving concurrently on the road.&lt;SEP&gt;Development degree, plotted on the y-axis of the thematic map. It indicates how developed a theme is within the literature.&lt;SEP&gt;A material feature with a correlation coefficient of 0.156 with machine clamping force.&lt;SEP&gt;Bayesian network variable for vehicle density, with linguistic values low, medium, and high. Density and flooding attacks are the two parents of congestion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Routing Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Routing Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing input parameter (type of protocol) of the causal graph. It maintains links in the network to perform packet forwarding. VANET has many types, and choosing one depends on factors such as the mobility model and the environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bandwidth">
  <data key="d0">Bandwidth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing input parameter of the causal graph. It is the maximum throughput for transmitting packets between nodes without disrupting existing network flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frequency">
  <data key="d0">Frequency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing input parameter of the causal graph. It is the number of occurrences of a repeating event per unit of time. High frequency leads to short-range communication and poor connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Obstacle">
  <data key="d0">Obstacle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing input parameter of the causal graph. Obstacles are things such as buildings, trees, hills and bridges that can diffract or block road signals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weather">
  <data key="d0">Weather</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing input parameter of the causal graph. Adverse weather such as rain, snow and dust attenuates signal transmission and harms the connectivity of high-speed data links.&lt;SEP&gt;Bayesian network variable with linguistic values extreme, medium, and normal.&lt;SEP&gt;Input variable of the Bayesian model. Adverse weather degrades the quality of wireless communications in a VANET through signal attenuation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internet Data">
  <data key="d0">Internet Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data processing input parameter of the causal graph. It is the amount of data uploaded from the internet, which can improve productivity, travel comfort and economic prosperity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OBU">
  <data key="d0">OBU</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">On-board unit. As a data processing input parameter, it is the amount of data exchanged with the OBU, including V2V and V2I communications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="V2V Communication">
  <data key="d0">V2V Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vehicle-to-vehicle communication, one part of the data exchanged with the OBU.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
