<node id="Sensors">
  <data key="d0">Sensors</data>
  <data key="d1">venue</data>
  <data key="d2">"Sensors" refers to several distinct entities that share the same name: a data processing input parameter in a causal graph, an academic journal, and physical sensing devices within a Digital Twin system.

As a data processing input parameter of the causal graph, Sensors represents the amount of data collected from sensor systems about the vehicle state or the external environment. These sensor systems include radar, video cameras, and image processing.

As an academic journal, Sensors has published a wide range of research across several fields. In 2020 it published "Selfishness in Vehicular Delay-Tolerant Networks: A Review," the work cited as reference [49], and the paper by Pop et al. that combined Kalman filtering with Takagi–Sugeno fuzzy inference. It also published the paper cited as [13] in 2021. In 2023 it published the paper cited as [18], a paper on fuzzy PID control for remotely operated vehicles (ROVs), and Chaddad et al.'s survey of explainable AI techniques in healthcare.

In the context of a Digital Twin, Sensors are devices distributed throughout the physical system. They collect enterprise, operational, and environmental data, and they enable real-time bidirectional communication between the physical system and its virtual counterpart.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal that published reference [35].&lt;SEP&gt;Journal that published the 2020 paper on Kalman filtering combined with a Takagi-Sugeno fuzzy inference system.&lt;SEP&gt;An information technology that Ecodid integrates so vehicles can exchange information with other vehicles, warehouses and road infrastructure.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal that published references 20 and 27 in 2020.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;25293-55764-1-PB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
