<node id="Interference">
  <data key="d0">Interference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediate effect in the causal graph. It is caused by any signal other than the one configured in the network, and it leads to slower speeds, higher latency, frequent disconnects or failure to connect.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Congestion">
  <data key="d0">Congestion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediate effect in the causal graph. It is a network state with overloaded links, which increases transmission delay and decreases throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;Channel congestion variable with low/medium/high states over a 0-100% universe. Its parents are density and flooding attacks, and nine fuzzy rules govern it.&lt;SEP&gt;BN variable with low, medium and high states depending on density and flooding attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Connectivity">
  <data key="d0">Connectivity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediate effect in the causal graph that ensures successful data transmission from a source vehicle to a destination. It improves as the number of active vehicles increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Bayesian network variable with linguistic values bad, medium, and good.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="End-To-End Delay">
  <data key="d0">End-To-End Delay</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">E2ED, an intermediate effect in the causal graph. It is the time required to send a packet from its origin to its destination.&lt;SEP&gt;Network performance metric that is lowered by the FADA-based approach compared to standard AODV.&lt;SEP&gt;E2ED, a QoS metric used by related works [8], [10], [11] and [16].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002</data>
