  <data key="d0">Ref [56] Logistic Delivery Delay Risk Prediction</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [56]; combines BN and FL to predict risks of delays in deliveries in logistic services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combination of BN and FL is used in many domains">
  <data key="d0">Combination of BN and FL is used in many domains</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "In many domains and studies, the combination of the BN and the FL system is used, for example, predicting the population status of a rare animal using the inference mechanism in the ecological domain [54], determining the severity scale of a disease based on fuzzy medical rules [55], predicting the risks of delays in deliveries in logistic services [56] and others."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision Making in Transportation">
  <data key="d0">Decision Making in Transportation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Decision support in the transportation domain, which the study aids by providing an approach for generating massive data that help in making decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Criteria QoS Prediction">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Criteria QoS Prediction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prediction of QoS in VANET as a function of multiple criteria considered simultaneously. Classical approaches and existing studies can only consider a few parameters at once, which makes them insufficient when decisions depend on several criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Massive Database Generation">
  <data key="d0">Massive Database Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Generation of a massive database by the proposed approach. The database supports decision-making, helps determine the origin of risks degrading QoS in the network, and can be extended progressively using deep learning techniques.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Estimations">
  <data key="d0">Expert Estimations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A data resource, alongside learning databases, on which the Bayesian Network bases its evaluation of causal relations between nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
