<node id="Smart DLSP Project">
  <data key="d0">Smart DLSP Project</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The Smart DLSP Project is a Moroccan research project carried out within the AL KHAWARIZMI IA-PROGRAM. The program name appears in some sources as the AL KHAWARIZMI AI-PROGRAM. The two spellings refer to the same initiative, since "IA" is the French abbreviation for artificial intelligence and "AI" is the English one. The project is part of Morocco's national effort to promote research in artificial intelligence and related fields.

The Smart DLSP Project receives funding and institutional backing from three Moroccan bodies:
- the Ministry of Higher Education, Scientific Research and Innovation
- the Digital Development Agency (DDA)
- the Centre National pour la Recherche Scientifique et Technique (CNRST)

The project supported and funded the research presented in the associated paper, a 2024 study on burnout. That study is acknowledged as having been conducted under the Smart DLSP Project, which makes the project the main funding framework behind the work.&lt;SEP&gt;Moroccan research project under the AL KHAWARIZMI IA-PROGRAM that supported the review. It is backed by the Ministry of Higher Education, Scientific Research, and Innovation, the DDA and CNRST.&lt;SEP&gt;Research project within the AL KHAWARIZMI IA-PROGRAM, funded by Moroccan institutions, that supports the AHP-TOPSIS machine selection research.&lt;SEP&gt;Research project under the AL KHAWARIZMI IA-PROGRAM through which the work is funded.&lt;SEP&gt;Project that aims to provide an intelligent digital ecosystem to supply chain actors and to improve freight management and supply chain efficiency in a sustainable development context.&lt;SEP&gt;Project whose first interest is QoS in VANET in urban environments, because the majority of the companies involved are urban. Poor management of transport operations by logistics providers can harm the reputations of these companies.&lt;SEP&gt;Project under the AL KHAWARIZMI IA-PROGRAM through which the research was supported in Morocco.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-008</data>
