<node id="Fuzzy Logic Controller">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Logic Controller</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Controller based on fuzzy logic. It is studied in references [50] and [52].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Takagi-Sugeno Fuzzy Inference System">
  <data key="d0">Takagi-Sugeno Fuzzy Inference System</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Fuzzy inference system that reference [49] combines with Kalman filtering.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of fuzzy inference system. It is combined with Kalman filtering for online calibration of a car-following model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DBSCAN">
  <data key="d0">DBSCAN</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Density-based clustering algorithm that reference [51] improves using fuzzy logic and a genetic algorithm.&lt;SEP&gt;Alternative density-based clustering algorithm applied for comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;Density-based clustering algorithm tested with eps = 1.5 and min_samples = 14. It is known for robustness to noise and arbitrary-shaped clusters, but it failed to produce usable clusters and classified most points as noise.&lt;SEP&gt;Density-based clustering algorithm. Rad and Abdolrazzagh-Nezhad improve it for data cube clustering.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bayesian Belief Network">
  <data key="d0">Bayesian Belief Network</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Probabilistic graphical model discussed in references [47], [54] and [55].&lt;SEP&gt;Probabilistic graphical model. Cited works apply it to employee performance evaluation and, combined with fuzzy logic, to human error investigation and bankruptcy causes.&lt;SEP&gt;Probabilistic graphical model. Reference [37] generates its conditional probabilities with fuzzy logic, and reference [38] constructs one with fuzzy rules.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">10.2478_acss-2022-0011.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
