<node id="This Paper">
  <data key="d0">This Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">"This Paper" is a generic label for several distinct research articles, each referred to as "the article being read" in its own context. Many involve Abdellah Azmani and Moroccan institutions. Several were funded by the Smart DLSP Project of the AL KHAWARIZMI AI Program, supported by Morocco's Ministry of Higher Education, Scientific Research and Innovation, the Digital Development Agency (DDA) and CNRST.

The most frequently described instance is by F. Tayalati et al. (IJE Transactions B, Vol. 38, No. 02, February 2025, pp. 488–502). It reviews injection molding and MCDM methods and proposes a hybrid AHP-TOPSIS approach for selecting an injection molding machine. Four experts provided consistency-checked pairwise comparisons, from which AHP weights eleven sub-criteria under five criteria: investment cost, quality rate, performance rate, availability rate and operating cost. TOPSIS then ranks HAIT 320T, ARB 200T and a third machine, reported inconsistently as ARB 205T or ARB250T, using S+, S- and Si scores. The study uses real data from an automotive workshop in northern Morocco and is validated with three sensitivity scenarios on HAIT 320T's scrap and breakdown rates. A related paper (MVML 120) classifies hole-position and burr defects on injection-molded packaging boxes from northern Morocco. It applies Canny edge detection before a two-layer CNN on 256x256 OK/NOK images, which raised the F1-score from 97.03% to 99.72%.

A large group of descriptions concerns an IEEE Access article (DOI 10.1109/ACCESS.2025.3589285, 2025) presenting FSMicroGenerator. This tool generates full-stack microservice applications from UML-defined data models. It manages a package lifecycle of creation, validation, adaptation and pre-integration, and organizes output into packages, modules and projects. Its template-based engine uses dynamic and static templates to produce several kinds of output:
- backend files: models, repositories, schema validators, controllers, Express.js routes, communication, tests, documentation, Dockerfiles and .env files;
- Angular frontend components and internationalization files;
- DevSecOps-inspired infrastructure configuration with embedded monitoring, security, standards and design patterns.

The paper reviews MDA-based and code generation tools. It compares FSMicroGenerator with manual development on a MEAN-stack inventory management case study. Quantitative measures cover effort, codebase size, performance under load, scalability and resource usage. A qualitative expert rubric assesses modularity, reusability, clarity/consistency and maintainability. The paper discusses threats to validity, reports gains in development speed and architectural quality supported by an industrial use case, and notes real-world adoption.

Other instances include:
- A PRISMA review by D. Wilson and A. Azmani (IJE Transactions B, Vol. 39, No. 02, 2026) of GANs in finance. It covers 30 of 53 papers from 2019–2024 and 16 GAN variants, and identifies limitations including mode collapse and training instability.
- An Infocommunications Journal paper on blockchain authentication for MANETs using Ethereum smart contracts, fog computing, SHA-256, Keccak256 and ECC/ECDSA. Its references cover MANET security and blockchain authentication.
- An IEEE Access Hyperledger Fabric 2.4 benchmark (DOI 10.1109/ACCESS.2026.3677633). Its best configuration was B100T50, and it recommends OR endorsement and 1–4 peers per organization.
- I. Boukrouh et al.'s hybrid LSTM–SARIMA–Holt-Winters sales forecasting model (IJE Transactions A, 2025), which improved MAPE by 9–43%.
- Further works on SPC and LSTM-Autoencoder anomaly detection, LIME-based machine allocation, bibliometrics in market analysis, oncology and HRM, FAHP-Entropy-TOPSIS supplier selection, and fuzzy Bayesian risk prediction.</data>
