<node id="VANET">
  <data key="d0">VANET</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A VANET (Vehicular Ad hoc Network) is a wireless network formed by vehicles that enables communication and information storage between neighboring vehicles, making it a viable technology even when the Internet is unavailable. VANETs offer easy configuration and quick deployment, and their components include sensors, roadside units (RSUs), and edge boxes. However, the technology faces many problems, particularly Quality of Service (QoS) risks and security issues.

VANETs are defined by high vehicle mobility, which produces a highly dynamic topology. Network density varies, and vehicles join and leave the network quickly. Other characteristics include scalability, an open environment, and the absence of a centralized control unit. Further challenges include the hidden node issue, limited resources, and an insecure communication medium. High mobility and dynamic topology make VANETs especially vulnerable to attacks. Together, these traits expose VANETs to significant security and data processing problems and make QoS provisioning very complex. QoS is also affected by weather, obstacles, mobility, density, selfish node behavior, and attacks.

Because of these complexities, VANETs serve as the networking context and application domain for QoS research, including the Ecodid work. In this research, the factors influencing QoS are studied to identify input parameters, intermediate effects, and final impacts. The QoS risk of VANETs is analyzed and QoS is evaluated through fuzzy inference, with security, routing, and data processing parameters modeled as part of the analysis. VANET QoS is also predicted across urban, rural, and highway environments. QoS is the central focus of this paper and of related works.

VANETs are the subject of a range of cited works addressing security, road anomalies, logistics, connectivity, roadside-sensor monitoring, and related issues, including references [13] and [14]. Notably, blockchain-based access authentication work has been applied to VANETs, and the Blockchain-based authentication system [14] builds a secure, decentralized system that provides confidentiality and privacy for vehicular communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-008</data>
