<node id="FisPro">
  <data key="d0">FisPro</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">FisPro is a fuzzy inference system software tool used during the model development phase of the burnout study to build and integrate fuzzy logic inference systems. The authors used it to implement the paper's fuzzy project and rule base, and in particular to infer node states such as the CPU State variable.

The authors also used FisPro to produce the figures showing the fuzzy rules and the activated rules. For the fuzzy inference of the CPU State variable, the software displays a crisp centroid output of 0.784. This centroid value serves only as a visual diagnostic and plays no role in the conditional probability table (CPT) generation pipeline.

In the study's references, FisPro is cited as [38] via Software Informer, with an access date of September 4, 2025.&lt;SEP&gt;Software (https://www.fispro.org/en/) used to design a fuzzy inference system based on numerical data and expert rules.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
