  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factor influencing burnout considered in data collection and modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Factor influencing burnout; burnout is lower under high workload with weak communication and low obstacles, and higher with occasional workload spikes and moderate obstacles.&lt;SEP&gt;Amount of work assigned to employees; it can induce stress, anxiety and frustration.&lt;SEP&gt;Having many tasks with limited time or resources; a contributor to burnout.&lt;SEP&gt;Categorical variable identifying the type of application or service running on the virtual machine (dev 20.5%, devops 69.5%, sre 10%), introducing semantic variability and enabling logical constraints.</data>
