<node id="Fuzzy Bayesian Approach">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Bayesian Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Methodology combining Bayesian networks and fuzzy logic, used to quantify burnout variables.&lt;SEP&gt;Fusion of Bayesian networks and fuzzy logic. It has been applied to human errors, employee performance, delay risk, and accident prevention across the industry, healthcare, and finance sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk-analysis method combining fuzzy logic and Bayesian inference. Benallou et al. (2023) use it for truck-driver accident risk, and Bouhadi et al. (2022) use it for delivery delay risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Approach that reference [88] uses to evaluate accident risk caused by truck drivers.&lt;SEP&gt;FB approach that combines FL theory and expert knowledge via BN modeling for risk prediction. It fuses a causal relationship graph with conditional probabilities calculated by the FL system.&lt;SEP&gt;Proposed FB approach combining BN and FL to quantify QoS in VANET across three scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;FB approach that merges fuzzy logic and Bayesian probability theory and is presented as yielding more precise and reliable predictions than methods using only one of the two. It has been used in the ecological domain, medicine, logistics and VANET collision warning systems. Its limitations include difficulty incorporating all factors affecting QoS in VANET and subjectivity in selecting fuzzy sets and assigning membership degrees, which can introduce bias and inconsistent outcomes. The text advises using it with caution and in conjunction with other methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
