<node id="Probabilistic Graphical Models">
  <data key="d0">Probabilistic Graphical Models</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Class of models for representing probabilistic dependencies between variables. OpenMarkov is a software platform for building these models, and Bayesian networks are a type of them.&lt;SEP&gt;Class of models that recent research integrates with fuzzy logic to provide transparent, uncertainty-aware decision-making.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425274</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy Inference System">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Inference System</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A Fuzzy Inference System (FIS) is a rule-based reasoning system built on fuzzy logic. It maps input variables to outputs through a pipeline of fuzzification, an inference mechanism applying fuzzy if-then rules, and defuzzification. Researchers have reviewed heuristic methods for designing such systems over three decades. Software tools such as FisPro support building them, and a study on burnout used FisPro for this purpose.

Fuzzy Inference Systems have a wide range of applications. They have been used for wound hydration monitoring with biosensors, as reported in reference [90]. Reference [76] combined an FIS with IoT technologies to regulate room temperature and humidity. In its Takagi–Sugeno form, the FIS has been applied to calibrating car-following models. In network security, an FIS has been used to detect and prevent cooperative black hole attacks.

One driver-behavior application initializes the FIS with input values at the peaks of Gaussian membership distributions. It uses 27 fuzzy rules that relate Driver Condition, Distraction and Visibility to Driver Reaction Time, and 18 of these rules are activated in the illustrated example.

In another approach, an FIS supports conditional probability table (CPT) construction. The per-label aggregated firing strengths (µ_j) are extracted directly from the system and normalized into conditional probabilities. The FIS's standard weighted-average crisp output is not used in this setting.&lt;SEP&gt;Inference system with 180 fuzzy rules that produced 540 conditional probabilities for the Bayesian network.&lt;SEP&gt;Fuzzy reasoning method applied to hydration monitoring with biosensors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-010</data>
