<node id="Work-Life Balance">
  <data key="d0">Work-Life Balance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of three intermediate inputs, alongside depression and disengagement, in the Bayesian network of Lee et al., 2019.&lt;SEP&gt;Balance that allows employees to rest, spend time with family and maintain a healthy lifestyle.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonious integration of work and personal life. A lack of balance can take away rest time.&lt;SEP&gt;Work-life balance achievement is a factor that is not directly visible in the factorial analysis plot. It is threatened when employees sacrifice free time to manage their workload.&lt;SEP&gt;Factor in the burnout landscape and a component of comprehensive burnout prevention initiatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-010</data>
