<node id="Stress">
  <data key="d0">Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Psychological or emotional state that an employee experiences due to challenging work, high demand or external pressures.&lt;SEP&gt;Psychological strain experienced by employees. Workload can induce it, and together with harassment it can lead to depression.&lt;SEP&gt;An intermediate variable with linguistic values Minimal, Manageable and Overwhelming.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the interconnected variables in the burnout landscape, along with anxiety, pressure, tension, frustration and others.&lt;SEP&gt;Model variable describing the driver's stress, with states Stressed, Normal and Relax.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Harassment">
  <data key="d0">Harassment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mistreatment that employees can suffer at work. Together with stress, it can lead to depression and an inability to work.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depression">
  <data key="d0">Depression</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mental health condition that harassment and workplace stress can lead to, leaving employees unable to do their work.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Task Dependency">
  <data key="d0">Task Dependency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dependence of work tasks on one another. It can harm employees by leaving them out of control while they wait for things to be done, and it creates a sense of inefficacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Salary">
  <data key="d0">Salary</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Employee pay. Low salary is cited as an important factor in workplace conflicts, and status and salary concerns are most present in the public and administrative sector.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421472</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recognition and Self-Esteem">
  <data key="d0">Recognition and Self-Esteem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
