<node id="Fuzzy Bayesian Network">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Bayesian Network</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">The Fuzzy Bayesian Network (FBN) is a hybrid probabilistic graphical modeling approach that fuses Bayesian networks with fuzzy logic theory and expert knowledge. It is designed for problems involving uncertain, imprecise, or incomplete variables. It combines quantitative data with expert judgment to represent complex causal dependencies, and it supports risk prediction and failure forecasting in complex systems. The model pairs the causal structure of a Bayesian network, a directed acyclic graph (DAG) with conditional probability tables (CPTs), with fuzzy-derived probabilities. This enables failure probability assessment, system state estimation under different scenarios, and sensitivity analysis. A noted limitation is that inference can be computationally intensive for large networks.

In one specific implementation, the FBN is used for the intelligent predictive maintenance of critical IT components. Expert-elicited fuzzy rules are processed through fuzzy inference, and the rule firing strengths are normalized into conditional probabilities that populate the network's pre-calibrated CPTs. The model estimates the probability that an IT system enters a Normal, Degraded, or Critical state. It explicitly handles uncertainty and incomplete observations, integrates expert knowledge, and can be updated as new evidence becomes available. Its interpretable outputs, such as P(System_State=Critical), support maintenance planning, incident triage, and risk-based prioritization, and the model is well suited to cold-start contexts with little historical data. In this application, inference on the CPU subnetwork yields P(CPU_State=Critical)=0.984, which serves as the initiating event probability for a subsequent Event Tree Analysis (ETA).

The FBN is also widely applied in the literature for risk and safety analysis. Yazdi and Kabir (2017) present it as an approach for risk analysis in the process industries, and Zarei et al. (2019) apply it to the safety analysis of process systems. Other cited works use FBNs for human error investigation, microfinance customer satisfaction, inventory risk, delivery delay risk, and prognostics and health management. A fuzzy rough copula variant has been used for hospital service quality assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Probabilistic graphical model combining fuzzy logic and Bayesian networks, proposed to analyze accident occurrence factors; its inference is computationally expensive for large or multistate networks.&lt;SEP&gt;The predictive modeling approach used in the paper for road safety; future work aims to optimize its computational efficiency for real-time applications and expand it to incorporate a broader range of factors and scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mamdani Method">
  <data key="d0">Mamdani Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Common fuzzy inference method relying on defuzzification for fuzzy outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Fuzzy inference approach where the output is a fuzzy set, requiring defuzzification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sugeno Method">
  <data key="d0">Sugeno Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Common fuzzy inference method computing result values through a weighted average; chosen in the study for lower processing time, needing only the first two steps.&lt;SEP&gt;A fuzzy inference method that the paper implements to determine burnout probabilities from four activated rules.&lt;SEP&gt;Fuzzy inference approach where the output is a constant or linear function of inputs, offering higher computational efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425296</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uncertainty">
  <data key="d0">Uncertainty</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Imprecision in variables and decision-making addressed by Bayesian networks and fuzzy logic.&lt;SEP&gt;Vagueness in expert judgments that FAHP addresses within the FAHP-Entropy-TOPSIS approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Situation in which precise and reliable mathematical probabilities are lacking. Fuzzy Logic is suited to decision-making under it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
