<node id="Linguistic Values">
  <data key="d0">Linguistic Values</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Linguistic labels assigned to numerical values of input, intermediate and output variables; a crucial step in fuzzy logic applications enabling handling of imprecision and uncertainty.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative labels assigned to the input, intermediate and output variables of the fuzzy burnout model. Examples are Low, Medium and High, or Weak, Medium and High.&lt;SEP&gt;Discrete fuzzy labels assigned to Bayesian network nodes: Low/Medium/High; Normal/Warning/Critical for temperatures; None/Low/High for disk error counts; Non-overclocked/Moderate/High for overclocking; Normal/Degraded/Critical for component and system states.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
