<node id="Fuzzy Sets">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Sets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sets defined within a fuzzy logic system. Together with membership functions and input values, they determine which rules are activated during inference.&lt;SEP&gt;Mathematical sets integrated with AHP in FAHP to represent uncertainty through fuzzy numbers and linguistic variables.&lt;SEP&gt;Mathematical notion that FAHP integrates with traditional AHP to address uncertainties often present in human opinions.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [14]. Paper by L. A. Zadeh, Information and Control, vol. 8, no. 3, pp. 338–353, June 1965.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
