<node id="Membership Functions">
  <data key="d0">Membership Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Functions defined within a fuzzy logic system. Together with fuzzy sets and input values, they determine which rules are activated during inference.&lt;SEP&gt;Fuzzy membership functions whose subjective choice may influence risk estimates; future work envisions their automatic optimization through Bayesian learning or evolutionary methods.&lt;SEP&gt;Functions used to translate input values into fuzzy representations and assess membership degree.&lt;SEP&gt;Functions that translate input values into fuzzy representations and assess the membership degree of each fuzzy subset. They are created during variable definition.&lt;SEP&gt;Functions used during fuzzification, together with fuzzy linguistic values, to convert input variables into fuzzy subsets.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">4597JPB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
