<node id="Burnout: A Pervasive Challenge Threatening Workplace Well-Being and Organizational Success">
  <data key="d0">Burnout: A Pervasive Challenge Threatening Workplace Well-Being and Organizational Success</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">"Burnout: A Pervasive Challenge Threatening Workplace Well-Being and Organizational Success" is a 2024 article by Loubna Bouhsaien and Abdellah Azmani, published in the International Journal of Professional Business Review (Miami, v. 9, n. 4, pp. 01-21, e04597). The manuscript was received on January 22, 2024 and accepted on March 22, 2024. The article addresses the growing prevalence of employee burnout and treats it as a threat to workplace well-being and organizational success. It examines workplace dynamics and reviews the factors that lead to burnout.

The article's central contribution is a novel hybrid methodology, the fuzzy Bayesian approach, which combines Bayesian networks and fuzzy logic to identify and address burnout risks comprehensively. The model is built on burnout-related variables drawn from the existing literature, and the article summarizes the relationships among these variables. The authors implement the approach with OpenMarkov for the Bayesian network component and FisPro for the fuzzy logic component.

The fuzzy logic system uses the Sugeno inference method. Its inputs include frustration and work-life balance achievement, and the system is used to quantify burnout variables. The findings show that communication overload and obstacle level are positively correlated with burnout, and that communication effectiveness moderates this relationship.

The article also includes a bibliometric analysis of the Scopus database, carried out partly with Biblioshiny. This analysis covers:
- the growth of burnout publications from 1979 to 2023,
- scientific production on employee burnout by subject area,
- a factorial analysis of the field.

The reference list draws on literature about Bayesian networks, fuzzy logic and burnout. Overall, the article adds to the scientific discourse on burnout, aims to support evidence-based interventions, and advocates a healthier, more balanced and sustainable approach to work.&lt;SEP&gt;Article by L. Bouhsaien and A. Azmani (2024) in International Journal of Professional Business Review, 9(4), e04597, on burnout as a threat to workplace well-being.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [91]. Bouhsaien L and Azmani A, Journal of Professional Business Review. The paper discusses burnout as a threat to workplace well-being and organizational success.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [91]. Bouhsaien L and Azmani A, J Professional Business Review, 2024, 9(4):e04597. Discusses burnout as a threat to workplace well-being and organizational success.</data>
