<node id="Assessing Musculoskeletal Disorder Susceptibility in Professional Drivers Using K-Means Algorithms">
  <data key="d0">Assessing Musculoskeletal Disorder Susceptibility in Professional Drivers Using K-Means Algorithms</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, published in Informatica 49 (2025) 801–812. It proposes a driver profiling model using the K-means clustering algorithm to establish risk profiles for musculoskeletal disorders (MSDs) in professional drivers, integrating personal and professional variables such as age, work experience, BMI, weekly hours worked and physical exercise. The model estimates that only 21% of drivers are at low risk of developing MSDs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
