<node id="Ref [9]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [9]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Ref [9] is a citation label that appears in multiple, unrelated documents, each with its own reference list. The descriptions therefore refer to several distinct cited works that share the designation "[9]" rather than to one source. Each is summarized separately below.

In the context of occupational health, Ref [9] is cited for evidence that a high Body Mass Index (BMI) and a lack of exercise contribute to musculoskeletal disorders (MSDs).

In a business and customer-management context, Ref [9] is cited for the claim that companies spend six times more to acquire new customers than to retain existing ones. This underscores the economic value of customer retention.

In a machine learning context, Ref [9] is cited for the effectiveness of the Boruta algorithm, a feature-selection method.

In a manufacturing context, Ref [9] is a cited work on the operating principle of the injection molding process.

In the blockchain domain, Ref [9] is cited for its description of how blockchain operates, covering transaction blocks, the role of miners, consensus mechanisms, and the maintenance of distributed copies of the ledger. A related citation labeled Ref [9] shows the use of blockchain technology in the Internet of Things (IoT). It is uncertain whether these two blockchain citations are the same work or separate references in different documents.

In the software engineering domain, Ref [9] is a reference on the capabilities of Generative AI in software development. It also addresses the challenges of ensuring that AI-generated code complies with coding standards.

In the legal technology domain, Ref [9] is cited for the view that chatbots able to give precise answers to complex questions are valuable tools for legal clarification.&lt;SEP&gt;A cited comparative study of existing VANET routing protocols and algorithms. It aims to select an efficient protocol that improves QoS parameters such as delay, jitter, throughput and packet loss ratio across network scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Related work in Table 1 that uses various routing algorithms with different mobility patterns to improve QoS in VANET. Its metrics are throughput, packet delivery ratio, jitter, delay and packet loss ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;25293-55764-1-PB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [10]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [10]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Ref [10] is a citation label that appears across several distinct source documents. In each document it points to a different cited work, so the label refers to multiple separate references rather than a single source. Each is summarized below.

In the context of occupational health, Ref [10] is cited for evidence on work absence linked to musculoskeletal disorders (MSDs) in European companies. It also supports the observation that MSDs can lead to permanent disability.

In the context of machine learning and feature selection, Ref [10] is cited as a reference for integrating Random Forest with the Boruta algorithm. It is used to support claims about Boruta's effectiveness as a feature selection method and its combination with Random Forest classifiers.

In manufacturing, Ref [10] refers to a cited work on materials widely used in injection molding.

In distributed computing, Ref [10] is cited for its description of fog computing, including its three-layer architecture.

In software engineering, Ref [10] serves as a reference on the capabilities of Generative AI in software development.

In the legal domain, Ref [10] is cited for the view that chatbots able to give precise answers to complex questions are valuable tools for legal clarification.

In cybersecurity, Ref [10] refers to a cited work describing passive attacks. That work characterizes them as compromising confidentiality and as a bridge to other, more dangerous attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Proposes QMM-VANET, a clustering routing protocol.&lt;SEP&gt;Related work on improving security and connectivity, using the metrics packet delivery ratio and E2ED.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
