<node id="Long Short-Term Memory">
  <data key="d0">Long Short-Term Memory</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) is a recurrent neural network (RNN) architecture introduced by S. Hochreiter and J. Schmidhuber in the paper published in Neural Computation (vol. 9, no. 8, pp. 1735–1780, November 1997), cited as reference [49]. LSTM was proposed to increase the memory capacity of standard RNNs. It adds long-term memory states, known as cell states, and regulates information flow through input, output, and forget gates. This design lets LSTM capture long-term dependencies, and it is well known for modeling long-term memory in time-series data. Sherstinsky (2020) presents its fundamentals, and other cited works cover LSTM cells, MIA-LSTM forecasting, KPI anomaly detection, and LSTM-based autoencoders.

LSTM is used across many applications. A deep LSTM forms the time-series forecasting module of the system by Matos et al. [11]. LSTM networks have also been used to predict epileptic seizures from EEG signals. In Kumar et al.'s stock prediction method, an LSTM acts as the generator of a Generative Adversarial Network (GAN). Qais et al. (2023) use LSTM within stacked autoencoders for anomaly detection.

In hybrid anomaly detection, LSTM (cited as [14]) is a core component. It serves as the basis of an Autoencoder for time-series sequences, the LSTM-AE. During tuning of this LSTM-AE, the number of LSTM cells per layer was set to either 32 or 64. LSTM is also a component of a hybrid deep learning model that outperforms standalone LSTM by 9%, showing the gains possible from combining LSTM with complementary techniques.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
