<node id="K-Nearest Neighbors">
  <data key="d0">K-Nearest Neighbors</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">K-Nearest Neighbors (K-NN or KNN) is a supervised classification algorithm introduced by Fix and Hodges in 1951. It assigns an observation to the most frequent class among the K most similar observations in the training data. Its simplicity and interpretability make it a widely used baseline and comparison model across application domains.

In customer churn prediction, K-NN is a common supervised technique and serves as a comparison model in multiple churn studies. In one study it was one of seven classification models compared for predicting churn. There, it reached an accuracy of about 84% (0.8418), with a confusion matrix of 452 true negatives, 17 false positives, 73 false negatives and 27 true positives. For the non-churn class (Class 0), it achieved 86% precision, 96% recall and a 91% F1-score. Its non-churn precision was the lowest among the compared models. For the churn class (Class 1), it achieved only 27% recall and a 38% F1-score, which shows limited ability to identify customers who actually churn.

The reported churn-class precision is inconsistent within that study: the text gives 71%, while Table 1 gives 61%. The confusion matrix supports the Table 1 figure, since 27 true positives out of 44 predicted positives yields about 61%. That value also agrees with the reported 38% F1-score.

Beyond churn prediction, KNN has also been used in healthcare. Obukhov et al. [18] found that it gave good results for classifying user movements during musculoskeletal rehabilitation exercises.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine learning model compared by Patre et al. for predicting product sales in e-commerce.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002</data>
