<node id="Assessing Musculoskeletal Disorder Susceptibility in Professional Drivers">
  <data key="d0">Assessing Musculoskeletal Disorder Susceptibility in Professional Drivers</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, published in Informatica 49 (2025) 801–812; it uses a k-means clustering approach on data from 277 professional drivers to identify risk driver profiles for musculoskeletal disorders, comparing against hierarchical clustering, DBSCAN and GMM.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, by I. Benallou et al., published in Informatica 49 (2025) 801–812; it applies K-Means clustering to segment professional drivers by musculoskeletal disorder (MSD) risk, validated with the Silhouette Score and Calinski-Harabasz Index.&lt;SEP&gt;Article by I. Benallou et al. in Informatica 49 (2025), pages 801–812. The running header truncates the title after "Professional…", so "Drivers" is inferred from the text's focus on drivers. The article builds a dataset of professional drivers and replaces several working-condition columns with a composite Working Conditions Score (WCS). It expands the original 277 observations to 1,385 synthetic individuals, validates them, and standardizes the data for a distance-based model.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, published in Informatica 49 (2025) 801–812. The running header truncates the title as "Assessing Musculoskeletal Disorder Susceptibility in Professional…", so the completion "Drivers" is inferred from the text. The paper clusters professional drivers by musculoskeletal disorder (MSD) risk using K-means (k = 3). It compares K-means with hierarchical clustering, DBSCAN and GMM using internal validation metrics. It then assigns cluster labels to drivers to guide targeted preventive measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
