<node id="Engineering Applications of Artificial Intelligence">
  <data key="d0">Engineering Applications of Artificial Intelligence</data>
  <data key="d1">venue</data>
  <data key="d2">Journal that published the paper cited as [11] in 2024.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal that published reference [11]. The venue name is truncated in the text as "Engineering Applications of Artificial".&lt;SEP&gt;Journal that published the 2019 review on the heuristic design of fuzzy inference systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501144</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertical Vibrations">
  <data key="d0">Vertical Vibrations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Exposure of drivers to vertical vibrations. Reference [6] studies this exposure as a risk factor for adverse health effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Equation Model">
  <data key="d0">Structural Equation Model</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Statistical modeling approach that reference [2] uses to predict traffic sanctions of public transport drivers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design of Experiments">
  <data key="d0">Design of Experiments</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Experimental design approach that reference [6] uses to statistically predict the risk of adverse health effects on drivers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ergonomic Work Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Ergonomic Work Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Ergonomic assessment approach applied in reference [7] to bus drivers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Sectional Study">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Sectional Study</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Observational study design used in references [8] and [9].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Evidence-synthesis procedure used to study musculoskeletal disorders among taxi drivers.&lt;SEP&gt;Evidence synthesis method used in reference [10] to estimate the prevalence and incidence of work-related musculoskeletal disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Series Machine Learning">
  <data key="d0">Time Series Machine Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine learning on time series data, used in reference [11] with motion capture to prevent work-related musculoskeletal disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Learning Approach to Determine the Decision Rules in Ergonomic Assessment of Working Posture in Sewing Machine Operators">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning Approach to Determine the Decision Rules in Ergonomic Assessment of Working Posture in Sewing Machine Operators</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [12]. By J.-M. Su, J.-H. Chang, N. L. D. Indrayani and C.-J. Wang, published in the Journal of Safety Research, vol. 87, pp. 15-26, December 2023. The paper applies machine learning to derive decision rules for the ergonomic assessment of sewing machine operators' working posture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wearable Inertial Measurement Unit Sensing System for Musculoskeletal Disorders Prevention in Construction">
  <data key="d0">Wearable Inertial Measurement Unit Sensing System for Musculoskeletal Disorders Prevention in Construction</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [13]. By J. Zhao, E. Obonyo and S. G. Bilén, published in Sensors, vol. 21, no. 4, January 2021. The paper presents a wearable IMU sensing system for preventing musculoskeletal disorders in construction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-010</data>
