<node id="Work-Related Musculoskeletal Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Work-Related Musculoskeletal Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Occupational health problem that several cited works address through motion capture, wearable sensors and machine learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Determining of Cluster in K-means Clustering">
  <data key="d0">Determining of Cluster in K-means Clustering</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [22], although the start of the title is cut off in the text. Published in International Journal of Advance Research in Computer Science and Management Studies, vol. 1, pp. 90-95, January 2013. It deals with determining clusters in K-means clustering.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance analysis of Kmeans with modified initial centroid selection algorithms and developed Kmeans9+ model">
  <data key="d0">Performance analysis of Kmeans with modified initial centroid selection algorithms and developed Kmeans9+ model</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [23]. Written by A. A. Abdulnassar and L. R. Nair and published in Measurement: Sensors, vol. 25, p. 100666, February 2023. It analyzes K-means with modified initial centroid selection algorithms and develops the Kmeans9+ model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biomechanical evaluation of midwifery tasks and its relationship with the prevalence of musculoskeletal disorders">
  <data key="d0">Biomechanical evaluation of midwifery tasks and its relationship with the prevalence of musculoskeletal disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [24]. Written by N. Hasheminejad, M. Amirmahani and S. Tahernejad and published in Heliyon, vol. 9, no. 9, September 2023. It evaluates midwifery tasks biomechanically and relates them to the prevalence of musculoskeletal disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Musculoskeletal disorders among taxi drivers: a systematic review and meta-analysis">
  <data key="d0">Musculoskeletal disorders among taxi drivers: a systematic review and meta-analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [25]. Written by E. Rezaei et al. and published in BMC Musculoskelet Disord, vol. 25, no. 1, p. 663, August 2024. It is a systematic review and meta-analysis of musculoskeletal disorders among taxi drivers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prediction of Work-Related Risk Factors among Bus Drivers Using Machine Learning">
  <data key="d0">Prediction of Work-Related Risk Factors among Bus Drivers Using Machine Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [26]. Written by P. K. Hanumegowda and S. Gnanasekaran and published in International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health, vol. 19, no. 22, 2022. It predicts work-related risk factors among bus drivers using machine learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prevalence of Musculoskeletal Disorders in Heavy Vehicle Drivers and Office Workers: A Comparative Analysis Using a Machine Learning Approach">
  <data key="d0">Prevalence of Musculoskeletal Disorders in Heavy Vehicle Drivers and Office Workers: A Comparative Analysis Using a Machine Learning Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [27]. Written by M. Raza et al. and published in Healthcare, vol. 12, no. 24, 2024. It compares the prevalence of musculoskeletal disorders in heavy vehicle drivers and office workers using machine learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421575</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
