<node id="Musculoskeletal Disorders">
  <data key="d0">Musculoskeletal Disorders</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Musculoskeletal Disorders (MSDs) are health conditions affecting the muscles, joints and back. Examples include low back pain caused by overload of the musculoskeletal system. MSDs are a major global health problem and a leading cause of permanent disability. They reduce quality of life and cause injuries among staff, and they lead to economic losses through absenteeism and medical expenses.

MSDs are the central topic of the paper and of many cited works. The research looks at their prevalence, risk factors and susceptibility, with particular emphasis on professional drivers, a group in which these disorders are highly prevalent. Risk among professional drivers is assessed through methods such as cluster analysis, with MSDs treated as the main health outcome. The literature also covers MSDs at the levels of prevention, diagnosis and rehabilitation, including work-related forms among drivers and other workers. Populations studied include midwives, taxi drivers, heavy vehicle drivers, office workers, teachers and industrial workers.

Separately, the name "Musculoskeletal Disorders" also refers to a journal, which published the work cited as [10] in 2021 (vol. 22, no. 1). Its DOI prefix, 10.1186, suggests that the journal is BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c6cf0e7751b1667f02411ba9fa2e2995-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">7561-ArticleText-31951-37131-10-20251228.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421588</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Explainable Machine Learning Models Applied to Predicting Customer Churn for E-Commerce">
  <data key="d0">Explainable Machine Learning Models Applied to Predicting Customer Churn for E-Commerce</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, published in IAES International Journal of Artificial Intelligence (IJ-AI), Vol. 14, No. 1, February 2025, pp. 286-297. It proposes seven machine learning classification models (DT, RF, SVM, LR, NB, K-NN, ANN) to predict customer churn in e-commerce. ANN achieves the highest accuracy at 92.09%, followed by RF at 91.21%, while NB performs worst at 75.04%. SHAP and LIME are used to explain the models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">25293-55764-1-PB.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791421985</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
