<node id="Customer Churn">
  <data key="d0">Customer Churn</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The transition of a customer from one service provider to another. Businesses cannot completely avoid customer churn.&lt;SEP&gt;Occurs when a customer stops using a company's product or service. It causes missed profit opportunities and is a critical challenge for e-commerce companies.&lt;SEP&gt;Classification target of the E-Commerce Dataset, focusing on customers leaving an online retailer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">25293-55764-1-PB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423712</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="E-Commerce">
  <data key="d0">E-Commerce</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The industry in which the study predicts customer churn. AI techniques in e-commerce enhance marketing, payments and logistics.&lt;SEP&gt;Electronic commerce, a rapidly growing field in which business transactions are conducted on the internet.&lt;SEP&gt;Field of online commerce, including B2C e-commerce, in which customer churn prediction and XAI applications are studied.&lt;SEP&gt;Business sector to which Ikhlass Boukrouh's doctoral research in artificial intelligence and data science is applied.&lt;SEP&gt;Sector to which Ikhlass Boukrouh's Ph.D. research in artificial intelligence and data science is applied.&lt;SEP&gt;Application sector of Ikhlass Boukrouh's Ph.D. research in artificial intelligence and data science.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-016</data>
