  <data key="d2">Neural network model compared in several churn prediction studies, including Najjar et al. and as a reference classifier in Amin et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Model based on neurons, typically consisting of an input layer, one or more hidden layers and an output layer.&lt;SEP&gt;Model whose implementation requires choosing hyperparameters such as the number of hidden layers, the number of neurons in each layer, activation functions and optimizer functions. These are tuned through iterative training to minimize a chosen quality metric.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine learning model that reference [13] combines with a genetic algorithm to identify significant crash factors.</data>
