  <data key="d2">Cited as [35]. Source describing decision trees as an inductive learning method that is easy to interpret, reliable and widely preferred in classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work [35] describing logistic regression, SVM, and K-NN origins and properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Review of the AHP method that shows the use of the geometric mean method across various research studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work, identified as [35], supporting the controlled-overlap criterion for determining the spread of Gaussian membership functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Work cited regarding selfish nodes refusing to participate in routing on highways to save resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [35]; Hyperledger Fabric performance study.</data>
