  <data key="d0">Reference [46]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work [46] describing the objectives of interpretable machine learning.&lt;SEP&gt;Work cited as [46]. Its authors, title and year are not visible in the input text. It is cited for the procedure of obtaining external weights of sub-criteria by multiplying internal weights by the weight of their corresponding criterion.&lt;SEP&gt;Work cited as [46] by Kjærulff and van der Gaag. It describes the analytic sensitivity method for Bayesian networks, which expresses a target posterior as a rational linear function of a CPT parameter.</data>
