<node id="Procedia Computer Science">
  <data key="d0">Procedia Computer Science</data>
  <data key="d1">venue</data>
  <data key="d2">Procedia Computer Science is a scholarly journal and publication venue that appears repeatedly as a source of cited works across the referenced literature. It has published research spanning multiple years, from at least 2015 through 2024, which shows its sustained role as an outlet for computer science research.

Several specific works are attributed to Procedia Computer Science. It published Nayak et al. (2016) and reference [4] in 2015. Its 2020 publications include reference [7], reference [40], and a paper presenting a blockchain-based architecture for Flying Ad Hoc Networks (FANETs), which appeared in volume 173. It published reference 39 in 2022. In 2023 it published a paper by Liu et al. on text similarity detection in volume 228. It also published reference [22] in 2024, as well as references [24] and [25], whose publication years are not specified.

Taken together, these citations show that Procedia Computer Science covers a broad range of computing topics, including networking and blockchain applications as well as text analysis and similarity detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal that published reference [14] in 2018.&lt;SEP&gt;Publication venue of reference [9], 2023.</data>
