  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artificial Neural Network">
  <data key="d0">Artificial Neural Network</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">The Artificial Neural Network (ANN) is a machine learning and deep learning model used across many domains. It is best documented as a supervised classification model for predicting customer churn, and it can be optimized for that task. In a comparison of seven supervised models for churn prediction, the ANN achieved the highest overall accuracy, 92.09% (0.9209, often rounded to 92%), and ranked among the two highest-performing models.

The ANN's confusion matrix in that study recorded 459 true negatives, 10 false positives, 35 false negatives, and 65 true positives. For the non-churn class (class 0), it achieved 93% precision, 98% recall, and a 95% F1-score. For the churn class (class 1), it achieved 87% precision, 65% recall, and a 74% F1-score, the best churn F1-score among the compared models. Because it outperformed the other models, the ANN was selected for explainability analysis, and its predictions were interpreted using both Kernel SHAP and LIME.

The ANN also appears widely in related churn prediction literature:
- Kumar and Kumar applied a neural network model to predict customer churn.
- Larasati et al. reported 76.35% accuracy with their ANN.
- Momin et al. reported 82.83% accuracy with theirs.
- A neural network model is also reviewed in reference [44].

Beyond churn prediction, the ANN has many other applications:
- **Medical diagnosis:** ANN classification has been used to detect knee osteoarthritis from vibroarthrography signals.
- **Energy and business forecasting:** Jeong et al. combined an ANN with SARIMA to forecast electricity consumption. ANN models have also been used for energy cost budget estimation (reference 17) and within a hybrid sales forecasting model (reference 15).
- **Mobile ad hoc networks (MANETs):** cited works use ANNs for parameter training, cluster-head selection, and black hole attack detection.
- **Road safety:** study [9] lists the ANN as a method for road traffic accident forecasting, citing [18], where an ANN was applied to predict accident severity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-015</data>
