  <data key="d0">Oumaima Semmar</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Author of the bibliometric analysis of feature selection techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;First and corresponding author of the bibliometric analysis of feature selection techniques; affiliated with the Laboratory of Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of the bibliometric analysis of feature selection techniques published in Int J Artif Intell.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the article being read. Contributions include conceptualization, methodology, validation, formal analysis, original draft writing, review and editing, and project administration.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of the article being read, "A Bibliometric Analysis of Feature Selection Techniques", which appeared in Int J Artif Intell.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of This Paper. She holds a bachelor's degree in Mathematics and Applications and a Master's degree in Applied Analysis and Statistical Engineering. She is a Ph.D. student in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence at IABL, Faculty of Science and Technology of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaadi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Ph.D. student in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence at the Intelligent Automation and Bio Med Genomics Laboratory (IABL), Faculty of Science and Technology of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaadi University. Holds a bachelor's degree in Mathematics and Applications and a Master's degree in Applied Analysis and Statistical Engineering. Researches the transformative potential of artificial intelligence in the insurance industry, aiming to bridge theoretical mathematical frameworks and practical AI solutions.</data>
