<node id="Feature Selection">
  <data key="d0">Feature Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Feature Selection is a strategy in artificial intelligence and machine learning that identifies and retains the most relevant and predictive variables, or features, for building models. As a dimensionality reduction approach, it encompasses related techniques such as attribute selection. Unlike methods that transform the data, it keeps a subset of the original features and so preserves their physical meaning. Its main purposes are to address the challenges of high-dimensional data, improve model efficiency, and enhance both the performance and the interpretability of predictive models.

By removing irrelevant features, Feature Selection simplifies models, makes them more computationally efficient and easier to interpret, and can reduce noise and overfitting. Studies have found that it generally improves classification performance, particularly precision and F1-score. These benefits depend on the characteristics of the dataset, and the impact may be negligible when all features are already relevant. Research nonetheless emphasizes its importance for achieving optimal model performance. In practice it is often carried out with the Boruta algorithm, the Boruta package, and Boruta-based algorithms.

Feature Selection is also an interdisciplinary research field. It spans remote sensing, image processing, bioinformatics, and medical diagnostics, and has been applied in finance, manufacturing, technology, transportation, agriculture, energy, medicine, and insurance. It is the central topic of many surveys and applied studies.

As the subject of a bibliometric analysis, the field comprised 2,079 documents published between 2014 and 2024. Output peaked in 2023 and declined in 2024, giving an annual growth rate of -27.8%. Despite this recent decline, the analysis identified Feature Selection as one of the most central and well-developed themes in its domain, with growing importance for tackling high-dimensional data.&lt;SEP&gt;Model optimization technique recommended for future work to refine accuracy and reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
