</node>
<node id="Curse of Dimensionality">
  <data key="d0">Curse of Dimensionality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phenomenon where adding features leads to data dispersion, complicating model generalization and increasing overfitting risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Phenomenon in which too many features degrade machine learning models. Reference [1] discusses this phenomenon.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Web of Science">
  <data key="d0">Web of Science</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Web of Science (WoS) is a comprehensive, multidisciplinary bibliographic and literature database available by subscription. According to the source descriptions, it was developed by Eugene Garfield in 1997 and has been managed by Clarivate Analytics since 2016. It is used across many disciplines and is regarded as a highly academic and reliable resource that complements Scopus. It is a primary data source for bibliometric analyses, and in the studies described, documents and bibliometric data were drawn from it, including the bibliometric data of the article itself. In one instance, a search query in Web of Science returned 1,328 documents.

Web of Science often served as one of several data sources combined into an integrated dataset. Its records were merged with Scopus and, in at least one study, with PubMed. Records were retrieved from WoS as plain text. The Web of Science format was adopted as the standard for data integration, so records from the other databases were converted to match its structure. Several cited works similarly compare Web of Science with other databases or merge it with them for bibliometric purposes.

Web of Science has also been a source for systematic reviews. It was one of the four databases from which the 30 papers in a review were drawn, including a systematic review on generative adversarial networks (GANs) in finance. It was also used to analyze documents on artificial intelligence and machine learning applications in oncology.

Beyond its role as a data source, Web of Science has been an object of comparison, notably in studies comparing its journal coverage with that of Scopus. Because of this overlap, at least one study chose not to use Web of Science, partly to avoid duplicating journals already indexed in Scopus.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
