<node id="A Bibliometric Analysis of Feature Selection Techniques: Trends, Innovations">
  <data key="d0">A Bibliometric Analysis of Feature Selection Techniques: Trends, Innovations</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, by Oumaima Semmar, published in Int J Artif Intell Vol. 14, No. 6, December 2025 (pp. 4403-4414). It performs a bibliometric analysis of 2,079 papers on feature selection techniques from 2014-2024 using descriptive analysis and scientific mapping.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, by Oumaima Semmar, published in Int J Artif Intell, Vol. 14, No. 6, December 2025, pages 4403-4414. It analyzes 2,079 documents on feature selection techniques, covering country productivity, citation counts, author productivity via Lotka's law, top cited documents and frequent keywords.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, by Oumaima Semmar, published in Int J Artif Intell, Vol. 14, No. 6, December 2025, pp. 4403-4414. It conducts a bibliometric analysis of 2,079 documents published between 2014 and 2024 in Scopus and Web of Science on feature selection techniques, examining conceptual structure (co-occurrence network, thematic map) and social structure (author, country, and institution collaboration networks).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
