<node id="Feature Extraction">
  <data key="d0">Feature Extraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frequent keyword in feature selection publications. It is used in hyperspectral classification and image retrieval work.&lt;SEP&gt;Part of a research cluster alongside deep learning and selection techniques identified in the co-occurrence network.&lt;SEP&gt;Dimensionality reduction approach that transforms features into a lower-dimensional space while preserving essential information.&lt;SEP&gt;Process of extracting features from the collected images, performed after the images were resized to 256x256 pixels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperspectral Data Classification">
  <data key="d0">Hyperspectral Data Classification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Classification of hyperspectral remote sensing data. It is addressed by Chen et al. [30] using deep learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
