  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A small proportion of authors produce most scientific publications">
  <data key="d0">A small proportion of authors produce most scientific publications</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Proposed by Alfred James Lotka in 1926 [29], this statistical principle describes how scientific output is distributed among authors: a small proportion accounts for the majority of publications, while most authors contribute only a few works."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422137</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature selection research is interdisciplinary">
  <data key="d0">Feature selection research is interdisciplinary</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text about the top cited documents: "These publications span diverse domains such as remote sensing, image processing, bioinformatics, and medical diagnostics, reflecting the interdisciplinary nature of feature selection research."</data>
