<node id="Convolutional Neural Networks">
  <data key="d0">Convolutional Neural Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) are deep learning architectures that changed computer vision and can efficiently process large volumes of image data. Their accuracy depends on several factors, including dataset size, available computational resources and network depth. CNNs have been surveyed in the literature, for example in reference [19], and are widely used across many research and applied domains.

In remote sensing, Convolutional Neural Networks have been used for road extraction from satellite images. CNNs combined with transfer learning have been used specifically for the road-presence classification step, which shows how pre-trained models can be adapted to specialized image analysis tasks.

In industrial quality control, CNNs have been applied to defect inspection, as described in reference [23], where these models classify manufactured parts as good or defective. Beyond engineering, Convolutional Neural Networks have also been adopted in oncology research.

Convolutional Neural Networks are also regarded as a foundational topic in feature selection research. However, their role in that area is still developing and needs further attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Listed by study [9] as a method used for road traffic accident forecasting, cited with [17].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-001</data>
