<node id="China">
  <data key="d0">China</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">China is consistently identified across multiple bibliometric studies as one of the world's leading contributors to research in artificial intelligence and related computational fields. It plays a dominant role in both publication volume and international collaboration.

In feature selection research, China has the highest level of collaboration and the largest number of published documents. In AI applied to human resource management (HRM), it leads research contributions with 91 articles and shows a remarkable increase in output on AI in HR practices. In AI for market analysis, China is at the forefront of contributions and has one of the largest levels of collaboration and one of the highest document counts. In AI oncology, China is the leading contributor to global production, with over 2,596 publications.

At the regional level, China leads Asia's scientific production. It is one of the largest nodes in the country collaboration network and is home to three of the top 10 institutions. One analysis, however, ranks China as the second most productive country, with 2,357 documents, 5,288 total citations and an average of 9.50 citations per article. This differs from the descriptions of China as the top contributor, most likely because the studies covered different research domains or datasets. Even in that analysis, China's output increased significantly over time, which is consistent with its growing prominence in global AI-related research.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_AIapplicationinmarketanalysis.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423314</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
