<node id="IEEE">
  <data key="d0">IEEE</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers) is a professional organization that organizes, hosts, and publishes the proceedings of many international conferences, and also publishes journals. It is closely associated with research in electronics, communications, computing, signal processing, and related engineering fields.

IEEE hosts and publishes the 2024 IEEE 4th International Conference on Electronic Communications, Internet of Things and Big Data (ICEIB), and it was the organization behind the 2010 IEEE 26th Convention of Electrical and Electronics Engineers in Israel. It is the publisher of a wide range of conference proceedings, including the ICCAKM 2023 proceedings (which include the work of Inani et al., 2023) and the 2020 11th International Conference on Information and Communication Systems (ICICS). Its publications also include the proceedings of WI-IAT 2020, CSNT 2024, icABCD 2023, EUSIPCO 2021, BCCA 2020, ICACCI 2016, and ICSESS 2017. In addition, IEEE published the 2011 4th International Congress on Image and Signal Processing and the Joint 9th IFSA World Congress and 20th NAFIPS International Conference (2001).

Beyond conference proceedings, IEEE publishes the journal IEEE Access. Its publications span more than two decades and many research areas, which makes IEEE a major venue for disseminating scholarly work in technology and engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers. It publishes the journal IEEE Access and organizes the 6th Workshop on Advances in Information, Electronic and Electrical Engineering (AIEEE).&lt;SEP&gt;Publisher of the ICEMIS 2017 and ISACC 2015 proceedings.&lt;SEP&gt;Publisher of the 2020 10th Annual Computing and Communication Workshop and Conference (CCWC) proceedings containing reference [17].&lt;SEP&gt;Publisher of the proceedings of the 2017 2nd International Conference on Anti-Cyber Crimes (ICACC), which include reference [5].&lt;SEP&gt;Publisher of the ICBC 2021 and TrustCom 2025 proceedings and of journals such as IEEE Access, IEEE Networking Letters and IEEE Communications Surveys &amp; Tutorials.&lt;SEP&gt;Publisher of the 1994 Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science proceedings and organizer of the 2021 International Conference on Blockchain and Cryptocurrency.</data>
