  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy Set Theory">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Set Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Theory developed by Zadeh that is adept at handling the nuances and ambiguity of human judgment.&lt;SEP&gt;Theory integrated into subjective methods to represent the uncertainty and ambiguity of expert knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;Theory integrated into subjective methods to represent uncertainty and ambiguity in human reasoning and expert judgment.&lt;SEP&gt;Theory of fuzzy sets introduced by L. A. Zadeh in 1965. Fuzzy set theory underlies the fuzzy AHP and intuitionistic fuzzy approaches in the references.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
