<node id="Fuzzy set theory handles nuances of human judgment">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy set theory handles nuances of human judgment</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "This issue can be mitigated either by integrating objective methods with subjective ones or by employing the fuzzy sets theory developed by Zadeh [14], which is adept at handling the nuances of human judgment."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supplier selection research was initiated by Dickson in 1966">
  <data key="d0">Supplier selection research was initiated by Dickson in 1966</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The early research into supplier selection and evaluation, initiated by Dickson in 1966 [15]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subjective approaches such as DEMATEL, SMART and AHP weight criteria using expert judgments">
  <data key="d0">Subjective approaches such as DEMATEL, SMART and AHP weight criteria using expert judgments</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The supplier selection process generally consists of two main phases: first, assigning weights to criteria to establish their importance, which can be achieved through subjective approaches such as Decision-Making Trial and Evaluation Laboratory (DEMATEL)[4], Simple Multi-Attribute Rating Technique (SMART) [5], and Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) [6], to quantify their relevance using judgments and experts' opinions..."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Objective methods such as Entropy and CRITIC weight criteria based on data variability">
  <data key="d0">Objective methods such as Entropy and CRITIC weight criteria based on data variability</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "...or objective methods like entropy [7], and Criteria Importance Through Inter-criteria Correlation (CRITIC) [8], to determine weights based on data variability without relying on subjective judgments."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Suppliers are ranked using techniques such as TOPSIS, COPRAS, VIKOR and PROMETHEE">
  <data key="d0">Suppliers are ranked using techniques such as TOPSIS, COPRAS, VIKOR and PROMETHEE</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Following this, suppliers are ranked according to these weighted criteria using techniques such as Technique for Order Preference by Similarity to Ideal Solution (TOPSIS) [9], [10], Complex Proportional Assessment (COPRAS) [11], multi-criteria optimization and compromise solution (VIKOR) [12], and Preference Ranking Organization Method for Enrichment Evaluation (PROMETHEE) [13]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dickson 1966 Supplier Selection Survey">
  <data key="d0">Dickson 1966 Supplier Selection Survey</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [15]. Early research on supplier selection and evaluation by Dickson in 1966; a survey of 274 companies affiliated with the National Association of Purchasing in Canada and the United States, finding that supplier choices depend on factors such as pricing, quality and delivery speed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
