  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entropy Method">
  <data key="d0">Entropy Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Objective, data-driven method for calculating criteria weights.&lt;SEP&gt;Objective weighting method that normalizes the decision matrix and computes entropy values e_i for each criterion and e_i1, e_i2 and e_i3 for sub-criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Objective weighting method computing entropy values of criteria and sub-criteria from a normalized decision matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;Objective weighting approach aiming to mitigate personal bias using quantitative data; identified Delivery as most significant and Financial situation as less significant; yielded ranking A2 &gt; A1 &gt; A3 &gt; A4.&lt;SEP&gt;Objective weighting method used in the citing article. It computes entropy values (ei) from the normalized matrix and derives internal weights for criteria and sub-criteria. External sub-criterion weights are obtained by multiplying internal weights by the criterion weights. The method identifies C3 as the most important criterion and C4 as the least important. Among sub-criteria, C32 is the most critical (0.2872) and C42 has the smallest impact (0.0040).&lt;SEP&gt;Objective weighting method whose inclusion reduces potential biases, yielding more objective and accurate evaluations.&lt;SEP&gt;Entropy-based MCDM weighting technique. Chodha et al. use it with TOPSIS to select an industrial arc welding robot.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP-TOPSIS">
  <data key="d0">AHP-TOPSIS</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid method combining AHP weighting with TOPSIS ranking, widely used in supplier selection.&lt;SEP&gt;Method that showed the longest average Euclidean distance to scenario scores.&lt;SEP&gt;Combined Analytic Hierarchy Process and TOPSIS multi-criteria decision model. Tayalati et al. (2024) designed it to optimize the selection of injection molding machines.&lt;SEP&gt;A combined multi-criteria decision model (Analytic Hierarchy Process with TOPSIS). Reference [19] designs it for selecting injection molding machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Combined AHP and TOPSIS methodology, proposed in a five-step procedure for injection molding machine selection.&lt;SEP&gt;Combined multi-criteria decision-making approach whose primary advantage is minimizing errors and uncertainties in decision-making when selecting the optimal machine.&lt;SEP&gt;Combined method that minimizes errors and uncertainties in decision-making by considering both qualitative factors (quality, reliability, expert feedback) and quantitative metrics (performance, costs, efficiency).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FAHP-TOPSIS">
  <data key="d0">FAHP-TOPSIS</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid method combining fuzzy AHP with TOPSIS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-002</data>
