<node id="Online Retail Supplier Evaluation Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Online Retail Supplier Evaluation Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">New set of evaluation criteria introduced by This Paper specifically for the online retail sector, focusing on financial stability, service quality and operational efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Decision Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrix DM whose element dij represents the assessment of alternative j with respect to criterion i.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrices that score the four suppliers against criteria (Table 6) and sub-criteria (Table 7). Sub-criteria are scored from 1 (least satisfactory) to 10 (most satisfactory), and criteria values are averages of their sub-criteria. C62 and C72 are unfavorable criteria, for which a lower value is better.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix of evaluations presented in Table 5. It is normalized using Eq. (8) as the first step of the entropy method, producing the normalized decision matrix in Table 17.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pairwise Comparison Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Pairwise Comparison Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Step 2 of AHP. Experts directly compare the relative importance of one criterion against another, using Saaty's scale and survey results.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix of expert judgments on the relative significance of one criterion over another. It is aggregated, normalized by column sums, and used to compute weights.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrices comparing criteria and sub-criteria pairwise, built from three experts' survey responses, aggregated by the geometric mean, then normalized to compute weights in AHP. Fuzzy versions are used in FAHP.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix of fuzzy pairwise comparisons between criteria (Table 11) that serves as input for the computation of fuzzy weights.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix used in AHP to compare criteria according to their relative importance; elements are divided by column sums and rows averaged to obtain weights.&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix in which criteria and sub-criteria are compared pairwise based on expert consensus. It is used to compute weighted sums and the largest eigenvalue for consistency checking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Saaty's Scale">
  <data key="d0">Saaty's Scale</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Numerical scale that assigns values to levels of preference, used to build pairwise comparison matrices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thomas Saaty">
  <data key="d0">Thomas Saaty</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Referred to as Saaty. He introduced the AHP method in 1971 and created Saaty's scale.&lt;SEP&gt;Pioneer of the Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Panel">
  <data key="d0">Expert Panel</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Decision-making committee of three decision-makers with 8, 10 and 12 years of industry experience. The panel applies the subjective weighting methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supplier Evaluation Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Supplier Evaluation Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven criteria groups: Quality, Price, Delivery, Reputation, Service, Financial Position and Inventory Management. Each group has three sub-criteria. Six criteria came from a literature review; the others were added through expert consultation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference [29]">
  <data key="d0">Reference [29]</data>
