  <data key="d0">Reference [30]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work describing the six steps of AHP and its three-level hierarchical structure (objective, criteria, alternatives).&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work stating that a CR below 0.1 confirms the acceptability of comparison results.&lt;SEP&gt;Work cited as [30] regarding fuzzification and the advantages of Gaussian membership functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work, labeled [30], discussing the drawbacks of traditional heterogeneous web technology stacks. These stacks require diverse expertise and their technologies were not designed to work together.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work stating that common stacks such as LAMP/WAMP and .NET combine heterogeneous tools, increasing required expertise and integration difficulty.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited study [30] that relied on expert insights.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [30] regarding black hole attacks.</data>
