<node id="Inventory Management">
  <data key="d0">Inventory Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inventory Management is a business domain concerned with controlling stock levels. It appears in two distinct contexts: as a criterion for evaluating suppliers, and as a business activity that benefits from sales forecasting.

In the supplier evaluation context, Inventory Management is one of the seven main supplier selection criteria identified in response to RQ1 for evaluating and ranking suppliers. Within this framework it forms one of the seven criteria groups and contains three sub-criteria.

In the sales forecasting context, Inventory Management is a business process and planning area that accurate sales prediction helps optimize. It is informed by a hybrid model's prediction of sales for the next "n" days. Alongside pricing strategies and promotional planning, it is one of the activities that draws on the model's forecasts, and the paper states that these forecasts should be taken into account when planning inventory. Effective Inventory Management in this sense means aligning production and inventory levels with anticipated demand. This reduces stockouts, overstock, and storage costs. Overstocking is described as a critical issue within this domain, which makes reliable demand forecasts especially valuable for keeping stock at appropriate levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8153b8d12e35b15bf93bd763cdd0b2f2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;M3A_24_Book_of_Abstracts-31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426589</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geometric Mean Method">
  <data key="d0">Geometric Mean Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Method used to aggregate individual expert judgments into a group pairwise comparison matrix, where pij is the Nth root of the product of the individual assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Aggregation method used to derive final pairwise comparison matrices from expert evaluations, with rounding to the nearest whole number for Saaty scale alignment (e.g., 5.31 rounded to 5).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weighted Arithmetic Mean Method">
  <data key="d0">Weighted Arithmetic Mean Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Alternative method for integrating individual expert opinions into a collective matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Saaty Scale">
  <data key="d0">Saaty Scale</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Scale that assigns numerical values to different levels of preference in AHP pairwise comparisons (Table 4).&lt;SEP&gt;Pairwise comparison scale whose TFN representation is presented in Table 6 and Figure 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Numerical scale for pairwise comparisons to which aggregated geometric mean values are aligned by rounding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Consistency Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">CR = CI/RI. Used to assess the consistency of judgments; a CR below 0.1 confirms that the comparison results are acceptable.&lt;SEP&gt;Validity check for pairwise comparison weights; values below 0.1 indicate the weights are valid.&lt;SEP&gt;Indicator used to verify the accuracy of pairwise comparisons in AHP.&lt;SEP&gt;Indicator (CR = CI/RI) used to evaluate the coherence of comparisons within the judgment matrix. In the case study, CR equals 0.0702, which is below the 0.1 threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency Index">
  <data key="d0">Consistency Index</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">CI = (λmax − n)/(n − 1). Used to assess the overall consistency of pairwise judgments.&lt;SEP&gt;Index defined as CI = (λmax − n)/(n − 1), where λmax relates to the largest eigenvalue of the pairwise comparison matrix and n is the number of criteria. The computed value is 0.0787 for λmax = 5.31 and n = 5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
