<node id="Reference [34]">
  <data key="d0">Reference [34]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference [34] is a citation label that appears across several distinct source documents. The descriptions associated with it point to multiple different cited works rather than a single publication, so each is summarized separately below.

In the context of fuzzy systems, Reference [34] is attributed to Zadeh and concerns possibility theory. It provides the theoretical grounding for interpreting activation degrees as relative plausibility scores rather than probabilities. Related descriptions also cite [34] as a work on fuzzy logic, which defines intermediate values mathematically so that computers can reason in a more human-like way. Another description cites [34] as supporting the controlled-overlap criterion for setting the spread of Gaussian membership functions. These fuzzy-related citations may refer to the same Zadeh work or to separate fuzzy-logic references, and this remains uncertain.

In the context of multi-criteria decision-making, Reference [34] is cited as a work on aggregating individual expert judgments into a collective matrix, using either the geometric mean or the weighted arithmetic mean. A separate mention describes [34] as a study that relied on expert insights, which may relate to this same expert-judgment aggregation work.

In the context of cloud infrastructure, Reference [34] is cited as describing Prometheus, a widely adopted cloud-native monitoring solution. Prometheus collects metrics through a pull-based model and does not require agents.

In the context of vehicular networks, Reference [34] is cited regarding rural VANET (Vehicular Ad Hoc Network) scenarios. These scenarios are characterized by low node density, poor infrastructure, and very low attack rates.

In the context of blockchain systems, Reference [34] is cited as a performance study of Hyperledger Fabric, the permissioned blockchain platform.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
