<node id="Lambda Max">
  <data key="d0">Lambda Max</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">λmax, the principal eigenvalue estimate. It is calculated by multiplying the pairwise comparison matrix by the priority vector, dividing each element of the weighted sum vector by the corresponding priority, and averaging the results. It is used to compute the Consistency Index.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Priority Vector">
  <data key="d0">Priority Vector</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Vector of criterion and sub-criterion weights, obtained by averaging the rows of the normalized pairwise comparison matrix (Eq. 9). It is used in the consistency validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pairwise Comparison Matrix Normalization">
  <data key="d0">Pairwise Comparison Matrix Normalization</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Step 3 of the AHP procedure. Each element of the pairwise comparison matrix is divided by the sum of its column (Eq. 8) to standardize the values.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
