<node id="Fuzzy Analytic Hierarchy Process (FAHP)">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Analytic Hierarchy Process (FAHP)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Decision-making framework that integrates fuzzy sets with the traditional AHP to address uncertainties in human opinions. It proceeds in four steps: building the fuzzy pairwise comparison matrix, calculating criterion fuzzy weights, defuzzification and consistency validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP)">
  <data key="d0">Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Traditional multi-criteria decision method whose pairwise comparison matrices and validated weights form the basis of FAHP.&lt;SEP&gt;Systematic decision-making approach pioneered by Thomas Saaty that decomposes complex problems into hierarchies of criteria and alternatives and uses pairwise comparisons; steps include problem structuring, pairwise comparisons, weighted score calculation, consistency checking and validation.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-criteria decision-making method used and studied by many of the referenced works, which apply it to project management, sorting, mining, career paths and injection molding.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-criteria decision-making method used for process settings, process selection, machine selection and EDM optimization in several references.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Triangular Fuzzy Number (TFN)">
  <data key="d0">Triangular Fuzzy Number (TFN)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Fuzzy number defined by three parameters (l minimum, m most probable, u maximum). It is widely used to convert fuzzy linguistic variables into fuzzy numbers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy Pairwise Comparison Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Pairwise Comparison Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrix derived from AHP using TFNs, with diagonal elements set to (1,1,1) and reciprocal symmetric elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy Geometric Mean">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Geometric Mean</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Aggregate measure of pairwise comparisons used to compute criterion fuzzy weights.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique used within FAHP to compute fuzzy weights of criteria and sub-criteria from the fuzzified pairwise comparison matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Center of Gravity Defuzzification">
  <data key="d0">Center of Gravity Defuzzification</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Function that converts fuzzy criterion weights into crisp values by averaging l, m and u.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entropy Weight Method">
  <data key="d0">Entropy Weight Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Method that assesses a criterion's significance and weight by calculating its information entropy, based on the variation of the initial data matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;An objective weighting method that assesses a criterion's significance from its information entropy, based on the variation of the data matrix. It proceeds through normalization, entropy calculation and weight calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;An entropy-based criteria weighting technique that is combined with AHP and TOPSIS in supplier evaluation and selection models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Information Entropy">
  <data key="d0">Information Entropy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Measure of uncertainty in information sources, adapted by Shannon in 1948 from thermodynamic entropy.&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of uncertainty in information sources, adapted from thermodynamic entropy by Shannon in 1948.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-006</data>
