  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TFN Membership Function">
  <data key="d0">TFN Membership Function</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Membership function µT of a triangular fuzzy number T = (l, m, u). It is given by Equation (12), cited to [38], and illustrated in Figure 3. It is piecewise linear, rising from l to m, where it equals 1, and falling to u.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TFN Operational Rules">
  <data key="d0">TFN Operational Rules</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Primary arithmetic rules for two triangular fuzzy numbers, given in Equation (13) and cited to [40]. Multiplication is component-wise (l1×l2, m1×m2, u1×u2). Addition is component-wise (l1+l2, m1+m2, u1+u2). The inverse is (1/u1, 1/m1, 1/l1).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Evaluation Consistency Validation">
  <data key="d0">Evaluation Consistency Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Step 4 of the FAHP process. Because FAHP comparison matrices are based on validated AHP matrices, the FAHP-derived weights are also considered appropriate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
