<node id="Interval-Valued Pythagorean Fuzzy AHP">
  <data key="d0">Interval-Valued Pythagorean Fuzzy AHP</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Fuzzy extension of AHP based on interval-valued Pythagorean fuzzy sets. Reference [3] uses it in a hybrid with COPRAS for supplier selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy-AHP-TOPSIS">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy-AHP-TOPSIS</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Integrated multi-criteria decision support system combining fuzzy AHP and TOPSIS. Reference [2] proposes it for supplier selection in Pakistan's textile industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Judgement">
  <data key="d0">Expert Judgement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Subjective input from specialists, used in subjective MCDM methods. The article notes it as a potential source of bias.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entropy method reduces bias and improves objectivity of evaluations">
  <data key="d0">Entropy method reduces bias and improves objectivity of evaluations</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "While AHP and FAHP offer valuable insights into subjective preferences, the inclusion of the Entropy method reduces potential biases, resulting in more objective and accurate evaluations."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FAHP-Entropy-TOPSIS is a particularly effective approach for supplier selection">
  <data key="d0">FAHP-Entropy-TOPSIS is a particularly effective approach for supplier selection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "This research demonstrates the importance of combining subjective and objective MCDM approaches in supplier selection, with the FAHP-Entropy-TOPSIS method emerging as a particularly effective approach for achieving a comprehensive evaluation."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
