<node id="Pairwise Comparison">
  <data key="d0">Pairwise Comparison</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Comparison technique that Saaty describes as central in mathematics for measuring intangible factors within the analytic hierarchy/network process.&lt;SEP&gt;AHP step comparing criteria and alternatives by scaling the strength of importance of each comparison based on subjective judgments.&lt;SEP&gt;An AHP step that compares each criterion and sub-criterion against the others to find their relative importance. It uses a scale that typically runs from 1 to 9: 1 means the same level of significance, 3 slight priority, 5 medium priority, 7 high significance and 9 extreme significance. The even values 2, 4, 6 and 8 fall between adjacent points.&lt;SEP&gt;Comparison procedure used with expert validation to derive criteria weights in the AHP step.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique for judging the relative importance of criteria in AHP. Fuzzy logic is proposed as a future way to capture its uncertainty and vagueness.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013</data>
