<node id="AHP-Entropy">
  <data key="d0">AHP-Entropy</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">AHP-Entropy is a hybrid, or combined, weighting method that integrates the Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) with the Entropy method. It merges the subjective weights derived from AHP with the objective weights obtained through Entropy to compute a set of combined weights. The method is used to calculate the weights of both criteria and sub-criteria. Pairing expert-based judgment with data-driven objectivity gives it a balanced weighting approach.

In its application, AHP-Entropy identified criterion C3 as the most significant, with a weight of 0.2995. Criterion C4 was the least significant, with a weight of 0.0071.

When applied to rank alternatives, AHP-Entropy produced the ordering A1 &gt; A2 &gt; A4 &gt; A3. This was considered the most probable ranking across all four alternatives. The method also showed stable results across the sensitivity analysis scenarios, which indicates its robustness and reliability for decision-making.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422483</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensitivity Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Sensitivity Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Sensitivity Analysis is the study of how a model's outputs depend on its input parameters. Reference [46] addresses how to perform it efficiently for probabilistic models. The descriptions apply the technique in several distinct contexts, summarized separately below.

In the supplier selection framework proposed in This Paper, Sensitivity Analysis is the final phase of the methodology. It verifies the robustness, stability, and reliability of the results by formulating scenarios, recalculating criteria weights, and re-ranking suppliers to observe how changing conditions affect outcomes. It uses 21 scenarios that vary the criteria weights, which test the stability of the supplier rankings, validate the methods employed, and check whether differences between the weighting methods are robust. In the case study, it is one of four subsections, alongside the problem statement, weight calculation, and supplier ranking. Its results appear in Table 27, which compares the most probable ranking with the rankings produced by the five methods studied.

In multi-criteria decision-making more broadly, Sensitivity Analysis examines how results respond to variations in the values of the most highly weighted criteria. Within the AHP validation step, it assesses the robustness of results and how changes in criteria priorities affect the rankings of alternatives.

In a machine selection case, Sensitivity Analysis is a scenario-based validation procedure. It examines how the decision outcome responds to changes in key criteria such as scrap rate, cost breakdown, quality, and machine reliability. Three scenarios improve the scrap rate by 0.2%, the breakdown rate by 2%, or both, focusing on the HAIT 320T machine. The results show that the rankings are sensitive to these critical criteria: HAIT 320T rises from third to first place in the combined scenario.

In system reliability and degradation modeling, Sensitivity Analysis is enabled by a Fuzzy Bayesian Network. It identifies the parameters that most influence component-level and system-level reliability and degradation, using local (partial) and global sensitivity indices. With System_State set to Critical as the evidence condition, it quantifies how individual component conditions, and combinations of them, affect overall system risk. The results are visualized in a tornado diagram. The influential parameters identified include CPU temperature, load average, RAM fragmentation, overclocking, GPU usage, VRAM availability, and hard disk error counts. In this setting, it complements monotonicity validation and interval-based robustness analysis to evaluate the model's reliability under data scarcity.

In an anomaly detection context, Sensitivity Analysis consists of four trials that vary detection thresholds. The upper limit ranges from 95% down to 80% of the maximum threshold, and the lower limit ranges from 10% to 64% of the minimum threshold. The results were as follows:

- Trial 1 (0.0277 / 0.0029) detected 7 points (1.71%), all of type 1 only.
- Trial 2 (0.0262 / 0.0072) detected 13 anomalies of types 1, 2, and 4.
- Trial 3 detected 178 anomalies (43.6%) of types 1, 2, and 4.
- Trial 4 (0.0243 / 0.0188) detected 235 anomalies (57.5%) covering all four types.

The Discussion section reports some of these values inconsistently. It lists 0.0277 as both the maximum and minimum for Trial 1, and gives 0.243 as the maximum for Trial 4.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013</data>
