<node id="Human Resource Management">
  <data key="d0">Human Resource Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Management of an organization's workforce, which AI is reshaping through talent management, recruitment and automation.&lt;SEP&gt;HRM, the management domain whose intersection with AI is studied.&lt;SEP&gt;Field ranging from traditional human resource management to AI applications in business contexts; keywords such as "HR" and "e-HR" were used in the Scopus search.&lt;SEP&gt;Prominent research theme (HRM) that evolved to encompass client satisfaction, employee performance, and incorporation of AI and big data for decision-making; term frequency increased from 2019 to 2023.&lt;SEP&gt;HRM; a central theme in the analyzed literature, increasingly integrated with AI and new technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;HRM; a central theme of the co-word network, evolving toward incorporating AI and big data for decision-making, customer satisfaction, and employee performance.&lt;SEP&gt;HRM, the field whose intersection with AI and new technologies is analyzed bibliometrically. The scope covers recruitment, performance analysis, compensation and talent management.</data>
