<node id="Risk Management">
  <data key="d0">Risk Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk Management is a concept that appears in several distinct contexts within the provided descriptions: occupational safety research, financial markets, and transport supply chain quality.

In occupational safety research, Risk Management is a research theme that emerged to address occupational risks and accident prevention. It reflects a broader approach that integrates artificial intelligence (AI) technologies and Bayesian networks to identify, assess, and mitigate workplace hazards. The theme is prominently highlighted in the co-word network analysis, which shows how it developed alongside these AI-driven methods.

In financial markets, Risk Management refers to financial risk management and is identified as an application area for Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) and their variants, as covered in a review of GAN applications. Within this area, Gu et al.'s RAGIC model provides insights for financial risk management, while Allen et al. address it through Value-at-Risk (VaR) estimation.

In logistics, Risk Management denotes the control and prevention of risks such as accidents, property damage, and additional costs. It is described as a critical component of transport supply chain quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501162</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
