  <data key="d0">Flexible Job Shop Scheduling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Production planning problem that Gong et al. (2019) address by considering energy and labor costs under dynamic electricity pricing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Energy- and labor-aware scheduling minimizes production costs under volatile prices">
  <data key="d0">Energy- and labor-aware scheduling minimizes production costs under volatile prices</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">A flexible workshop planning model, integrated with numerous objectives, considering energy and labor, to optimize production costs in a context of volatile electricity prices and wages. Through tailored algorithms and experiments, it demonstrates efficient resource allocation to minimize costs under various operational conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scientific publications on AI in HRM have surged significantly">
  <data key="d0">Scientific publications on AI in HRM have surged significantly</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding of This Paper: "The analysis revealed a significant surge in scientific publications, indicating a growing recognition of the transformative potential of AI technologies in reshaping HR practices and organizational dynamics."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422721</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Research on HR and AI is concentrated in China and USA">
  <data key="d0">Research on HR and AI is concentrated in China and USA</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding of This Paper: "the geographic distribution of research contributions highlighted the global awareness, interest, and collaborative nature of research in HR and AI, particularly in China and USA."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf</data>
