<node id="Systematic Review">
  <data key="d0">Systematic Review</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A Systematic Review is a literature review methodology that follows a defined protocol to gather relevant research papers and synthesize their insights qualitatively. It is a research method that consolidates knowledge from both empirical and theoretical studies to uncover hidden patterns and research trends, with an emphasis on the qualitative aspects of a research field. The approach is described as rooted in Western positivist traditions. Bibliometric tools such as the Biblioshiny library are commonly used to support this type of review.

The method has been applied across several research contexts. Vrontis et al. (2022) used it as their literature review method, and it has also been used to study the fusion of medical imaging and electronic health records with deep learning.

In one notable application, a Systematic Review examined Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) for financial data generation. The procedure applied Boolean keyword queries across four major databases: IEEE Xplore, Web of Science, Scopus, and ArXiv. It then passed the results through structured screening and eligibility phases, which yielded 53 papers, of which 30 relevant studies were included in the final analysis. These thirty papers were reviewed qualitatively to synthesize key findings, identify challenges, and highlight the limitations of GANs in generating financial data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_AIapplicationinmarketanalysis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
