<node id="Transfer Learning">
  <data key="d0">Transfer Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Transfer Learning is a machine learning technique that reuses knowledge from pre-trained models to train new models for related tasks, which is especially valuable when target datasets are small. In the descriptions provided, it appears mainly as model-based transfer learning, where models are reused to draw on knowledge gained from other vision tasks. It forms part of a broader knowledge reuse strategy for training convolutional neural network (CNN) models.

In road analysis from satellite imagery, Transfer Learning is applied to the VGG16 and VGG19 classifiers. These networks are pre-trained on ImageNet and then fine-tuned to classify whether roads are present in satellite image tiles. This road-presence classification forms the initial stage of the analysis pipeline. It filters out irrelevant tiles, which reduces computational cost and lowers the rate of false positives. VGG19 in particular is also used for general image classification within this framework.

Transfer Learning is also used to predict road quality from satellite imagery. In this approach, a CNN is first trained on data from the United States and then fine-tuned on a smaller Nigerian dataset. This allows road quality assessment in a region where labeled data is limited.

Beyond remote sensing, Transfer Learning has been used in industrial quality inspection, specifically defect detection in injection molding products trained on small datasets, as documented in reference [8]. This application shows how the technique addresses data scarcity across different domains.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
