<node id="Wei et al. (10)">
  <data key="d0">Wei et al. (10)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work by Wei et al. proposing a three-step road extraction approach of segmentation enhancement, tracing and fusion. It uses an FCN with iterative refinement by a lighter FCN, and a CNN-integrated tracing step that starts from road intersections.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liu et al. (11) RoadCT">
  <data key="d0">Liu et al. (11) RoadCT</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work by Liu et al. proposing RoadCT, a hybrid CNN-Transformer model that uses a relational fusion block for road extraction from satellite images.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as (11). Liu et al. propose RoadCT, a hybrid model combining CNN and Transformer networks via a relational fusion block that merges information from different image parts with different receptive fields, enhancing the representation of roads extracted from satellite images.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wei">
  <data key="d0">Wei</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Lead author (Wei et al.) of the three-step segmentation, tracing and fusion road extraction method.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liu">
  <data key="d0">Liu</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Lead author (Liu et al.) of the RoadCT hybrid model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Roads are occluded and vary in appearance in satellite images">
  <data key="d0">Roads are occluded and vary in appearance in satellite images</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Roads may be occluded by trees, buildings, or shadows, and can vary in texture and appearance (5).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CNNs detect features indicative of roads">
  <data key="d0">CNNs detect features indicative of roads</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">By using multiple layers of convolutional filters, CNNs can detect edges, textures, and more complex patterns that are indicative of roads (6).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DeepLabV3+ captures multi-scale context to enhance segmentation accuracy">
  <data key="d0">DeepLabV3+ captures multi-scale context to enhance segmentation accuracy</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Advanced architectures such as DeepLabV3+ incorporate techniques like atrous convolution and spatial pyramid pooling to capture multi-scale contextual information, further enhancing the accuracy of segmentation tasks (7).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Labeled data availability and computational cost are hurdles for road extraction">
  <data key="d0">Labeled data availability and computational cost are hurdles for road extraction</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Additionally, the availability of labeled training data and the computational cost of training deep learning models are significant hurdles (8).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Atrous Convolution">
  <data key="d0">Atrous Convolution</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Technique incorporated in DeepLabV3+ to capture multi-scale contextual information.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spatial Pyramid Pooling">
  <data key="d0">Spatial Pyramid Pooling</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Technique incorporated in DeepLabV3+ to capture multi-scale context.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road-Presence Classification Pipeline">
  <data key="d0">Road-Presence Classification Pipeline</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Practical road extraction pipeline in which a preliminary classification stage ensures that only tiles containing roads are segmented. This reduces computational overhead and false positives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fully Convolutional Network">
  <data key="d0">Fully Convolutional Network</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Network used by Wei et al. to segment road surfaces, with iterative refinement by a lighter FCN.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relational Fusion Block">
  <data key="d0">Relational Fusion Block</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Block in RoadCT that combines road features extracted by the CNN and Transformer networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Block in RoadCT that combines road characteristics extracted by CNN and Transformer networks, merging information from different image parts with different receptive fields.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road Extraction From Satellite Imagery">
  <data key="d0">Road Extraction From Satellite Imagery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Task of accurately extracting road networks from satellite and remote sensing images. It is relevant to urban planning and transport management and remains challenging because of occlusion, varying road widths, complex intersections and similar-looking non-road features.&lt;SEP&gt;The task of identifying roads in satellite images, made complex by diversity in road density, width and surrounding land use.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road networks can be extracted with high precision">
  <data key="d0">Road networks can be extracted with high precision</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text (truncated at the start): "...networks with high precision (4)."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CNN classification and DeepLabV3+ segmentation improve road detection in complex visual contexts">
  <data key="d0">CNN classification and DeepLabV3+ segmentation improve road detection in complex visual contexts</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">CNNs are used for classification, and the DeepLabV3+ model is applied to segment road networks, with the aim of improving their detection and delineation in complex visual contexts (9).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road extraction methods bring incremental improvements in accuracy and efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Road extraction methods bring incremental improvements in accuracy and efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">From intricate frameworks, including the three-step segmentation enhancement, tracing, and fusion approach proposed by Wei et al. (10), to hybrid models such as the one introduced by Liu et al. (11), each method brings incremental improvements in the accurate and efficient extraction of road networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iterative FCN refinement improves road segmentation accuracy and connectivity">
  <data key="d0">Iterative FCN refinement improves road segmentation accuracy and connectivity</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Wei et al.'s (10) method utilizes a fully convolutional network (FCN) to segment the road surface, which is then iteratively refined using a lighter FCN to improve both accuracy and connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fusing segmentation and tracing produces refined road segmentation and core maps">
  <data key="d0">Fusing segmentation and tracing produces refined road segmentation and core maps</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finally, the fusion step combines the segmentation and tracing results to produce refined road segmentation and core maps (10).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relational fusion of CNN and Transformer features enhances road representation">
  <data key="d0">Relational fusion of CNN and Transformer features enhances road representation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"Additionally, hybrid models like Roadct, proposed by Liu et al. (11) used a relational fusion block to combine the characteristics of the roads extracted by the two types of networks (CNN and transform)." The text adds that this block merges information with different receptive fields, enhancing the representation of extracted roads.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transformer">
  <data key="d0">Transformer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Attention-based network type. It is combined with CNNs in the hybrid RoadCT model, and transformer-based methods are cited as a possible extension of the proposed pipeline.&lt;SEP&gt;Network type combined with CNNs in the hybrid RoadCT model to extract road characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road Tracing">
  <data key="d0">Road Tracing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Step in the method of Wei et al. that automatically generates starting points from road intersections and tracks entire road networks through an iterative search strategy integrated into a CNN.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Topology-Aware Methods">
  <data key="d0">Topology-Aware Methods</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Class of road extraction methods identified as a possible future extension of the proposed pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transport Management">
  <data key="d0">Transport Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Application field in which road extraction from remote sensing images plays an important role.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Khan et al. (5)">
  <data key="d0">Khan et al. (5)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (5). Khan et al. recommend fine-tuning U-Net with BRISQUE to enhance road detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as (5); applies U-Net to satellite imagery (E-Prime) at 1m resolution, reporting ~87% IoU and ~91% Dice with ~31M parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wei et al. (12)">
  <data key="d0">Wei et al. (12)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (12). Wei et al. introduce a multi-starting point tracer combining road segmentation and tracking, and apply RSRCNN with a road-structure-based loss function to extract roads from aerial images.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as (12); proposes RSRCNN on aerial images at 0.5m resolution, reporting 90+% IoU and 92+% Dice with medium complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Yue Li et al. (13)">
  <data key="d0">Yue Li et al. (13)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (13). Yue Li et al. propose a framework for road network extraction from high-resolution SAR images using CNN features, an enhanced Radon transform and Markov random field.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Article (14) on Aerial Image Road Extraction">
  <data key="d0">Article (14) on Aerial Image Road Extraction</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (14). Explores road extraction from aerial/orthophoto images using principal component analysis and object-based image analysis for preprocessing, integrating spectral, spatial and textural information, CNN classification, and open/close operations; evaluated with precision, recall, F1 score, total accuracy and IoU, with average percentages ranging from 87.21% to 95.32%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference (15)">
  <data key="d0">Reference (15)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (15) regarding the use of basic open and close operations to extract road components and eliminate holes.&lt;SEP&gt;A work cited as (15) for the use of a 1-to-9 scale in AHP pairwise comparisons.&lt;SEP&gt;Work cited as (15) to support the rule that a consistency ratio below 0.1 indicates consistent pairwise comparison judgments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eerapu et al. (16)">
  <data key="d0">Eerapu et al. (16)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (16). Eerapu et al. present the Dense Refinement Residual Network (DRR Net) for semantic segmentation of aerial imagery addressing class imbalance.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as (16); proposes DRR-Net on the Massachusetts dataset (1171 tiles), reporting 84% IoU and 89% Dice with medium complexity.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work [16] by Eerapu et al. that proposes DRR-Net for road extraction, evaluated on the Massachusetts dataset (1171 tiles) with reported scores of 84 and 89 and medium complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ghandorh et al. (17)">
  <data key="d0">Ghandorh et al. (17)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (17). Ghandorh et al. emphasize the significance of road sensing technology in applications including traffic monitoring and urban applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work by Ghandorh et al. that integrates semantic segmentation with edge detection to improve road detection, using SegNet with attention blocks and combining focal Tversky loss with weighted cross-entropy loss; evaluated on datasets from Massachusetts and Saudi Arabia.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as (17); proposes SegNet + Attention on Saudi Arabia and Massachusetts data, reporting 88% IoU and 90% Dice with medium complexity.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work [17] by Ghandorh et al. that proposes SegNet + Attention for road extraction, evaluated on Saudi Arabia and Massachusetts data with reported scores of 88 and 90 and medium complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BRISQUE">
  <data key="d0">BRISQUE</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Technique integrated by Khan et al. to further refine road detection results.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Starting Point Tracer">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Starting Point Tracer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Approach by Wei et al. combining road segmentation and tracking to address unreached areas and improve road connectivity, giving an 8% IoU improvement over recent tracking methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jaccard Similarity Index (IoU)">
  <data key="d0">Jaccard Similarity Index (IoU)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Evaluation metric for road extraction; used to report improvements in road extraction completeness.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)">
  <data key="d0">Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Deep learning architecture used across road extraction methods for feature extraction and classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Neural network model (written as 'Conventional Neural Network' in the text) used for defect classification in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enhanced Radon Transform">
  <data key="d0">Enhanced Radon Transform</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Transform used by Yue Li et al. for road network extraction from identified candidates in SAR images.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Markov Random Field (MRF)">
  <data key="d0">Markov Random Field (MRF)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
