<node id="VGG16 suits constrained resources while maintaining high accuracy">
  <data key="d0">VGG16 suits constrained resources while maintaining high accuracy</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">VGG16 is particularly well-suited for tasks with constrained computational resources, yet it maintains a high level of accuracy in image classification tasks (23).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VGG19 extends VGG16 with three more convolutional layers">
  <data key="d0">VGG19 extends VGG16 with three more convolutional layers</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">VGG19 extends the VGG16 architecture by adding three more convolutional layers, resulting in a total of 19 layers with learnable weights (24).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Increased depth lets VGG19 capture more complex features and finer details">
  <data key="d0">Increased depth lets VGG19 capture more complex features and finer details</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The increased depth allows VGG19 to capture more complex features and finer details in the images (25)...</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deeper networks capture more complex features essential for road extraction">
  <data key="d0">Deeper networks capture more complex features essential for road extraction</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">However, deeper networks are generally capable of capturing more complex features, which is essential for accurate road extraction (27).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data augmentation enhances robustness and generalization">
  <data key="d0">Data augmentation enhances robustness and generalization</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Data augmentation methods play a pivotal role in enhancing the robustness and generalization capabilities of machine learning models (28).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Augmentations mirror real-world variations in satellite imagery">
  <data key="d0">Augmentations mirror real-world variations in satellite imagery</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">By systematically altering the orientation, perspective, and scale of the input images, these augmentations expose the model to a diverse range of transformations, mirroring real-world variations in satellite imagery (29).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ASPP enables DeepLabV3+ to handle objects of various sizes">
  <data key="d0">ASPP enables DeepLabV3+ to handle objects of various sizes</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This capability allows DeepLabV3+ to effectively handle objects of various sizes, including small road segments and larger road networks visible in satellite images (30).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decoder module produces more accurate segmentation maps">
  <data key="d0">Decoder module produces more accurate segmentation maps</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The decoder module enhances segmentation predictions by combining low-level features with high-level semantic information, resulting in more accurate and precise segmentation maps (31).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model produces binary road segmentation mask">
  <data key="d0">Model produces binary road segmentation mask</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The model predicts road probabilities for each pixel in the input image, producing a binary segmentation mask wherein road pixels are designated a value of 1, while non-road pixels are assigned a value of 0 (32).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decoder Module">
  <data key="d0">Decoder Module</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">DeepLabV3+ component that captures multi-scale contextual information and refines segmentation boundaries by combining low-level features with high-level semantic information, producing more accurate and precise segmentation maps.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal and Vertical Flips">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal and Vertical Flips</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Augmentation strategy in which each original image undergoes horizontal and vertical flips. Each original image yields four images: the original plus three augmented versions. Flips emulate variations in road layout and orientation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rotations">
  <data key="d0">Rotations</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Data augmentation method that simulates changes in satellite viewing angles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zooms">
  <data key="d0">Zooms</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Data augmentation method that replicates differences in image resolution and perspective.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generalization">
  <data key="d0">Generalization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ability of machine learning models to perform well on unseen scenarios. Data augmentation improves it.&lt;SEP&gt;A model's ability to make predictions on novel, unseen data. NB and LR show limited generalization. SVM, RF and DT progressively approach training accuracy, showing they can predict data never encountered before.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DeepGlobe Challenge">
  <data key="d0">DeepGlobe Challenge</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Challenge that includes the Road Extraction Challenge Track used as the training database in this study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ablation Study">
  <data key="d0">Ablation Study</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Experimental procedure that was not performed for data augmentation due to time constraints. Only a qualitative observation was made: models trained without augmentation showed less stable convergence and reduced segmentation quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Depth">
  <data key="d0">Network Depth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factor affecting CNN accuracy. No clear rules exist for determining the optimal depth, but deeper networks generally capture more complex features.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ASPP">
  <data key="d0">ASPP</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Atrous Spatial Pyramid Pooling, used within DeepLabV3+ in the segmentation stage to enhance multi-scale feature representation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Image-Level Accuracy">
  <data key="d0">Image-Level Accuracy</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Principal metric for evaluating the VGG16 and VGG19 classifiers. It is the percentage of correctly classified images among all images, computed from TP, TN, FP and FN at the image level (Equation 1).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dice Coefficient">
  <data key="d0">Dice Coefficient</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Overlap measure computed from the number of pixels in the predicted mask, the number of pixels in the ground truth mask, and the number of overlapping pixels (Equation 2). It is used for segmentation evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intersection over Union (IoU)">
  <data key="d0">Intersection over Union (IoU)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Segmentation evaluation metric, also known as the Jaccard Index. It is computed as the ratio of the intersection of the predicted and ground truth masks to their union (Equation 4). The study uses a 0.5 threshold, so a pixel counts as correctly segmented if its predicted probability is 0.5 or higher. A higher IoU indicates greater overlap between predicted and actual road pixels. The metric was integrated into training and validation and evaluated at each epoch.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road Segmentation">
  <data key="d0">Road Segmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Task of identifying and delineating road pixels in satellite images. It is characterized by class imbalance, since road pixels may be significantly fewer than non-road pixels.&lt;SEP&gt;Pixel-level binary mask prediction of roads, performed with DeepLabV3+.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref (33)">
  <data key="d0">Ref (33)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as (33) as a reference for accuracy being a conventional measure for image classification tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref (34)">
  <data key="d0">Ref (34)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as (34) in relation to Dice Loss used as the primary loss function during training.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref (35)">
  <data key="d0">Ref (35)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as (35) in relation to IoU (Jaccard Index) as a common segmentation metric and to integrating metrics into training and validation for real-time feedback.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref (26) DeepGlobe Challenge">
  <data key="d0">Ref (26) DeepGlobe Challenge</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as (26) describing the DeepGlobe Challenge, whose Road Extraction Challenge Track provided the dataset used in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accuracy is a conventional measure for image classification">
  <data key="d0">Accuracy is a conventional measure for image classification</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Accuracy evaluates the percentage of correctly classified images among the total images, as given by Equation 1, and is a conventional measure for image classification tasks (33).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dice Loss serves as the primary loss function for segmentation training">
  <data key="d0">Dice Loss serves as the primary loss function for segmentation training</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Dice Loss serves as the primary loss function during training (34).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IoU is a common evaluation metric for segmentation">
  <data key="d0">IoU is a common evaluation metric for segmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Another essential evaluation metric used is Intersection over Union (IoU), also known as the Jaccard Index (35). It is a common evaluation metric for segmentation tasks...</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metrics integrated into training provide real-time feedback">
  <data key="d0">Metrics integrated into training provide real-time feedback</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">These metrics were integrated into the training and validation processes to provide real-time feedback on the model's performance (35).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DeepGlobe Challenge focuses on automatic road extraction from satellite images">
  <data key="d0">DeepGlobe Challenge focuses on automatic road extraction from satellite images</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The dataset used in this study was obtained from the Road Extraction Challenge Track of the DeepGlobe Challenge (26), which focuses on automatically extracting roads and road networks from satellite images, particularly in disaster areas and developing countries where maps and accessibility...</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road Extraction from Satellite Images">
  <data key="d0">Road Extraction from Satellite Images</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Problem of automatically extracting roads and road networks from satellite images. It is especially relevant in disaster areas and developing countries where maps and accessibility information may be lacking. It is the overall goal of the study's pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Image Pre-Processing">
  <data key="d0">Image Pre-Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Pipeline stage applied to raw satellite images that includes resizing, normalization, and optional noise reduction. It precedes the VGG16/VGG19 classification step.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Binary Road Mask">
  <data key="d0">Binary Road Mask</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Final output of the segmentation pipeline: a binary mask that delineates road pixels, produced by DeepLabV3+ with ASPP and Dice Loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DeepGlobe Challenge (26)">
  <data key="d0">DeepGlobe Challenge (26)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (26). Describes the DeepGlobe Challenge, including the Road Extraction Challenge Track, which focuses on automatically extracting roads and road networks from satellite images.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DeepGlobe Road Extraction Dataset">
  <data key="d0">DeepGlobe Road Extraction Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Dataset from the Road Extraction Challenge Track of the DeepGlobe Challenge; includes 6,226 RGB training satellite images of 1024 x 1024 pixels at 50 cm pixel resolution, 1,243 validation images, and 1,101 test images without corresponding masks; covers urban, suburban, and rural areas across multiple continents.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DigitalGlobe">
  <data key="d0">DigitalGlobe</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Satellite provider whose satellite collected the DeepGlobe road extraction images at a pixel resolution of 50 cm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Crisis Response">
  <data key="d0">Crisis Response</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Application area where maps and accessibility information derived from road extraction are essential, particularly in disaster areas and developing countries.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DeepGlobe road extraction track targets road network extraction from satellite images for crisis response">
  <data key="d0">DeepGlobe road extraction track targets road network extraction from satellite images for crisis response</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The dataset used in this study was obtained from the Road Extraction Challenge Track of the DeepGlobe Challenge (26), which focuses on automatically extracting roads and road networks from satellite images, particularly in disaster areas and developing countries where maps and accessibility information are essential to crisis response."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Collection">
  <data key="d0">Data Collection</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Stage of the study's pipeline in which the DeepGlobe Road Extraction Dataset was obtained. The training, validation and test splits were 6,226, 1,243 and 1,101 images, and the test images have no corresponding masks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Geographic Diversity">
  <data key="d0">Geographic Diversity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Property of the DeepGlobe Road Extraction Dataset, which covers urban, suburban and rural areas across multiple continents. This diversity introduces substantial variation in road appearance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Satellite Road Imagery Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Satellite Road Imagery Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Satellite images paired with grayscale road mask images in which white pixels mark roads. Files follow the formats 'id_sat.jpg' and 'id_mask.png'. Masks are binarized with a threshold of 128. Annotations are imperfect, particularly in rural regions, where small farmland roads were left unannotated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adam Optimizer">
  <data key="d0">Adam Optimizer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Optimizer used for classification (learning rate 1e-4, decayed on plateau) and for segmentation (learning rate 8e-5).&lt;SEP&gt;Optimizer used to train DeepLabV3+ with a learning rate of 8x10^-5.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimization algorithm used to train the LSTM model, with a learning rate of 0.001.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CosineAnnealingWarmRestarts">
  <data key="d0">CosineAnnealingWarmRestarts</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Learning rate scheduler used in the training of the DeepLabV3+ segmentation stage.&lt;SEP&gt;Learning-rate schedule used for DeepLabV3+ training with T₀=1, T_mult=2 and η_min=5×10⁻⁵.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Binary Cross-Entropy">
  <data key="d0">Binary Cross-Entropy</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Loss function used to train the VGG16/VGG19 classifiers.&lt;SEP&gt;Loss function used to train the classification models, and combined with Dice loss for the segmentation model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IoU">
  <data key="d0">IoU</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Intersection over Union. IoU@0.5 is the principal evaluation metric for segmentation, and the best validation IoU checkpoint is retained.&lt;SEP&gt;Intersection over Union metric, computed at threshold 0.5, measuring overlap between predicted and ground truth segmentation masks; used for early stopping and evaluation of DeepLabV3+.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accuracy, Precision, Recall And F1-Score">
  <data key="d0">Accuracy, Precision, Recall And F1-Score</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Image-level metrics used to evaluate the road-presence classification models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
