<node id="Road Tile Classification">
  <data key="d0">Road Tile Classification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">First stage of the pipeline, in which satellite image tiles are classified as road-positive or not using VGG16 and VGG19; only road-positive tiles are retained for segmentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Qualitative Evaluation">
  <data key="d0">Qualitative Evaluation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual assessment of segmentation output comparing original images, corresponding ground truth masks and predicted masks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DeepLabV3+ Reaches High Validation IoU On Road-Positive Subset">
  <data key="d0">DeepLabV3+ Reaches High Validation IoU On Road-Positive Subset</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding reported in the text: validation IoU of DeepLabV3+ rose from 0.945 to 0.958 and validation Dice loss fell from 0.035 to 0.022 over the first three epochs on the internal validation subset. "These values reflect the subset of road-positive tiles retained after the classification step, which explains their relatively high magnitude and makes them not directly comparable to benchmark-style results reported for the full DeepGlobe dataset."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VGG16 Outperforms VGG19 For Road Identification">
  <data key="d0">VGG16 Outperforms VGG19 For Road Identification</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding reported in the text: VGG16 shows "superior ability to effectively identify roads in satellite images", with validation accuracy 0.9909 and validation loss 0.0391 versus 0.9136 and 0.2312 for VGG19.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422754</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intersection Over Union">
  <data key="d0">Intersection Over Union</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Segmentation metric (IoU) used to evaluate road delineation; the validation subset reached about 0.95-0.96 at early epochs on road-positive tiles.&lt;SEP&gt;IoU metric used to evaluate DeepLabV3+ road segmentation performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011</data>
