<node id="DeepLabV3+">
  <data key="d0">DeepLabV3+</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">DeepLabV3+ is a state-of-the-art convolutional neural network architecture for pixel-wise semantic segmentation. It extends the DeepLab family by combining atrous (dilated) convolution and Atrous Spatial Pyramid Pooling (ASPP) with a decoder module. In this paper, DeepLabV3+ segments road networks from satellite images, classifying road pixels to produce a binary road mask.

The model uses a ResNet-50 encoder backbone pretrained on ImageNet. A final sigmoid activation produces the binary road mask, and the full model has approximately 41 million parameters. Training used 512×512 image crops, a batch size of 4, and the Adam optimizer with a learning rate of 8×10⁻⁵ under a CosineAnnealingWarmRestarts schedule. The loss function combined Dice Loss with Binary Cross-Entropy (BCE). Training was configured for up to 50 epochs, with early stopping based on validation Intersection over Union (IoU).

DeepLabV3+ performed strongly, reaching a validation IoU of about 0.958 (≈95.8%) and a Dice score of about 97.9% on the road-positive validation subsets, which corresponds to a low Dice Loss. These results came after only three epochs of training, which took roughly 3 hours and 16 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422757</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
