<node id="Road Extraction">
  <data key="d0">Road Extraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Road Extraction is the remote sensing task of automatically identifying and extracting roads and road networks from imagery. It is applied mainly to satellite images, and also to aerial photographs, orthophotos and Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) data. The goal is to delineate roads precisely and to recover the connected structure of road networks. In some research it is the central objective of the work, and it is a dominant theme across a large body of related literature.

The task has several practical applications, including urban planning, transportation management and disaster response. It is especially valuable in disaster-affected areas and developing countries, where up-to-date maps and accessibility information are essential for crisis response. In these settings, extracting roads from satellite imagery can supply information that is otherwise unavailable.

Road Extraction faces several challenges. Trees, buildings, shadows and vehicles often occlude roads. Roads can be hard to distinguish from visually similar surfaces, and complex backgrounds make accurate segmentation harder. Deep learning has transformed the field and become the prevailing approach, substantially improving the identification of roads in remote sensing imagery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dice Loss">
  <data key="d0">Dice Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Dice Loss is a segmentation loss function and evaluation metric based on the Dice coefficient, which measures the similarity, or overlap, between predicted segmentation masks and ground truth masks. It served as the primary loss function and main training objective for the DeepLabV3+ segmentation model, and it was also used as a key measure for evaluating that model. Dice Loss is particularly effective for imbalanced datasets such as road segmentation, where the target class may occupy only a small part of an image. Lower Dice Loss values indicate a better fit between predictions and ground truth.

Within the proposed pipeline, DeepLabV3+ achieved consistently low Dice Loss scores on road segmentation, and these results were reported alongside Intersection over Union (IoU). During training, the validation Dice loss fell from 0.035 to 0.022 over the first three epochs. The pipeline reached a Dice coefficient of approximately 97.9%. This value is consistent with the low loss values observed, since Dice Loss is commonly computed as one minus the Dice coefficient.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422760</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Augmentation">
  <data key="d0">Data Augmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Data Augmentation is a set of techniques for expanding and enriching training datasets so that machine learning models become more robust and less prone to overfitting. Common strategies include rotations, horizontal and vertical flips, zooms or scaling, and adjustments to brightness and contrast. These transformations increase the variety of the training data and improve model robustness to occlusion, scale differences, illumination changes, viewpoint and perspective shifts, and general variability in the input imagery.

In image segmentation, Data Augmentation is applied systematically and extensively during training, often by randomly applying rotations, flips, zooms, and brightness/contrast changes. In one paper's structured road extraction process, it serves as a dedicated pipeline step. That work describes a concrete implementation in which horizontal and vertical flips turn each original image into four images, which helps the model avoid overfitting.

Data Augmentation has also been addressed more broadly. Approaches include a supervised augmentation strategy and a catalogue of 65 augmentation techniques for medical imaging, which shows that the concept applies across domains beyond road extraction and general segmentation tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Application area for which Conditional GAN is primarily used.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique of enlarging training data with synthetic samples, used via WGAN-based market simulation to improve stock price prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;Methodology used in the AI implementation process for real-time quality prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique integrated with transfer learning in the knowledge reuse strategy of Liu et al. (2021).&lt;SEP&gt;Technique integrated into the knowledge reuse strategy to improve defect detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467085</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Segmentation">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Segmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic Segmentation is a computer vision task that assigns a class label to every pixel in an image. The field advanced significantly with the introduction of fully convolutional neural networks. It is applied in many domains, including road detection, aerial and satellite imagery analysis, biomedical imaging, fire detection and plant leaf analysis. Yang et al. (2020) and Ghandorh et al. (2022) are among the works that have addressed the task.

In road extraction, Semantic Segmentation is used to delineate road networks by classifying each pixel as either road or non-road. In the road extraction pipeline described in this context, the task is performed with the DeepLabV3+ architecture. DeepLabV3+ produces pixel-level road masks from satellite images, and these predicted masks are compared against ground truth masks to evaluate performance.

Current Semantic Segmentation architectures perform well in road-dominated scenarios. However, they struggle with background-dominated aerial images, where road pixels make up only a small fraction of the scene. This limitation is a key challenge for accurate road network extraction from remote sensing data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791422763</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="IJE Transactions C: Aspects">
  <data key="d0">IJE Transactions C: Aspects</data>
  <data key="d1">venue</data>
  <data key="d2">IJE Transactions C: Aspects, formally the International Journal of Engineering, Transactions C: Aspects, is the journal that published the article by I. Mayouche et al. The article is a study on road extraction. It appeared in Volume 39, Issue No. 09, in September 2026, on pages 2106–2117.

The descriptions agree on the volume, issue and publication date. Some also give the page range of 2106–2117 and describe the article's subject as road extraction. Together they identify IJE Transactions C: Aspects as the venue for this work.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
