</node>
<node id="Harnessing Multi-Source Data for AI-Driven Oncology Insights: Productivity, Trend, and Sentiment Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Harnessing Multi-Source Data for AI-Driven Oncology Insights: Productivity, Trend, and Sentiment Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, published in Applied Computer Science 2025, vol. 21, no. 1, pp. 70–82. A bibliometric study of 1,296 AI-in-oncology papers published between January 2019 and January 2024, analyzing productivity, emerging trends and researcher sentiment using merged WoS, Scopus and PubMed databases.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="10.35784/acs_6670">
  <data key="d0">10.35784/acs_6670</data>
  <data key="d1">identifier</data>
  <data key="d2">DOI of the AI-driven oncology bibliometric study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
