</node>
<node id="PRISMA">
  <data key="d0">PRISMA</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Framework used to select 1,296 papers for the bibliometric analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Four-step method (identification, screening, eligibility, inclusion) used to combine and select documents from Scopus, WoS and PubMed.&lt;SEP&gt;Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses; an evidence-based method providing a minimal set of items for rigorously reporting systematic reviews and meta-analyses, emphasizing transparency and completeness through a four-step process.&lt;SEP&gt;Reporting guidelines and framework for systematic reviews and meta-analyses. It has four steps: identification, screening, eligibility assessment and inclusion. Introduced by Moher in 2009.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_AIapplicationinmarketanalysis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425835</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CiteSpace">
  <data key="d0">CiteSpace</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Software used for bibliographic analysis in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Science mapping tool working principally with WoS-format data; used to resolve tagging discrepancies and remove duplicates.&lt;SEP&gt;Bibliometric software used to build collaboration networks of authors and countries, using the g-index measure with a scale factor of 25 and log-likelihood ratio for cluster labels.&lt;SEP&gt;Bibliometric software used to identify top institutions by citation count, top journals by betweenness centrality, and keyword co-occurrence networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Bibliometric tool used to address discrepancies in database tagging across Scopus, WoS and PubMed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sentiment Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Sentiment Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis of researchers' sentiment toward AI advancements in oncology; 90.5% viewed advancements positively.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative analysis of community sentiment toward the use of AI in oncology.&lt;SEP&gt;Task including sentiment extraction, classification, subjectivity detection, opinion summary and opinion spam detection; applied to classify 307 reviews as positive or negative.&lt;SEP&gt;Analysis of scientific community sentiment toward AI in oncology; found 91.5% of researchers viewed advancements positively.&lt;SEP&gt;Task of analyzing sentiment in text, applied to user-generated drug reviews using machine learning techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Text analysis technique whose use in tourism research is reviewed by Manosso et al. (2021).&lt;SEP&gt;Technique suggested to be incorporated into hybrid models to enhance GAN adaptability to real-world financial conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_AIapplicationinmarketanalysis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
