<node id="Multimodal AI">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal AI</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">AI methods that fuse various data types to identify cross-modal correlations and improve diagnostic accuracy, particularly in cancer research.&lt;SEP&gt;AI able to combine text and images in clinical image interpretation. ChatGPT-4's results show both its potential and its current limits, especially with complicated image datasets.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large Language Models">
  <data key="d0">Large Language Models</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Large Language Models (LLMs) are a class of advanced natural language processing systems trained on massive datasets to process and generate text. They are designed for tasks such as machine translation, summarization, and conversational interactions, and they can produce fluent, coherent text on a wide range of topics. Large-scale language models discussed in the literature (references [13], [14] and [15]) are noted for their few-shot learning abilities. The same works note that these models have difficulty learning long-tail knowledge.

Despite their capabilities, Large Language Models have well-documented limitations. They lack real-time access to specific or up-to-date information, they rely on knowledge that can become outdated, and they tend to hallucinate. In specialized domains such as law, standalone LLMs may lack specific legal facts and can generate incorrect or non-compliant information. To address these weaknesses, LLMs are often combined with external retrieval through Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). One example is integration with legal vector databases. The cited works also describe improving language models through external knowledge, automated feedback, and retrieval augmentation.

In healthcare, Large Language Models have been examined for clinical decision support and for providing patient information in oncology, and they are identified as a trending topic in AI cancer research. Models such as ChatGPT-4, ChatGPT-3.5 and Google Bard have been compared on their ability to answer immuno-oncology questions. These models show promise in this field but have problems with inaccurate and incomplete responses. When combined with multimodal interfaces, LLMs also offer opportunities for enhanced access to information and services.&lt;SEP&gt;Models explored for tabular synthetic generation and hybrid pipelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Models that Khalil et al. (2025) use together with CTGANs to create synthetic student data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
