</node>
<node id="Supervised Machine Learning">
  <data key="d0">Supervised Machine Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prominent research theme in AI for oncology, represented by multiple clusters in 2019-2021 and cluster #0 in 2022-2024.&lt;SEP&gt;Class of ML algorithms used in the research to forecast optimal machine selection for new plastic parts. The algorithms were RF, DT, SVM, SGD classifier, LR, and NB.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine learning methods that reference [11] applies to predict the cooling time parameter in injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breast Cancer Prediction">
  <data key="d0">Breast Cancer Prediction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Detection and prediction of breast cancer, an early focus of classical supervised methods and of McKinney SM's AI system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extreme Learning Machine">
  <data key="d0">Extreme Learning Machine</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">ELM; used in a cloud-based remote breast cancer diagnosis system and integrated with deep learning optimized via crow-search algorithms (ICS-ELM).&lt;SEP&gt;Machine learning method used in a cloud computing-based framework for breast cancer diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;ELM model found most effective for coffee price prediction by Deina et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Learning method used as the basis of a coffee price forecasting methodology in reference 18.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GoogLeNet">
  <data key="d0">GoogLeNet</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Pre-trained CNN used to extract features from brain MRI images.&lt;SEP&gt;Convolutional neural network whose fine-tuned features are used for brain tumor classification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ResUNet++">
  <data key="d0">ResUNet++</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Model leveraged for colorectal cancer detection, combined with CRF and TTA for improved generalizability.&lt;SEP&gt;Segmentation architecture used for colorectal cancer detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Segmentation architecture used for colorectal polyp segmentation, combined with conditional random field and test-time augmentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stimulated Raman Scattering Microscopy">
  <data key="d0">Stimulated Raman Scattering Microscopy</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Imaging technique combined with a CNN to analyze histopathology of fresh prostate biopsies.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging technique used together with a CNN to perform Gleason scoring of prostate core needle biopsies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generalizability">
  <data key="d0">Generalizability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical focus in supervised learning for oncology; addressed by improved cross-dataset performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Key challenge in translating supervised learning models into clinical practice.&lt;SEP&gt;Model property that the study seeks to improve. Suggested routes are larger datasets and testing across all five machine classes and a broader range of part characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425067</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gain Ratio Feature Selection">
  <data key="d0">Gain Ratio Feature Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Feature selection method used to eliminate insignificant features before applying ELM.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUC-ROC">
  <data key="d0">AUC-ROC</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance metric enhanced by segmentation-aided feature extraction for lung node classification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ELM-based cloud system enables remote breast cancer diagnosis">
  <data key="d0">ELM-based cloud system enables remote breast cancer diagnosis</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">after eliminating insignificant features by applying the gain ratio feature selection method, Extreme Learning Machine (ELM) was employed in a cloud computing-based system for remote breast cancer diagnosis (Lahoura et al., 2021).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-trained GoogLeNet features enable brain MRI classification">
  <data key="d0">Pre-trained GoogLeNet features enable brain MRI classification</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The features of the brain MRI images were extracted using a pre-trained CNN, i.e., GoogLeNet, and then classified using classifiers such as Softmax, Support Vector Machine (SVM), and K-nearest neighbor (K-NN) (Sekhar et al., 2022).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Segmentation algorithms improve lung node classification">
  <data key="d0">Segmentation algorithms improve lung node classification</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Segmentation algorithms aided in feature extraction for classifying lung nodes (Murugesan et al., 2022), ultimately enhancing the AUC-ROC performance metric.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SRS microscopy with CNN enables rapid automated Gleason scoring">
  <data key="d0">SRS microscopy with CNN enables rapid automated Gleason scoring</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">a recent study demonstrated that by combining stimulated Raman scattering microscopy with a convolutional neural network, it became possible to quickly analyze histopathology and automatically determine Gleason scores on fresh prostate biopsies, without the need for complex processing (Ao et al., 2023).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ResUNet++ with CRF and TTA improves cross-dataset generalizability">
  <data key="d0">ResUNet++ with CRF and TTA improves cross-dataset generalizability</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Generalizability also emerged as a critical focus, as demonstrated by a study leveraging ResUNet++ for colorectal cancer detection (Jha et al., 2021). By integrating Conditional Random Fields (CRF) and Test-Time Augmentation (TTA), the model achieved improved cross-dataset performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
