<node id="ChatGPT-4 performs better on non-image questions than image interpretation in ophthalmology">
  <data key="d0">ChatGPT-4 performs better on non-image questions than image interpretation in ophthalmology</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The chatbot performed better on non-image-based questions (82%) compared to those requiring image interpretation (65%), with a significant difference (χ² = 12.2, P &lt; .001). It excelled in retinal cases (77%) but showed lower accuracy in neuro-ophthalmology (58%), highlighting both the potential and current limitations of multimodal AI in clinical image interpretation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
