<node id="Multimodal Data Fusion">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Data Fusion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combining heterogeneous data modalities, such as images, clinical data, histology and genomics, for cancer screening, diagnosis, classification and prognosis. It is the topic of several cited works.&lt;SEP&gt;Combining medical imaging such as CT with clinical variables or electronic health records for prediction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Precision Oncology">
  <data key="d0">Precision Oncology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tailoring cancer care to individual patients. Boehm et al. (2022) discuss advancing it through multimodal data integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_25_66701.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423275</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
