<node id="Data Duplication Across Databases">
  <data key="d0">Data Duplication Across Databases</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk that data presented in different forms across multiple databases could be duplicated, potentially leading to biased results.&lt;SEP&gt;The risk that the same records appear in different forms across databases, because some journals are indexed in both Scopus and Web of Science. This Paper notes that such duplication could lead to biased bibliometric results.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">acs_AIapplicationinmarketanalysis.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423294</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
