</node>
<node id="10.5829/ije.2025.38.04a.16">
  <data key="d0">10.5829/ije.2025.38.04a.16</data>
  <data key="d1">identifier</data>
  <data key="d2">DOI of the hybrid sales forecasting paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Sales Forecasting Model">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Sales Forecasting Model</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A model combining LSTM, SARIMA and Triple Exponential Smoothing (Holt-Winters). It is designed to capture complex patterns, handle linear trends and seasonal patterns, and emphasize recent sales trends. It outperforms its individual components on MAPE.&lt;SEP&gt;Proposed hybrid model showing performance 9%, 39% and 43% better than LSTM, SARIMA and Holt-Winters models respectively, with enhanced ability to identify complex patterns and seasonal variations in sales data.&lt;SEP&gt;Novel hybrid model combining classical time series analysis with advanced deep learning techniques (LSTM, SARIMA, Holt-Winters) to capture complex patterns, handle linear trends and seasonal patterns, and emphasize recent sales trends.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seasonal Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average">
  <data key="d0">Seasonal Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">SARIMA, a Box-Jenkins time series model, used as a component of the hybrid model. The hybrid model surpasses SARIMA by 39%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mean Absolute Percentage Error">
  <data key="d0">Mean Absolute Percentage Error</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">MAPE, the metric used in the comparative analysis of the hybrid model and its individual components.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Series Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Time Series Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Classic analysis approach combined with deep learning in the hybrid model.&lt;SEP&gt;Analysis of time series data, which requires the data to be stationary and may involve trends and seasonality.&lt;SEP&gt;Classical forecasting approach combined with deep learning in the hybrid model.&lt;SEP&gt;Analysis of trend and seasonality components integrated into FE-GAN alongside GBM-derived volatility modeling to enhance VaR estimation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recurrent Neural Network">
  <data key="d0">Recurrent Neural Network</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">The Recurrent Neural Network (RNN) is a class, or family, of deep learning neural network architectures characterized by a short-term memory capacity. Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) belongs to this family and was proposed to enhance the RNN's limited memory capabilities. The fundamentals of the RNN architecture are presented by Sherstinsky (2020), and the family is also the subject of the book "Recurrent Neural Networks: Design and Application," which counts LSTM among its members.

In applied research, the Recurrent Neural Network appears as a keyword of a hybrid sales forecasting paper, in which an LSTM component, an RNN variant, forms part of the hybrid model. RNN architectures have also been used in generative settings: Wiese et al. employ a recurrent architecture within Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) to simulate option price time series. This shows the family's versatility in modeling sequential and financial time-series data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-44e660d542a189a6d2b6161acf6e6b98-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;ComparativestudiesoftheSARIMAandLSTM.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Box-Jenkins">
  <data key="d0">Box-Jenkins</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Classic time series modeling methodology listed as a keyword of the paper. SARIMA, a component of the hybrid model, follows this approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exponential Smoothing">
  <data key="d0">Exponential Smoothing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Time series forecasting technique listed as a keyword of the paper. Triple Exponential Smoothing (Holt-Winters) is used in the hybrid model.&lt;SEP&gt;Traditional time series forecasting technique. Melekşen and Eyduran applied it to predict avocado production in Turkey for 2016 to 2025. Holt-Winters is an exponential smoothing model.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear forecasting technique used by Deina et al. (18) for coffee price prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;Univariate time series forecasting method that gives more weight to recent observations through exponentially diminishing weights. It has twelve trend/seasonality configurations, which can be additive or multiplicative.&lt;SEP&gt;Family of time series forecasting models compared in reference 29.&lt;SEP&gt;Time series forecasting method based on exponentially weighted averages; the subject of references 29, 31, 32, 33, 34, 35 and 36.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pricing Strategies">
  <data key="d0">Pricing Strategies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Business activity informed by the hybrid model's sales predictions for the next 'n' days, used to optimize sales performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Business planning area that the paper says should take the sales forecasts into account.&lt;SEP&gt;Business strategies that the hybrid model's sales forecasts inform, alongside inventory management and promotional planning, to optimize sales performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Promotional Planning">
  <data key="d0">Promotional Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Business activity informed by the hybrid model's sales predictions for the next 'n' days, used to optimize sales performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Planning of promotional activities that the hybrid model's sales forecasts for upcoming days inform, in order to optimize sales performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marketplace Management">
  <data key="d0">Marketplace Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Business domain that benefits significantly from the improved forecasting accuracy of the hybrid model, which offers more reliable sales predictions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid LSTM-SARIMA-Holt-Winters Model">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid LSTM-SARIMA-Holt-Winters Model</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Novel hybrid forecasting model that integrates linear and non-linear methods (LSTM, SARIMA and Holt-Winters exponential smoothing) to predict future sales from daily company data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Holt-Winters Exponential Smoothing">
  <data key="d0">Holt-Winters Exponential Smoothing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Exponential smoothing technique, also called Winter's smoothing, used to emphasize recent sales trends.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARIMA">
  <data key="d0">ARIMA</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average, a traditional time series forecasting model.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average model capturing linear aspects of time series.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoregressive integrated moving average model, combined with a neural network for sales forecasting in reference 15.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoregressive integrated moving average time-series forecasting model, used in reference 7 and, combined with RFM, in reference 11.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoregressive integrated moving average model evaluated for consumer retail sales forecasting in reference 44.&lt;SEP&gt;Autoregressive integrated moving average model, evaluated by Ramos et al. (2015) for consumer retail sales forecasting.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-44e660d542a189a6d2b6161acf6e6b98-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;ComparativestudiesoftheSARIMAandLSTM.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Box-Jenkins Methodology">
  <data key="d0">Box-Jenkins Methodology</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Statistical time series modeling methodology to which SARIMA belongs.&lt;SEP&gt;Time series modeling approach consisting of model identification, parameter estimation, model validation and forecasting. It ends by diagnosing residuals for white noise and then predicting future values.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Superstore Daily Sales Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Superstore Daily Sales Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Dataset of 13 years of daily total sales from a superstore in the USA, built from four separate periods. It can be aggregated monthly or by any other period.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Time Series Forecasting">
  <data key="d0">Time Series Forecasting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Forecasting based on chronological sequences of data. It is an important application of AI, and its accuracy depends on the data's characteristics, components and context.&lt;SEP&gt;Forecasting future values from time series data, where accounting for variations such as seasonal patterns is essential.&lt;SEP&gt;Research topic of forecasting future values from time-ordered data, central to the exponential smoothing and LSTM references.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Seasonality">
  <data key="d0">Seasonality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Seasonal patterns in time series data, such as higher demand for winter coats in colder months.&lt;SEP&gt;Seasonal patterns in time series data, e.g. increased winter coat demand in colder months.&lt;SEP&gt;Periodic pattern in non-stationary time series processes handled by SARIMA models.&lt;SEP&gt;Periodic patterns in time series data captured by SARIMA's seasonal parameters P, D, Q and periodicity m.&lt;SEP&gt;Seasonal and periodic structures in retail sales time series that LSTM may struggle to capture and SARIMA is suited to model.&lt;SEP&gt;Periodic component of a time series. Its presence or absence, together with trend, determines which exponential smoothing model to use. It can be modeled as none, additive or multiplicative.&lt;SEP&gt;Recurring periodic patterns in the sales data. Together with trends, seasonality motivated the choice of time series models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
