</node>
<node id="Selecting the most effective time series forecasting model remains a challenge for decision-makers">
  <data key="d0">Selecting the most effective time series forecasting model remains a challenge for decision-makers</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Identifying the most effective forecasting model for time series analysis remains a significant challenge for decision-makers (39)."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Winters-Holt">
  <data key="d0">Winters-Holt</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Exponential smoothing forecasting method (written as Winters-Hold in the text) used as one of the models to forecast daily sales and as a component of the hybrid model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Min-Max Normalization">
  <data key="d0">Min-Max Normalization</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Scaling technique applied to the sales data to prepare it for more effective model training.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Preprocessing">
  <data key="d0">Data Preprocessing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Process comprising five steps: data cleaning, reduction, scaling, transformation and partitioning; significantly influences model performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Preprocessing of sales data, including handling of missing values and outliers, recommended as essential to ensure high data quality when implementing the hybrid sales forecasting approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorough preprocessing applied to the sales data before building the models. Future work plans more robust techniques for handling missing or noisy data.&lt;SEP&gt;Techniques for preparing data, including normalization, discussed in references 37 and 38.&lt;SEP&gt;Steps including mode/mean imputation of missing values, label encoding of categorical variables, MinMax scaling to [0,1], and an 80/20 train-test split.&lt;SEP&gt;Second step of the proposed ML methodology. It determines correlations in the collected data and prepares the data for model implementation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Auto-ARIMA">
  <data key="d0">Auto-ARIMA</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Function from the pmdarima Python library used to perform a grid search over SARIMA parameters (p, d, q, P, D, Q) to minimize AIC values.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="pmdarima">
  <data key="d0">pmdarima</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Python library providing the auto-arima function used for SARIMA parameter selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AIC">
  <data key="d0">AIC</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Akaike Information Criterion, minimized during the grid search to identify the appropriate SARIMA configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Residual Error Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Residual Error Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Technique of modeling residual errors of LSTM predictions with SARIMA to refine forecasts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adjusted Residuals">
  <data key="d0">Adjusted Residuals</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Residual component remaining after the SARIMA residual modeling. Its prediction at time t (R̂t) is one of the three terms summed in the final forecasting model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Data Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Preprocessing step that restructures the dataset from individual orders per row into aggregated daily sales, which supports the objective of daily sales prediction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Data Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Preprocessing step usually aimed at categorical data. The study skipped this step because the dataset has no categorical variables.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM-SARIMA">
  <data key="d0">LSTM-SARIMA</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid model in which SARIMA is fitted on the residuals of LSTM predictions. A Holt-Winters model is then applied to the residuals derived from the LSTM-SARIMA predictions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proposed Hybrid LSTM-SARIMA-Holt-Winters Model">
  <data key="d0">Proposed Hybrid LSTM-SARIMA-Holt-Winters Model</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">The paper's proposed model, which combines LSTM, SARIMA (2, 1, 2)(1, 0, 1)7 and Holt-Winters with α=0.08, β=0.2 and γ=0.08.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Residual Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Residual Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic procedure that uses residual plots, ACF plots and histograms to check whether residuals behave as white noise. It is used to validate the SARIMA models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autocorrelation Function">
  <data key="d0">Autocorrelation Function</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">ACF plot used to show that the residuals have no significant autocorrelation within a 95% confidence interval.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ADAM">
  <data key="d0">ADAM</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Optimizer used to train the LSTM models with a learning rate of 0.001.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MAPE">
  <data key="d0">MAPE</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Mean absolute percentage error. It is used as the optimization target for the grid search and as an evaluation metric.&lt;SEP&gt;Mean Absolute Percentage Error, the mean of absolute errors relative to actual values multiplied by 100; used as the main evaluation metric.&lt;SEP&gt;Mean absolute percentage error metric used to compare the forecasting models (Figure 4).&lt;SEP&gt;Mean Absolute Percentage Error metric used for comparative analysis of forecasting performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Mean Absolute Percentage Error, used as a quality indicator for evaluating forecasting models.&lt;SEP&gt;Mean Absolute Percentage Error, an evaluation metric. The LSTM-AE achieved 0.0146.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-44e660d542a189a6d2b6161acf6e6b98-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;ComparativestudiesoftheSARIMAandLSTM.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ME">
  <data key="d0">ME</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Mean error, a metric used to evaluate forecast performance (Formula 17).&lt;SEP&gt;Mean Error, the average of differences between actual observations and predicted values.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MAE">
  <data key="d0">MAE</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Mean absolute error, a metric used to evaluate forecast performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Mean Absolute Error, the average of absolute differences between actual observations and predicted values.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RMSE">
  <data key="d0">RMSE</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Root mean squared error, a metric used to evaluate forecast performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Root Mean Squared Error, the square root of the mean of squared differences between actual and predicted values.&lt;SEP&gt;Root Mean Squared Error, used as a quality indicator for evaluating forecasting models.&lt;SEP&gt;Root Mean Square Error metric. Kumar et al.'s method achieves an RMSE of 0.0585.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-44e660d542a189a6d2b6161acf6e6b98-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;ComparativestudiesoftheSARIMAandLSTM.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MPE">
  <data key="d0">MPE</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Mean percentage error, a metric used to evaluate forecast performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sales Series">
  <data key="d0">Sales Series</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Sales time series with a seasonal period of 7. It is best fitted with SARIMA (2, 1, 1)(2, 0, 2)7 and is also modeled with a Holt-Winters additive model whose coefficients are smoothing level 0.03, smoothing trend 0.2 and smoothing seasonal 0.01.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Residuals Series">
  <data key="d0">Residuals Series</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Residual series used in two places. The residuals derived from LSTM predictions are modeled with SARIMA (2, 1, 2)(1, 0, 1)7. The residuals derived from LSTM-SARIMA model predictions are modeled with a Holt-Winters additive model whose optimal coefficients are smoothing level 0.08, smoothing trend 0.2 and smoothing seasonal 0.08.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference 41">
  <data key="d0">Reference 41</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as (41) to support the statement that accuracy is not always the best measure for diverse data features.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference 42">
  <data key="d0">Reference 42</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as (42) for the most commonly used quality indicators of forecast models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference 43">
  <data key="d0">Reference 43</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as (43) as the source of metric Formulas 17 and 18.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference 44">
  <data key="d0">Reference 44</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as (44) as the source of metric Formulas 19 and 20, and for the recommendation to express indicators as percentages.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
