</node>
<node id="Accuracy is not always the best measure for diverse data features">
  <data key="d0">Accuracy is not always the best measure for diverse data features</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Though accuracy frequently stands as the principal metric in model evaluation, it doesn't always serve as the most accurate measure for diverse data features (41).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ME, MAE, RMSE, MPE and MAPE are the most used forecast quality indicators">
  <data key="d0">ME, MAE, RMSE, MPE and MAPE are the most used forecast quality indicators</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The most used quality indicators for measuring and comparing the performance of forecast models are (42): ME, MAE, RMSE, mean percentage error (MPE) and MAPE.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Percentage forms of forecast error indicators ease interpretation">
  <data key="d0">Percentage forms of forecast error indicators ease interpretation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">To facilitate the interpretation of the indicators, it is recommended to use their percentage (44).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
