</node>
<node id="Histogram Of Residuals">
  <data key="d0">Histogram Of Residuals</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Diagnostic plot showing that the residuals of both SARIMA models are approximately normally distributed, which indicates that the models are adequately fitted.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423544</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Normal Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distribution that the SARIMA residuals approximately follow according to the histograms. This is taken as evidence of adequate model fit.&lt;SEP&gt;Gaussian distribution assumption whose verification is fundamental for reliable SPC outcomes; the cushion parameter dataset adheres closely to it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Holt-Winters">
  <data key="d0">Holt-Winters</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Holt-Winters is a time series forecasting method based on exponential smoothing, specifically known as Triple Exponential Smoothing. It models trend and seasonality explicitly, and it gives greater weight to recent observations than to older ones. These properties make it well suited to data with recurring seasonal patterns, such as daily sales, where it has been applied as a forecasting model. It is also regarded as a strong alternative to the Box-Jenkins family of models.

Within the proposed hybrid forecasting approach, Holt-Winters serves as an integral component. It is applied in the final stage to the adjusted residuals produced by the LSTM-SARIMA model, where it accounts for seasonality and emphasizes the most recent values.

Holt-Winters also serves as a traditional, standard baseline for evaluating the proposed hybrid model. In these comparisons, the hybrid model outperforms the standalone Holt-Winters method by 43%, showing the benefit of combining it with LSTM and SARIMA techniques rather than using it alone.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
