<node id="Sales Forecasting">
  <data key="d0">Sales Forecasting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sales Forecasting is the task of predicting future sales and sales trends. It involves estimating sales for one or more products or suppliers at various granularities, such as daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, or annual. These forecasts may cover either short-term or long-term horizons. Common applications include predicting daily sales in retail stores and in e-commerce settings.

Sales Forecasting is regarded as an essential business task. It enables suppliers and retailers to analyze customer preferences, optimize profits, reduce costs, and minimize product returns. It also informs a range of operational and strategic decisions, including inventory management, pricing strategies, promotional planning, revenue forecasts, and resource distribution. In doing so, it ultimately contributes to improved customer satisfaction.

In the research context, Sales Forecasting is the central problem addressed by This Paper and by several cited works. It is the task that the paper's proposed and evaluated models are designed to solve. This Paper notes that incorporating external factors can improve the accuracy of sales forecasts. Such factors include weather conditions, holidays, promotions, and customer demographics.&lt;SEP&gt;Predicting future sales; described as an essential tool for managing a marketplace that helps suppliers increase profits and reduce costs and returns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-44e660d542a189a6d2b6161acf6e6b98-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;ComparativestudiesoftheSARIMAandLSTM.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM">
  <data key="d0">LSTM</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) is a recurrent neural network architecture introduced by Hochreiter and Schmidhuber. It is designed to process sequential data through a memory mechanism. Its core is a recurrent memory cell regulated by forget, input and output gates. The cell computes a candidate memory state using a tanh activation, updates the cell state using the input gate and the cell input activation, and then produces the hidden state, or output, from the output gate activation, the current cell state and the input. Working through samples one at a time, LSTM cells decide whether to keep or discard information in long-term memory. This lets the network learn complex non-linear temporal patterns. LSTM is therefore regarded as a preferred method for complex sequence prediction and is widely used for time series forecasting, where it supplies temporal learning within hybrid approaches.

In sales forecasting research, LSTM was the first model applied to a sales time series. It was chosen for its ability to handle sequential data and capture complex non-linear patterns, although it may struggle with seasonal structures. Its configuration had an input layer, three hidden layers of 50 neurons each (150 hidden neurons in total) and an output layer, optimized with Adam at a learning rate of 0.001 to forecast daily sales. Its predictions were used to derive a residuals series. LSTM thus served both as a component of the proposed hybrid model, where it captured data complexity, and as a standard baseline, where it was outperformed by the hybrid model by 9%. It was also used for sales forecasting with and without exogenous variables. Related literature applies LSTM to sales, time series and trading forecasting (references 16, 19, 21, 22), to purchase prediction in single and multiple separate configurations (reference 3), to demand forecasting (reference 39), and to multidimensional time series prediction of gas concentration (reference 40).

In manufacturing, LSTM was used to model the injection molding process and predict the Melt Cushion parameter. The network was trained offline on historical data to predict the next Melt Cushion value. It used a two-layer architecture with 50 or 100 units per layer, tuned across four hyperparameter configurations (Tune1–Tune4). Tune 4, with 100 units in the second layer, performed best. More broadly, LSTM is applied in manufacturing to life prediction, predictive maintenance and quality prediction, including remaining useful life prediction (reference 35). It is also used in autoencoder-based models for manufacturing and anomaly detection, including convolutional autoencoders (reference 36).&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory sequential deep learning model; slightly best performer with R-squared of 0.765.&lt;SEP&gt;Long Short-Term Memory recurrent neural network, used by Hijam et al. (2024) for Telugu text generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-44e660d542a189a6d2b6161acf6e6b98-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-56015fdaac28ae50466d3ddc4439d39b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-012</data>
