<node id="Feature Selection and Classification Performance: A Multi-Dataset Comparative Analysis Using Boruta Algorithm and Random Forest">
  <data key="d0">Feature Selection and Classification Performance: A Multi-Dataset Comparative Analysis Using Boruta Algorithm and Random Forest</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, published in the Proceedings of EECSS'24 (Barcelona, 2024) as Paper No. CIST 174. It evaluates classification models with and without Boruta-based feature selection using Random Forest classifiers across three datasets, finding that feature selection improves performance when irrelevant features are present.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423712</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
