<node id="Boruta Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Boruta Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Feature selection algorithm that iteratively compares original feature importance against randomly generated shadow features, retaining significantly important features.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature selection algorithm developed by Miron B. Kursa et al. It uses a wrapper method to assess feature importance by comparing features to random noise features, and categorizes them as selected, tentative, or rejected.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature selection algorithm used to select relevant features; it selected 7 of 20 features for Dataset 1, 15 of 29 for Dataset 2, and retained all 21 features for Dataset 3. Its effectiveness underscores its value in improving model performance, simplifying models, and making them more interpretable and computationally efficient.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature selection algorithm used to enhance model accuracy, precision, recall and F1-score; effective at identifying relevant features.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423712</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boruta-ERT">
  <data key="d0">Boruta-ERT</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Combination of Boruta with an ensemble learning algorithm.&lt;SEP&gt;Ensemble learning combination cited as [11] that can be integrated with Boruta to enhance its efficacy. It is listed alongside Random Forest and XGBoost as an ensemble learning algorithm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423712</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
