<node id="Ref [13]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [13]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Ref [13] is a citation label that appears in several distinct source documents. Because the descriptions cover unrelated subject areas, they most likely refer to different cited works that share the same reference number in their respective bibliographies. They are summarized here by topic.

In a machine learning or feature selection context, Ref [13] is cited for the effectiveness of the Boruta algorithm, a feature selection method.

In vehicular and mobile networking contexts, Ref [13] is cited to support the claim that Vehicular Ad Hoc Network (VANET) systems improve transportation security and reduce the number of accidents. A related citation labeled [13] states that Mobile Ad Hoc Networks (MANETs) have two kinds of security measures: routing protection schemes and data security schemes. These two citations may come from the same networking-focused document or from separate ones.

In a software development context, Ref [13] is a reference on Low-Code/No-Code (LCNC) platforms. It addresses the scalability issues of these platforms, along with the related concerns of shadow IT and technical debt.

In a generative AI context, Ref [13] is cited for the capacity of Large Language Models (LLMs) to generate coherent text on a wide range of topics. It also positions Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) as a major advancement in generative models and states that RAG models can be used for information retrieval. These descriptions likely refer to a single work, or to closely related works, on LLMs and RAG.

Finally, Ref [13] is cited to support the statement that artificial intelligence can help with data selection and security. This citation may belong to the generative AI or data-focused literature, but its exact source is unclear from the available descriptions.&lt;SEP&gt;Uses roadside units with Dijkstra's dedicated short-range communication protocol to collect and transmit traffic data.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work that used roadside units (RSUs) to collect and transmit traffic data via Dijkstra's dedicated short-range communication protocol (DDSRC). The algorithm finds the shortest route to the destination based on the cost of each transmission path. Table 1 lists packet delivery delay as its metric.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
