<node id="Implementation of Digital Twin and Deep Learning for Process Monitoring: Case Study in Injection Molding Manufacturing">
  <data key="d0">Implementation of Digital Twin and Deep Learning for Process Monitoring: Case Study in Injection Molding Manufacturing</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, presented at EECSS'24 (Barcelona, Spain, August 19-21, 2024) as Paper No. CIST 171. It proposes a data-centric digital twin architecture for injection molding, an LSTM-based deep learning model to forecast the melt cushion parameter, and a hybrid edge-cloud computing approach for data acquisition and simulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Abdelah Azmani">
  <data key="d0">Abdelah Azmani</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Third author of the injection molding digital twin paper, affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMed Genomics Laboratory, Abdelmalek Essaadi University.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="10.11159/cist24.171">
  <data key="d0">10.11159/cist24.171</data>
  <data key="d1">identifier</data>
  <data key="d2">DOI of the paper on digital twin and deep learning for injection molding process monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twin">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Digital Twin is a virtual representation, or digital replica, of a real physical system, asset, process, or production environment. It mirrors its physical counterpart and interacts with it bidirectionally, linking the virtual and physical worlds. Digital Twins are used for automation, data collection, real-time monitoring, analysis, diagnostics, prognostics, prediction, and performance optimization. They work by integrating artificial intelligence, machine learning, and analytics with the large volumes of data generated by physical systems. Through real-time data and predictive analytics, they improve efficiency, quality, and responsiveness, which helps manufacturing systems adapt to changing conditions.

The Digital Twin is regarded as a central concept of the Smart Industry revolution and is closely associated with Industry 4.0 and the Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT). It is the main topic of many cited works covering a range of domains, including Industry 4.0, IIoT, the Oil &amp; Gas industries, supply chains, and manufacturing systems in general.

Injection molding is a particularly prominent application area. In this field, Digital Twins support process automation, monitoring, data collection, and the prediction and control of part quality. They are proposed as a promising way to adapt to changing conditions in injection molding and to deliver predictive insights and optimized performance for the injection process. One study develops a Digital Twin architecture that simulates real communication between the physical and virtual systems of an injection process. This work builds on a body of research dedicated to smart injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426351</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data-Centric Digital Twin Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Data-Centric Digital Twin Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Novel digital twin architecture tailored for injection molding processes, serving as a foundation for process monitoring and control.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Edge-Cloud Computing Approach">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Edge-Cloud Computing Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Approach combining edge and cloud computing for data acquisition, simulation, and real-time predictive analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Melt Cushion Parameter">
  <data key="d0">Melt Cushion Parameter</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Crucial indicator of process stability in injection molding, forecast by the LSTM model.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection molding process parameter whose prediction indicates process stability; 6000 observations were collected.&lt;SEP&gt;A crucial parameter of the injection molding process. The proposed model monitors variations in it.&lt;SEP&gt;Also called decompression distance; distance between screw end and nozzle tip when the injection stroke ends, critical for process stability and machine mechanical integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Process parameter monitored with control charts; X-bar center at 6.61 cm3 and R chart center at 0.107 cm3, showing good production stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection molding process parameter that the paper monitors. The training data contains melt cushion values within a typical range, and the testing data includes anomalies encountered during production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Process Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Process Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoring of manufacturing processes in smart factories, the main problem addressed by the paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edge Computing">
  <data key="d0">Edge Computing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Computing at the edge of the IoT infrastructure, used for real-time predictive analysis during simulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical computing edge from which data is acquired for real-time predictions by the LSTM integrated into the Digital Twin.&lt;SEP&gt;Computing paradigm used to extract real-time machine data and forward it to the cloud, simulated with Raspberry Pi devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Computing paradigm used in [23] for CNN-based defect inspection.&lt;SEP&gt;Information technology integrated by Ecodid to develop the abilities of vehicles to exchange information with their environments.&lt;SEP&gt;An information technology that Ecodid integrates so vehicles can exchange information with their environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fusion of IoT and digital concepts gave rise to the Smart Industry paradigm">
  <data key="d0">Fusion of IoT and digital concepts gave rise to the Smart Industry paradigm</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In the dynamic landscape of Industry 4.0, the fusion of Internet of Things (IoT) technologies with advanced digital concepts has given rise to the Smart Industry paradigm [1].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twins offer a virtual mirror of physical systems for real-time monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twins offer a virtual mirror of physical systems for real-time monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">At the heart of this revolution lies the concept of Digital Twins, offering a virtual mirror of physical systems for real-time monitoring, analysis, and optimization [2].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twins in injection molding optimize parameters, quality, downtime and costs">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twins in injection molding optimize parameters, quality, downtime and costs</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">By leveraging real-time data analytics, manufacturers can optimize process parameters, enhance product quality, minimize downtime, and reduce costs [3].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integrating Digital Twins with IoT edge and cloud infrastructure is a significant challenge">
  <data key="d0">Integrating Digital Twins with IoT edge and cloud infrastructure is a significant challenge</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Furthermore, integrating Digital Twin solutions with the diverse IoT infrastructure, including edge computing and cloud management, presents a significant challenge [4].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection molding injects plastic into a mold cavity under high pressure">
  <data key="d0">Injection molding injects plastic into a mold cavity under high pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The Injection molding is an industrial technique, involves injecting plastic material into a mold cavity under high pressure, which can range from hundreds to thousands of bars [5].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injected plastic cools and solidifies taking the shape of the mold">
  <data key="d0">Injected plastic cools and solidifies taking the shape of the mold</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Once injected, the plastic cools and solidifies within the mold cavity, taking the shape of the mold and producing a specific plastic product [6].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Industry">
  <data key="d0">Smart Industry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Paradigm arising from the fusion of IoT technologies with advanced digital concepts within Industry 4.0. Digital Twins lie at its heart.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Factory">
  <data key="d0">Smart Factory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factory under the Factory 4.0 paradigm. The paper aims to improve process monitoring, operational efficiency and performance optimization in smart factories.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing paradigm whose growing significance motivates sensor data-based anomaly detection research.&lt;SEP&gt;Industry 4.0 manufacturing environment. Po and Kim [34] detect abnormal events there to improve operational efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426315</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Molding Machine">
  <data key="d0">Injection Molding Machine</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine comprising a hopper, a heating unit (barrel, screw, heating resistances), an injection unit, a clamping unit, and controls regulating temperature, pressure and other parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine that facilitates the injection molding process. Its injection system comprises a hopper, barrel, screw system and nozzle. Its clamping unit comprises a mold, a clamping mechanism and an ejector mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing machine whose melt cushion parameter is monitored for anomalies.&lt;SEP&gt;Type of production machine whose alternatives (two ARBURG and one HAITIAN) are evaluated in the paper.&lt;SEP&gt;Production machine whose optimal selection for product allocation is studied.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heating Unit">
  <data key="d0">Heating Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine component consisting of a barrel, screw, and heating resistances used to melt the raw plastic material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hopper">
  <data key="d0">Hopper</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine component used to feed the raw plastic material into the injection molding machine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Molding Production Cycle">
  <data key="d0">Injection Molding Production Cycle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard production cycle of injection molding comprising injection phase, packing phase, cooling phase, dosing and plasticizing phase, and ejection phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Standard injection molding production cycle with five main stages: dosing and plasticizing, filling, packing, cooling and ejection phases.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clamping unit holds mold halves together during injection and cooling">
  <data key="d0">Clamping unit holds mold halves together during injection and cooling</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Additionally, the machine features a clamping unit to securely hold the mold halves together during the injection and cooling phases [7]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clamping unit holds fixed and moved mold sides together under pressure">
  <data key="d0">Clamping unit holds fixed and moved mold sides together under pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The clamping Unit [8] is responsible for holding the fixed and the moved side of the mold together under pressure during the injection and cooling process."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection unit screw pushes molten material through heated barrel into mold under high pressure">
  <data key="d0">Injection unit screw pushes molten material through heated barrel into mold under high pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "In contrast, the Injection Unit involves a screw mechanism that pushes the molten material through a heated barrel and into the mold under high pressure [9]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Phase">
  <data key="d0">Injection Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase of the injection molding production cycle in which the injection unit injects molten plastic into the mold cavity while the clamping unit keeps the mold closed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Packing Phase">
  <data key="d0">Packing Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase of the injection molding production cycle listed among the main steps of the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase of the injection molding process during which the clamping force must keep the mold properly closed and held.&lt;SEP&gt;The phase in which the screw maintains pressure on the plastic to compensate for material shrinkage as the part starts to cool.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cooling Phase">
  <data key="d0">Cooling Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase of the injection molding production cycle during which the clamping unit holds the mold halves together under pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase of the injection molding process during which the part solidifies while the clamping force keeps the mold closed.&lt;SEP&gt;The phase that solidifies the part until the desired rigidity is reached, through thermal transfer applied by the mold.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dosing and Plasticizing Phase">
  <data key="d0">Dosing and Plasticizing Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase of the injection molding production cycle (written "Dozing&amp; plasticizing phase" in the text) listed among the main steps of the process.&lt;SEP&gt;The injection molding phase in which material falls from the hopper to the screw. The material is then melted by screw shearing and by heating resistances, and metered for one part cycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ejection Phase">
  <data key="d0">Ejection Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase of the injection molding production cycle listed among the main steps of the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase where, after the part attains sufficient rigidity, the mold opens and the part is ejected through a designated ejection mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;The phase in which the mold opens and the part is ejected once it has attained sufficient rigidity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Controls">
  <data key="d0">Machine Controls</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Controls of the injection molding machine that regulate temperature, pressure and other parameters to ensure the production of high-quality parts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydraulic System">
  <data key="d0">Hydraulic System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">System that the movable platen of the clamping unit is typically connected to.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screw Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Screw Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanism in the injection unit that pushes molten material through a heated barrel and into the mold under high pressure; the screw is also part of the heating unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mold">
  <data key="d0">Mold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tool with fixed and moved sides into whose cavity the molten material is injected; it is mounted on a fixed platen and held closed by the clamping unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sigmoid Activation Function">
  <data key="d0">Sigmoid Activation Function</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Activation function used in the LSTM forget gate to produce an output value between 0 and 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Activation function σ(x) = e^x/(e^x+1), used in the LSTM forget, input and output gates to produce values between 0 and 1 (equations 10, 11, 14, 16).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manufacturing Execution System">
  <data key="d0">Manufacturing Execution System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">System through which manufacturers monitor system performance with a Digital Twin.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twin Integrates IT With Operational Technology To Create New Value">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twin Integrates IT With Operational Technology To Create New Value</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Digital Twin plays a crucial role in the Fourth Industrial Revolution by integrating information technology with operational technology, thereby linking the preparatory production stage with real production to create new value [10].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twin Concept Model Comprises Three Main Components">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twin Concept Model Comprises Three Main Components</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The Digital Twin concept model comprises three main components [11] as indicated on figure 3: Physical products in real space, virtual products in virtual space, and the data and information connections between these physical and virtual spaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twin Model Comprises Five Essential Components">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twin Model Comprises Five Essential Components</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The Digital Twin model comprises five essential components: sensors and physical assets from the physical system, integration technology, data, analytics, and responsive actions [12].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twin Makes Operations Visible To Authorized Personnel">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twin Makes Operations Visible To Authorized Personnel</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">A Digital Twin makes the operations of individual machines and interconnected systems visible to authorized personnel in areas like manufacturing, procurement, and logistics [13].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM Enhances RNN Short-Term Memory With Cell States">
  <data key="d0">LSTM Enhances RNN Short-Term Memory With Cell States</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) is proposed to enhance the short-term memory capacity of recurrent neural networks (RNNs) by incorporating long-term memory states, commonly referred to as cell states [14].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="What-If Analysis">
  <data key="d0">What-If Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analytics technique used, along with predictive analysis, by a Digital Twin to simulate real-time conditions and predict future states, enabling manufacturers to visualize processes and compare options.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integration Technology">
  <data key="d0">Integration Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the five essential Digital Twin components; includes communication interfaces enabling real-time, bidirectional communication between physical and virtual systems via sensors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Information Technology And Operational Technology Integration">
  <data key="d0">Information Technology And Operational Technology Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Integration of information technology with operational technology through Digital Twin, linking the preparatory production stage with real production to create new value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twin Simulates Real-Time Conditions And Predicts Future States">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twin Simulates Real-Time Conditions And Predicts Future States</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Using analytics techniques such as what-if and predictive analysis, a Digital Twin simulates real-time conditions and predicts future states, enabling manufacturers to visualize processes, compare options, and collaborate across different sections.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liau et al. 2018 Digital Twin Framework for Injection Molding">
  <data key="d0">Liau et al. 2018 Digital Twin Framework for Injection Molding</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [16]. Y. Liau et al. (2018); introduces a framework for applying the Digital Twin concept to the injection molding process, from mold making to final production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wang et al. 2021 Digital Twin in Injection Molding Industry">
  <data key="d0">Wang et al. 2021 Digital Twin in Injection Molding Industry</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [17]. Zhiyong Wang et al. (2021); explores Digital Twin technology in the injection molding industry, describing an integrated industrial Internet architecture and a smart factory architecture verified through industrial applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference [15] LSTM Cell Structure">
