<node id="Tanh Activation Function">
  <data key="d0">Tanh Activation Function</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Activation function tanh(x) = (e^x − e^{-x})/(e^x + e^{-x}) used to generate the candidate memory state and hidden state in the LSTM.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperbolic tangent activation tanh(x) = (e^x − e^−x)/(e^x + e^−x), used to generate the candidate memory state g_t and the hidden state h_t in the LSTM cell (equations 12, 13, 17).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Industrial Internet Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Industrial Internet Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Integrated architecture involving intelligent equipment, production lines, and factories, described for the injection molding industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Factory Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Smart Factory Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factory architecture established using key technologies such as injection molding control systems and MES-based management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MES-Based Management">
  <data key="d0">MES-Based Management</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Manufacturing Execution System-based management, a key technology in the smart factory architecture for injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twin frameworks have been introduced for injection molding from mold making to final production">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twin frameworks have been introduced for injection molding from mold making to final production</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Numerous studies, including Y. Liau et al. (2018) [16], have introduced frameworks for applying the Digital Twin concept to the injection molding process, from mold making to final production."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Twin technology has been applied in the injection molding industry via smart factory architecture">
  <data key="d0">Digital Twin technology has been applied in the injection molding industry via smart factory architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Zhiyong Wang et al. (2021) [17] explored the Digital Twin technology in the injection molding industry." The architecture's feasibility was verified through industrial applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Memory Cell State">
  <data key="d0">Memory Cell State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The LSTM's updated memory cell state c_t, computed in equation (6) from the candidate memory state g_t and the forget state f_t. The text renders equation (6) incompletely as "g(t) + f(t)".</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidden State">
  <data key="d0">Hidden State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The LSTM's updated hidden state h_t, produced by the output gate from the updated memory cell state and the output state o_t as h_t = tanh(c_t) o_t (equation 8).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Candidate Memory State">
  <data key="d0">Candidate Memory State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A new memory state g_t, generated by feeding x_t and h_{t-1} into the tanh activation function: g_t = tanh(W_gx x_t + W_gh h_{t-1} + b_g).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weight Matrices and Bias Vectors">
  <data key="d0">Weight Matrices and Bias Vectors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The LSTM gate parameters: W denotes the weight matrices of the gates and b denotes the bias vectors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Molding Control Systems">
  <data key="d0">Injection Molding Control Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A key technology that Wang et al. (2021) focused on, alongside MES-based management, to establish a smart factory architecture for injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Real-Time Data">
  <data key="d0">Real-Time Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Live process data that the Digital Twin uses to support bidirectional interaction with the physical process and real-time adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
