  <data key="d2">Venue label appearing in the page header (CIST 171-7) of the article.&lt;SEP&gt;Venue named in the page header (CIST 174-7) of the article being read.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423736</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Melt Cushion">
  <data key="d0">Melt Cushion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection molding process parameter predicted by the LSTM model.&lt;SEP&gt;The material left at the screw's front during its forward position in injection molding. It serves as a buffer for proper material packing, transmits pressure into the cavity, and compensates for variations in material viscosity and mold temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;Process parameter whose time series variations are captured by the LSTM-AE model. Its anomaly threshold is set at the maximum residual error, which is below 0.04.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426315</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperparameter Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Hyperparameter Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tuning process across four LSTM configurations (Tune1-Tune4), reported in Table 1 and Fig. 7. All configurations used 2 LSTM layers, with 50 units per layer in Tune1-Tune3 and 100 units in Tune4. The optimizers were Adam (Tune1-Tune3) and SGD (Tune4). The activation functions were ReLU (Tune1, Tune3, Tune4) and tanh (Tune2). The batch sizes were 8 (Tune1), 1 (Tune2) and 32 (Tune3, Tune4). The epoch counts in the text and Table 1 disagree. The text says Tune2 used 50 epochs, while Table 1 lists 50 epochs for Tune3 and 100 for the others. Tune2 achieved the best results: training R2 0.7796, MSE 0.0051 and MAE 0.0496; test R2 0.7567, MSE 0.0040 and MAE 0.0482. Tune4 performed worst, with a test R2 of 0.0575.&lt;SEP&gt;Selecting the best parameters, such as number of trees, tree depth and features considered per split, to maximize Random Forest accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SGD">
  <data key="d0">SGD</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Stochastic Gradient Descent optimizer used in Tune4, which produced the poorest performance (test R2 0.0575).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ReLU">
  <data key="d0">ReLU</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Activation function used in Tune1, Tune3 and Tune4.&lt;SEP&gt;Activation function commonly used in CNNs to introduce non-linearity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tanh">
  <data key="d0">Tanh</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Activation function (written 'tangh') used in Tune2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="R2">
  <data key="d0">R2</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Coefficient of determination metric indicating goodness of fit; values ranged from approximately 0.0575 to 0.7796 across training and test sets.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mean Squared Error">
  <data key="d0">Mean Squared Error</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">MSE metric used to assess model performance; lower values indicate better performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mean Absolute Error">
  <data key="d0">Mean Absolute Error</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">MAE metric used to assess model performance; lower values indicate better performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Regression error metric (MAE). The text mentions it in the Accuracy item ("We can calculate the mean absolute error (MAE) using the (1)"), even though equation (1) defines accuracy, not MAE.&lt;SEP&gt;Error metric. The LSTM-AE model achieved a value of 0.0146 in training.&lt;SEP&gt;MAE, used as the reconstruction loss function of the LSTM-AE model.&lt;SEP&gt;MAE metric, used both as the reconstruction loss and as a performance metric; the best model achieved 0.0206 on training and 0.0146 on validation.&lt;SEP&gt;MAE metric used to quantify reconstruction error. A test sequence is flagged as an anomaly if its MAE exceeds the threshold of 0.04.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
