<node id="Final Loop Of The Digital Twin">
  <data key="d0">Final Loop Of The Digital Twin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The final loop of the Digital Twin involves executing actions on the physical systems directly from the Digital Twin. The paper does not address it and identifies it as a prospective avenue for further research.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Real-Time Prediction">
  <data key="d0">Real-Time Prediction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Real-time predictions of process parameters based on data acquired from the physical computing edge. They are enabled by integrating the trained LSTM into the Digital Twin, and simulations demonstrate real-time communication between predictive values and physical systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Physical-Virtual Communication">
  <data key="d0">Physical-Virtual Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Real communication between the physical and virtual systems, simulated by the Digital Twin architecture. Communication is listed as a component of the framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
