<node id="SHION">
  <data key="d0">SHION</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Smart tHermoplastic InjectiON: an interactive digital twin supporting real-time shopfloor operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model-Driven Development">
  <data key="d0">Model-Driven Development</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Software engineering approach used to develop a digital twin for injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligent Manufacturing">
  <data key="d0">Intelligent Manufacturing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Manufacturing paradigm that uses advanced digital technologies. The 2021 Complexity study examines it for the injection molding industry, using a digital twin-based industrial internet.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Industrial Internet">
  <data key="d0">Industrial Internet</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Networked industrial infrastructure. The 2021 Complexity study investigates it for intelligent manufacturing in the injection molding industry, based on digital twin technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Injection Molding">
  <data key="d0">Smart Injection Molding</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection molding enhanced with smart, data-driven technologies such as digital twin modeling. It is the subject of the 2024 paper by Nasiri et al.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Real-Time Shopfloor Operations">
  <data key="d0">Real-Time Shopfloor Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Live production-floor operations in manufacturing. The SHION interactive digital twin is designed to support them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermoplastic Injection">
  <data key="d0">Thermoplastic Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection molding of thermoplastic materials. It is the target process of the SHION (Smart tHermoplastic InjectiON) digital twin.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423714</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adele Cutler">
  <data key="d0">Adele Cutler</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-developer of Random Forest, cited as [15].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leo Breiman">
  <data key="d0">Leo Breiman</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-developer of Random Forest, cited as [15].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Random Forest was developed by Adele Cutler and Leo Breiman">
  <data key="d0">Random Forest was developed by Adele Cutler and Leo Breiman</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Random Forest, developed by Adele Cutler and Leo Breiman [15], employs a unique splitting strategy for model construction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Random Forest trees grow to maximum depth on feature subsets">
  <data key="d0">Random Forest trees grow to maximum depth on feature subsets</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">These trees grow to their maximum depth based on a specific subset of features [16].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Random Forest performance improves as the number of trees increases">
  <data key="d0">Random Forest performance improves as the number of trees increases</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">While the accuracy of individual decision trees might be lower compared to a single tree trained on the full dataset [2], the overall performance of Random Forests improves as the number of trees increases, leveraging their combined strengths for enhanced model reliability and predictive performance [2].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bayesian optimization efficiently explores hyperparameter space by learning from previous iterations">
  <data key="d0">Bayesian optimization efficiently explores hyperparameter space by learning from previous iterations</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian optimization employed to efficiently explore the hyperparameters space and find the best configuration, progressively refining its strategy by learning from the outcomes of previous iterations [17].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A variety of metrics can evaluate classification models">
  <data key="d0">A variety of metrics can evaluate classification models</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">To evaluate the effectiveness of classification models, a variety of metrics can be applied [18].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Marketing Response Prediction">
  <data key="d0">Marketing Response Prediction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Classification objective of the Marketing Campaign Dataset: predicting whether a customer accepts an offer, based on the target column 'Response'.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Missing Value Imputation">
  <data key="d0">Missing Value Imputation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Preprocessing step that replaces missing categorical values with the mode and missing numerical values with the mean.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Individual decision trees may be less accurate than a single tree trained on the full dataset">
  <data key="d0">Individual decision trees may be less accurate than a single tree trained on the full dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">While the accuracy of individual decision trees might be lower compared to a single tree trained on the full dataset [2], the overall performance of Random Forests improves as the number of trees increases...</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="F1 Score">
  <data key="d0">F1 Score</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Evaluation metric obtained from the confusion matrix, listed alongside accuracy, precision, and recall.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation metric defined as the harmonic mean of precision and recall (Eq. 4), providing a single metric that balances both.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation metric used to assess the classification models.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation metric used in the study. Random Forest reached an F1 score of 95%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="True Positives">
  <data key="d0">True Positives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Correctly predicted positive instances; a component of the confusion matrix used in accuracy, precision, and recall.&lt;SEP&gt;Confusion matrix outcome (TP): cases where the model correctly identifies that a quality defect exists.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="True Negatives">
  <data key="d0">True Negatives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Correctly predicted negative instances (TN); a component of the confusion matrix used in accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Confusion matrix outcome (TN): cases where the model correctly identifies that no quality defect is present.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="False Negatives">
  <data key="d0">False Negatives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Positive instances incorrectly predicted as negative (FN); a component of the confusion matrix used in accuracy.&lt;SEP&gt;Confusion matrix outcome (FN): cases where the model misses a quality defect that is genuinely present.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Classification Model Evaluation">
  <data key="d0">Classification Model Evaluation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Assessment of a classification model's effectiveness; the confusion matrix gives a comprehensive overview of it, and accuracy, precision, recall, and F1 score are derived from the matrix to quantify it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noise">
  <data key="d0">Noise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Irrelevant information introduced by irrelevant features. Removing those features through feature selection can reduce noise and improve model performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature Selection Generally Improves Random Forest Performance">
  <data key="d0">Feature Selection Generally Improves Random Forest Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "These results demonstrate that feature selection generally enhances the performance of the Random Forest classifiers, particularly in terms of precision and F1-score. However, the impact of feature selection can vary depending on the dataset."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature Selection Benefits Are Negligible When All Features Are Relevant">
  <data key="d0">Feature Selection Benefits Are Negligible When All Features Are Relevant</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "Conversely, when all features are relevant, the benefits of feature selection may be negligible." Dataset 3 illustrates this finding, since its results were identical with and without feature selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature selection generally improves classification performance">
  <data key="d0">Feature selection generally improves classification performance</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "Our findings indicate that feature selection generally improves the performance of classification models, especially in terms of precision and F1-score."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Benefits of feature selection depend on dataset characteristics">
  <data key="d0">Benefits of feature selection depend on dataset characteristics</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "for Dataset 3, where all features were deemed relevant, the impact of feature selection was minimal, suggesting that the benefits of feature selection are contingent on the dataset's characteristics."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature selection simplifies models and improves interpretability and efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Feature selection simplifies models and improves interpretability and efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text that feature selection identifies relevant features, "simplifying models, and making them more interpretable and computationally efficient."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automated Machine Learning (AutoML)">
  <data key="d0">Automated Machine Learning (AutoML)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Frameworks proposed for future work that would integrate feature selection and hyperparameter tuning to streamline model development.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791423726</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
