<node id="Machine Learning-Assisted Decision Support in Industrial Manufacturing: A Case Study on Injection Molding Machine Selection">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning-Assisted Decision Support in Industrial Manufacturing: A Case Study on Injection Molding Machine Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, published in IAES International Journal of Artificial Intelligence (IJ-AI) Vol. 14, No. 1, February 2025, pp. 270-285. It explores machine learning methods for injection molding machine selection based on product, material, and mold criteria, testing six supervised learning techniques on a dataset of 70 plastic parts and five machines; random forest achieved the best accuracy of 93%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="10.11591/ijai.v14.i1.pp270-285">
  <data key="d0">10.11591/ijai.v14.i1.pp270-285</data>
  <data key="d1">identifier</data>
  <data key="d2">DOI of the paper on machine learning-assisted injection molding machine selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soulaimane Idiri">
  <data key="d0">Soulaimane Idiri</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-author of the injection molding machine selection study.&lt;SEP&gt;Obtained an engineering degree in Electrical Engineering and Industrial Management in 2021. He is a Ph.D. candidate at the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory, and his research focuses on AI for predictive maintenance of vehicles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Learning Curve">
  <data key="d0">Learning Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Keyword of the injection molding machine selection study, related to model evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Analysis used to check how effectively each model learned from the training dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagnostic used in the study. Its trends supported the conclusion that a larger dataset is needed to improve the SGD, LR, and NB models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Molding Machine Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Injection Molding Machine Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Dataset comprising 70 plastic parts and five machines used to test six supervised learning techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-world dataset from an automotive industry workshop comprising 70 distinct molds or parts across five machines. It was oversampled to 100 records and split 85% for training and 15% for testing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine selection in injection molding requires extensive knowledge and experience">
  <data key="d0">Machine selection in injection molding requires extensive knowledge and experience</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Selecting the appropriate machine for a new product remains a challenging task in the injection molding industry, requiring extensive knowledge and experience [1]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Classification Algorithms">
  <data key="d0">Classification Algorithms</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Algorithms that predict machine selection. The study suggests that injection molding businesses should consider their significance for the manufacturing process.&lt;SEP&gt;Algorithms that handle multi-criteria problems by learning from diverse sets of input features and making predictions or classifications based on learned patterns. In the paper, they are applied to predict the clamping force machine from machine, material, mold and part parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conventional Machine Selection Approach">
  <data key="d0">Conventional Machine Selection Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Conventional machine selection process segmented into three phases: force calculation, clamping unit validation, and injection unit validation, illustrated as a flowchart.&lt;SEP&gt;Traditional approach to injection molding machine selection. It involves theoretical clamping force calculations, mechanical validations of the mold and real trials for new parts. It is time-consuming, costly and requires a high level of expertise.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mold Mechanical Validation">
  <data key="d0">Mold Mechanical Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanical validation of the mold, performed as part of the conventional approach to injection molding machine selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Real Trials for New Parts">
  <data key="d0">Real Trials for New Parts</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Real production trials carried out for new parts as part of the conventional approach to injection molding machine selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small and Medium-Sized Industries">
  <data key="d0">Small and Medium-Sized Industries</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Industries where machine selection decisions become more complex, especially when a diverse range of products must be managed with a limited number of available machines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Selection Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Machine Selection Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factors that influence injection molding machine selection: product characteristics (weight, geometric specifications, material type), mold specifications (weight, dimensions) and the production rate requested by the customer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine learning can guide prediction of injection molding machine selection">
  <data key="d0">Machine learning can guide prediction of injection molding machine selection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding of the study: "The results indicate that ML can provide guidance for predicting machine selection, with a preference for the random forest (RF), decision tree (DT), and support vector machine (SVM) models."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wrong machine selection increases product cost">
  <data key="d0">Wrong machine selection increases product cost</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "Discrepancies in the cost centers of machines mean that selecting the wrong machine can automatically increase the product's cost."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Learning-Assisted Decision Support in Industrial Machine Selection">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning-Assisted Decision Support in Industrial Machine Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read. Its running header shows a truncated title beginning "Machine learning-assisted decision support in industrial ..." and credits Faouzi Tayalati. It was published in Int J Artif Intell, Vol. 14, No. 1, February 2025, pp. 270-285. The article applies six machine learning classification methods (SVM, RF, DT, NB, SGD, LR) to select the suitable injection-molding machine for each product. It presents these methods as an alternative to subjective multi-criteria methods such as AHP and TOPSIS. According to the article, the RF, DT and SVM models predict the correct machine with accuracies of approximately 93% and 87%, even with limited training data.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read. Its running header gives the title only in truncated form, "Machine learning-assisted decision support in industrial ...". It is authored by Faouzi Tayalati and published in Int J Artif Intell, Vol. 14, No. 1, February 2025, pages 270-285. The article proposes machine learning methods to select injection molding machines for new products. It uses a real-world automotive-sector dataset of 70 parts across five machines. Random Forest performed best (93% accuracy, 95% F1 score), followed by Decision Tree and Support Vector Machine. The study's stated limitations are data size, the lack of hyperparameter optimization, and testing on only two new parts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425038</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine selection is a multi-criteria problem">
  <data key="d0">Machine selection is a multi-criteria problem</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">According to the literature, machine selection is categorized as a multi-criteria problem [3].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
