<node id="Injection Molding Process">
  <data key="d0">Injection Molding Process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Injection Molding Process is one of the most widely used manufacturing processes in the plastics industry. Plastic material is injected under high pressure into a mold cavity, where it cools and solidifies to form high-precision plastic parts. The process is carried out by an injection molding machine. Despite its prevalence, the industry faces rising production costs and increasingly demanding quality standards.

The process is described as a sequence of distinct phases, each governed by specific parameters. Descriptions name these phases slightly differently, but they are consistent. The cycle begins with dosing and plasticizing, where the material is prepared and melted. Next comes filling, also referred to as injection, in which the molten plastic is forced into the mold. Packing follows, then cooling, and finally ejection of the finished part.

Because so many parameters influence product quality, the Injection Molding Process is a significant subject of research. Studies cited in references 1–3 examine how artificial intelligence and machine learning can be used to set and monitor process parameters. The process is also the application domain of an article proposing an anomaly detection approach. That approach combines Statistical Process Control (SPC) with a Long Short-Term Memory Autoencoder (LSTM-AE) to identify process anomalies. In addition, injection molding is a manufacturing field where Multi-Criteria Decision-Making (MCDM) methods are applied across various dimensions of process planning and evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
