</node>
<node id="Part Characteristics">
  <data key="d0">Part Characteristics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Part dimensions, weight, and thickness, described as the most significant machine selection parameters. Part dimensions affect the required opening stroke, and part thickness affects the required injection pressure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Material Characteristics">
  <data key="d0">Material Characteristics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Material types with diverse chemical compositions, ranging from simple to highly technical and aggressive materials. These significantly impact the selection of the injection unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Screw And Barrel">
  <data key="d0">Screw And Barrel</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection unit components whose specifications and treatment must withstand the chemical aggressiveness of the processed material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Learning-Assisted Decision Support in Industrial Manufacturing">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning-Assisted Decision Support in Industrial Manufacturing</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Article by Faouzi Tayalati published in the International Journal of Artificial Intelligence (ISSN 2252-8938); addresses machine selection and allocation for injection molding using machine learning, with a five-step methodology and LIME-based interpretability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nyanga et al. [14]">
  <data key="d0">Nyanga et al. [14]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [14]; explored a multi-agent system with AHP-based criteria (clamping force, tie bar distances, shot weight, time, cost) to select the most suitable injection molding machine, reducing short shots by 10%, sink marks by 5%, and flashing by 30%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trivedi et al. [15]">
  <data key="d0">Trivedi et al. [15]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [15]; applied multi-criteria decision-making using an optimized fuzzy TOPSIS method to 14 electrical molding machines with eight criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lin and Yang [5]">
  <data key="d0">Lin and Yang [5]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [5]; developed an AHP-based model, prototype framework and software integrating the expert-system concept for machine selection to improve cost-effectiveness and workshop flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425062</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dominguez et al. [16]">
  <data key="d0">Dominguez et al. [16]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [16]; recent study comparing CODAS, TOPSIS and AHP for choosing among five machines in the pastry industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425062</data>
