</node>
<node id="Multi-agent system reduced molding defects">
  <data key="d0">Multi-agent system reduced molding defects</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The study demonstrated that the system effectively reduced short shot defects by 10%, sink marks by 5%, and flashing by 30%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP and CODAS provide approximate machine selections">
  <data key="d0">AHP and CODAS provide approximate machine selections</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Results indicated that AHP and CODAS provided approximate machine selections, with potential refinement through complementary studies using variance analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Few studies tackle machine selection with AI">
  <data key="d0">Few studies tackle machine selection with AI</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">While numerous studies have delved into machine selection allocation, only a limited few have tackled the issue using artificial intelligence methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pastry Industry">
  <data key="d0">Pastry Industry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Industrial domain in which Dominguez et al. investigated CODAS, TOPSIS and AHP for choosing among five machines using price, capacity, warranty, product weight and speed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variance Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Variance Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis suggested as a complementary study to refine the approximate machine selections given by AHP and CODAS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Comparison">
  <data key="d0">Performance Comparison</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fourth step of the proposed ML methodology. It compares the different ML methods to select the optimal approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Final stage of the study's pipeline, which compares model performance using accuracy, precision, F1-score and recall.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy TOPSIS makes machine selection more autonomous">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy TOPSIS makes machine selection more autonomous</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">By incorporating fuzzy logic, the fuzzy TOPSIS method provided results oriented toward selected membership functions, thereby making the machine selection process more autonomous.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP-based expert system optimizes machine selection cost-effectiveness and flexibility">
  <data key="d0">AHP-based expert system optimizes machine selection cost-effectiveness and flexibility</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Their primary goal was to optimize machine selection, enhancing both cost-effectiveness and workshop flexibility with existing parts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multicriteria methods are effective for pastry industry machine selection">
  <data key="d0">Multicriteria methods are effective for pastry industry machine selection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This study highlighted the effectiveness of these multicriteria selection methods in choosing machines for the pastry industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local Interpretable Model-Agnostic Explanations (LIME)">
  <data key="d0">Local Interpretable Model-Agnostic Explanations (LIME)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Explanation method used in a final verification step to assess the influence of individual features on the models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automotive Injection Molding Workshop Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Automotive Injection Molding Workshop Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Dataset collected from a real workshop in the automotive industry located in northern Morocco. It contains 70 unique molds of varying sizes and weights, five machine types with clamping capacities from 150 to 400 tons, and 10 plastic material types. The data is grouped into part_data, material_data, mold_data and machine_data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correlation">
  <data key="d0">Correlation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A measure of the relationship between variables. Changes in the magnitude of one variable are linked to changes in another, either in the same direction (positive) or the opposite direction (negative).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Allocation">
  <data key="d0">Machine Allocation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Selecting the injection machine size for a part. The selection is strongly influenced by mold dimensions and characteristics: small molds go to smaller machines and large molds to larger ones.&lt;SEP&gt;Prediction task of allocating samples to machines; sample N°4 belongs to machine number 3.&lt;SEP&gt;The problem of selecting optimal injection machines (e.g., 250 t, 320 t) for producing new plastic parts, supported by ML predictions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Correlation quantifies relationships between variables in the same or opposite direction">
  <data key="d0">Correlation quantifies relationships between variables in the same or opposite direction</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "In correlated data, alterations in the magnitude of one variable are linked to changes in the magnitude of another variable, either in the same direction (positive correlation) or in the opposite direction (negative correlation) [19]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clamping force is strongly correlated with mold dimensions">
  <data key="d0">Clamping force is strongly correlated with mold dimensions</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding in the text: "The correlation matrix confirms a significant relation between clamping force and features related to mold dimensions, with strong positive coefficients classified as follows: mold weight (0.788), mold height (0.737), mold length (0.741), and mold width (0.761)."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425063</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
