<node id="Oversampling">
  <data key="d0">Oversampling</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Technique used to equilibrate the imbalanced dataset by generating additional records for minority machine classes so each machine has 20 records.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique used to increase the dataset from 70 molds to 100 records.&lt;SEP&gt;Traditional data balancing technique outperformed by GAN-generated synthetic data in financial market supervision.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SGD Classifier">
  <data key="d0">SGD Classifier</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Stochastic gradient descent classifier; one of six classification algorithms applied.&lt;SEP&gt;Stochastic gradient descent classifier and the worst-performing model. Table 3 reports 27% accuracy, 12% precision, 40% recall and 18% F1-score. The text notes precision below 44% and a lower capability to predict relevant instances.</data>
