<node id="Machine Learning-Assisted Decision Support in Industrial ...">
  <data key="d0">Machine Learning-Assisted Decision Support in Industrial ...</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read. It was published in the Int J Artif Intell (ISSN 2252-8938), and its running header lists Faouzi Tayalati as author. The title is truncated in the text. The paper deals with machine learning-assisted decision support in an industrial setting, and its reference list includes works on classifiers, learning curves, overfitting and explainable AI.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Using the Confusion Matrix for Improving Ensemble Classifiers">
  <data key="d0">Using the Confusion Matrix for Improving Ensemble Classifiers</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [27]. Written by N. D. Marom, L. Rokach and A. Shmilovici and published at the 2010 IEEE 26th Convention of Electrical and Electronics Engineers in Israel (Nov. 2010, pp. 555–559). The paper uses the confusion matrix to improve ensemble classifiers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Learning Curve Models and Applications: Literature Review and Research Directions">
  <data key="d0">Learning Curve Models and Applications: Literature Review and Research Directions</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [28]. Written by M. J. Anzanello and F. S. Fogliatto and published in the International Journal of Industrial Ergonomics, vol. 41, no. 5, Sep. 2011. The paper reviews learning curve models and their applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="An Overview of Overfitting and Its Solutions">
  <data key="d0">An Overview of Overfitting and Its Solutions</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [29]. Written by X. Ying and published in the Journal of Physics: Conference Series, vol. 1168, Feb. 2019. The paper gives an overview of overfitting and ways to address it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Learning Curves: A Novel Approach for Robustness Improvement of Load Forecasting">
  <data key="d0">Learning Curves: A Novel Approach for Robustness Improvement of Load Forecasting</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [30]. Written by C. Giola, P. Danti and S. Magnani and presented at the 7th International Conference on Time Series and Forecasting (MDPI, Basel, Jul. 2021). The paper proposes using learning curves to make load forecasting more robust.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Explainable AI Methods - A Brief Overview">
  <data key="d0">Explainable AI Methods - A Brief Overview</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [31]. Written by A. Holzinger, A. Saranti, C. Molnar, P. Biecek and W. Samek and published in xxAI-Beyond Explainable AI, 2022, pp. 13–38. The paper gives a brief overview of explainable AI methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Evaluation of Classifiers for a Vision-Based Automated Mold Protection System Using Modified LBP Features">
  <data key="d0">Evaluation of Classifiers for a Vision-Based Automated Mold Protection System Using Modified LBP Features</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [32]. Written by M. R. Asadi-Gandomania, S. S. Hashemib and M. T. Sadeghi and published in the International Journal of Robotics, Theory and Applications, vol. 8, no. 1, 2022. The paper evaluates classifiers for a vision-based mold protection system that uses modified LBP features.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="The Random Forest Model Has the Best Accuracy Among the Four Pressure Ulcer Prediction Models Using Machine Learning Algorithms">
  <data key="d0">The Random Forest Model Has the Best Accuracy Among the Four Pressure Ulcer Prediction Models Using Machine Learning Algorithms</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [33]. Written by J. Song et al. and published in Risk Management and Healthcare Policy, vol. 14, Mar. 2021. The paper reports that random forest gives the best accuracy among four machine learning models for predicting pressure ulcers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">document.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425073</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
