<node id="Configuration Driven Performance Analysis of Hyperledger Fabric: An Empirical Study">
  <data key="d0">Configuration Driven Performance Analysis of Hyperledger Fabric: An Empirical Study</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read; an empirical evaluation of Hyperledger Fabric performance focusing on endorsement policies, block size, batch timeout, and peer scalability, accepted for publication in IEEE Access. It finds the OR endorsement policy outperforms AND, a block size of 100 transactions with 50-100 ms timeout gives the best trade-off, and performance remains stable up to 2-4 peers per organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [36]. By N. Lechhab Ouadrassi, M. S. Boukhryss, A. Azmani and K. Jebari Hassani, published in IEEE Access, vol. 14, pp. 48145–48156, 2026. An empirical, configuration-driven performance analysis of Hyperledger Fabric.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference [36], published in IEEE Access, vol. 14, pp. 48145–48156, 2026. It is an empirical study of how configuration affects Hyperledger Fabric performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nihad Lechhab Ouadrassi">
  <data key="d0">Nihad Lechhab Ouadrassi</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Nihad Lechhab Ouadrassi is a researcher and Ph.D. candidate in Computer Science at Abdelmalek Essaâdi University (also written Abdelmalek Essaadi University) in Morocco, specializing in artificial intelligence and blockchain technologies. Ouadrassi received a Master's degree (M.S.) in Computer and Mobile Systems from the Faculty of Sciences and Technologies of Tangier (FST Tangier) in 2024. Ouadrassi's research interests include blockchain-based security, artificial intelligence for digital ecosystems, predictive analytics, and intelligent information systems.

Ouadrassi is affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory (IABL) at Abdelmalek Essaâdi University. Some sources render the laboratory's name as the Intelligence Automation BioMed Genomics Laboratory, but these appear to refer to the same IABL unit.

Ouadrassi has authored several scholarly works. Ouadrassi served as corresponding author of a paper on the configuration-driven performance analysis of Hyperledger Fabric, and as first and corresponding author of another paper. Ouadrassi is also the author of a poster on a blockchain-based vehicle management system and has co-authored additional articles and papers with colleagues at IABL. Together, these works reflect a sustained focus on applying blockchain and AI technologies to practical systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26549e3ff493405b55b221c1d804516e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;poster_nihad.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502188</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mohammed Said Boukhryss">
  <data key="d0">Mohammed Said Boukhryss</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-author of the paper on configuration-driven performance analysis of Hyperledger Fabric.&lt;SEP&gt;Received a Master's in AI and Data Science in 2024 from FST Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University; Ph.D. candidate in AI and Data Science; interests include machine learning, predictive analytics and intelligent systems for digital transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;First and corresponding author of the article. Affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory (IABL), Abdelmalek Essaâdi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of the article being read and of its reproducibility package. He received a Master's degree in artificial intelligence and data science in 2024 from the Faculty of Sciences and Techniques of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University. He is pursuing a Ph.D. in artificial intelligence and data science focused on the IT sector. His research interests include machine learning, predictive analytics and intelligent systems for digital transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;First author of the paper, affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the paper, affiliated with Abdelmalek Essaadi University.&lt;SEP&gt;Received an M.S. in AI and Data Science in 2024 from the Faculty of Sciences and Techniques of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaadi University. Currently a Ph.D. candidate in AI and Data Science. Research interests include machine learning, predictive analytics and intelligent systems for digital transformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502182</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Khalid Jebari Hassani">
  <data key="d0">Khalid Jebari Hassani</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Khalid Jebari Hassani is a Moroccan computer scientist and academic researcher affiliated with Abdelmalek Essaâdi University, specifically with the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory (IABL). His academic training was completed at the Faculty of Sciences, Mohammed V University, in Rabat, Morocco. There he earned a B.S. degree in computer science in 1992, an M.S. degree in computer science, multimedia, and telecommunications in 2008, and a Ph.D. in 2013.

His research interests include metaheuristics, machine learning, dynamic optimization, multi-objective optimization, granular computing, and e-learning. These areas reflect a focus on intelligent computational methods and their application to complex problem-solving and educational technologies.

Khalid Jebari Hassani has co-authored several scholarly works in blockchain technology. These include a paper on the configuration-driven performance analysis of Hyperledger Fabric and a poster presenting a blockchain-based vehicle management system. In these and other co-authored papers and articles, he is listed with his affiliation at IABL, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26549e3ff493405b55b221c1d804516e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-042</data>
