<node id="Batch Timeout">
  <data key="d0">Batch Timeout</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The TIMEOUT parameter: maximum time allowed for batch processing, set to 50 ms, 100 ms and 200 ms.&lt;SEP&gt;Fabric block timeout parameter; 50-100 ms gave the best trade-off with block size 100.&lt;SEP&gt;Block-cutting timeout parameter tuned in the experiments (50, 100, 200 ms).&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperledger Fabric timeout configuration parameter affecting throughput; evaluated in This Paper.&lt;SEP&gt;Time limit for batching transactions into a block (50, 100, 200 ms), which jointly with block size drives latency and throughput.&lt;SEP&gt;Timeout parameter T evaluated with values of 50 ms, 100 ms and 200 ms. The figures compare how each value affects throughput and P95 latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Batching mechanism parameter; a timeout of 50–100 ms maintains responsive block formation and avoids long queuing delays.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-017</data>
