</node>
<node id="Performance Degradation">
  <data key="d0">Performance Degradation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The phenomenon measured in the chart. Degradation in latency and throughput grows with larger configurations and exceeds 200% at the highest settings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425172</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Degradation Percentage Values">
  <data key="d0">Degradation Percentage Values</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The degradation percentages shown in the chart: 54.0%, 43.3%, 44.9%, 37.6%, 53.5%, 49.6%, 66.4%, 61.8%, 109.6%, 144.4%, 123.8%, 103.2%, 150.2%, 131.1%, 216.0% and 219.5%. Values rise sharply at the larger configurations, and the highest values exceed 200%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425172</data>
