<node id="Tail Latency">
  <data key="d0">Tail Latency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">High-percentile transaction latency. It rises when peers are added beyond roughly 2–4 per organization. In geographically distributed deployments, network delay and gossip behavior can dominate it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425172</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuration Guidelines">
  <data key="d0">Configuration Guidelines</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Guidelines derived from the study's findings. They help practitioners choose performance-oriented Hyperledger Fabric settings while staying consistent with application endorsement requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425172</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Workload Profiles">
  <data key="d0">Workload Profiles</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proposed future extension covering read-heavy mixes, higher-contention key-access patterns, larger payloads, and smart contracts with heavier computation and state access.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425172</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heterogeneous Topologies">
  <data key="d0">Heterogeneous Topologies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proposed future scalability assessment covering larger numbers of organizations, multi-channel deployments, private data collections and geographically distributed peers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425172</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud And Hybrid Deployment">
  <data key="d0">Cloud And Hybrid Deployment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proposed future evaluation environment. It would measure variability from shared infrastructure, autoscaling behavior and resource contention, which often determine production performance more than nominal parameter choices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
