<node id="Endorsement Policies">
  <data key="d0">Endorsement Policies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Policies in Hyperledger Fabric that govern the endorsement of transactions. They are covered by the documentation [12], the endorsement performance analysis [19] and the endorsement-process framework [10].&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperledger Fabric feature governing endorsement collection; signatures are embedded in endorsement payloads, increasing post-quantum migration complexity.&lt;SEP&gt;Fabric configuration that specifies which peers must endorse transactions. It is a key characteristic of Fabric and affects performance, and existing post-quantum evaluations often describe it only in limited detail.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-004</data>
