<node id="Event Tree Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Event Tree Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Tree Analysis (ETA) is a probabilistic risk analysis technique that models the possible outcomes of a critical initiating event and the mitigation measures that follow it, using a tree-structured diagram. The method traces sequences of events leading to success or failure. It begins with an initiating event, which branches through a series of intermediate events representing the success or failure of each mitigation mechanism. ETA is typically built in four steps: identifying the initiating event, defining the intermediate events, determining the consequences, and quantifying probabilities. The probability of each outcome is obtained by multiplying the branch probabilities along its path.

ETA is widely used to evaluate the effectiveness of different maintenance strategies, to quantify the effects of preventive and corrective interventions on overall system stability, and to provide actionable insights for minimizing failure risks. In one application to a CPU critical state scenario, the tree branches through three mitigation mechanisms: the cooling system, load balancing, and administrator intervention. The success rate in this scenario is 60.22% when all mechanisms work and 0.295% when all of them fail.

ETA has also been applied to Vehicular Ad Hoc Networks (VANETs) to address low Quality of Service (QoS) caused by blocking or reducing elements. In this context, the outputs of a fuzzy-Bayesian (FB) model serve as inputs to the ETA, which then predicts connection loss and assesses the importance and impact of the system's security mechanisms.

Beyond engineering and network systems, ETA has been used as a risk analysis method for marine accidents in Bangladesh, as reported in reference [36].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
