<node id="Reproducibility Package [39]">
  <data key="d0">Reproducibility Package [39]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Publicly available reproducibility package cited as [39]. It contains the complete CPT files, raw probability inputs, the calibration script (calibration.py) and the calibration report.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three-axiom validation method is widely recognized for BN validation">
  <data key="d0">Three-axiom validation method is widely recognized for BN validation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">To ensure the reliability of the BN model, the three-axiom validation method was employed, widely recognized in the literature [40], [41], [42], [43].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three-Axiom Validation Method">
  <data key="d0">Three-Axiom Validation Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation method for Bayesian Networks. Axiom 1 requires that any change in a parent node's probability leads to a corresponding change in the child node's probability. It is verified on nodes such as Pages swapped out, Pages swapped in and Swap memory used.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brier Score">
  <data key="d0">Brier Score</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Calibration metric. For CPU State it yielded 0.0051 (Normal), 0.0266 (Degraded) and 0.0244 (Critical), averaging 0.0187, below the 0.05 threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Calibration metric; reported for CPU State as an internal calibration check on elicited probabilities, but not computable robustly at system level from real data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Elicitation Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Expert Elicitation Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Procedure in which a panel of three experts (a PhD in computer science/AI, a full professor, and a senior engineer) independently judged the rules. Final labels were set by majority vote or discussion, and each rule received a confidence rating of High, Medium or Low.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monte Carlo Uncertainty Quantification">
  <data key="d0">Monte Carlo Uncertainty Quantification</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Robustness analysis using a Dirichlet perturbation. The concentration parameter alpha is set according to the level of expert consensus.&lt;SEP&gt;Procedure that perturbs CPT rows via Dirichlet sampling centered on baseline probabilities, runs exact inference for each replicate, and records posteriors P(System_State) per scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;Procedure assessing robustness of CPT parameters by generating replicates via Dirichlet perturbation of baseline CPTs, performing exact Bayesian inference, and computing 95% credible intervals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dirichlet Perturbation">
  <data key="d0">Dirichlet Perturbation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Perturbation of CPT rows. Lower expert consensus gives a smaller alpha (wider epistemic uncertainty); unanimous agreement gives a larger alpha.&lt;SEP&gt;Stochastic procedure used in the Monte Carlo robustness analysis, with the random seed fixed to 42 to support reproducibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Probabilistic Calibration">
  <data key="d0">Probabilistic Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The degree to which predicted probabilities align with observed frequencies. It is assessed via Brier scores.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Epistemic Uncertainty">
  <data key="d0">Epistemic Uncertainty</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Uncertainty arising from limited expert consensus. It is reflected by the Dirichlet concentration parameter.&lt;SEP&gt;Uncertainty in the CPT parameters, quantified to provide statistical reporting suited to the scenario-driven setting.&lt;SEP&gt;Uncertainty in CPT parameters that is quantified to provide statistical reporting given rare critical events in industrial telemetry.&lt;SEP&gt;Uncertainty and potential bias introduced by expert-elicited probabilities, managed through structured elicitation, periodic recalibration and robustness checks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Row-Sum Check">
  <data key="d0">Row-Sum Check</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Probabilistic consistency verification that confirms every CPT row sums to unity (sum of Pi = 1, Eq. 11).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weighted Centroid">
  <data key="d0">Weighted Centroid</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Defuzzification output computed in FisPro. Its value of 0.784 lies close to the Critical label center (c=0.8) and serves only as a visual diagnostic, playing no role in CPT generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Majority Vote">
  <data key="d0">Majority Vote</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Rule used to set the final label of each fuzzy rule from three independent expert judgements. A short discussion was used when no majority emerged.&lt;SEP&gt;Aggregation of three experts' qualitative judgements (Normal/Degraded/Critical) per rule, with consensus discussion when required.&lt;SEP&gt;Aggregation rule that derives the final expert-elicitation decision, with consensus discussion when required.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Confidence Rating">
  <data key="d0">Expert Confidence Rating</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Three-level scale (High, Medium, Low). Unanimous rules received high confidence, majority-vote rules medium, and discussion-resolved rules low. The ratings informed the Dirichlet concentration parameter alpha.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warning Label">
  <data key="d0">Warning Label</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">State label used exclusively for intermediate physical sensor nodes (CPU, RAM, GPU and Disk Temperature), reflecting a sensor-level alert threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Degraded Label">
  <data key="d0">Degraded Label</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">State label reserved for component-level and system-level nodes (CPU, RAM, GPU, Hard Disk and System State), reflecting an operational health assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pages Swapped Out">
  <data key="d0">Pages Swapped Out</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Parent node used to verify Axiom 1. Raising it from 65% High to 85% raised the child Swap Memory Used from 48% to 58.5%.&lt;SEP&gt;Parent node of 'swap memory used'. When both parents are at 100%, the child reaches 99.1%, a 15.23% variation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pages Swapped In">
  <data key="d0">Pages Swapped In</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Parent node used to verify Axiom 2. Raising it from 67% High to 87% raised the child Swap Memory Used from 53% to 62.8%.&lt;SEP&gt;Parent node of 'swap memory used'. Increasing its probability from 67% to 87% raised the child probability from 53% to 62.8%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Swap Memory Used">
  <data key="d0">Swap Memory Used</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Child node used in the Axiom 1 and Axiom 2 verification tables (Tables 6 and 7). Its probability changes consistently with changes in its parent nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Child node in the Bayesian network whose parents are 'pages swapped in' and 'pages swapped out'. It is used to show validation results for Axioms 2 and 3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibration Supplementary Materials">
  <data key="d0">Calibration Supplementary Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplementary materials comprising raw probability inputs (Calibration_data_probabilities.csv, Calibration_data_target.csv), the reproducible calibration script calibration.py, and Calibration_report.pdf.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Numerical Perturbation Approach">
  <data key="d0">Numerical Perturbation Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation procedure in which parent node probabilities are perturbed at five absolute levels (+20%, +10%, baseline, −5%, −10%) within the range [0%, 100%] to observe the effect on child nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spearman's Rank Correlation Test">
  <data key="d0">Spearman's Rank Correlation Test</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Statistical test used to formally confirm monotonicity for Axioms 1 and 2. All 22 parent-child relationships showed perfect monotonic correlation (ρ = 1.0) with p-value &lt; 0.001.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monte Carlo Uncertainty Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Monte Carlo Uncertainty Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis that the paper begins to describe ('we perform Monte...'; the text is truncated) as a way to quantify epistemic uncertainty in the CPT parameters and report uncertainty intervals on the key output probabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exact Bayesian Inference">
  <data key="d0">Exact Bayesian Inference</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Inference performed on expert-elicited CPTs within a knowledge-based, scenario-driven evaluation protocol, as opposed to supervised learning on labeled failure logs.&lt;SEP&gt;Inference that propagates evidence through the DAG using pre-calibrated CPTs to compute marginal posterior probabilities of the system_state variable. It is run for each Monte Carlo replicate and for each scenario.&lt;SEP&gt;Inference run on each Dirichlet-perturbed network to record the posterior probability in the Monte Carlo uncertainty quantification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monotonicity">
  <data key="d0">Monotonicity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Property that parent node influence on child nodes is consistent in direction, confirmed by axiom verification and Spearman tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axiom_Validation.xlsx">
  <data key="d0">Axiom_Validation.xlsx</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplementary file containing validation results for the remaining ten child nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axiom_data.json">
  <data key="d0">Axiom_data.json</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplementary material containing the Spearman correlation data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sparse Labeled Failure Data">
  <data key="d0">Sparse Labeled Failure Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Data constraint in which fully labeled degradation trajectories are rarely available in real operational monitoring logs and 'Critical' events are sparse. This prevents a complete supervised evaluation and makes classical significance tests not directly applicable.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BN parent influence is monotonic, coherent and jointly reinforcing">
  <data key="d0">BN parent influence is monotonic, coherent and jointly reinforcing</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "The validation provides evidence that the influence of parent nodes is monotonic, directionally coherent, and jointly reinforcing, thereby supporting the robustness of the model."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axiom_tests.py">
  <data key="d0">Axiom_tests.py</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplementary Python code used to run the Spearman correlation monotonicity tests for Axioms 1 and 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axiom 1">
  <data key="d0">Axiom 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">First of the three validation axioms for the Bayesian network. Its monotonicity was formally confirmed by Spearman's rank correlation tests, with mean, minimum and maximum ρ all equal to 1.00 and 11/11 (100%) parent-child pairs significant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axiom 2">
  <data key="d0">Axiom 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation axiom stating that changes in the probability distributions of parent nodes should produce a consistent effect on the child node. Spearman tests gave ρ = 1.00 for all 11/11 (100%) pairs. Table 7 shows the effect on 'swap memory used' as 'pages swapped in' is perturbed, for example from 67% to 87% raising the child from 53% to 62.8%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axiom 3">
  <data key="d0">Axiom 3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation axiom stating that the combined effect of all parent nodes on a child node must exceed the effect of each parent individually. Table 8 confirms it: raising both parents to 100% gives 99.1% (+15.23%), compared with +6.74% and +8.25% for individual increases.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bayesian Inference">
  <data key="d0">Bayesian Inference</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Probabilistic reasoning combined with fuzzy logic in the proposed predictive maintenance approach for IT components.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Probability Calibration">
  <data key="d0">Probability Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis shown in Figure 7 that evaluates the calibration of predicted probabilities across CPU state classes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Classical Significance Tests and Statistical Power Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Classical Significance Tests and Statistical Power Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Statistical procedures that the paper considers not directly applicable to its scenario comparisons, because scenarios are not random samples from a labeled population and critical events are rare in the available industrial telemetry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Industrial Telemetry">
  <data key="d0">Industrial Telemetry</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Available operational monitoring logs of IT components, in which fully labeled degradation trajectories are rare and 'Critical' events are sparse.&lt;SEP&gt;The available industrial monitoring data, in which critical events are rare. This scarcity motivates uncertainty-based statistical reporting instead of conventional significance testing across scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uncertainty and Incomplete Observations">
  <data key="d0">Uncertainty and Incomplete Observations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Problem in monitoring IT components that the fuzzy Bayesian approach is designed to handle explicitly.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dirichlet Sampling">
  <data key="d0">Dirichlet Sampling</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Sampling technique used to perturb conditional probability table rows around baseline probabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Sampling used to perturb baseline CPTs with a concentration parameter reflecting moderate epistemic uncertainty in expert elicitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="95% Credible Intervals">
  <data key="d0">95% Credible Intervals</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Interval summaries (2.5th–97.5th percentiles) and interval widths used to indicate stability of scenario conclusions under parameter uncertainty.&lt;SEP&gt;Intervals computed from the empirical posterior distributions. Scenarios 1, 3, 5 and 6 had narrow intervals (width&lt;0.13), while Scenarios 2 and 4 showed moderate uncertainty (width≈0.21).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spearman Rank Test">
  <data key="d0">Spearman Rank Test</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Statistical test used for monotonicity validation of the BN model (p &lt; 0.001).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Scenario Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis that, together with sensitivity analysis, identifies the conditions under which critical component states are most likely.&lt;SEP&gt;Predictive procedure using six expert-guided synthetic scenarios. Each scenario sets root node states (Normal, Degraded, Critical) across CPU, RAM, GPU, hard disk and CSP parameters. Root nodes are fixed with quasi-certain evidence (probability = 1), and evidence is propagated to estimate system state probabilities. Reclassified from Concept to Methodology because the paper applies it as a procedure.&lt;SEP&gt;Validation of the final model through three distinct scenarios showing how key criteria such as cost breakdown and scrap rate affect the final ranking.&lt;SEP&gt;Assessment of accident probability across four scenarios (S1: all favourable; S2: unfavourable driver and planning; S3: unfavourable road and traffic; S4: unfavourable vehicle condition).&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation of accident occurrence probability across four scenarios; scenario 2 (driver behavior and delivery planning) showed the most significant influence.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Scarcity">
  <data key="d0">Data Scarcity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Setting where critical events are rare in available industrial telemetry, motivating uncertainty-based reporting.&lt;SEP&gt;Limited labeled failure events in industrial IT operations; risk and critical states are rare and cannot be induced deliberately.&lt;SEP&gt;Lack of sufficient financial market data for analysis and trading system development, addressed by GAN-based simulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Challenge in data generation for IT infrastructure applications. Related challenges include dependency complexity and limitations of traditional data collection.&lt;SEP&gt;Lack of high-quality, labeled data. In predictive maintenance for IT infrastructure, failures and anomalies are rare, so obtaining enough training data for machine learning models is difficult.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combined degraded or critical component states significantly increase system failure likelihood">
  <data key="d0">Combined degraded or critical component states significantly increase system failure likelihood</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding: "These results indicate that combined degraded or critical states across multiple components significantly increase the likelihood of system failure." Scenario 6 yields 99.8% critical failure probability; Scenario 5 yields 99.4%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hard disk failures critically influence system reliability">
  <data key="d0">Hard disk failures critically influence system reliability</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding: Scenario 3 shows a dominant probability of critical failure (92.8%), "emphasizing the critical influence of hard disk failures on overall system reliability"; Scenario 4 rises to 97.3%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAM deterioration significantly impacts system stability">
  <data key="d0">RAM deterioration significantly impacts system stability</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding: In Scenario 2, the degraded state probability is 67.8% and critical rises to 28.6%, "highlighting the significant impact of RAM deterioration on system stability."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Root Node State Assignments">
  <data key="d0">Root Node State Assignments</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplementary file (root_node_state_assignments.xlsx) that provides the exact root node state assignments for the six scenarios summarized in Table 10.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monotonicity Validation">
  <data key="d0">Monotonicity Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation of the BN model's monotonic behavior using Spearman rank tests (p &lt; 0.001). It is complemented by interval-based robustness analysis and sensitivity analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Probability Propagation">
  <data key="d0">Probability Propagation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Process of configuring root node states and analyzing their impacts on the system state through the BN.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Operation Yields Stable System Performance">
  <data key="d0">Normal Operation Yields Stable System Performance</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding: "In Scenario 1, the system exhibits a high probability of remaining in a normal state (63.6%), moderate degradation likelihood (29.8%), and a low probability of critical failure (6.6%), indicating that when all components (CPU, RAM, GPU, hard disk, and CSP) are in normal condition, system performance remains stable."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="All-Critical Parameters Lead to Inevitable System Collapse">
  <data key="d0">All-Critical Parameters Lead to Inevitable System Collapse</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding: "Finally, in Scenario 6, where all parameters are critical, the system exhibits a 99.8% probability of critical failure, underlining the inevitable system collapse under such conditions."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bayesian Network Model">
  <data key="d0">Bayesian Network Model</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">BN model integrating CPU, GPU, RAM and hard disk subnetworks into a unified network with a System_State node; provides a robust framework for anticipating system failure risks and supporting predictive maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BayesFusion LLC">
  <data key="d0">BayesFusion LLC</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Company producing GeNIe Academic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kjærulff and van der Gaag Analytic Sensitivity Method">
  <data key="d0">Kjærulff and van der Gaag Analytic Sensitivity Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analytic method for Bayesian network sensitivity expressing target posterior as a rational linear function of a CPT parameter, T(p)=(ap+b)/(cp+d).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local Sensitivity Index">
  <data key="d0">Local Sensitivity Index</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">First derivative of the rational function with respect to p at nominal value p0: (ad−bc)/(cp0+d)^2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Sensitivity Index">
  <data key="d0">Global Sensitivity Index</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Change in target probability T(pmax)−T(pmin) when the parameter varies ±10% around its nominal value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Junction Tree">
  <data key="d0">Junction Tree</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Network representation from which the constants a, b, c, d are computed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System Failure">
  <data key="d0">System Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical failure of the IT system, whose likelihood increases substantially with combined degraded or critical component states.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combined degraded or critical component states increase system failure likelihood">
  <data key="d0">Combined degraded or critical component states increase system failure likelihood</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding in the text: "These results indicate that combined degraded or critical states across multiple components significantly increase the likelihood of system failure."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensitivity analysis helps anticipate failures and enhance system reliability">
  <data key="d0">Sensitivity analysis helps anticipate failures and enhance system reliability</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "It facilitates anticipating potential failures and implementing preventive measures to enhance system reliability [44]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uffe Kjærulff">
  <data key="d0">Uffe Kjærulff</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Kjærulff, co-developer of the analytic sensitivity method for Bayesian networks cited as [46].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Van Der Gaag">
  <data key="d0">Van Der Gaag</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Van der Gaag, named with Kjærulff as the developer of the analytic sensitivity method for Bayesian networks cited as [46].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kjærulff">
  <data key="d0">Kjærulff</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Kjærulff, named with van der Gaag as the developer of the analytic sensitivity method for Bayesian networks cited as [46]. The text gives no first name, so the earlier entry "Uffe Kjærulff" was unsupported and is corrected here.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario conclusions are robust under CPT perturbation">
  <data key="d0">Scenario conclusions are robust under CPT perturbation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding in the text: "High-confidence cases (posterior&gt;0.94 or &lt;0.02) remained stable under Dirichlet perturbation. The analysis, provided in the supplementary file monte_carlo_scenarios.py, confirms that the scenario conclusions are robust and reliable."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="All-critical scenario yields 99.8% probability of critical failure">
  <data key="d0">All-critical scenario yields 99.8% probability of critical failure</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding in the text: "Scenario 6, where all parameters are critical, the system exhibits a 99.8% probability of critical failure, underlining the inevitable system collapse under such conditions."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Component-Level Sensitivity Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Component-Level Sensitivity Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Partial sensitivity analysis of each hardware component in its own subnetwork, targeting CPU_State, GPU_State, RAM_State or Hard_Disk_State in the Critical state. It identifies the most influential parameters per component, for example CPU usage and system load average for the CPU, VRAM usage and out-of-memory errors for the GPU, UltraDMA CRC error count and power-on hours for the hard disk, and active memory, fragmentation rate, overclocking and ambient temperature for RAM.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System-Level Sensitivity Analysis">
  <data key="d0">System-Level Sensitivity Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Global sensitivity analysis on the unified Bayesian network that integrates the CPU, GPU, RAM and Hard_Disk subnetworks, with System_State as the target node.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETA models outcomes of an initiating event and subsequent mitigation measures">
  <data key="d0">ETA models outcomes of an initiating event and subsequent mitigation measures</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Event Tree Analysis (ETA) is a probabilistic technique that models the possible outcomes of a critical initiating event and the performance of subsequent mitigation measures through a tree-structured diagram [28].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETA evaluates how preventive and corrective actions affect failure progression in PdM">
  <data key="d0">ETA evaluates how preventive and corrective actions affect failure progression in PdM</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Within PdM, ETA offers a structured way to evaluate how preventive and corrective actions-such as cooling mechanisms, workload balancing, or administrator intervention-affect the progression of potential failures [47].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Outcome probability equals the product of branch probabilities">
  <data key="d0">Outcome probability equals the product of branch probabilities</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The probability of the final result is calculated by multiplying the probabilities associated with each of the branches [48] that lead to that outcome.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tornado Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Tornado Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Visualization (Fig. 10) of sensitivities: red bars mark configurations leading to System_State=Critical and green bars mark configurations of lower criticality. Bar length shows the magnitude of sensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GeNIe">
  <data key="d0">GeNIe</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Software tool used for CPU subnetwork inference, yielding P(CPU_State=Critical)=0.984.&lt;SEP&gt;Bayesian network modeling software; the paper's BN model is stored as a GeNIe .xdsl file.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Elicitation">
  <data key="d0">Expert Elicitation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Procedure used to specify branch success/failure probabilities: cooling 0.8/0.2, load balancing 0.9/0.1, administrator intervention 0.85/0.15.&lt;SEP&gt;Procedure in which experts provide fuzzy rules and qualitative judgements; for the CPU State node three experts judge each rule and the final decision is by majority vote with consensus discussion. Introduces epistemic uncertainty and potential bias.&lt;SEP&gt;Procedure in which three experts give qualitative judgements (Normal / Degraded / Critical) for each rule of a node, such as the CPU State node.&lt;SEP&gt;Acquisition of expertise from field specialists via written surveys, one-on-one interviews, or collaborative brainstorming sessions.&lt;SEP&gt;Obtaining conditional probabilities by asking experts in the relevant field. The paper judges it impractical because the developed network needs 56,739,144 conditional probabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cooling System Activation">
  <data key="d0">Cooling System Activation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ETA intermediate mitigation event (success 0.8±0.1). Success means temperature stabilization; failure means persistent overheating.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Load Balancing">
  <data key="d0">Load Balancing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">ETA intermediate mitigation event (success 0.9±0.05). Success means workload redistribution; failure means the overload is maintained.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation mechanism in the CPU critical state event tree with success probability 0.9±0.05.&lt;SEP&gt;API Gateway function distributing requests in a balanced way for optimized performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Administrator Intervention">
  <data key="d0">Administrator Intervention</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">ETA intermediate mitigation event (success 0.85±0.05). Success means manual recovery; failure means an unresolved incident.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation mechanism in the CPU critical state event tree with success probability 0.85±0.05. Timely administrator intervention is highlighted as crucial for preserving operational continuity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CPU Critical State">
  <data key="d0">CPU Critical State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Initiating event of the ETA: the CPU reaches a critical state due to overheating or overload, with probability 0.984 derived from the FBN.&lt;SEP&gt;Initiating event scenario for the event tree analysis, mitigated by cooling system, load balancing and administrator intervention.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CPU">
  <data key="d0">CPU</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical IT component modeled as a subnetwork in the unified Bayesian network. Its input nodes are user space, nice, kernel space, hardware interrupts, software interrupts, wait, steal time, ambient temperature and overclocking. Its critical state is the initiating event of the ETA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPU">
  <data key="d0">GPU</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical IT component modeled as one of the four subnetworks integrated into the unified Bayesian network.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAM">
  <data key="d0">RAM</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Critical IT component modeled as a subnetwork. Its indicators are active memory, inactive memory, fragmentation rate, overclocking and ambient temperature.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overheating">
  <data key="d0">Overheating</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the causes of the CPU reaching a critical state. Persistent overheating is the failure outcome of cooling system activation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quantitative Sensitivity Scores">
  <data key="d0">Quantitative Sensitivity Scores</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplementary file quantitative_sensitivity_scores.xlsx providing detailed numerical values of the sensitivity analysis for System_State=Critical.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operational Resilience">
  <data key="d0">Operational Resilience</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Goal supported by ETA-based decision-making, alongside reducing downtime.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predictive Maintenance Framework">
  <data key="d0">Predictive Maintenance Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid PdM framework combining a knowledge-based fuzzy rule layer with Bayesian probabilistic reasoning; validated using three axioms and evaluated on six degradation scenarios, with decision rules that trigger and schedule maintenance actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monte Carlo Robustness Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Monte Carlo Robustness Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Robustness analysis using stochastic Dirichlet perturbations with a fixed random seed of 42, implemented in Python.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conditional Probability Table Generation">
  <data key="d0">Conditional Probability Table Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">CPT generation from fuzzy rules, allowing Bayesian network parameterization under scarce or imprecise failure data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision-Support Pipeline">
  <data key="d0">Decision-Support Pipeline</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Rule-based escalation mechanism comparing P(System_State=Critical) against a risk threshold θ=0.70 with a persistence filter over two consecutive monitoring cycles, generating Priority 1 tickets or Priority 2 warnings, and logging the system as stable below θ_low=0.40.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uncertainty Handling">
  <data key="d0">Uncertainty Handling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Management of uncertainty and imprecise expert knowledge in failure risk assessment, addressed by integrating fuzzy logic into Bayesian networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Component Degradation">
  <data key="d0">Component Degradation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Degradation of components such as hard disk, RAM, CPU and GPU, which increases the probability of the system entering a critical state; simultaneous failures almost guarantee system collapse.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NumPy">
  <data key="d0">NumPy</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Python library (v1.24.4) used in the implementation of the predictive maintenance pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pandas">
  <data key="d0">Pandas</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Python library (v2.1.4) used in the implementation of the predictive maintenance pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SciPy">
  <data key="d0">SciPy</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Python library (v1.10.1) used in the implementation of the predictive maintenance pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Matplotlib">
  <data key="d0">Matplotlib</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Python library (v3.7.2) used in the implementation of the predictive maintenance pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cooling System">
  <data key="d0">Cooling System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mitigation mechanism in the CPU critical state event tree with success probability 0.8±0.1. Cooling efficiency is highlighted as critical for IT system reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Persistence Filter">
  <data key="d0">Persistence Filter</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Component of the decision-support pipeline. It verifies whether the risk threshold has been exceeded for at least two consecutive monitoring cycles (e.g., two 5-minute intervals) in order to suppress transient spikes before a Priority 1 ticket is escalated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axiom-Based Validation">
  <data key="d0">Axiom-Based Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation of the framework using three axioms to ensure consistency and reliability.&lt;SEP&gt;Validation of the PdM framework using three axioms to ensure consistency and reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Degradation Scenario Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Degradation Scenario Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Evaluation of six degradation scenarios. The analysis showed that individual failures such as hard disk or RAM degradation significantly increase the probability of a critical system state, and that simultaneous failures almost guarantee system collapse.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid PdM Framework">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid PdM Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid predictive maintenance framework for IT systems combining Bayesian Networks and Fuzzy Logic; outputs P(System State=Critical) mapped to maintenance actions through a decision threshold, relying primarily on expert knowledge under data scarcity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AUC">
  <data key="d0">AUC</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance metric that the real dataset cannot support robustly due to scarce critical events; planned for future comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Precision/Recall">
  <data key="d0">Precision/Recall</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance metrics not robustly computable on the current real dataset; planned for future comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bayesian Updating">
  <data key="d0">Bayesian Updating</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Method to periodically refine expert-derived parameters using newly collected failure data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum-Likelihood Estimation">
  <data key="d0">Maximum-Likelihood Estimation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Alternative method to refine expert-derived parameters using newly collected failure data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Survival Models">
  <data key="d0">Survival Models</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard machine learning baselines planned for comparison with the proposed FBN.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Fuzzy Bayesian Network">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Fuzzy Bayesian Network</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Future extension of the framework to dynamic fuzzy Bayesian networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Evolutionary Methods">
  <data key="d0">Evolutionary Methods</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Methods envisioned for automatic optimization of membership functions and CPT parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Industrial Server Telemetry Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Industrial Server Telemetry Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Real dataset from a monitored server park, covering mostly normal or mildly degraded states and only part of the state space.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Field Trial Roadmap">
  <data key="d0">Field Trial Roadmap</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Staged deployment with pilot, controlled and production phases for practical adoption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Decision Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Threshold θ mapping P(System State=Critical) to maintenance actions, balancing false alarms and missed detections.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supervised Learning Models">
  <data key="d0">Supervised Learning Models</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Models that future hybrid approaches may combine with fuzzy Bayesian networks to enhance predictive performance while preserving interpretability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bayesian Learning">
  <data key="d0">Bayesian Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Method envisioned in future work for automatic optimization of membership functions and CPT parameters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calibration">
  <data key="d0">Calibration</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Standard evaluation metric planned for comparing the proposed FBN with a classical BN and ML baselines on shared test sets.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Online Inference">
  <data key="d0">Online Inference</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Real-time inference including periodic CPT re-evaluation, with computational requirements compatible with edge or on-premise deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold-Start Contexts">
  <data key="d0">Cold-Start Contexts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Settings with little historical data, for which the fuzzy Bayesian network is suitable because it integrates expert knowledge while remaining updatable as new operational evidence becomes available.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Telemetry Security and Privacy">
  <data key="d0">Telemetry Security and Privacy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment consideration noting that telemetry streams may reveal sensitive operational information, requiring encryption, access control, and data minimization or anonymization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zenodo Repository Artefacts">
  <data key="d0">Zenodo Repository Artefacts</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [39]. Open Zenodo repository deposited by the authors of "Intelligent Predictive Maintenance Using Fuzzy Bayesian Networks for Critical IT Components"; contains the GeNIe BN model (.xdsl), the complete FisPro project and rule base, scripts converting fuzzy outputs into CPT entries, full numeric CPTs for every node in CSV/JSON, and an example of real industrial machine data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zenodo">
  <data key="d0">Zenodo</data>
  <data key="d1">venue</data>
  <data key="d2">Open repository (data and artefact archive) where the artefacts required to replicate the experiments of "Intelligent Predictive Maintenance Using Fuzzy Bayesian Networks for Critical IT Components" are deposited, cited as [39].&lt;SEP&gt;Repository that hosts the reproducibility package by M. S. Boukhryss under DOI 10.5281/zenodo.17699824.&lt;SEP&gt;Open research repository on which the experimental package [38] of the paper was deposited.&lt;SEP&gt;Repository hosting the TrustMesh PQC reproducibility package.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502213</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artefacts are openly deposited for reproducibility">
  <data key="d0">Artefacts are openly deposited for reproducibility</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "To support reproducibility, we deposited all artefacts required to replicate our experiments, ... in an open repository on Zenodo [39]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy-Bayesian Network Construction and CPT Generation Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy-Bayesian Network Construction and CPT Generation Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Algorithm 1: defines discrete states (Normal, Degraded, Critical) and fuzzy sets for variables, elicits fuzzy rules from experts, evaluates fuzzy inference for each parent-state combination to generate CPT rows, checks normalization, and assembles the BN for exact inference.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CPT Perturbation">
  <data key="d0">CPT Perturbation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Robustness check perturbing CPT values, recommended alongside interval reporting to manage expert-elicitation uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cold-Start Problem">
  <data key="d0">Cold-Start Problem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Context with scarce labeled failure events where expert knowledge must substitute for data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Telemetry Heterogeneity">
  <data key="d0">Telemetry Heterogeneity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment challenge from different hardware generations, monitoring agents and sampling rates requiring stable mapping from raw metrics to discrete states.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Industrial Machine Data">
  <data key="d0">Industrial Machine Data</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Example of real industrial machine data deposited in the open Zenodo repository.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System State Node">
  <data key="d0">System State Node</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Top-level BN node with 81 fuzzy rules, whose posterior P(System_State=Critical) supports risk-based decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Node of the Bayesian network representing overall system condition, listed with 81 entries.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Activity Node">
  <data key="d0">User Activity Node</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fuzzy BN node with 9 rules combining User Space and Nice inputs into Low/Medium/High user activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="State Mapping">
  <data key="d0">State Mapping</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Discretization of raw telemetry metrics into the discrete states Normal, Degraded and Critical; must be stable across heterogeneous telemetry and may need periodic revision when infrastructure changes. Implemented as a state-mapping module in the inference workflow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Quality Checks">
  <data key="d0">Data Quality Checks</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Basic checks recommended before injecting evidence into the BN: outlier filtering, missing-value handling and confidence flags, to counter missing data and noisy sensors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Interval Reporting">
  <data key="d0">Interval Reporting</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Robustness check reporting uncertainty intervals on posteriors, recommended alongside CPT perturbation to manage expert-elicitation uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lightweight Inference Service">
  <data key="d0">Lightweight Inference Service</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Engineering workflow integrating the approach into existing monitoring stacks: collectors produce normalized metrics, a state-mapping module discretizes evidence, the BN inference engine produces posteriors and uncertainty intervals, and downstream systems trigger alerts, tickets and dashboards.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Exact Inference">
  <data key="d0">Exact Inference</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian network inference enabled after assembling the BN with calibrated CPTs in Algorithm 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Missing Data and Noisy Sensors">
  <data key="d0">Missing Data and Noisy Sensors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Deployment challenge in which missing data and noisy sensors can distort the evidence entered into the BN.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Out-of-Sample Validation">
  <data key="d0">Out-of-Sample Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Planned stronger validation using labels enriched from incident tickets and failure logs across multiple infrastructures and workload regimes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eafe46d984faf5ae72cd0cf550c6ec66-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">From_Uncertainty_to_Decision_An_Intelligent_Predic.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
