<node id="Jaccard Similarity">
  <data key="d0">Jaccard Similarity</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Set-based similarity metric used in the first ticket recurrence prediction method. It achieved an accuracy of 0.7419.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ef486f441df72175f968e398ffdd23d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">ICRAMCS2025F.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425570</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cosine Similarity">
  <data key="d0">Cosine Similarity</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Vector similarity metric used in the second ticket recurrence prediction method. It achieved an accuracy of 0.8710.&lt;SEP&gt;Similarity measure used by the Answer Relevance metric. It averages the similarity between the original question and synthetic questions derived from the generated answer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ef486f441df72175f968e398ffdd23d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">ICRAMCS2025F.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791500933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SBERT">
  <data key="d0">SBERT</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Sentence-BERT embedding model, combined with Cosine similarity in the hybrid ticket recurrence prediction approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7ef486f441df72175f968e398ffdd23d-chunk-000</data>
