<node id="Generative Adversarial Networks: A Systematic Review of Characteristics, Applications, and Challenges in Financial Data Generation and Market Modeling: 2019-2024">
  <data key="d0">Generative Adversarial Networks: A Systematic Review of Characteristics, Applications, and Challenges in Financial Data Generation and Market Modeling: 2019-2024</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read; a systematic review by D. Wilson and A. Azmani published in the International Journal of Engineering, Transactions B: Applications, Vol. 39, No. 02 (February 2026), pages 395-406. It reviews thirty papers from IEEE Xplore, Web of Science, Scopus and arXiv on GAN architectures applied to financial data generation and market modeling. It finds that GANs enhance data privacy and accessibility but face mode collapse, training instability and regulatory concerns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425821</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
