<node id="Vanilla GAN">
  <data key="d0">Vanilla GAN</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">The original GAN introduced by Goodfellow and his team in "Generative Adversarial Nets"; suffers from vanishing gradients and mode collapse.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conditional GAN">
  <data key="d0">Conditional GAN</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">cGAN; extends the original GAN by feeding conditional data y to both generator and discriminator, enabling generation based on conditions or labels; used for text generation, audio synthesis, data augmentation and video generation.&lt;SEP&gt;cGAN; used to generate synthetic financial transaction data for fraud detection.&lt;SEP&gt;GAN variant conditioned on auxiliary information; combined with DRAGAN by Efimov et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Conditional generative adversarial network used by Xu et al. (2019) to model tabular data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501853</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep Convolutional GAN">
  <data key="d0">Deep Convolutional GAN</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">DCGAN; GAN variant known for generating high-quality images, using convolutional layers to stabilize training.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wasserstein GAN">
  <data key="d0">Wasserstein GAN</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">WGAN; GAN variant leveraging the Wasserstein distance to address vanishing gradients and mode collapse, enhancing training stability.&lt;SEP&gt;WGAN; ensures stable training and consistent data generation but has low column-wise fidelity; used for data augmentation in stock price prediction.&lt;SEP&gt;A GAN variant (WGAN) used to improve the quality of generated sequences and to generate synthetic financial data.&lt;SEP&gt;WGAN, a GAN variant cited (27) as a technique to mitigate mode collapse and training instability.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference [27]. Arjovsky, Chintala and Bottou, arXiv, 2017. Introduces the Wasserstein GAN.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CopulaGAN">
  <data key="d0">CopulaGAN</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Copula flows for Synthetic Data Generation; GAN variant generating synthetic tabular data while preserving dependencies between variables using copula functions to model the joint distribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
