<node id="WGAN addresses vanishing gradients and mode collapse">
  <data key="d0">WGAN addresses vanishing gradients and mode collapse</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "The original GAN struggles with vanishing gradients and mode collapse issues. Arjovsky et al. (27) presented WGAN, this GAN significantly addresses those issues by leveraging the Wasserstein distance, enhancing training stability and making the process more robust."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conditional GAN conditions generation on labels">
  <data key="d0">Conditional GAN conditions generation on labels</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "This variant of GAN extends the original GAN framework by incorporating conditional data (denoted as y), which is fed into both the generator and the discriminator. This allows the model to generate data based on specific conditions or labels." Attributed to Mirza &amp; Osindero (12).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DCGAN stabilizes training with convolutional layers">
  <data key="d0">DCGAN stabilizes training with convolutional layers</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "In DCGAN, the discriminator is designed for image classification tasks, and the use of convolutional layers helps stabilize the training process, addressing challenges present in the original GAN." Attributed to Radford et al. (7).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
