<node id="CTGAN">
  <data key="d0">CTGAN</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Conditional Tabular GAN that generates realistic synthetic tabular data modeling discrete and continuous distributions, handling multimodal continuous and imbalanced discrete columns; outperforms traditional statistical and deep learning methods.&lt;SEP&gt;A Conditional Generative Adversarial Network. A modified CTGAN that incorporates contextual information is used to generate synthetic data for portfolio optimization.&lt;SEP&gt;Existing generative model for tabular data that the framework complements rather than competes with.&lt;SEP&gt;Conditional Tabular GAN, proposed by Xu et al. (2019). It uses conditional sampling and mode-specific normalization to jointly learn numeric and categorical columns, and is frequently used as a strong baseline.&lt;SEP&gt;Learned generative model for tabular data, compared against LLMs and blended with them.&lt;SEP&gt;Conditional tabular generative adversarial network used for synthetic data generation, as referenced in the titles of the Khalil et al. (2025) and Parise et al. (2025) papers.&lt;SEP&gt;Conditional tabular GAN for synthetic tabular data generation, based on conditional GAN modeling of tabular data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
