  <data key="d0">TAGAN</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Attention-based GAN that improves the modeling of long-range dependencies but struggles with regime changes and extreme market events.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Market Regime Shifts">
  <data key="d0">Market Regime Shifts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sudden changes in financial markets such as market crashes or economic policy changes, which GANs struggle to capture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidden Markov Models">
  <data key="d0">Hidden Markov Models</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">HMMs; regime-switching models proposed for integration with GANs to detect and adapt to sudden market shifts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recurrent Neural Networks">
  <data key="d0">Recurrent Neural Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">RNNs with state transitions, proposed for integration with GANs to detect sudden market shifts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lambert W Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Lambert W Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Transformation used by some studies to address heavy tails in GAN-based financial modeling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Extreme Value Theory">
  <data key="d0">Extreme Value Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">EVT; suggested for incorporation into GAN architectures to better model financial anomalies and extreme events.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heavy Tails and Extreme Events">
  <data key="d0">Heavy Tails and Extreme Events</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Characteristics of financial markets, including rare events like market crashes, that existing GAN models often fail to capture accurately.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Streaming GANs">
  <data key="d0">Streaming GANs</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">GANs continuously updated with incoming market data, enabling real-time market monitoring together with online learning techniques.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Online Learning">
  <data key="d0">Online Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Techniques allowing models to evolve with changing market conditions while avoiding overfitting to outdated patterns.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique proposed as a future direction. It lets models evolve with changing market conditions while avoiding overfitting to outdated patterns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GAN Evaluation Metrics">
  <data key="d0">GAN Evaluation Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lack of a universally accepted evaluation metric for GAN-generated financial data; existing variants rely on distributional metrics or dependence measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Market Competition and Strategic Interactions">
  <data key="d0">Market Competition and Strategic Interactions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Competitive market dynamics including interactions between market participants, market microstructure and strategic competition, rarely accounted for by GANs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Macroeconomic Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Macroeconomic Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Largely unexplored application of GANs to inflation, business cycles, and the impact of monetary and fiscal policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Long-Range Dependencies">
  <data key="d0">Long-Range Dependencies</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temporal dependencies spanning long horizons in financial time series. Attention-based GANs such as TAGAN and TTGAN improve the modeling of these dependencies.&lt;SEP&gt;A market aspect that remains underexplored in GAN applications to financial data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Financial Data Scarcity and Quality">
  <data key="d0">Financial Data Scarcity and Quality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Limitation in which suitable financial data remain scarce. GANs require extensive training data, and noisy or incomplete datasets can significantly impact GAN performance. Financial datasets also suffer from structural breaks, non-stationarity and regulatory-driven changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Improved Loss Functions">
  <data key="d0">Improved Loss Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Improved GAN loss functions suggested, alongside WGANs and gradient penalty regularization, to mitigate mode collapse.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tail-Risk-Aware Loss Functions">
  <data key="d0">Tail-Risk-Aware Loss Functions</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Loss functions proposed for GAN architectures to better model financial anomalies and extreme events.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distributional Metrics and Dependence Measures">
  <data key="d0">Distributional Metrics and Dependence Measures</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Evaluation measures on which the reviewed GAN variants rely to assess generated financial data. A unified approach incorporating financial risk, market efficiency and predictive performance is still lacking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asset Price and Volatility Modeling">
  <data key="d0">Asset Price and Volatility Modeling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Financial application area in which GANs have been effective, including asset price modeling, stock market prediction and risk management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GAN">
  <data key="d0">GAN</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Generative Adversarial Networks, a generative modeling approach introduced in 2014. GANs can generate high-fidelity financial data and are applied to portfolio analysis, risk management, market simulation and stock market analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Generative adversarial networks whose training can be parallelized across GPUs and TPUs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Market Simulation">
  <data key="d0">Market Simulation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Simulation of financial markets, a market aspect addressed by GAN applications. Hybrid GAN-reinforcement learning models could make market simulations more realistic and robust.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Classification of Optical Coherence Tomography Images Using Generative Adversarial Networks">
  <data key="d0">Classification of Optical Coherence Tomography Images Using Generative Adversarial Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 1. Paper by Seyed Aghaei, Rashno and Fadaei, published in IJE Transactions B: Applications, 2025, 38(2):389-99. It classifies OCT images using GANs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generating Multi-label Discrete Patient Records using Generative Adversarial Networks">
  <data key="d0">Generating Multi-label Discrete Patient Records using Generative Adversarial Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 2. Paper by Choi, Biswal, Malin, Duke, Stewart and Sun, posted on arXiv in 2017. It generates patient records using GANs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backpropagation Applied to Handwritten Zip Code Recognition">
  <data key="d0">Backpropagation Applied to Handwritten Zip Code Recognition</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 3. Paper by LeCun, Boser, Denker et al., published in Neural Computation, December 1989, 1(4):541-51.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Improving Deep Learning-based Saliency Detection Using Channel Attention Module">
  <data key="d0">Improving Deep Learning-based Saliency Detection Using Channel Attention Module</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 4. Paper by Farsi, Ghermezi, Barati and Mohamadzadeh, published in IJE Transactions B: Applications, 2024, 37(11):2367-79.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Empowering Face Recognition Methods using a GAN-based Single Image Super-Resolution Network">
  <data key="d0">Empowering Face Recognition Methods using a GAN-based Single Image Super-Resolution Network</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 6. Paper by Shahbakhsh and Hassanpour, published in IJE Transactions A: Basics, 2022, 35(10):1858-66. It uses a GAN-based super-resolution network to improve face recognition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unsupervised Representation Learning with Deep Convolutional Generative Adversarial Networks">
  <data key="d0">Unsupervised Representation Learning with Deep Convolutional Generative Adversarial Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 7. Paper by Radford, Metz and Chintala, posted on arXiv in 2015. It introduces deep convolutional GANs.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference 7. The visible part of the title reads "...Learning with Deep Convolutional Generative Adversarial Networks". It is an arXiv preprint from 2015 on deep convolutional generative adversarial networks (DCGAN).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="StackGAN: Text to Photo-Realistic Image Synthesis with Stacked Generative Adversarial Networks">
  <data key="d0">StackGAN: Text to Photo-Realistic Image Synthesis with Stacked Generative Adversarial Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 8. Paper by Zhang, Xu, Li, Zhang, Wang, Huang and Metaxas, published in IEEE proceedings. It synthesizes images from text using stacked GANs.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference 8. Zhang H, Xu T, Li H, Zhang S, Wang X, Huang X and Metaxas DN, published in Proceedings of the IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision 2017, pp. 5907-5915. It covers text-to-image synthesis using stacked GANs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-011</data>
