<node id="Generative Adversarial Networks in Finance: An Overview">
  <data key="d0">Generative Adversarial Networks in Finance: An Overview</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 39. Authored by Eckerli F and Osterrieder J and published on arXiv in 2021. It gives an overview of Generative Adversarial Networks in finance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generative AI for Banks: Benchmarks and Algorithms for Synthetic Financial Transaction Data">
  <data key="d0">Generative AI for Banks: Benchmarks and Algorithms for Synthetic Financial Transaction Data</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 40. Authored by Karst FS, Chong SY, Antenor AA, Lin E, Li MM and Leimeister JM and published on arXiv in 2024. It presents benchmarks and algorithms for synthetic financial transaction data for banks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Augmentation of High Frequency Financial Data Using Generative Adversarial Network">
  <data key="d0">Data Augmentation of High Frequency Financial Data Using Generative Adversarial Network</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 41. Authored by Naritomi Y and Adachi T and published at the 2020 IEEE/WIC/ACM WI-IAT conference in Melbourne, Australia, pp. 641-8. It applies GANs to augment high-frequency financial data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthetic Data Generation and Handling Data Imbalance for Mobile Financial Transactions">
  <data key="d0">Synthetic Data Generation and Handling Data Imbalance for Mobile Financial Transactions</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 42. Authored by Mohapatra A, Kumar A, Kumar B, Agarwal H and Priyadarshini R and published at the 2024 IEEE CSNT conference in Jabalpur, India, pp. 1197-202. It addresses synthetic data generation and data imbalance in mobile financial transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VTCGAN: A Proposed Multimodal Approach to Financial Time Series and Chart Pattern Generation for Algorithmic Trading">
  <data key="d0">VTCGAN: A Proposed Multimodal Approach to Financial Time Series and Chart Pattern Generation for Algorithmic Trading</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 43. Authored by Mtetwa JT, Ogudo K and Pudaruth S and published at the 2023 icABCD conference in Durban, South Africa, pp. 1-5. It proposes VTCGAN, a multimodal approach to generating financial time series and chart patterns for algorithmic trading.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Can GANs Learn the Stylized Facts of Financial Time Series?">
  <data key="d0">Can GANs Learn the Stylized Facts of Financial Time Series?</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 44. Authored by Kwon S and Lee Y and published on arXiv in 2024. It examines whether GANs can learn the stylized facts of financial time series.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAGIC: Risk-Aware Generative Adversarial Model for Stock Interval Construction">
  <data key="d0">RAGIC: Risk-Aware Generative Adversarial Model for Stock Interval Construction</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 45. Authored by Gu J, Du W and Wang G and published on arXiv in 2024. It proposes RAGIC, a risk-aware generative adversarial model for stock interval construction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Towards Realistic Financial Time Series Generation via Generative Adversarial Learning">
  <data key="d0">Towards Realistic Financial Time Series Generation via Generative Adversarial Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 46. Authored by Dogariu M, Stefan LD, Boteanu BA, Lamba C and Ionescu B and published at the 2021 EUSIPCO conference in Dublin, Ireland, pp. 1341-5. It generates realistic financial time series with generative adversarial learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthesizing Individual Consumers' Credit Historical Data Using Generative Adversarial Networks">
  <data key="d0">Synthesizing Individual Consumers' Credit Historical Data Using Generative Adversarial Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 47. Authored by Park N, Gu YH and Yoo SJ and published in Applied Sciences in 2021 (11(3):1126). It synthesizes individual consumers' credit historical data with GANs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A Machine Learning Plus-Features Based Approach for Optimal Asset Allocation">
  <data key="d0">A Machine Learning Plus-Features Based Approach for Optimal Asset Allocation</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 48. Authored by Ramirez D, Peña JM, Suárez F, Larré O and Cifuentes A and published at the 4th ACM International Conference on AI in Finance in Brooklyn, NY, 2023, pp. 549-56. It proposes a machine learning plus-features approach for optimal asset allocation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generative Adversarial Network (GAN) and Enhanced Root Mean Square Error (ERMSE): Deep Learning for Stock Price Movement Prediction">
  <data key="d0">Generative Adversarial Network (GAN) and Enhanced Root Mean Square Error (ERMSE): Deep Learning for Stock Price Movement Prediction</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 49. Authored by Kumar A, Alsadoon A, Prasad PWC, Abdullah S, Rashid TA, Pham DTH and others and published in Multimedia Tools and Applications in 2022 (81(3):3995-4013). It uses a GAN and ERMSE for stock price movement prediction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GANs and Synthetic Financial Data: Calculating VaR">
  <data key="d0">GANs and Synthetic Financial Data: Calculating VaR</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 50. Authored by Allen DE, Mushunje L and Peiris S and published in Applied Economics in 2024, pp. 1-16. It uses GANs and synthetic financial data to calculate Value at Risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep Hedging: Learning to Simulate Equity Option Markets">
  <data key="d0">Deep Hedging: Learning to Simulate Equity Option Markets</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 51. Authored by Wiese M, Bai L, Wood B and Buehler H in 2019 with an arXiv DOI. It learns to simulate equity option markets for deep hedging.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthetic Data Generation with Hybrid Quantum-Classical Models for the Financial Sector">
  <data key="d0">Synthetic Data Generation with Hybrid Quantum-Classical Models for the Financial Sector</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference 52. Authored by Pires OM, Nooblath MQ, Silva YAC, Da Silva MHF, Galvão LQ and Albino AS. It studies synthetic data generation with hybrid quantum-classical models for the financial sector. The venue is truncated in the text and begins 'The European Physical...'.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference 52. Pires OM, Nooblath MQ, Silva YAC, Da Silva MHF, Galvão LQ and Albino AS. Published in The European Physical Journal B in November 2024, 97(11):178. Covers hybrid quantum-classical synthetic data generation for finance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791425841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
