</node>
<node id="IJE Transactions B: Applications">
  <data key="d0">IJE Transactions B: Applications</data>
  <data key="d1">venue</data>
  <data key="d2">IJE Transactions B: Applications is an academic journal, part of the International Journal of Engineering (IJE), that publishes research articles in applied engineering and related fields. It has published at least two notable articles across separate volumes.

In Volume 38, Issue No. 02, released in February 2025, IJE Transactions B: Applications published an article by F. Tayalati et al. on pages 488–502. The article addresses machine selection using a combined AHP-TOPSIS (Analytic Hierarchy Process and Technique for Order of Preference by Similarity to Ideal Solution) multi-criteria decision-making approach.

In Volume 39, Issue No. 02, released in February 2026, the journal published a systematic review by D. Wilson and A. Azmani on the use of Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) for generating financial data. This review appears on pages 395–406 of that issue.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426451</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Approach Integrating Deep Learning-Autoencoder With Statistical Process Control Chart for Anomaly Detection: Case Study in Injection Molding Process">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Approach Integrating Deep Learning-Autoencoder With Statistical Process Control Chart for Anomaly Detection: Case Study in Injection Molding Process</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Article published in IEEE Access in July 2024 (received 11 June 2024, accepted 5 July 2024). It proposes integrating Statistical Process Control with an LSTM-based Autoencoder to detect anomalies in the Melt Cushion parameter of the injection molding process. The model achieves an R-squared of 0.993 and a Mean Absolute Error of 0.0146 in training. It combines Upper Limit Control, Lower Limit Control, Maximum Threshold and Minimum Threshold, and detects anomalies in four scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intelligent Automation and Biomed Genomics Laboratory">
  <data key="d0">Intelligent Automation and Biomed Genomics Laboratory</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Laboratory at the FST of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University, Tetouan, Morocco. It is the affiliation of the authors.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory with which Abdellah Azmani is affiliated.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory at FST of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaadi University, Tetouan, Morocco.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory at the FST of Tangier, part of Abdelmalek Essaadi University in Tetouan, Morocco.&lt;SEP&gt;Laboratory at FST of Tangier, Abdelmalek Essaadi University, Tetouan, Morocco, where the authors are affiliated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-56015fdaac28ae50466d3ddc4439d39b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;M3A_24_Book_of_Abstracts-57.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM-Based Autoencoder">
  <data key="d0">LSTM-Based Autoencoder</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Long Short-Term Memory based Autoencoder (LSTM-AE). It determines optimal threshold levels from reconstruction loss rates across time-series sequences.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control Chart">
  <data key="d0">Control Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">SPC tool with upper and lower limits. In the article it is enhanced with LSTM-AE thresholds (ULC, LLC, Maximum Threshold, Minimum Threshold).&lt;SEP&gt;Standard quality control technique in manufacturing; its integration with LSTM for injection molding is identified as unexplored.&lt;SEP&gt;SPC control chart built on sample means, with upper and lower control limits. It is integrated with the LSTM-AE thresholds to form a unified control chart.&lt;SEP&gt;Essential tool in statistical process control displaying Upper Control Limit (UCL) and Lower Control Limit (LCL).&lt;SEP&gt;SPC tool where the mean value is enclosed by upper and lower control limits; classified into attribute and variables types.&lt;SEP&gt;A statistical tool for monitoring processes. Its variants include dynamic, attribute (multivariate Poisson), Xbar and CUSUM charts, which are discussed in the cited works.&lt;SEP&gt;Charts used in SPC to monitor process variation and pinpoint anomalies in production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-56015fdaac28ae50466d3ddc4439d39b-chunk-000</data>
