<node id="Statistical Process Control">
  <data key="d0">Statistical Process Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Statistical Process Control (SPC) is a traditional, widely used quality control and process monitoring framework. It relies on statistical tools, mainly control charts and capability indices, to monitor process stability, assess process variability, and detect anomalies or irregularities. SPC uses historical process data to establish upper and lower control limits (UCL and LCL, also called Upper Limit Control (ULC) and Lower Limit Control (LLC)). These limits serve as anomaly indicators and can define distinct anomaly types, such as types 1 and 2. SPC is also used to construct control charts and to run capability studies.

SPC can detect predefined patterns such as systematic, shift, cyclic, and mixture patterns, but it is limited beyond these patterns. Its documented weaknesses include:
- difficulty detecting sporadic or systematic shifts;
- reduced effectiveness in complex processes;
- dependence on normality assumptions;
- reliance on historical data;
- delayed detection of process changes.

Because reliable outcomes depend on data normality, cited works on normality testing, control chart selection, and short-run monitoring address it.

SPC has been applied in manufacturing, notably injection molding and injection mould manufacturing, to monitor process stability, reduce variability, and improve quality. References [5], [10], [12], and [13] apply it in these contexts. In one application, SPC yielded a process capability index (Cp) of 2.37 and a Cpk of 2.36.

In the article under discussion, SPC is combined with deep learning, specifically an LSTM-based autoencoder (LSTM-AE), to detect anomalies from process data. Data from the SPC mean control chart serve as training data for the model, integrating traditional statistical quality control with modern deep learning techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Key quality management tool based on control charts to detect irregularities in product quality and machine deviation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-56015fdaac28ae50466d3ddc4439d39b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;M3A_24_Book_of_Abstracts-57.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426614</data>
