<node id="LSTM-Autoencoder">
  <data key="d0">LSTM-Autoencoder</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">LSTM-AE deep learning model with significant advancements in anomaly detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep learning model combining LSTM temporal learning with autoencoder feature extraction. It is trained on normal data, and its maximum residual is used as the anomaly detection threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Proposed architecture integrating LSTM layers as sequential layers within an Autoencoder; encoder of two LSTM layers (64 and 32 units), a repeat-vector latent layer, and decoder of two LSTM layers (32 and 64 units), trained by minimizing reconstruction loss.&lt;SEP&gt;LSTM-Autoencoder (LSTM-AE) is a deep learning model trained on data from the mean control chart. It relies on reconstruction error to detect anomalies. In the article it achieved a MAPE of 0.0146 and an R-squared of 0.992.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426321</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
