</node>
<node id="Process Capability">
  <data key="d0">Process Capability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Statistical metric gauging the capacity of a process to consistently produce output within specified upper and lower tolerance limits.&lt;SEP&gt;Ability of a manufacturing process to meet specifications, evaluated with control charts and the indices Cp and Cpk; improved significantly in the Uluksan [27] study.&lt;SEP&gt;Measure of a process's ability to meet desired criteria, calculated in the paper.&lt;SEP&gt;The ability of a process to meet specifications, quantified by process capability indices. Cited works on capable processes and on reviews of the indices discuss it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-018</data>
