  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM is applied in manufacturing for predictive maintenance and quality prediction">
  <data key="d0">LSTM is applied in manufacturing for predictive maintenance and quality prediction</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "While existing research, such as the work by Essien and Giannetti [36], has explored LSTM applications in manufacturing for predictive maintenance and quality prediction, a gap remains in integrating control chart techniques with LSTM specifically for injection molding."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual-Actual Correction Model">
  <data key="d0">Virtual-Actual Correction Model</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine learning model proposed by Huang et al. [32] that uses an autoencoder for feature extraction and a multilayer perceptron to relate simulated and actual mold cavity pressures. It does not require extensive training data and raised the simulated-actual cavity pressure correlation from 81% to 98%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Feature Importance Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Feature Importance Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis used by Jung et al. [31]. It identified temperature and time as significant factors affecting injection molding quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Temperature and time significantly affect injection molding quality">
  <data key="d0">Temperature and time significantly affect injection molding quality</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "Feature importance analysis identifies temperature and time as significant factors affecting quality."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integration of control charts with LSTM in injection molding is unexplored">
  <data key="d0">Integration of control charts with LSTM in injection molding is unexplored</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "Control charts are standard for quality control in manufacturing, but their combination with LSTM for real-time anomaly detection or quality prediction in injection molding is unexplored."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Few works combine LSTM and Autoencoder in injection molding">
  <data key="d0">Few works combine LSTM and Autoencoder in injection molding</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "While some works have explored the use of LSTM or Autoencoder individually, few have combined these two methods in the field of the injection molding process."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Scarcity and Heterogeneity">
  <data key="d0">Data Scarcity and Heterogeneity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Challenge of sparse and heterogeneous data in advanced and smart manufacturing. Ramezankhani et al. [33] address it with sim-to-real transfer learning.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mold Cavity Pressure">
  <data key="d0">Mold Cavity Pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection molding quantity whose simulated values diverge from actual measurements. Huang et al. [32] improve its prediction accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermoforming Process">
  <data key="d0">Thermoforming Process</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Industrial case study in which Ramezankhani et al. [33] evaluated a ConvVAE and sim-to-real transfer learning framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality Control">
  <data key="d0">Quality Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Manufacturing process for ensuring product quality. Control charts are its standard tool, and automated systems enhance it in injection molding.&lt;SEP&gt;Field to which the study contributes. Integrating advanced machine learning with traditional process control is described as improving quality assurance and preventing defects in industrial settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Manufacturing quality control whose costs could be reduced by the combined Canny and CNN approach; also the subject of reference [3].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467116</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cushion Parameter Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Cushion Parameter Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Dataset of 10,160 observations of the melt cushion parameter collected over more than 100 production hours. It contains 8,934 normal and 1,226 anomalous observations and was collected in a workshop in northern Morocco.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARBUG-Gmbh Injection Molding Machine">
  <data key="d0">ARBUG-Gmbh Injection Molding Machine</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">150-ton injection molding machine from which the data was collected.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normality Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Normality Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Assessment of whether data follows a Gaussian distribution, which is essential for establishing SPC control limits. The melt cushion data showed a mean of 6.06 cm3 and a standard deviation of 0.07 cm3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Histogram">
  <data key="d0">Histogram</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Graphical technique used to assess normality of data.&lt;SEP&gt;Graphical method used to illustrate the distribution's symmetry around the mean, reinforcing the normality of the cushion parameter dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Box-and-Whisker Plot">
  <data key="d0">Box-and-Whisker Plot</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Graphical technique used to assess normality of data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SPC requires Gaussian distribution for accurate control limits">
  <data key="d0">SPC requires Gaussian distribution for accurate control limits</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Assessing the normality of a dataset is a crucial step, particularly in Statistical Process Control (SPC), where adherence to a Gaussian distribution is often essential for the accurate establishment of control limits and the evaluation of process stability [37].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Histograms and box plots are used to assess normality">
  <data key="d0">Histograms and box plots are used to assess normality</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Various techniques, such as constructing histograms [38] and box-and-whisker plots [39], are commonly employed in this analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Capability Study">
  <data key="d0">Capability Study</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Process capability analysis carried out on the normal-situation dataset within the Statistical Process Control framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Upper and Lower Control Limits">
  <data key="d0">Upper and Lower Control Limits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Upper Control Limit and Lower Control Limit of the process. Both are derived from the SPC control chart and serve as two critical indicators for anomaly detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Residual Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Residual Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maximum residual (reconstruction error) of the LSTM-AE model trained on normal data. It is used as the threshold for anomaly detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specification Limits">
  <data key="d0">Specification Limits</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Engineering tolerance limits of the cushion parameter from the production datasheet: Lower Specification Limit (LSL) of 6.11 cm3 and Upper Specification Limit (USL) of 7.11 cm3. Values outside these limits are identified as anomalies.&lt;SEP&gt;Upper specification limit (USL) and lower specification limit (LSL) that define the tolerances, or acceptable range of variation, for key product characteristics. They are used in the Cp and Cpk formulas.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gaussian Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Gaussian Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Normal distribution model. Adherence to it is often essential for accurate SPC control limits, and the melt cushion data was found to follow it closely.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Post-Defect Indicators">
  <data key="d0">Post-Defect Indicators</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Indicators such as product weight and final dimensions. According to the text, existing injection molding research mainly focuses on these rather than on pre-defect indicators like the cushion parameter.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality Assurance">
  <data key="d0">Quality Assurance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Goal enhanced by the integrated SPC, LSTM and Autoencoder approach through improved accuracy and efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Process Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Process Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Goal supported by the integrated anomaly detection approach in injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Connector Cables">
  <data key="d0">Connector Cables</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Automotive-sector product made in the injection molding workshop in northern Morocco where the data was collected.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Oberoi et al. [40]">
  <data key="d0">Oberoi et al. [40]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [40]; defines process capability as a statistical metric gauging a process's capacity to consistently generate output aligned with predefined criteria or customer expectations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Palmer and Tsui [42]">
  <data key="d0">Palmer and Tsui [42]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [42]; explains how a process can be interpreted according to the values obtained for the Cp and Cpk capability indices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cp (Process Capability Index)">
  <data key="d0">Cp (Process Capability Index)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Index computed as Cp = (USL - LSL)/6σ, the ratio of tolerance width to process variation; assesses whether the distribution fits within specification limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cpk (Process Capability Index Adjusted for Centering)">
  <data key="d0">Cpk (Process Capability Index Adjusted for Centering)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Index computed as Cpk = min((USL − µ)/3σ, (µ − LSL)/3σ); accounts for both spread and centering of the process relative to the target value.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cushion Parameter Normal Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Cushion Parameter Normal Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Normal dataset of cushion parameter values with mean 6.06 cm3 and standard deviation 0.07 cm3 (Table 1). Its histogram is symmetric around the mean, and the text reports that approximately 90% of observations fall within 6.5 cm3 to 6.57 cm3. It is used for normality verification and process capability analysis (Figure 7).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Process capability is a metric of a process's ability to consistently meet predefined criteria">
  <data key="d0">Process capability is a metric of a process's ability to consistently meet predefined criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "As defined by Oberoi et al. [40], Process capability is a statistical metric that gauges the capacity of a process to consistently generate output that aligns with predefined criteria or customer expectations."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Process interpretation depends on Cp and Cpk values">
  <data key="d0">Process interpretation depends on Cp and Cpk values</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Palmer and Tsui [42] explained that the interpretation of the process can be done according to the value obtained of each capability index"; e.g. Cp &gt; 1 and Cpk &gt; 1 indicates a capable, well-centered process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Upper Control Limit">
  <data key="d0">Upper Control Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">UCL, the upper boundary displayed on a control chart (Figure 8).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lower Control Limit">
  <data key="d0">Lower Control Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LCL, the lower boundary displayed on a control chart (Figure 8).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Process Capability Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Process Capability Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis that determines whether the inherent variability of a process is small enough to ensure most output falls within tolerance limits. It is typically evaluated using the Cp and Cpk indices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cp &gt; 1 and Cpk &gt; 1 indicates a capable, well-centered process">
  <data key="d0">Cp &gt; 1 and Cpk &gt; 1 indicates a capable, well-centered process</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Interpretation attributed to Palmer and Tsui [42]: "If (Cp &gt; 1 and Cpk &gt; 1): The process is capable, and the process mean is well-centered within the specification limits."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cp &gt; 1 and Cpk &lt; 1 indicates a capable but off-center process">
  <data key="d0">Cp &gt; 1 and Cpk &lt; 1 indicates a capable but off-center process</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Interpretation attributed to Palmer and Tsui [42]: "If (Cp &gt; 1 and Cpk &lt; 1): The process is capable, but the process mean is not well-centered."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cp &lt; 1 and Cpk &lt; 1 indicates an incapable, off-center process">
  <data key="d0">Cp &lt; 1 and Cpk &lt; 1 indicates an incapable, off-center process</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Interpretation attributed to Palmer and Tsui [42]: "If (Cp &lt; 1 and Cpk &lt; 1): The process is not capable, and the process mean is not well-centered." Immediate improvement actions are then required.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
