<node id="X-Bar And R Chart">
  <data key="d0">X-Bar And R Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Control chart pair assessing the mean (X-bar) and range (R) of subgroups of continuous data; used to compute UCL and LCL for the melt cushion parameter.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attribute Control Chart">
  <data key="d0">Attribute Control Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Control chart type subdivided into charts for percentage defectives and number of defects per unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variables Control Chart">
  <data key="d0">Variables Control Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Control chart type focused on monitoring fluctuations in the average and range of measurements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM Autoencoder">
  <data key="d0">LSTM Autoencoder</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Unsupervised deep learning model applied to unlabeled time series data of normal and abnormal operational states.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep learning autoencoder based on LSTM, trained on normal scenarios. Anomalies are identified when the reconstruction error crosses the defined thresholds.&lt;SEP&gt;Long short-term memory autoencoder technique. Reference [14] uses it for forecasting and anomaly detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unlabeled Time Series Data">
  <data key="d0">Unlabeled Time Series Data</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Substantial unlabeled time series data representing normal and abnormal operational states, plus a dataset generated from control-chart samples of 3 observations each.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control charts are essential SPC tools for real-time monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Control charts are essential SPC tools for real-time monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Control charts are essential tools in statistical process control (SPC) for monitoring and controlling processes in real time [43].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control chart type selection depends on data characteristics and goals">
  <data key="d0">Control chart type selection depends on data characteristics and goals</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The selection of a control chart type depends on the characteristics of the data being monitored and the specific goals of the analysis [44].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control charts are classified into attributes and variables types">
  <data key="d0">Control charts are classified into attributes and variables types</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 9 illustrates the common types of control charts, which are classified into two main types: attributes, as discussed by Chiu and Kuo [45], and variables, as elaborated by Gibra [46].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X-bar and R charts suit small subgroups and normally distributed data">
  <data key="d0">X-bar and R charts suit small subgroups and normally distributed data</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">X-bar and R charts are ideal for processes with relatively small subgroup sizes (typically fewer than 10) and normally distributed data [47].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X-Bar Chart">
  <data key="d0">X-Bar Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Control chart that shows the average of a subgroup of measurements and monitors the central tendency of a process. For the melt cushion parameter, the center line is at 6.61 cm3, the UCL is 6.67 cm3 and the LCL is 6.54 cm3. Its limits are computed as the grand mean plus or minus A2 times the mean range.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="R Chart">
  <data key="d0">R Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Range chart that shows the range of the same subgroup and tracks process variation. For the melt cushion parameter, the center line is at 0.107 cm3, the lower limit is 0 and the upper limit is 0.276 cm3. Its limits are computed as D4 and D3 times the mean range.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control Chart Constants A2, D3, D4">
  <data key="d0">Control Chart Constants A2, D3, D4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Constants that depend on the number of observations per subgroup (listed in Table 3). They are used with the mean range to calculate the control limits of X-bar and R charts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Control Chart Generated Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Control Chart Generated Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">New dataset generated with the X-bar and Range control chart approach, made of samples of 3 observations each. It serves as input to the LSTM Autoencoder.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426323</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Repeat Vector">
  <data key="d0">Repeat Vector</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Latent layer that duplicates the encoder output to match the input requirements of the decoder.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SPC Chart">
  <data key="d0">SPC Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Statistical process control chart (mean and range control chart with LCL, UCL and mean) from which a new dataset is generated for the LSTM-AE.&lt;SEP&gt;Statistical Process Control chart integrated with the deep learning autoencoder in the hybrid approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SPC-Derived Time Series Dataset">
  <data key="d0">SPC-Derived Time Series Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Newly generated dataset originating from the SPC chart, initially comprising 2978 observations, segmented into sliding sequences of 5 observations for training the LSTM-AE.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [50]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [50]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [50] for LSTM being proposed to enhance RNN short-term memory via cell states.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work describing Retrieval-Augmented Generation as retrieving texts from an external corpus for an LLM.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work on stopping distance and its dependence on speed, reflexes, weather and road grip.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-004</data>
