  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [52]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [52]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [52] for the latent layer functioning as a repeat vector.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work on integrating retrieved texts into LLMs via cross-attention.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work on diplomatic visits and unforeseen events disrupting traffic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conventional Autoencoders struggle to capture temporal patterns in time series">
  <data key="d0">Conventional Autoencoders struggle to capture temporal patterns in time series</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">However, conventional Autoencoders struggle to effectively capture the temporal patterns inherent in time series data[48].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM captures long-term memory in time series data">
  <data key="d0">LSTM captures long-term memory in time series data</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">...integrating long short-term memory (LSTM) neural networks as sequential layers within the Autoencoder (AE) framework, renowned for its ability to capture long-term memory in time series data [49].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM enhances RNN memory through cell states">
  <data key="d0">LSTM enhances RNN memory through cell states</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) is proposed to enhance the short-term memory capacity of recurrent neural networks (RNNs) by incorporating long-term memory states, commonly referred to as cell states [50].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM cell comprises input, output, and forget gates">
  <data key="d0">LSTM cell comprises input, output, and forget gates</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 12 illustrates the internal structure of an LSTM cell, which comprises input, output, and forget gates [51].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Repeat vector latent layer duplicates encoder output for the decoder">
  <data key="d0">Repeat vector latent layer duplicates encoder output for the decoder</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The latent layer functions as a repeat vector, duplicating the output of the encoder to match the input requirements of the decoder [52].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mean and Range Control Chart">
  <data key="d0">Mean and Range Control Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">SPC chart with calculated LCL, UCL and mean (Figure 10), analyzed using randomized data points from 10 production cycles (Figure 11). In the example, no instances fall outside tolerance limits and no ascending, descending or cyclic trend is observed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sliding Window Sequencing">
  <data key="d0">Sliding Window Sequencing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Data preparation procedure that segments the SPC-derived dataset into overlapping sequences of 5 observations (X1 = {x1..x5}, X2 = {x2..x6}, ...) for training the LSTM-AE.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM Encoder">
  <data key="d0">LSTM Encoder</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Sequence folding layer transforming features into time-organized feature sequences; Layer 1 outputs [5 × 64], Layer 2 with 32 LSTM cells outputs a [1 × 32] encoded feature vector.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LSTM Decoder">
  <data key="d0">LSTM Decoder</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Sequence unfolding layer reconstructing compressed input across timesteps; Layer 4 LSTM(32) mirrors Layer 2 and Layer 5 LSTM(64) corresponds to Layer 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RepeatVector Layer">
  <data key="d0">RepeatVector Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Third layer replicating the [1 × 32] encoded vector per timestep, producing [5 × 32]; acts as a bridge between the encoder and decoder.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TimeDistribution Layer">
  <data key="d0">TimeDistribution Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Supplementary layer (size 64 × 1) whose output is matrix-multiplied with LSTM layer outputs (size 5 × 64) in the decoder.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sliding Window Sequence Preparation">
  <data key="d0">Sliding Window Sequence Preparation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Data preparation producing 2974 overlapping sequences of 5 observations each, reshaped into a 2-dimensional array of samples and time steps.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hyperparameter Fine-Tuning">
  <data key="d0">Hyperparameter Fine-Tuning</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Procedure evaluated through loss curves for four hyperparameter fine-tuning configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Iterative tuning of the number of layers, LSTM cells, optimizer, epochs, batch size, learning rate and dropout rate; tuning number 4 was found to be optimal.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prepared Sequence Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Prepared Sequence Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Training data built for the LSTM-AE. It consists of 2974 sequences of 5 observations each, reshaped into a 2-dimensional array of samples and time steps with final size [2974 × 5].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loss Curve">
  <data key="d0">Loss Curve</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Evaluation metric visualization shown in Figure 16. It is used to compare hyperparameter fine-tuning configurations 1–4.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X-Bar Control Chart">
  <data key="d0">X-Bar Control Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">SPC control chart used to generate the training data, consisting of 2978 observations clustered around the chart's mean.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reconstruction Error Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Reconstruction Error Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Threshold set to the maximum reconstruction error observed on the normal training data; test samples whose error exceeds it are flagged as anomalies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Min-Max Scaler">
  <data key="d0">Min-Max Scaler</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Maximum-minimum normalization applied to the training data before the model is trained.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RMSprop">
  <data key="d0">RMSprop</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Optimizer considered as an option during hyperparameter tuning.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TimeDistributed Layer">
  <data key="d0">TimeDistributed Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Output layer of size 64 x 1 that produces a vector matching the input size.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reconstruction-Based Time Series Anomaly Detection">
  <data key="d0">Reconstruction-Based Time Series Anomaly Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An anomaly detection approach in which a model reconstructs time series sequences. Observations with reconstruction errors above a threshold are categorized as anomalies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reconstruction Residual Error">
  <data key="d0">Reconstruction Residual Error</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Absolute error between predicted and actual data from the trained LSTM-AE. It is used to set the anomaly thresholds: a trial limit at 0.02916 and a novel minimum-residual limit at 0.0188.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anomaly Types">
  <data key="d0">Anomaly Types</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Four anomaly types defined in the testing data: type 1 (above ULC), type 2 (below LLC), type 3 (ascendant or descendant trend), and type 4 (mean deviating from the principal mean and exceeding the tolerance range).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minimum Residual Limit">
  <data key="d0">Minimum Residual Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Novel limit based on the minimum residual, set at 0.0188. It detects previously unnoticed type 4 anomalies whose errors did not exceed the 0.02916 threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trial Limit">
  <data key="d0">Trial Limit</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Initial anomaly limit derived from the maximum residual of the reconstructed LSTM-AE model, set at 0.02916. Type 4 anomalies whose errors did not exceed this limit were considered acceptable by the initial model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anomaly Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Anomaly Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference point for judging how far an observation deviates from normal. It is set at the maximum reconstruction error of the normal training samples, which is 0.04 for the Melt cushion. Observations or test sequences whose error or MAE surpasses the threshold are flagged as anomalies, and the model raises an alert. The text notes that as the threshold approaches zero, the constructed data aligns more closely with the original data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statistical Process Mean Control Chart">
  <data key="d0">Statistical Process Mean Control Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">SPC control chart of the mean with lower and upper control limits (LLC and ULC). The paper enhances it with additional dynamic minimum and maximum thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Control Charts">
  <data key="d0">Smart Control Charts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mean control charts enhanced with dynamic minimum and maximum thresholds in addition to the static LLC and ULC. The added thresholds boost anomaly detection capability and can be adjusted to application requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minimum Residual Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Minimum Residual Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A novel dynamic lower limit based on the minimum residual, set at 0.0188. Points whose reconstruction error falls below it are flagged in green. It uncovers previously unnoticed type 4 anomalies, which the initial model had accepted because their errors did not exceed its 0.02916 threshold.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Reconstruction Error Threshold">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Reconstruction Error Threshold</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">An upper limit on the reconstruction error, set at 0.0243 (80% of the maximum threshold). Points exceeding this limit are flagged as anomalies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Melt Injection Parameter">
  <data key="d0">Melt Injection Parameter</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Process parameter data from injection molding, used as the case study in the paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anomaly Type 3 Trend">
  <data key="d0">Anomaly Type 3 Trend</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anomaly type characterized by ascending or descending trends. The model recognizes it early, for example through three successive points in a positive trend.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anomaly Type 4">
  <data key="d0">Anomaly Type 4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anomalies with errors below the 0.02916 threshold that the initial model considered acceptable. They are detected through the minimum residual limit.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lower and Upper Control Limits (LLC and ULC)">
  <data key="d0">Lower and Upper Control Limits (LLC and ULC)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">The static lower and upper control limits of the existing mean control chart. The paper keeps them and adds dynamic minimum and maximum thresholds alongside them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anomaly Type 1">
  <data key="d0">Anomaly Type 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The only anomaly type detected in the first sensitivity trial (thresholds 0.0277 and 0.0029). It was also detected in all later trials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anomaly Type 2">
  <data key="d0">Anomaly Type 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An anomaly type detected in the second, third and fourth sensitivity trials, but not in the first.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Detection Sensitivity Depends On Thresholds">
  <data key="d0">Detection Sensitivity Depends On Thresholds</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "These findings underscore the sensitivity of the models to threshold adjustments. The identification of anomalies within observations is highly affected by the precise thresholds set."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mean Control Chart">
  <data key="d0">Mean Control Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">An SPC control chart of the mean. The article used it to divide 10160 raw values into samples of three, yielding 3389 values for training the LSTM-AE.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early Anomaly Detection">
  <data key="d0">Early Anomaly Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The ability to detect anomalies early, including ascending and descending trends, before defective parts are produced or machines malfunction. The article demonstrates this mainly for anomaly type 3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Melt Injection">
  <data key="d0">Melt Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The critical injection molding parameter that the article's anomaly detection approach focuses on.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426328</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
