<node id="Multi-Objective Bayesian Optimization">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Objective Bayesian Optimization</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">An optimization method that reference [18] uses, together with constrained generative inverse design networks, to optimize the injection molding process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two Phases Anomaly Detection Based on Clustering and Visualization for Plastic Injection Molding Data">
  <data key="d0">Two Phases Anomaly Detection Based on Clustering and Visualization for Plastic Injection Molding Data</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [24]. Paper by S. Lee, Y. Yun, S. Park, S. Oh, C. Lee and J. Jeong, published in Procedia Computer Science vol. 201, pp. 519–526, in 2022. It presents a two-phase anomaly detection approach for plastic injection molding data that uses clustering and visualization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predictive Maintenance on Injection Molds by Generalized Fault Trees and Anomaly Detection">
  <data key="d0">Predictive Maintenance on Injection Molds by Generalized Fault Trees and Anomaly Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [25]. Paper by P. Nunes, E. Rocha, J. Santos and R. Antunes, published in Procedia Computer Science vol. 217, pp. 1038–1047, in 2023. It addresses predictive maintenance of injection molds using generalized fault trees and anomaly detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enhance the Injection Molding Quality Prediction with Artificial Intelligence to Reach Zero-Defect Manufacturing">
  <data key="d0">Enhance the Injection Molding Quality Prediction with Artificial Intelligence to Reach Zero-Defect Manufacturing</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [26]. Paper by B. Silva, R. Marques, D. Faustino, P. Ilheu, T. Santos, J. Sousa and A. D. Rocha, published in Processes vol. 11, no. 1, p. 62, in Dec. 2022. It applies artificial intelligence to injection molding quality prediction with the goal of zero-defect manufacturing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decreasing Defects in Plastic Injection Molding and Vibration Welding Processes Through Statistical Process Control">
  <data key="d0">Decreasing Defects in Plastic Injection Molding and Vibration Welding Processes Through Statistical Process Control</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [27]. Paper by M. Uluskan, published in Open Journal of Nano vol. 6, no. 2, pp. 7–18, in 2021. It applies statistical process control to reduce defects in plastic injection molding and vibration welding processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shewhart Control Charts Implementation for Quality and Production Management">
  <data key="d0">Shewhart Control Charts Implementation for Quality and Production Management</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [28]. Paper by M. Malindzakova, K. Čulková and J. Trpčevská, published in Processes vol. 11, no. 4, p. 1246, in Apr. 2023. It covers the implementation of Shewhart control charts for quality and production management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426330</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy Process Capability Plots for Families of One-Sided Specification Limits">
