<node id="Hybrid Approach Integrating Deep Learning-Autoencoder With SPC Chart">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Approach Integrating Deep Learning-Autoencoder With SPC Chart</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">"Hybrid Approach Integrating Deep Learning-Autoencoder With SPC Chart" is a research article by F. Tayalati et al., published in Volume 12 (2024), spanning pages from about 95577 to 95595. It proposes a hybrid anomaly detection method for injection molding. The method combines Statistical Process Control (SPC) charts with a deep learning, LSTM-based Autoencoder (LSTM-AE) to perform unsupervised anomaly detection on time series production data. The case study monitors the melt cushion parameter of an injection molding machine. In some sections this is called the "Melt Injection Parameter," which appears to refer to the same process variable.

The article reviews anomaly detection methods in injection molding, the use of SPC in injection molding, and machine learning and autoencoder applications in the field, including LSTM-AE techniques. It discusses melt cushion irregularities and the limitations of traditional SPC. It identifies several research gaps:
- integrating control charts with LSTM,
- combining LSTM with autoencoders, and
- monitoring the cushion parameter.

Methodologically, the authors first verify that the cushion parameter dataset is normally distributed. They then evaluate process capability, reporting a Cp of 2.37 and a Cpk of 2.36. X-bar and R control charts, including the Statistical Process Mean Control Chart, use subgroups of three observations, and these subgroups generate the dataset fed to the LSTM-AE. The paper details sequence preparation and the model architecture: an LSTM encoder, a RepeatVector layer, and an LSTM decoder. It also presents loss curves for four hyperparameter fine-tuning configurations.

Anomalies are detected using thresholds on the reconstruction residual error. The model achieved a Mean Absolute Percentage Error (MAPE) of 0.0146 and an R-squared of 0.992. It identified four types of anomalies, including early detection of the type 3 anomaly. The article's reference list covers SPC, injection molding, anomaly detection, LSTM, autoencoders, and digital twins for injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1920bb99aa33c3c871f9dc257956e3ca-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Hybrid_Approach_Integrating_Deep_Learning-Autoencoder_With_Statistical_Process_Control_Chart_for_Anomaly_Detection_Case_Study_in_Injection_Molding_Process1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426338</data>
