</node>
<node id="Design of Combined Ahp-Topsis Model for Optimizing Selection of Injection Molding Machines">
  <data key="d0">Design of Combined Ahp-Topsis Model for Optimizing Selection of Injection Molding Machines</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Article published in International Journal of Engineering, Transactions B: Applications, Vol. 38 No. 02 (February 2025), pages 488-502. The paper combines AHP and TOPSIS to select the optimal injection molding machine from three alternatives. AHP weights five main criteria and eleven sub-criteria covering cost and performance, and TOPSIS ranks the machines against ideal and anti-ideal solutions. The model is validated through three scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combined AHP-TOPSIS Model">
  <data key="d0">Combined AHP-TOPSIS Model</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Decision support model that combines AHP weighting with TOPSIS ranking to select injection molding machines. It is validated through three scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
