<node id="Machine selection in injection molding is a multi-criteria decision-making challenge">
  <data key="d0">Machine selection in injection molding is a multi-criteria decision-making challenge</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "...selection the optimum machine from several alternatives still one of the challenging task in the field of injection molding manufacturing, which is recognized as a multi-criteria decision-making challenge, usually managed by professionals and experienced adjusters (5)."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Investment Cost">
  <data key="d0">Investment Cost</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the five main selection criteria weighted by AHP. Its sub-criteria are machine cost and installation cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion including machine cost (ex-works price plus transportation and logistics) and installation cost (energy and utilities installation).&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion with a final weight of 0.108.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five main criteria for selecting an injection molding machine. The text mentions pneumatic, electrical and cooling water installation expenses. In the expert pairwise comparison (Table 4), quality rate (3) and availability rate (3) were rated more important than investment cost, and operating cost (2) was rated moderately more important. Investment cost was rated more important than performance rate (2).&lt;SEP&gt;Main criterion with weight 0.108, comprising machine cost (0.093 global) and installation cost (0.016 global).&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion in the machine selection with two sub-criteria: machine cost (176 K€ for HAIT 320T) and installation cost (15 K€ for HAIT 320T). It is unchanged across all scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality Rate">
  <data key="d0">Quality Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the five main selection criteria weighted by AHP. Its sub-criteria are scrap cost and rework cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion comprising scrap rate and rework rate of machines.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion with the highest importance, with a priority weight of 43.1%.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five main criteria for injection molding machine selection, linked to the scrap rate and rework rate definitions. In the expert pairwise comparison (Table 4), it was judged the most important criterion. It was rated 3 against investment cost, 4 against performance rate, 4 against availability rate and 3 against operating cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Main criterion with weight 0.431, comprising scrap rate and rework rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion with two sub-criteria: scrap (0.60% initially for HAIT 320T, 0.40% in Scenarios 1 and 3) and rework (1.00%).&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion that, combined with scrap rate, holds the greatest influence on the choice of machine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Rate">
  <data key="d0">Performance Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the five main selection criteria weighted by AHP. Its sub-criteria are speed loss rate and micro stoppage rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion comprising speed loss rate and changeover rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion with a final weight of 0.074.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five main criteria for injection molding machine selection, linked to the low speed and micro stoppage definitions. In the expert pairwise comparison (Table 4), it was rated less important than every other criterion.&lt;SEP&gt;Main criterion with weight 0.074, comprising speed loss rate and changeover/micro stoppage rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion with two sub-criteria: speed loss rate (0.70%) and micro stoppage rate (2.40%). It is unchanged across all scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Availability Rate">
  <data key="d0">Availability Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the five main selection criteria weighted by AHP. Its sub-criteria are changeover rate and breakdown rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion comprising breakdown rate and changeover rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion ranked second in importance, with a priority weight of 24.5%.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five main criteria for injection molding machine selection, linked to the breakdown rate and changeover rate definitions. In the expert pairwise comparison (Table 4), it was rated 3 against investment cost, performance rate and operating cost, and 1/4 against quality rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Main criterion with weight 0.245, comprising breakdown rate and changeover rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion with two sub-criteria: breakdown rate (5% initially for HAIT 320T, 3% in Scenarios 2 and 3) and changeover rate (1.50%).&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion that ranks second in influence on machine choice and is particularly affected by the breakdown rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operating Rate">
  <data key="d0">Operating Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the five main selection criteria weighted by AHP. Its sub-criteria are energy consumption, labor cost and maintenance cost.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario-Based Validation">
  <data key="d0">Scenario-Based Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation of the final AHP-TOPSIS model through three distinct scenarios. The scenarios show how key criteria such as cost breakdown and scrap rate can change the final selection ranking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Characteristics-Based Machine Selection">
  <data key="d0">Technical Characteristics-Based Machine Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Traditional approach that selects an injection molding machine from technical characteristics such as clamping force, distance between tie bars and maximum shot volume. It is limited because a single product may suit multiple machines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polymer Products">
  <data key="d0">Polymer Products</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Products made from polymers. They are used in a wide array of industries, including automotive, aerospace and civil engineering.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426425</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automotive Workshop Data">
  <data key="d0">Automotive Workshop Data</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Real data collected from an actual workshop operating in the automotive industry, used for the case study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MCDM framework applies to machine selection">
  <data key="d0">MCDM framework applies to machine selection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "This article addresses the selection problem associated with injection molding machines using multi-criteria decision-making (MCDM) framework (5, 6)."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
