</node>
<node id="Injection molding injects plastic under high pressure">
  <data key="d0">Injection molding injects plastic under high pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Injection molding is an industrial technique, involves injecting plastic material into a mold cavity under high pressure, which can range from hundreds to thousands of bars (2)."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Evaluation Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Evaluation Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Five main criteria used for evaluation: quality, machine availability, performance, operating cost and investment cost. The text says they comprise nine sub-criteria but lists eleven: rework rate, scrap rate, breakdown rate, changeover time, production speed, micro stoppage frequency, energy consumption, labor cost, maintenance cost, purchasing price and installation cost. AHP assigns weights to eleven criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP and TOPSIS are combined for injection molding machine selection">
  <data key="d0">AHP and TOPSIS are combined for injection molding machine selection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The main principle of the suggested approach is based on combination of two models, the Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) (7) and Technique for Order of Preference by Similarity to Ideal Solution (TOPSIS) (8, 9) methodologies to facilitate decision-making in injection molding machine selection."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision-Making Framework for Injection Molding">
  <data key="d0">Decision-Making Framework for Injection Molding</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Structured framework that the article introduces for managers and technical experts in the injection molding sector. It integrates AHP weighting and TOPSIS ranking to select the most suitable machine based on predetermined criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
