<node id="Injection molding uses pressures from hundreds to thousands of bars">
  <data key="d0">Injection molding uses pressures from hundreds to thousands of bars</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection molding is an industrial technique, involves injecting plastic material into a mold cavity under high pressure, which can range from hundreds to thousands of bars (2).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injected plastic cools and solidifies taking the mold shape">
  <data key="d0">Injected plastic cools and solidifies taking the mold shape</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Once injected, the plastic cools and solidifies within the mold cavity, taking the shape of the mold and producing a specific plastic product (10, 11).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection molding machine comprises hopper, heating, injection and clamping units">
  <data key="d0">Injection molding machine comprises hopper, heating, injection and clamping units</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">These include a hopper for feeding the raw plastic material, a heating unit consisting of a barrel, screw, and heating resistances to melt the material, and an injection unit responsible for injecting the molten material into the mold cavity. Additionally, the machine features a clamping unit to securely hold the mold halves together during the injection and cooling phases (12, 13).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clamping unit holds mold halves together under pressure">
  <data key="d0">Clamping unit holds mold halves together under pressure</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The clamping Unit (1, 14) is responsible for holding the fixed and the moved side of the mold together under pressure during the injection and cooling process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection unit screw pushes molten material into the mold">
  <data key="d0">Injection unit screw pushes molten material into the mold</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In contrast, the Injection Unit involves a screw mechanism that pushes the molten material through a heated barrel and into the mold under high pressure (15).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP was pioneered by Thomas Saaty">
  <data key="d0">AHP was pioneered by Thomas Saaty</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) is a systematic decision-making approach pioneered by Thomas Saaty (16).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP synthesizes pairwise judgments to determine priorities">
  <data key="d0">AHP synthesizes pairwise judgments to determine priorities</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">AHP involves pairwise comparisons between criteria and alternatives based on subjective judgments, which are then synthesized to determine their relative importance or priority (17).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP is widely applied in engineering, management and operations research">
  <data key="d0">AHP is widely applied in engineering, management and operations research</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">AHP finds extensive application across diverse fields such as engineering, management, and operations research, aiding in effective decision-making in scenarios characterized by multiple conflicting objectives (18, 19).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consistency ratio verifies pairwise comparison accuracy">
  <data key="d0">Consistency ratio verifies pairwise comparison accuracy</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">After completing the pairwise comparison, the subsequent step involves verifying the accuracy of the comparison by using the consistency ratio as an indicator (22, 23).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP weights derived by aggregating pairwise judgments">
  <data key="d0">AHP weights derived by aggregating pairwise judgments</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This involves multiplying the pairwise comparison judgments and aggregating them to derive the relative weights (21).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pairwise comparisons scale the strength of importance between criteria">
  <data key="d0">Pairwise comparisons scale the strength of importance between criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The next step involves conducting pairwise comparisons between criteria to evaluate their relative importance. This is achieved by scaling the strength of importance for each pairwise comparison (20).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Problem Structuring">
  <data key="d0">Problem Structuring</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">First AHP step: establishing the overall goal of the problem and listing the criteria and the sub-criteria associated with the main objective, forming a hierarchical structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weighted Score Calculation">
  <data key="d0">Weighted Score Calculation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">AHP step that calculates weighted scores for each criterion and alternative by multiplying and aggregating pairwise comparison judgments to derive relative weights.&lt;SEP&gt;Step that sums the elements of each row of the pairwise comparison matrix to get weighted sums. Each sum is then divided by the total of all weighted sums to obtain normalized weights that represent the relative importance of each criterion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP Validation">
  <data key="d0">AHP Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">AHP step computing each alternative's overall score by multiplying criteria priority weights by alternative performance scores and summing them, followed by sensitivity analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426442</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grey Relational Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Grey Relational Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">GRA; MCDM method.&lt;SEP&gt;Method used to solve multiple attribute decision-making problems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ELECTRE">
  <data key="d0">ELECTRE</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Elimination and Choice Expressing Reality; MCDM method.&lt;SEP&gt;Family of outranking methods for multiple criteria decision analysis, founded on the outranking approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Simple Additive Weighting">
  <data key="d0">Simple Additive Weighting</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">SAW; MCDM method.&lt;SEP&gt;Multiple criteria decision analysis method that Kaliszewski and Podkopaev present as a metamodel.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
