  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref (32) ELECTRE">
  <data key="d0">Ref (32) ELECTRE</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (32) for ELECTRE.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref (33) SAW">
  <data key="d0">Ref (33) SAW</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (33) for Simple Additive Weighting.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref (34) WPM">
  <data key="d0">Ref (34) WPM</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (34) for the Weighted Product Model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hrițuc et al. (35)">
  <data key="d0">Hrițuc et al. (35)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Used AHP to select among three injection machine technologies; vertical injection underweight found most suitable.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Al Kaabneh et al. (36)">
  <data key="d0">Al Kaabneh et al. (36)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Developed a multi-agent system using AHP to aid machine selection for scheduling, considering quality, time and cost over eleven alternatives; also cited (as Al Khannan et al.) for combined AHP and Taguchi design in plastic molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ivan et al. (37)">
  <data key="d0">Ivan et al. (37)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Used AHP to choose among 3D printing, Fused Deposition Modelling and Selective Laser Sintering; concluded Selective Laser Sintering is best.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Budiman et al. (38)">
  <data key="d0">Budiman et al. (38)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Applied AHP with four criteria and nine sub-criteria to choose the best secondhand injection machine from three alternatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TOPSIS selects the most favorable alternative considering multiple criteria">
  <data key="d0">TOPSIS selects the most favorable alternative considering multiple criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">TOPSIS ... serves as multi-criteria decision-making (MCDM) tool aimed at selecting the most favorable alternative from a given set, taking into account multiple criteria (24).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TOPSIS originated from Hwang and Yoon in 1981">
  <data key="d0">TOPSIS originated from Hwang and Yoon in 1981</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Originating from the work of Hwang and Yoon in 1981 (25), TOPSIS evaluates alternatives by assessing their proximity to the ideal solution and their deviation from the worst solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision making is selecting among available courses of action">
  <data key="d0">Decision making is selecting among available courses of action</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Decision making is the process of selecting from among two or more available courses of action (28).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Selective Laser Sintering is the best process choice">
  <data key="d0">Selective Laser Sintering is the best process choice</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Ivan et al. (37) conclude that the Selective Laser Sintering process is the best choice according to six evaluated criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertical injection underweight is the most suitable machine">
  <data key="d0">Vertical injection underweight is the most suitable machine</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Hrițuc et al. (35) found via AHP that vertical injection underweight is the suitable solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weighted Sum Method">
  <data key="d0">Weighted Sum Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Aggregation step that multiplies the priority weights of criteria by the performance scores of alternatives for each criterion and then sums the products.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-criteria analysis method covered in San Cristóbal Mateo's 2012 chapter on multi criteria analysis in the renewable energy industry.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Selective Laser Sintering">
  <data key="d0">Selective Laser Sintering</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Manufacturing process evaluated by Ivan et al. (37) with AHP. It was judged the best choice against six criteria: dimensional, mechanical, process cost, process time and post process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fused Deposition Modelling">
  <data key="d0">Fused Deposition Modelling</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Manufacturing process that Ivan et al. (37) compared as an alternative using AHP.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ideal Solution">
  <data key="d0">Ideal Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">In TOPSIS, the solution with the maximum values for each criterion. Alternatives are ranked by their proximity to the ideal solution and their distance from the anti-ideal (worst) solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference point in TOPSIS. Best and worst distances from the ideal solution are computed to rank the alternatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MCDM comprises various methods including AHP, fuzzy AHP, TOPSIS, GRA, PROMETHEE, ELECTRE, SAW and WPM">
  <data key="d0">MCDM comprises various methods including AHP, fuzzy AHP, TOPSIS, GRA, PROMETHEE, ELECTRE, SAW and WPM</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">According to the literature, MDCM regroups various methods, including, AHP, fuzzy AHP (29), TOPSIS, Grey Relational Analysis (GRA) (30), Preference Ranking Organization Method for Enrichment Evaluation (PROMETHEE) (31), Elimination and Choice Expressing Reality (ELECTRE) (32), Simple Additive Weighting (SAW) (33) and Weighted Product Model (WPM) (34).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP combined with Taguchi design selects the best experiment for quality in plastic molding">
  <data key="d0">AHP combined with Taguchi design selects the best experiment for quality in plastic molding</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"Al Khannan et al. (36) developed a combined AHP and Taguchi experimental design to select the best experiment to get the best totally quality in the plastic molding process." The citation label in this sentence (Al Khannan) differs from the earlier label for reference (36) (Al Kaabneh).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Al Khannan et al. (36)">
  <data key="d0">Al Khannan et al. (36)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (36). Developed a combined AHP and Taguchi experimental design to select the best of twenty-seven experiments for total quality in plastic molding, assessing volumetric shrinkage, warpage, sink mark, residual stress and cooling time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Nagahanumaiah et al. (39)">
  <data key="d0">Nagahanumaiah et al. (39)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (39). Applied fuzzy-AHP to evaluate rapid tooling manufacturability using mold feature manufacturability, elements compatibility and cost effectiveness criteria, and AHP fuzzy-control to evaluate geometrical elements of the model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Xin et al. (40)">
  <data key="d0">Xin et al. (40)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (40). Multi-objective optimization of injection molding process parameters using methods including GRA-TOPSIS to predict warpage and shrinkage and find the optimum solution from the optimal front.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Guevara et al. (41)">
  <data key="d0">Guevara et al. (41)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (41). Assessed the plastic injection machine maintenance system using the TOPSIS method to aid management decisions concerning each machine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moayyedian et al. (42)">
  <data key="d0">Moayyedian et al. (42)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (42). Combined Taguchi methodology, fuzzy AHP and TOPSIS to identify the optimal choice for the most favorable moldability index in injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Source (43)">
  <data key="d0">Source (43)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as (43). Applied AHP-TOPSIS to selecting optimal tooling for manufacturing, such as EDM electrodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GRA-TOPSIS">
  <data key="d0">GRA-TOPSIS</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Combined grey relational analysis and TOPSIS method used to find optimum solutions from an optimal front.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rapid Tooling Manufacturability">
  <data key="d0">Rapid Tooling Manufacturability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Manufacturability of rapid tooling evaluated during project development.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Objective Optimization Of Injection Molding Parameters">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Objective Optimization Of Injection Molding Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Optimization of injection molding process parameters considering multiple objectives such as warpage and shrinkage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Maintenance">
  <data key="d0">Machine Maintenance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Maintenance system of plastic injection machines assessed with MCDM methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Moldability Index">
  <data key="d0">Moldability Index</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Index measuring moldability in injection molding technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Few studies integrate AHP and TOPSIS for injection molding machine selection">
  <data key="d0">Few studies integrate AHP and TOPSIS for injection molding machine selection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "However, only a limited number of studies have integrated both AHP and TOPSIS methodologies to inform decision-making in injection molding machine selection processes during the initial setting."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP-TOPSIS has been applied to selecting manufacturing tooling such as EDM electrodes">
  <data key="d0">AHP-TOPSIS has been applied to selecting manufacturing tooling such as EDM electrodes</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "While the methodology has been extensively explored in other domains such as marketing, or in selecting optimal tooling for manufacturing, such as EDM electrodes for manufacturing as highlighted in source (43), its application within the realm of injection molding remains underexplored."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP Fuzzy-Control">
  <data key="d0">AHP Fuzzy-Control</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">AHP-based fuzzy-control approach that Nagahanumaiah et al. (39) used to evaluate the geometrical elements of the model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Warpage">
  <data key="d0">Warpage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection molding defect. Al Khannan et al. (36) assessed it as a quality criterion, and Xin et al. (40) predicted it with GRA-TOPSIS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shrinkage">
  <data key="d0">Shrinkage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection molding defect. Al Khannan et al. (36) assessed volumetric shrinkage as a criterion, and Xin et al. (40) predicted shrinkage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AHP-TOPSIS is underexplored in injection molding">
  <data key="d0">AHP-TOPSIS is underexplored in injection molding</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "There is a scarcity of research dedicated to the utilization of AHP-TOPSIS specifically in the context of injection molding processes." The text adds that its application within injection molding "remains underexplored".</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Existing AHP-TOPSIS studies lack detailed calculations">
  <data key="d0">Existing AHP-TOPSIS studies lack detailed calculations</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "Many existing studies that combine AHP and TOPSIS methodologies do not provide comprehensive or detailed calculations of the combined methods." The text says this undermines the transparency and rigor of the decision-making process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decision frameworks rarely consider economic and performance criteria simultaneously">
  <data key="d0">Decision frameworks rarely consider economic and performance criteria simultaneously</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "Another significant gap in the literature is the absence of simultaneous consideration of both economic considerations and performance metrics in decision-making processes." The economic criteria include production, material, labor and overhead costs. The performance metrics include cycle time, efficiency, reliability and maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MCDM studies in injection molding cover machine selection, material processability, parameter setting and maintenance">
  <data key="d0">MCDM studies in injection molding cover machine selection, material processability, parameter setting and maintenance</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "The literature review identified studies employing MCDM methods in the field of injection molding processes, which addressed multiple aspects, beginning with the selection the optimal injection machines..., studying the optimal processability of chosen plastic materials, defining optimal setting parameters, and applying MCDM to select the best maintenance approach for machines."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid AHP-TOPSIS Machine Selection Approach">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid AHP-TOPSIS Machine Selection Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Five-step methodology proposed in the paper that combines AHP for criteria weighting with TOPSIS for final ranking of injection molding machine alternatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Positive and Negative Ideal Solutions">
  <data key="d0">Positive and Negative Ideal Solutions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference solutions computed in TOPSIS to establish the final order of the best alternative.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Interviews and Literature Review">
  <data key="d0">Expert Interviews and Literature Review</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Interview sessions with field experts combined with an extensive literature review, used to identify factors associated with injection molding machines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Criteria Specifications Data">
  <data key="d0">Machine Criteria Specifications Data</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Data collected from an automotive industry workshop in northern Morocco on three injection molding machines (ARB205T/ARB200T/ARB250T, HAIT320T), covering investment cost, quality rate, performance rate, availability rate and operating cost sub-criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Operating Cost">
  <data key="d0">Operating Cost</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Criterion comprising hourly energy consumption, labor cost and maintenance cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion with a weight of 0.142. Its sub-criteria are energy consumption per hour, labor cost and maintenance cost.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the five main criteria for injection molding machine selection, linked to the energy consumption, labor cost and maintenance cost definitions. In the expert pairwise comparison (Table 4), it was rated 2 against investment cost and performance rate, 1/3 against quality rate and availability rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Main criterion with weight 0.142, comprising energy consumption per hour, labor cost and maintenance cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Criterion with three sub-criteria: energy consumption (52 kWh per hour), labor cost (1 € per 100 pieces) and maintenance cost (8 K€). It is unchanged across all scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARBURG">
  <data key="d0">ARBURG</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine brand of two of the evaluated injection molding machines (ARB200T and ARB250T, manufactured 2013).&lt;SEP&gt;Brand of two of the alternative injection molding machines (570 C 2000-800 and 630 S 2500-800), both manufactured in 2013.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAITIAN">
  <data key="d0">HAITIAN</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine brand of the HAIT320T injection molding machine (MA3200II/1700, manufactured 2015, 3200 kN clamping force).&lt;SEP&gt;Brand of the MA3200II/1700 injection molding machine, manufactured in 2015.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARB200T">
  <data key="d0">ARB200T</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">ARBURG injection molding machine (reference 570 C 2000-800, manufactured 2013, 2000 kN clamping force, 570 mm distance between bars). It is one of the alternatives evaluated in the paper. Listed sub-criteria: machine cost 190,000 €, installation cost 15,000 €, scrap rate 0.50%, rework rate 0.80%, speed loss rate 0.70%, breakdown rate 3%, energy consumption 42 kWh/hour and maintenance cost 12,000 €.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked second in scenarios 1 and 2. It ranked third in scenario 3 (Pi 0.2779), where its score decreased by 21%.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked second by TOPSIS with a score of 0.54278. In scenario 1 it closely aligns with HAIT320T, in scenario 2 its preference falls by about 4%, and in scenario 3 its score drops by 21% and it ranks third.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARB205T">
  <data key="d0">ARB205T</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Injection molding machine alternative listed in Table 1. Machine cost 210,000 €, installation cost 17,000 €, scrap rate 0.50%, rework rate 0.80%, speed loss rate 0.50%, changeover rate 1.20% (performance) and 1.50% (availability), breakdown rate 2.50%, energy consumption 47 kWh/hour and maintenance cost 14,000 €. It likely corresponds to the ARB250T in Table 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARB250T">
  <data key="d0">ARB250T</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">ARBURG injection molding machine listed in Table 2 (reference 630 S 2500-800, manufactured 2013, 2500 kN clamping force, 630 mm distance between bars). It is one of the three evaluated alternatives.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked first in scenarios 1 and 2 (Pi 0.5760 and 0.5403). It ranked second in scenario 3, where its score decreased by 23%.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked best by TOPSIS with a score of 0.62318. In sensitivity scenario 1 its score drops from 0.6231 to 0.5760, in scenario 2 its preference falls by about 8%, and in scenario 3 its score drops by 23% and it falls to second place.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAIT320T">
  <data key="d0">HAIT320T</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">HAITIAN injection molding machine (reference MA3200II/1700, manufactured 2015, 3200 kN clamping force, 680 mm distance between bars). Listed sub-criteria: machine cost 176,000 €, installation cost 15,000 €, scrap rate 0.60%, rework rate 1.00%, changeover rate 2.40%, breakdown rate 5%, energy consumption 52 kWh/hour and maintenance cost 8,000 €.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked third in scenarios 1 and 2. It ranked first in scenario 3 (Pi 0.5838) after combined improvements in scrap rate and breakdown rate, with its score rising from 37% to 58%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weighted Decision Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Weighted Decision Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Global weighted decision matrix computed by multiplying the initial matrix inputs by the AHP-derived criteria weights.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARBURG 570 C 2000-800">
  <data key="d0">ARBURG 570 C 2000-800</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">An ARBURG injection molding machine from 2013. Its clamping force is 2000 kN, the distance between bars is 570 mm and the screw diameter is 45 mm. It produces 46 kg/h with a maximum injection volume of 318 cm3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARBURG 630 S 2500-800">
  <data key="d0">ARBURG 630 S 2500-800</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">An ARBURG injection molding machine from 2013. Its clamping force is 2500 kN, the distance between bars is 630 mm and the screw diameter is 45 mm. It produces 46 kg/h with a maximum injection volume of 318 cm3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
