<node id="Pairwise comparisons use a 1 to 9 importance scale">
  <data key="d0">Pairwise comparisons use a 1 to 9 importance scale</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">According to the literature, a scale of (often 1 to 9) is used to assign values that represent the strength of importance or preference for each criterion or sub-criterion (15).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scrap rate is the proportion of parts discarded during production">
  <data key="d0">Scrap rate is the proportion of parts discarded during production</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Scrap rate: it refers to the proportion of parts that are discarded or scrapped during the production process (44).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rework rate is the percentage of products requiring additional work due to defects">
  <data key="d0">Rework rate is the percentage of products requiring additional work due to defects</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Rework rate: it's the percentage of products that require additional work after initial production due to defects (45).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low speed is the deviation from the expected cycle time">
  <data key="d0">Low speed is the deviation from the expected cycle time</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Low speed: it's the loss of speed in production, indicating the deviation from the expected cycle time (46).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breakdown rate is the frequency of machine failures causing unplanned downtime">
  <data key="d0">Breakdown rate is the frequency of machine failures causing unplanned downtime</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Breakdown rate: it signifies the frequency at which machines experience failures or malfunctions, leading to unplanned downtime during production (47).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Changeover rate is the duration needed to change a production setup">
  <data key="d0">Changeover rate is the duration needed to change a production setup</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Changeover rate: The duration needed to change a production setup from the current product configuration to another (48).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Energy consumption is the energy used by the machine during production">
  <data key="d0">Energy consumption is the energy used by the machine during production</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Energy consumption: it's the amount of energy used by the machine during the production (49).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Labor cost is the expenditure for employing workers to operate the machine">
  <data key="d0">Labor cost is the expenditure for employing workers to operate the machine</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Labor cost: it represents the expenditure associated with employing workers to operate the machine, including wages, benefits, and other related expenses (50).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426446</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rework Rate">
  <data key="d0">Rework Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sub-criterion defined as the percentage of products that require additional work after initial production due to defects.&lt;SEP&gt;Quality rate sub-criterion with a local weight of 0.200 and a global weight of 0.086. ARB 205T and ARB 200T score 5 on it, and HAIT 320T scores 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Quality rate criterion with a weight of 0.086. Its weighted values are 0.0530 for ARB 205T, 0.0530 for ARB 200T and 0.0424 for HAIT 320T.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low Speed">
  <data key="d0">Low Speed</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sub-criterion defined as the loss of speed in production, meaning the deviation from the expected cycle time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Micro Stoppage Rate">
  <data key="d0">Micro Stoppage Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sub-criterion defined as the frequency of short interruptions during planned production. In the study, it covers breakdowns lasting less than 5 minutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance rate sub-criterion, labeled 'Change O rate' in Table 8, with a local weight of 0.333 and a global weight of 0.025. ARB 205T scores 5, ARB 200T scores 4, and HAIT 320T scores 3.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance rate criterion with a weight of 0.025. Its weighted values are 0.0174 for ARB 205T, 0.0139 for ARB 200T and 0.0104 for HAIT 320T.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breakdown Rate">
  <data key="d0">Breakdown Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sub-criterion with an overall weight of 20.9%, ranked second among the sub-criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Sub-criterion defined as the frequency at which machines experience failures or malfunctions, leading to unplanned downtime.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability sub-criterion with local weight 0.856 and global weight 0.209 (20.9%), second most significant factor.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability rate sub-criterion measuring machine breakdown percentage; 5% initially for HAIT 320T.&lt;SEP&gt;Selection criterion for machine breakdown frequency. In scenario 2, a 2% improvement raised HAIT320T performance by about 4% but did not change the ranking.&lt;SEP&gt;Second most important sub-criterion with 20.9% of total weight; affects the availability rate and machine reliability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Changeover Rate">
  <data key="d0">Changeover Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sub-criterion defined as the duration needed to change a production setup from the current product configuration to another.&lt;SEP&gt;Availability rate sub-criterion with a local weight of 0.144 and a global weight of 0.035. ARB 205T scores 4, ARB 200T scores 5, and HAIT 320T scores 4.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Energy Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Energy Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Sub-criterion defined as the amount of energy used by the machine during production.&lt;SEP&gt;Sub-criterion listed among the criteria considered in machine selection.&lt;SEP&gt;MANET constraint due to limited node battery power that security approaches must minimize.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Labor Cost">
  <data key="d0">Labor Cost</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operating cost sub-criterion compared pairwise with energy consumption and maintenance cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Sub-criterion defined as the expenditure for employing workers to operate the machine, including wages, benefits and related expenses.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating cost sub-criterion with a local weight of 0.133 and a global weight of 0.019. All three alternatives score 5 on it.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating cost criterion with a weight of 0.019. Its weighted value is 0.0164 for all three alternatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maintenance Cost">
  <data key="d0">Maintenance Cost</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operating cost sub-criterion with an overall weight of 14%. It is judged more important than energy consumption and labor cost in the pairwise comparisons.&lt;SEP&gt;Sub-criterion defined as the expenditure for keeping the machine in proper working condition, covering repairs and spare part consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating cost sub-criterion with local weight 0.655 and global weight 0.093.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating cost criterion with a weight of 0.093. HAIT 320T has the highest weighted value on this criterion, 0.1139.&lt;SEP&gt;Sub-criterion in the machine selection evaluation. The text states that maintenance cost represents 0.9% of the total criteria weight.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Random Consistency Index">
  <data key="d0">Random Consistency Index</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference index (RI) that depends on the number of criteria in the hierarchy. A value of 1.12 is used for five criteria, as listed in Table 7.&lt;SEP&gt;Table of RI values by matrix size (e.g., 0.58 for 3, 0.90 for 4, up to 1.49 for 10) used to check pairwise comparison consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Energy Consumption Per Hour">
  <data key="d0">Energy Consumption Per Hour</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operating cost sub-criterion compared pairwise with labor cost and maintenance cost.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating cost criterion with a weight of 0.030. Its weighted values are 0.0281 for ARB 205T, 0.0281 for ARB 200T and 0.0211 for HAIT 320T.&lt;SEP&gt;Operating cost sub-criterion with a local weight of 0.211 and a global weight of 0.030.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A consistency ratio below 0.1 indicates consistent pairwise judgments">
  <data key="d0">A consistency ratio below 0.1 indicates consistent pairwise judgments</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "If the CR value is less than 0.1, the judgement according to the matric comparison is considered consistent (15)."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Consensus">
  <data key="d0">Expert Consensus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Source of the judgments behind the pairwise comparison tables. The comparison tables are described as providing insights drawn from expert consensus and analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normalized Weights">
  <data key="d0">Normalized Weights</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weights obtained by dividing each criterion's weighted sum by the sum of all weighted sums. They represent the relative importance of each criterion. The final values are 0.431 for quality rate, 0.245 for availability rate, 0.142 for operating cost, 0.108 for investment cost and 0.074 for performance rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weighted Normalized Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Weighted Normalized Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrix obtained by multiplying the normalized decision matrix by the vector of global criterion weights (rp_ij = r_ij * p_j, Equation 4).&lt;SEP&gt;Matrix used together with expert validation and pairwise comparison to classify and weight the eleven sub-criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARB 205T">
  <data key="d0">ARB 205T</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine alternative evaluated in the TOPSIS decision matrix (e.g., machine cost score 3, scrap rate 5, breakdown rate 5).&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked first, with S+ = 0.0450, S- = 0.0744 and Si = 0.62318. The text also refers to it as ARB 250T and reports a 62% deviation from the worst solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked first in Table 12, with S+ = 0.0450, S- = 0.0744, S+ + S- = 0.1194 and Si = 0.62318. In Scenario 1, the text states that "the ARB250T has decreased from a score of 0.6231 to 0.5760". This apparently refers to ARB 205T, the alternative whose initial score was 0.6231.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ARB 200T">
  <data key="d0">ARB 200T</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine alternative evaluated in the TOPSIS decision matrix (e.g., machine cost score 4, scrap rate 5, breakdown rate 4).&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked second, with S+ = 0.0459, S- = 0.0545 and Si = 0.54278, corresponding to a 54% deviation from the worst solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked second with S+ = 0.0459, S- = 0.0545 and score Si = 0.54278.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HAIT 320T">
  <data key="d0">HAIT 320T</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine alternative evaluated in the TOPSIS decision matrix (e.g., machine cost score 7, scrap rate 4, maintenance cost 8).&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked last. Its three main criteria weights are adjusted in the sensitivity verification.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative ranked third with S+ = 0.0745, S- = 0.0447 and score Si = 0.37503; initial data include 176 K€ machine cost, 15 K€ installation cost, 0.60% scrap, 1.00% rework, 0.70% speed loss, 2.40% micro stoppage, 5% breakdown, 1.50% changeover, 52 kWh energy, 1 €/100pc labor and 8 K€ maintenance cost. In Scenario 1 its rank becomes closely aligned with ARB 200T, about 42% far from the worst solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Machine alternative initially ranked third with a score of 0.37503. It gains about 5% preference in scenario 1 and about 4% in scenario 2. In scenario 3 it becomes the top choice, its score rising from 37% to 58%, a 21% improvement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Cost">
  <data key="d0">Machine Cost</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Investment cost criterion with a weight of 0.093.&lt;SEP&gt;Investment cost sub-criterion with a local weight of 0.856 and a global weight of 0.093. ARB 205T scores 3, ARB 200T scores 4, and HAIT 320T scores 7.&lt;SEP&gt;One of the eleven selection criteria in the AHP framework for choosing among ARB250T, ARB200T and HAIT320T.&lt;SEP&gt;Sub-criterion in the machine selection evaluation. The text states that machine cost represents 0.9% of the total criteria weight.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Installation Cost">
  <data key="d0">Installation Cost</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Investment cost sub-criterion with a local weight of 0.144 and a global weight of 0.016. ARB 205T scores 2, ARB 200T scores 3, and HAIT 320T scores 3.&lt;SEP&gt;Investment cost criterion with a weight of 0.016. Its weighted values are 0.0067 for ARB 205T, 0.0100 for ARB 200T and 0.0100 for HAIT 320T.&lt;SEP&gt;Least important of the eleven sub-criteria, accounting for 1.6% of the total weight.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Speed Loss Rate">
  <data key="d0">Speed Loss Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance rate sub-criterion with a local weight of 0.667 and a global weight of 0.049. ARB 205T scores 5, ARB 200T scores 4, and HAIT 320T scores 4.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance rate criterion with a weight of 0.049. Its weighted values are 0.0326 for ARB 205T, 0.0261 for ARB 200T and 0.0261 for HAIT 320T.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initial Decision Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Initial Decision Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">First TOPSIS step. Each machine alternative is evaluated against the established criteria on a standard scale from 1 to 9. The results are reported in Table 10.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TOPSIS Assessment Scale">
  <data key="d0">TOPSIS Assessment Scale</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Numerical rating scale used to build the initial TOPSIS decision matrix (Table 9). It ranges from 1 (Completely uninteresting) through 5 (Interesting) to 8 (Extremely interesting) and higher.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Best And Worst Solution Identification">
  <data key="d0">Best And Worst Solution Identification</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">TOPSIS step that calculates the best and worst solutions from the weighted normalized matrix and then ranks the alternatives. The calculation depends on whether a criterion j is to be maximized.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Global Criteria Weights">
  <data key="d0">Global Criteria Weights</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Global weights of the sub-criteria (Table 8), obtained from the main criteria weights and the local sub-criteria weights. They serve as the weight vector p_j in the TOPSIS weighted normalized matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weighted Normalized Decision Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Weighted Normalized Decision Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Matrix of criteria values that have been normalized and then weighted for each alternative (Table 11). It is used to determine the best (A+) and worst (A-) values for each criterion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Separation Measure">
  <data key="d0">Separation Measure</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Euclidean distance of each alternative from the positive ideal solution (S_i+) and from the negative ideal solution (S_i-), computed with Equations 7 and 8.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relative Closeness Ranking">
  <data key="d0">Relative Closeness Ranking</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Ranking score S_i = S_i- / (S_i+ + S_i-), defined in Equation 9 and used to rank the machine alternatives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sensitivity Verification">
  <data key="d0">Sensitivity Verification</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Final validation phase in which the three main weights associated with the HAIT 320T machine are adjusted to assess their influence on the ranking. The process produces three distinct scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Break Down Rate">
  <data key="d0">Break Down Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Availability rate criterion with a weight of 0.209.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Change Over Rate">
  <data key="d0">Change Over Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Availability rate criterion with a weight of 0.035. Its weighted values are 0.0187 for ARB 205T, 0.0233 for ARB 200T and 0.0187 for HAIT 320T.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario 1">
  <data key="d0">Scenario 1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario in which the scrap rate is improved by 0.2% (from 0.60% to 0.40%) while other criteria remain unchanged.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario 2">
  <data key="d0">Scenario 2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario in which the breakdown percentage is improved by 2% (from 5% to 3%) while other criteria remain unchanged.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario 3">
  <data key="d0">Scenario 3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario in which both the scrap rate improves by 0.2% and the breakdown rate improves by 2%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rankings are sensitive to scrap rate and breakdown rate improvements">
  <data key="d0">Rankings are sensitive to scrap rate and breakdown rate improvements</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Combining the improvement of the scrap rate and the breakdown rate by 0.2% and 2% respectively has led to a complete change in the ranking of the machines."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011</data>
