<node id="Minor quality improvements substantially influence machine selection">
  <data key="d0">Minor quality improvements substantially influence machine selection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "HAIT320T model, by more than 5%, resulting from a mere 0.2% variation in the scrap rate, demonstrates the profound impact of quality improvement on machine selection." The text adds that even minor enhancements in quality can substantially influence the perceived value and choice of a machine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Breakdown rate improvement alone does not change the machine ranking">
  <data key="d0">Breakdown rate improvement alone does not change the machine ranking</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "In the second scenario, even the breakdown percentage has improved by 2%, there is no significate impact on the final rank of the machines." The improvement still raised HAIT320T performance by about 4%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous improvement of scrap and breakdown rates enhances productivity and competitiveness">
  <data key="d0">Continuous improvement of scrap and breakdown rates enhances productivity and competitiveness</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "This detailed analysis underscores the importance of continuously improving the scrap rate and breakdown rate to enhance overall productivity and competitiveness."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Closeness Coefficient Pi">
  <data key="d0">Closeness Coefficient Pi</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">TOPSIS relative closeness score, computed from the separation measures S+ and S-, that is used to rank the alternatives. Values include 0.5760 for ARB250T in scenario 1 and 0.5838 for HAIT320T in scenario 3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scrap rate and quality rate have the greatest influence on machine choice">
  <data key="d0">Scrap rate and quality rate have the greatest influence on machine choice</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "It is concluded that the quality rate combined with the 'scrap rate' holds the greatest influence on the choice of machine, followed by the availability rate, particularly affected by the breakdown rate."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Validation">
  <data key="d0">Expert Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Expert-based validation step used together with pairwise comparison to rank the criteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small quality improvements significantly influence machine selection">
  <data key="d0">Small quality improvements significantly influence machine selection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding from scenario 1: "The HAIT320T model sees a notable 5% preference boost due to this minor quality change, highlighting how even small improvements in quality can significantly influence machine selection."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426448</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
