  <data key="d0">Cost Breakdown</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Key cost-related criterion whose variation, examined in the validation scenarios, can influence the final ranking of injection molding machines.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ideal and Anti-Ideal Solutions">
  <data key="d0">Ideal and Anti-Ideal Solutions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference solutions in TOPSIS against which each machine's performance is compared to determine its relative suitability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426459</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scrap Rate">
  <data key="d0">Scrap Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scrap Rate is a quality sub-criterion used in the multi-criteria model for selecting injection molding machines. It is defined as the proportion, or percentage, of parts that are discarded or scrapped during the production process. It sits under the quality rate criterion. Within that criterion it has a local weight of 0.800, and its global weight is 0.345, about 34.5% of the total weight.

Scrap Rate is the most significant factor in choosing the best machine. It carries the highest overall weight of any sub-criterion, and together with the broader quality rate criterion it has the greatest influence on the final choice. For the HAIT 320T machine, the initial scrap rate was 0.60%.

Because of its importance, Scrap Rate was examined in the sensitivity analyses of the model, alongside cost breakdown. It was also tested in the validation scenarios, which showed that changes in its value can alter the final ranking of the injection molding machines. In scenario 1, a 0.2% change in scrap rate shifted the HAIT 320T's score by more than 5%. This shows how strongly improvements in quality affect the outcome of the selection process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426462</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
