<node id="A Hybrid Probabilistic Modeling Approach to Analyzing Overstock Risk in Inventory Management: Integrating Bayesian Network Inference with Fuzzy Logic">
  <data key="d0">A Hybrid Probabilistic Modeling Approach to Analyzing Overstock Risk in Inventory Management: Integrating Bayesian Network Inference with Fuzzy Logic</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read. It proposes a hybrid methodology that assesses and manages overstock risk in inventory management by combining two techniques. Bayesian networks delineate the causal relationships among factors contributing to overstocking. Fuzzy logic computes the conditional probabilities of the network nodes. The methodology is validated using three axioms proposed by J. Wang et al.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8153b8d12e35b15bf93bd763cdd0b2f2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">M3A_24_Book_of_Abstracts-31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Overstock Risk">
  <data key="d0">Overstock Risk</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The risk of holding excess inventory, which must be balanced against storage costs. It is the core problem addressed by the hybrid methodology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8153b8d12e35b15bf93bd763cdd0b2f2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">M3A_24_Book_of_Abstracts-31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wang et al.'s three axioms validate the hybrid methodology">
  <data key="d0">Wang et al.'s three axioms validate the hybrid methodology</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The methodology's effectiveness is confirmed by validating three axioms proposed by J. Wang et al., which ensure its reliability and accuracy in managing overstock risks."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8153b8d12e35b15bf93bd763cdd0b2f2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">M3A_24_Book_of_Abstracts-31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
