<node id="Three Axioms of J. Wang et al.">
  <data key="d0">Three Axioms of J. Wang et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Set of three validation axioms proposed by J. Wang et al. in their 2010 Bayesian network maintenance planning paper. The hybrid overstock risk paper validates them to confirm its methodology's reliability and accuracy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8153b8d12e35b15bf93bd763cdd0b2f2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">M3A_24_Book_of_Abstracts-31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Bayesian Network and Fuzzy Logic Methodology">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Bayesian Network and Fuzzy Logic Methodology</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Novel hybrid methodology proposed in the overstock risk paper. Bayesian networks model the causal factors of overstocking. Fuzzy logic computes the conditional probabilities of the network nodes, which incorporates uncertainty in inventory decisions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8153b8d12e35b15bf93bd763cdd0b2f2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">M3A_24_Book_of_Abstracts-31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uncertainty in Inventory Management Decisions">
  <data key="d0">Uncertainty in Inventory Management Decisions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Inherent uncertainty in inventory management decisions. Fuzzy logic incorporates it to give a more nuanced and flexible prediction of overstock situations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8153b8d12e35b15bf93bd763cdd0b2f2-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">M3A_24_Book_of_Abstracts-31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791426577</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
