<node id="Decentralized Authentication Mechanism for Mobile Ad hoc Networks">
  <data key="d0">Decentralized Authentication Mechanism for Mobile Ad hoc Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Article published in Infocommunications Journal by Hafida Khalfaoui, Abderrazak Farchane and Said Safi; proposes a decentralized authentication mechanism for MANET based on fog computing and blockchain, and evaluates its security, motivated by community networks during Covid 19.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, published in Infocommunications Journal, September 2022, Volume XIV, Number 3. It proposes and evaluates a blockchain-based decentralized authentication mechanism for MANET nodes using Ethereum smart contracts and fog nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Article by Hafida Khalfaoui, Abderrazak Farchane and Said Safi, published in Infocommunications Journal, September 2022, Volume XIV, Number 3 (DOI 10.36244/ICJ.2022.3.4). It proposes a decentralized authentication mechanism for Mobile Ad hoc Networks based on fog computing technology and the blockchain concept. The work is motivated by Covid 19 and by community networks such as Zenzeleni that serve communities without commercial service providers. Its evaluation shows that the mechanism satisfies diverse security requirements and strongly protects networks from attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, published in Infocommunications Journal (September 2022, Volume XIV, Number 3). It reviews MANET attacks, blockchain technology, fog computing, and the state of the art in blockchain-based authentication for MANETs.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, published in Infocommunications Journal, September 2022, Volume XIV, Number 3. It proposes a distributed blockchain-based authentication mechanism for MANET using fog computing, with a device layer (admins and devices) and a fog layer.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, published in Infocommunications Journal, September 2022, Volume XIV, Number 3. It proposes a blockchain-based decentralized authentication mechanism for MANET nodes using Ethereum smart contracts, with device registration and authentication phases, implemented with Remix IDE, Hardhat, Ganache-CLI, ReactJS and Metamask.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="10.36244/icj.2022.3.4">
  <data key="d0">10.36244/icj.2022.3.4</data>
  <data key="d1">identifier</data>
  <data key="d2">DOI of "Decentralized Authentication Mechanism for Mobile Ad hoc Networks".</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decentralized Authentication Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Decentralized Authentication Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication mechanism for MANET nodes that is based on fog computing technology and the blockchain concept. It is designed to meet security requirements and protect networks from attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Authentication mechanism for MANET based on fog computing and blockchain, shown to satisfy diverse security requirements and protect networks from attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Blockchain-based security mechanism that authenticates resource-limited MANET nodes. Admins register devices and authenticate them through Ethereum smart contracts using tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;Authentication mechanism proposed by the paper to allow secure access to network resources, using the distributed nature and cryptographic characteristics of blockchain; registration and authentication times depend on admin availability, making it unsuitable for real-time applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Ad Hoc Network">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Ad Hoc Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Mobile Ad Hoc Network (MANET) is an instant, active, dynamic and self-configuring wireless network made up of movable nodes, such as computers or mobile phones. These nodes connect autonomously by radio waves, without fixed infrastructure, wired links, routers, access points or centralized administration. Because the network has no fixed topology, packets are forwarded through intermediate nodes. This makes the MANET a decentralized and cooperative network in which the participating nodes carry the routing work collectively.

MANETs are used in a variety of settings. These include rescue operations, the Internet of Things, virtual classrooms and military applications. MANETs have also been proposed as a way to reduce communication costs in community networks.

Despite their flexibility, MANETs face significant constraints. Their nodes have limited capacities, particularly in power and computational resources, and the network topology changes constantly. These features make MANETs highly vulnerable to many network threats and attacks. The vulnerability stems mainly from the dynamic topology, the lack of central management and the unsecured wireless medium. The same constraints make it critical yet challenging to implement mechanisms such as blockchain consensus within a MANET environment.

MANET is the central network paradigm addressed by a scholarly article and several of its cited references. That body of work covers MANET history, security, energy, clustering and authentication. In particular, the MANET is the main subject of a review focused on authentication in such decentralized wireless networks.&lt;SEP&gt;MANET: a network vulnerable to threats because it lacks wire links and a fixed architecture. Its intrinsic features are the underlying cause of various security issues.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distributed Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Distributed Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication approach that security experts proposed for MANET because there is no central authority to register and authenticate nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Authentication approach proposed in recent years by security experts for MANET because no central authority exists to register and authenticate nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Community Network">
  <data key="d0">Community Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network that lets rural and underprivileged communities own, control and market their own communication services.&lt;SEP&gt;Networks letting rural and underprivileged communities own, control and market their communication services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zenzeleni">
  <data key="d0">Zenzeleni</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">First community network in South Africa, founded in 2013 by University of the Western Cape PhD students and the tribal government of the Mankosi community. It began as a local wireless network using solar-powered routers and was later given internet access through a 3G modem.&lt;SEP&gt;First community network in South Africa, founded in 2013 by UWC PhD students and the Mankosi community's tribal government; started as a local wireless network with solar-powered routers, later adding a 3G internet connection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="University of the Western Cape">
  <data key="d0">University of the Western Cape</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">University whose PhD students co-founded the Zenzeleni community network.&lt;SEP&gt;South African university (UWC) whose PhD students co-founded the Zenzeleni community network in 2013.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001</data>
