<node id="Trusted Third Party">
  <data key="d0">Trusted Third Party</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediary authority that the proposed decentralized authentication approach does not need.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediary that the proposed decentralized authentication approach does not need.&lt;SEP&gt;TTP; a trusted entity that is absent in MANET, which makes the clustering technique suitable for such networks.&lt;SEP&gt;TTP or Certifying Authority (CA). Clustering-based authentication in [6] avoids needing one, while CAs issue vehicle pseudonyms in Zheng et al.'s scheme.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Security Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Analysis showing the proposed method satisfies identification, confidentiality, integrity and non-repudiation and resists certain attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation explaining how the proposed authentication method satisfies identification, confidentiality, integrity and non-repudiation, and how it resists certain attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Analysis in the paper explaining how the proposed authentication method satisfies security goals (identification, confidentiality, integrity and non-repudiation) and resists certain types of attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Analysis and discussion in the paper showing how the proposed authentication method satisfies security goals (identification, confidentiality, integrity and non-repudiation) and resists certain types of attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identification">
  <data key="d0">Identification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security goal satisfied by the proposed authentication method.&lt;SEP&gt;Security requirement that every node accessing the network has an ID. Each node has a unique identifier DID, a unique public address and a CID.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Repudiation">
  <data key="d0">Non-Repudiation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security goal satisfied by the proposed authentication method.&lt;SEP&gt;Security requirement satisfied because private keys sign all data, so sending and receiving parties cannot deny executing a transaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Security requirement: because private keys sign all data, sending and receiving parties cannot deny executing a transaction.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental security concept that MANET security requires.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MANET operates in direct and multi-hop communication modes">
  <data key="d0">MANET operates in direct and multi-hop communication modes</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">There are two modes of MANET: The first mode is when the nodes can directly interact with other nodes in their radio range. The second one is called multi-hop communication, when the intermediate nodes are employed to communicate with the nodes beyond their radio ranges [6].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attacks in MANET can be classified as passive/active and internal/external">
  <data key="d0">Attacks in MANET can be classified as passive/active and internal/external</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"There are two classifications of attacks according to [7], [8]." Attacks are classified by behavior as passive or active, and by origin as internal or external.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blockchain nodes keep simultaneously updated copies of the ledger to avoid a single point of failure">
  <data key="d0">Blockchain nodes keep simultaneously updated copies of the ledger to avoid a single point of failure</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finally, to avoid a single point of failure, each node in the network keeps a copy of the blockchain on hand. These copies are simultaneously updated and verified [9].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fog computing consists of end devices, fog nodes and cloud servers">
  <data key="d0">Fog computing consists of end devices, fog nodes and cloud servers</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The basic instruction of Fog computing consists of three layers: End devices, fog nodes and cloud servers [10].&lt;SEP&gt;Statement made in the text: "The basic instruction of Fog computing consists of three layers: End devices, fog nodes and cloud servers [10]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="External Attacks">
  <data key="d0">External Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attacks launched by unlicensed nodes outside the network that may flood it with fake packets or imitate legitimate nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Attacks launched by unlicensed nodes outside the network that may flood fake packets and imitate legitimate nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Attacks launched by unlicensed nodes outside the network that may flood fake packets or imitate legitimate nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Attacks launched by unlicensed nodes outside the network. These nodes may flood the network with fake packets and imitate legitimate nodes, mainly to create congestion or disrupt normal network operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Attacks by illegitimate persons who want to enter the network and may send faked packets causing network failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Internal Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attacks initiated by legitimate network nodes that selfishly consume resources such as battery, processing power and bandwidth.&lt;SEP&gt;Attacks initiated by legitimate network nodes that selfishly consume resources such as battery power, processing power and bandwidth.&lt;SEP&gt;Attacks initiated by legitimate network nodes that arbitrarily and selfishly take resources such as battery power, processing power and bandwidth from other nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Attacks occurring within the network, usually by selfish nodes, and difficult to predict.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proof of Work">
  <data key="d0">Proof of Work</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">PoW; consensus procedure used by miners to verify that block transactions follow predetermined criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;PoW; consensus procedure used by miners to ensure transactions in a block follow predetermined criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;A consensus procedure (PoW) that miners use to ensure transactions in a block follow predetermined criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Blockchain consensus algorithm used to validate blocks and keep the distributed database state consistent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infocommunications Journal">
  <data key="d0">Infocommunications Journal</data>
  <data key="d1">venue</data>
  <data key="d2">Infocommunications Journal is the scholarly journal in which the article "Decentralized Authentication Mechanism for Mobile Ad Hoc Networks" was published. The paper, which deals with decentralized authentication for Mobile Ad hoc Networks (MANET), appeared in the September 2022 issue, Volume XIV, Number 3. The journal's name also appears in the article's page headers, which read "INFOCOMMUNICATIONS JOURNAL" followed by page numbers such as 4 and 5, identifying it as the publication venue of the paper.

Infocommunications Journal also published a paper on beacon control in Vehicular Ad hoc Networks (VANET) in 2021. This shows that the journal has covered research on ad hoc and vehicular networking across more than one year.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decentralized Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Decentralized Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication of MANET nodes without an intermediary or trusted third party, using blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Authentication approach without an intermediary or trusted third party, the main contribution of the paper.&lt;SEP&gt;Authentication approach not requiring an intermediary or trusted third party, using blockchain to register and authenticate devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Authentication without a central authority. It is the focus of the article being read and of the blockchain-based IoT system described in reference [9].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fog computing reduces Internet burden by processing data near devices">
  <data key="d0">Fog computing reduces Internet burden by processing data near devices</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Fog computing is an extension of cloud computing, in which data processing is transferred to the near of devices instead of sending it to the cloud. This mechanism will lessen the burden of the Internet and give quick processing. The basic instruction of Fog computing consists of three layers: End devices, fog nodes and cloud servers [10].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blockchain transactions are grouped into blocks validated by miners via consensus">
  <data key="d0">Blockchain transactions are grouped into blocks validated by miners via consensus</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"Once the block is created, active nodes, known as miners, ensure that transactions inside the block follow predetermined criteria using a consensus procedure like proof of Work (PoW)." Part of the blockchain description supported by [9].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Miners">
  <data key="d0">Miners</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Active blockchain nodes that verify transactions inside a block against predetermined criteria using a consensus procedure and are rewarded for validating blocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Active nodes in a blockchain network that ensure transactions inside a block follow predetermined criteria using a consensus procedure such as Proof of Work; the miner who validates the block is rewarded.&lt;SEP&gt;Active blockchain nodes that ensure transactions inside a block follow predetermined criteria using a consensus procedure such as Proof of Work, and are rewarded for validating blocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Active blockchain nodes that use a consensus procedure such as Proof of Work to ensure transactions in a block follow predetermined criteria. The miner who validates a block is rewarded.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consensus Procedure">
  <data key="d0">Consensus Procedure</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Procedure by which blockchain miners ensure transactions in a block follow predetermined criteria; Proof of Work is one example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466837</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fog Nodes">
  <data key="d0">Fog Nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Middle layer of the fog computing architecture between end devices and cloud servers; in the proposed system, fog nodes synchronize data associated with registered MANET nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Middle layer of fog computing between end devices and cloud servers; in the proposed system, fog nodes synchronize data associated with registered MANET nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediate layer of fog computing between end devices and cloud servers; in the proposed system, fog nodes synchronize data associated with registered MANET nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Nodes of the fog layer. They provide localized storage and processing, and each group is associated with its nearest fog node. Fog nodes update the blockchain and distribute it to the other fog nodes to synchronize authentication data.&lt;SEP&gt;Network nodes over which blockchain services are distributed and duplicated along with admins.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466837</data>
