</node>
<node id="AODV">
  <data key="d0">AODV</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Ad Hoc On-Demand Distance Vector, a MANET routing protocol with low overhead but weak authentication and integrity checking.&lt;SEP&gt;Ad hoc routing protocol. Anand and Sasikala's 2019 paper improves AODV, as a better-quality AODV protocol, for energy optimization in MANETs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ad-Hoc On-Demand Distance Vector routing protocol. It identifies routes but lacks information on node legitimacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Ad hoc routing protocol used as the base and comparison baseline for the FADA mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Ad hoc On-Demand Distance Vector routing protocol. Luong et al. and Kaushik combine it with AI techniques for intrusion detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BAODV">
  <data key="d0">BAODV</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A blockchain-modified AODV that adds a Bnode field to RREQ and RREP packets and uses chaining to detect impersonation and black-hole attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Region Certificate Authority">
  <data key="d0">Region Certificate Authority</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">RCA; the most reliable node in a region. It issues a group key to the TCA and member keys to the member nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Top Certificate Authority">
  <data key="d0">Top Certificate Authority</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">TCA; the highest-reliability node elected from among the RCAs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vehicular Ad hoc Network">
  <data key="d0">Vehicular Ad hoc Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">VANET; the main platform for vehicle-to-vehicle communication. It is vulnerable to attacks because of high mobility and dynamic topology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flying Ad hoc Network">
  <data key="d0">Flying Ad hoc Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">FANET; a type of MANET in which blockchain is also implemented.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Black-hole Attack">
  <data key="d0">Black-hole Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A MANET attack detected by BAODV.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internal and External Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Internal and External Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A classification of attacks: external attacks come from unlicensed nodes, and internal attacks come from legitimate nodes that selfishly consume resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blockchain nodes keep synchronized ledger copies to avoid single point of failure">
  <data key="d0">Blockchain nodes keep synchronized ledger copies to avoid single point of failure</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finally, to avoid a single point of failure, each node in the network keeps a copy of the blockchain on hand. These copies are simultaneously updated and verified [9].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VANET improves transportation security and reduces accidents">
  <data key="d0">VANET improves transportation security and reduces accidents</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This system improves transportation security and reduces the number of accidents [13].&lt;SEP&gt;Statement in the text: "This system improves transportation security and reduces the number of accidents [13]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modification Attack">
  <data key="d0">Modification Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An example of an active attack in MANETs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
