</node>
<node id="Kashish et al. [15]">
  <data key="d0">Kashish et al. [15]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work by Kashish et al. proposing a decentralized network authentication approach for FANET. The approach uses a blockchain-based public key infrastructure. It shows constant throughput, latency and near-constant message overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [16]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [16]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work on algorithms for selecting suitable admins or cluster heads. It includes an ANN-based clustering algorithm using mobility, packet drop, energy and neighbor count.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [16]; reference on over-reliance on AI weakening developers' problem-solving skills.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work ([16]) on LLMs producing inaccurate or misleading information despite their fluency.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [16] regarding RAG producing natural, contextually appropriate and reliable responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Survey evaluating the routing process and strategies used by MANETs.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work applying fuzzy logic to node connectivity based on transmission range and node density to improve VANET QoS. It finds better QoS when the transmission range is under 250 m.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [17]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [17]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work defining Artificial Neural Networks as computer systems inspired by biological neural networks.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work ([17]) on RAG systems that integrate LLMs with vector databases.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work on the success of RAG on knowledge-intensive NLP tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work by Pearl presenting the Bayesian network as a probabilistic graphical model for reasoning under uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kashish">
  <data key="d0">Kashish</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">First author of the blockchain-based PKI authentication approach for FANET [15].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FANET">
  <data key="d0">FANET</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Flying ad hoc network of unmanned aerial vehicles used for delivery, rescue missions and terrain monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Flying ad hoc network. FANETs are addressed in reference [15] using blockchain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MANET">
  <data key="d0">MANET</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mobile ad hoc network. It is the target network type for the proposed decentralized authentication mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Mobile ad hoc network with limited node resources, the target environment for the authentication mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Mobile ad hoc network. Node authentication, parameter training and clustering in MANETs are addressed by references [12], [16] and [17].&lt;SEP&gt;Mobile ad hoc network. It is the focus of several cited works on security, authentication and routing.&lt;SEP&gt;Mobile Ad Hoc Network, characterized by decentralized architecture and mobile topology causing unpredictable changes in routing information and vulnerability to security attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Mobile Ad Hoc Network, a dynamic network environment in which security and clustering are important concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;Mobile ad hoc network with dynamic topology, no centralized control and energy-limited nodes, which makes security difficult.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anonymous Authentication Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Anonymous Authentication Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Blockchain-based scheme by Azees et al. in which RSUs anonymously authenticate vehicles and communicate through shared session keys.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blockchain-Based Public Key Infrastructure">
  <data key="d0">Blockchain-Based Public Key Infrastructure</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Decentralized PKI from Kashish et al. that shares public keys and authentication information via blockchain. It avoids a single point of failure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road Side Units">
  <data key="d0">Road Side Units</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Roadside infrastructure (RSUs) in VANET that authenticate vehicles. They securely transfer authentication codes to adjacent RSUs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Head Selection">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Head Selection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Problem of choosing suitable admins or cluster heads in a network using parameters such as mobility, packet drop, energy and neighbor count.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of choosing cluster heads in a MANET. In the ANN-based approach, it uses weight-based parameters derived from mobility, packet drop, energy and the number of neighbor nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Layer">
  <data key="d0">Device Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Layer of the proposed architecture containing clustered mobile nodes: admins, which act as certification authorities, and devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fog Layer">
  <data key="d0">Fog Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network of fog nodes enabling fog services, localized storage and processing near devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer containing a network of fog nodes that implement fog services and perform localized storage and processing near devices to reduce cloud latency and response time.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer of the proposed architecture containing a network of fog nodes that synchronize the blockchain for authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;Network of fog nodes enabling fog services, performing localized storage and processing near devices to reduce cloud latency and response time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Identifier">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Identifier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CID chosen by each admin and shared only with trusted nodes. A new node needs the CID to register in a cluster.&lt;SEP&gt;CID; identifier verified against the adding admin and used in device token generation.&lt;SEP&gt;CID; identifier of a device cluster, checked against the adding admin during registration and sent by devices during authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
