  <data key="d0">Blockchain is useful for different types of MANET</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text drawn from the cited works [14] and [15]: "The studies mentioned above demonstrate the utility of blockchain for different types of MANET."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unmanned Aerial Vehicles">
  <data key="d0">Unmanned Aerial Vehicles</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">UAVs are the nodes forming a FANET. They can carry out activities such as delivery of goods, rescue missions and terrain monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Admins">
  <data key="d0">Admins</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mobile nodes in the device layer that control device access and act as the certification authority of each group. They should have high-performance RAM, a fast processor and high storage capacity, ideally as fixed servers with redundant power. Admins are trusted, choose cluster identifiers and add blocks to the blockchain when registering devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Devices">
  <data key="d0">Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mobile nodes in the device layer. Each device is identified by its unique identifying information and can be added by one admin.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blockchain-Based Authentication Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Blockchain-Based Authentication Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication mechanism proposed in the paper enabling reliable communication between nodes over an untrusted network and prohibiting access of malicious users; node registration and authentication requests are transactions whose hash values are stored in the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Proposed mechanism in which node registration and authentication requests are transactions whose hash values are stored in the blockchain; includes initialization, admin registration and device registration phases, enabling reliable communication over an untrusted network and preventing malicious users' access.&lt;SEP&gt;Proposed mechanism enabling reliable communication between nodes over an untrusted network and preventing access by malicious users; comprises initialization, registration and authentication phases.&lt;SEP&gt;Proposed authentication mechanism in which node registration and authentication requests are transactions whose hash values are stored in the blockchain; comprises initialization, admin registration and device registration phases.&lt;SEP&gt;Decentralized authentication mechanism made up of initialization, registration (admin and device) and authentication phases. Registration and authentication requests are transactions whose hash values are stored in the blockchain, which keeps malicious users out of the network.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466841</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fog Computing">
  <data key="d0">Fog Computing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fog Computing is a distributed computing paradigm that extends cloud computing by moving data processing closer to end devices. This reduces the burden on the Internet and allows data to be processed quickly. Fog Computing is generally described as having three layers: end devices, fog nodes, and cloud servers. The fog layer consists of fog nodes that provide localized storage and processing near devices, which lowers the latency and response time associated with relying only on the cloud. The state of the art of Fog Computing is reviewed in reference [10].

Within the proposed system, Fog Computing is the technology on which the decentralized authentication mechanism is based. Its fog nodes synchronize the data associated with registered nodes, and they synchronize and distribute the blockchain among admins. Fog Computing also handles communication between admins by delivering blockchain updates whenever new nodes join or are added to the network. This keeps the shared ledger consistent across the administrative entities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fog Node">
  <data key="d0">Fog Node</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Node in the fog layer that performs localized storage and processing near devices to reduce cloud latency and response time; each group is associated with the nearest fog node, which updates and distributes the blockchain to other fog nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Node associated with each group in the network that communicates with other fog nodes to synchronize authentication data, updating and distributing the blockchain to other fog nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Node associated with each group that receives new blockchain blocks from admins, updates the blockchain and distributes it to other fog nodes for data synchronization.&lt;SEP&gt;Node in the fog layer associated with each group in the network. Fog nodes enable fog services, perform localized storage and processing, communicate to ensure data synchronization for authentication, and distribute updated blockchain copies to other fog nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cluster Identifier (CID)">
  <data key="d0">Cluster Identifier (CID)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Identifier chosen by each admin for its cluster and shared only with trusted nodes; a new node cannot sign up in the cluster without it.&lt;SEP&gt;Unique identifier chosen by each admin to register its cluster, shared only with trusted nodes; a new node cannot join a cluster without it.&lt;SEP&gt;Unique identifier chosen by each admin to register its cluster on the blockchain; shared only with trusted nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Unique identifier chosen by each admin to register its cluster; shared only with trusted nodes, and required for a new node to join a cluster.&lt;SEP&gt;Identifier that each admin chooses for its cluster and shares only with trusted nodes. A node cannot sign up in a cluster without the CID.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster identifier supplied when adding and authenticating devices; the addDevice function verifies that the CID corresponds to the adding admin, otherwise the transaction terminates with an error.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Admin Registration">
  <data key="d0">Admin Registration</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Registration stage in which a new admin sends its address AIP, CID and AID to an old admin via addAdmin(AIP, CID, AID); the smart contract checks existing registration, creates a token and triggers the AdminAdded event, generating a new block.&lt;SEP&gt;Registration stage in which a new admin sends its address AIP, cluster identifier CID and unique identifier AID via the addAdmin function; the smart contract verifies non-existence, creates a token, saves the admin and triggers the AdminAdded event.&lt;SEP&gt;Registration stage in which a new admin sends AIP, CID and AID to an old admin via addAdmin(AIP, CID, AID); the smart contract checks for existing registration, creates a Keccak256 token, saves the admin and triggers the AdminAdded event.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase where a new admin sends AIP, CID and AID to an existing admin via addAdmin; the smart contract checks for existing registration, creates a token and triggers the AdminAdded event.&lt;SEP&gt;Registration stage in which a new admin sends its AIP, CID and AID to an existing admin via addAdmin(). The smart contract checks for duplicates, creates a token with keccak256(AIP, CID, AID) and triggers the AdminAdded event.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Registration">
  <data key="d0">Device Registration</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Registration stage after cluster registration in which an admin adds a device to the network by sending device information including the device address DIP.&lt;SEP&gt;Registration stage following successful cluster registration in which an admin adds a device to the network by sending its information including the device address DIP.&lt;SEP&gt;Registration stage after successful cluster registration in which an admin adds a device by sending device information such as its address DIP.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase after cluster registration in which an admin adds a device by sending its information, such as the device address DIP.&lt;SEP&gt;Registration stage in which an admin adds a device via addDevice(DIP, CID, DID). The contract verifies that the CID belongs to the admin, checks for duplicates, creates a token with keccak256(DIP, CID, DID) and triggers the DeviceAdded event.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase where an admin adds a device via addDevice(DIP, CID, DID); the contract verifies the admin's CID, checks for existing device hashes, creates a token and triggers the DeviceAdded event.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase in which an admin submits DIP, CID and DID to the addDevice function; the contract verifies the admin's CID, checks for duplicates by hash, creates a keccak256 token and emits the DeviceAdded event.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initialization Phase">
  <data key="d0">Initialization Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase in which the smart contract constructor creates the first admin using the creator's address, a unique identifier AID and a cluster head identifier CID, then calculates and stores the admin's token.&lt;SEP&gt;Initial phase in which the smart contract constructor creates the first admin using the creator's address, a unique identifier AID and a cluster head identifier CID, then computes and stores its token.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase in which the smart contract's constructor creates the first admin using the creator's address, AID and CID, computes its token and saves it in the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Initial phase where the smart contract constructor creates the first admin, computes its token and saves it in the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;First phase of the mechanism. The smart contract constructor creates the first admin from the creator's address, a unique identifier AID and a cluster identifier CID, then computes and stores that admin's token.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AdminAdded Event">
  <data key="d0">AdminAdded Event</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Event triggered by the smart contract upon successful admin registration, broadcast to all nodes in the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Event triggered by the smart contract upon successful admin registration, broadcast to all blockchain nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Event triggered by the smart contract upon accepting an admin registration transaction; generates a new block designating successful admin registration and is broadcast to all nodes in the blockchain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Public/Private Key Pair">
  <data key="d0">Public/Private Key Pair</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Key pair assumed for each node for data encryption and integrity in the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Key pair assumed to be held by each node, used for data encryption and integrity in the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Key pair assumed for each node to provide data encryption and integrity in the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Each node is assumed to hold a key pair used for data encryption and integrity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Node Mobility">
  <data key="d0">Node Mobility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Movement of nodes from one group to other groups, handled since all admins receive updated blockchain copies.&lt;SEP&gt;Movement of nodes from one group to another, during which all admins can authenticate nodes thanks to the shared blockchain copy.&lt;SEP&gt;Movement of nodes from one group to other groups; the shared blockchain lets all admins authenticate mobile nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Movement of nodes from one group to another; supported because all admins receive updated blockchain copies and can authenticate all network nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Admin Unique Identifier (AID)">
  <data key="d0">Admin Unique Identifier (AID)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unique identifier AID of an admin, used together with the admin address AIP and the cluster identifier CID to create the first admin and to compute admin tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;Unique identifier of an admin node, used together with the admin address AIP and the cluster identifier CID to register the admin and to compute its token keccak256(AIP, CID, AID).&lt;SEP&gt;Unique identifier of an admin used together with the address AIP and CID to create the admin token and to check whether the admin is already registered.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="addAdmin Function">
  <data key="d0">addAdmin Function</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Function addAdmin(AIP, CID, AID) that a new admin uses to send its address, cluster identifier and unique identifier to an old admin in order to sign up.&lt;SEP&gt;Smart contract function addAdmin(AIP, CID, AID) through which a new admin sends its address AIP, cluster identifier CID and unique identifier AID to an old admin to sign up.&lt;SEP&gt;Smart contract function addAdmin(AIP, CID, AID) that a new admin uses to send its address, cluster identifier and unique identifier to an old admin in order to sign up.&lt;SEP&gt;Smart contract function addAdmin(AIP, CID, AID) used by a new admin to send its address AIP, cluster identifier CID and unique identifier AID to an old admin for registration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Admin Token">
  <data key="d0">Admin Token</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Token computed by the smart contract as keccak256(AIP, CID, AID) for each admin, including the first admin, and saved in the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Value computed as keccak256(AIP, CID, AID) and saved in the blockchain when a new admin, or the first admin during initialization, is registered.&lt;SEP&gt;Token computed as keccak256(AIP, CID, AID); it is created when the admin does not yet exist in the blockchain, and the first admin's token is computed by the smart contract during initialization.&lt;SEP&gt;Token computed as keccak256(AIP, CID, AID) by the smart contract for each admin, including the first admin, and saved in the blockchain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Credential Hashing">
  <data key="d0">Credential Hashing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Practice of saving node credentials as their hash instead of in plain text; the hash of registration and authentication request transactions is stored in the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Practice of saving node credentials in the blockchain as hashes instead of plain text.&lt;SEP&gt;Practice of saving node credentials as hashes instead of plain text in the blockchain; the smart contract checks for existing admins by searching the hash of their AID, AIP and CID.&lt;SEP&gt;Practice of saving node credentials in the blockchain as their hash instead of plain text; hash values of registration and authentication requests are stored in the blockchain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Admin">
  <data key="d0">Admin</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Trusted administrator node whose actions are assumed legitimate; it chooses its cluster identifier, registers its cluster, and adds devices to the network.&lt;SEP&gt;Trusted administrator node (cluster head) whose actions are assumed legitimate. Each admin chooses a cluster identifier, can add devices to the network, and shares the blockchain with its nearest fog node. Only admins can register clusters.&lt;SEP&gt;Trusted administrator node whose actions are assumed legitimate; chooses a cluster identifier (CID), registers its cluster on the blockchain, adds devices, and shares new blocks with its associated fog node.&lt;SEP&gt;Administrator role that registers devices through addDevice and authenticates devices registered in the blockchain using the smart contract.&lt;SEP&gt;Entity identified by a cluster identifier (CID) that registers devices via addDevice and can authenticate any registered device using the smart contract.&lt;SEP&gt;Administrator node that registers devices via addDevice and, in the authentication phase, can authenticate any device registered in the blockchain using the smart contract.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device">
  <data key="d0">Device</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network node identified by its unique identifying information, such as its address DIP, which one admin can add to the network.&lt;SEP&gt;Network node identified by its unique identifying information, such as its address DIP. Each device can be added by one admin.&lt;SEP&gt;Network node identified by unique identifying information (including address DIP) that can be added to the network by one admin after its cluster is registered.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Registration Phase">
  <data key="d0">Registration Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase in which each group and its associated nodes are registered in the blockchain. It is divided into admin registration and device registration.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase in which each group and its associated nodes are registered in the blockchain; divided into two stages, admin registration and device registration.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase of the authentication mechanism in which each group and its associated nodes are registered in the blockchain. It has two stages: admin registration and device registration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malicious Users">
  <data key="d0">Malicious Users</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unauthorized users whose access the authentication strategy prohibits on the untrusted network.&lt;SEP&gt;Unauthorized users whose access to the network the authentication strategy is designed to prevent.&lt;SEP&gt;Unauthorized users whose access to the network the blockchain-based authentication mechanism prohibits.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Node Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Node Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Problem of authenticating network nodes, including in the case of node mobility between groups, over an untrusted network.&lt;SEP&gt;Security problem of identifying and authenticating nodes, covering identification, confidentiality, integrity, non-repudiation and attack resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;Security requirement of verifying node identities in MANETs, addressed by the proposed blockchain mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Public-Key Cryptography">
  <data key="d0">Public-Key Cryptography</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Each node holds a private/public key pair for data encryption and integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental security layer for digital infrastructures, including public-key infrastructures, secure communication protocols and blockchain-based transaction systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502198</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Admin Address (AIP)">
  <data key="d0">Admin Address (AIP)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Address of an admin node that a new admin sends to an old admin during registration; used in the token computation keccak256(AIP, CID, AID).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Address (DIP)">
  <data key="d0">Device Address (DIP)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Address of a device that an admin sends when adding the device to the network during the device registration phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Admin Node">
  <data key="d0">Admin Node</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Trusted administrator node whose actions are assumed legitimate. Each admin chooses a cluster identifier, registers its cluster, and is the only node type allowed to perform cluster registration. Admins add devices and share new blocks with their associated fog node.&lt;SEP&gt;Administrator or cluster-head node that is assumed to be trusted, with all its actions legitimate. An admin registers its cluster with a chosen CID, adds devices, and authenticates devices using the smart contract. Only administrator nodes can perform cluster registration.&lt;SEP&gt;Network node with administrative role. An admin adds devices through the addDevice function, and its CID must match the cluster of the device being added. Any admin can authenticate registered devices by checking their tokens through the smart contract. Admin nodes digitally sign and validate all blockchain transactions in the network.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Untrusted Network">
  <data key="d0">Untrusted Network</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network that forwards packets between nodes without any security guarantees, which motivates the authentication strategy that blocks access by malicious users.&lt;SEP&gt;Network that forwards packets between nodes without any security guarantees. The authentication strategy enables reliable communication over this network and prevents access by malicious users.&lt;SEP&gt;Network that forwards packets between nodes without any security guarantees, motivating an authentication strategy to block malicious users.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud Latency">
  <data key="d0">Cloud Latency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Delay and response time of the cloud, which the fog layer reduces by performing storage and processing locally near the devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud Latency Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Cloud Latency Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Goal of the fog layer, which performs localized storage and processing near devices to reduce cloud latency and response time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decentralized Authentication Mechanism for Mobile Ad Hoc Networks">
  <data key="d0">Decentralized Authentication Mechanism for Mobile Ad Hoc Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, published in Infocommunications Journal (September 2022, Volume XIV, Number 3). It proposes a blockchain-based authentication mechanism in which admins (cluster heads) register clusters and devices via a smart contract, and node credentials are stored as Keccak256 hashes. The mechanism is implemented using Remix IDE on Ethereum.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read. It was published in Infocommunications Journal, September 2022, Volume XIV, Number 3. It is authored by Hafida Khalfaoui, Abderrazak Farchane and Said Safi, and addresses decentralized authentication for mobile ad hoc networks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authentication Phase">
  <data key="d0">Authentication Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase in which a device sends its DID, DIP and CID to any admin. The admin uses the smart contract to recompute the token and compare it with the stored tokens, then emits the Authenticated or NoAuthenticated event.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase in which a device sends its DID, DIP and CID to any admin. The admin uses the smart contract to recompute the token and compare it with the tokens stored on the blockchain, then emits Authenticated or NoAuthenticated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Remix IDE">
  <data key="d0">Remix IDE</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Open-source web tool for testing, debugging and deploying smart contracts. It also serves as a learning and teaching environment for Ethereum. It was used to implement the mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Open-source web tool aiding in testing, debugging and deploying smart contracts, serving as a learning and teaching environment for Ethereum blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Open-source web tool that aids in testing, debugging and deploying smart contracts and serves as a learning and teaching environment for Ethereum blockchain; used for smart contract compilation and deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Open-source web tool for testing, debugging and deploying smart contracts. It also serves as a learning and teaching environment for the Ethereum blockchain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elliptic Curves Cryptography (ECC)">
  <data key="d0">Elliptic Curves Cryptography (ECC)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Lightweight and robust signature scheme for restricted devices that Ethereum uses to secure transactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decentralized Applications (DApps)">
  <data key="d0">Decentralized Applications (DApps)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Applications that Ethereum makes easier to build.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Ad Hoc Networks">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Ad Hoc Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network type targeted by the decentralized authentication mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;MANETs are networks of nodes with limited resources. The proposed security mechanism authenticates these nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authentication Token">
  <data key="d0">Authentication Token</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Keccak256 hash of a node's address, cluster identifier and unique identifier (AID or DID). It is stored in the blockchain and later compared against recomputed tokens to verify legitimacy. Credentials are saved as hashes rather than plain text.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Contract Events">
  <data key="d0">Smart Contract Events</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Events emitted by the smart contract: AdminAdded and DeviceAdded after successful registration, and Authenticated or NoAuthenticated after an authentication attempt. Events are broadcast to all nodes in the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Events emitted by the smart contract. DeviceAdded marks successful registration and generates a new block. Authenticated is shared when a device's token exists. NoAuthenticated is shared when authentication fails.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elliptic Curves Cryptography">
  <data key="d0">Elliptic Curves Cryptography</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Lightweight and robust signature scheme for restricted devices (ECC) used by Ethereum to secure transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Lightweight and robust signature scheme (ECC) for restricted devices used by Ethereum to provide secure transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Lightweight and robust signature scheme (ECC) for restricted devices that Ethereum uses to provide secure transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;ECC is a lightweight and robust signature scheme for restricted devices. It is used by Ethereum and the blockchain for secure transactions and authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decentralized Application">
  <data key="d0">Decentralized Application</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DApp; an application interacting with the blockchain, built in the paper with ReactJS to allow interaction between users and Ethereum.&lt;SEP&gt;DApp; application type whose construction Ethereum simplifies; built with ReactJS to let users interact with Ethereum.&lt;SEP&gt;A DApp, built with ReactJS, that allows interaction between users and Ethereum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
