</node>
<node id="ReactJS">
  <data key="d0">ReactJS</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Framework used to develop the front-end decentralized application allowing interaction between users and Ethereum.&lt;SEP&gt;Front-end library used to build the decentralized application allowing interaction between users and Ethereum.&lt;SEP&gt;Library used to build the front-end decentralized application (Dapp) allowing interaction between users and Ethereum.&lt;SEP&gt;Framework used to build the front-end decentralized application (DApp) that lets users interact with Ethereum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metamask">
  <data key="d0">Metamask</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Wallet tool used to manage different accounts and connect the current user to the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Wallet used to manage different accounts and connect the current user to the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Wallet tool that manages different accounts and connects the current user to the blockchain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Device Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase where a device sends its DID, DIP and CID to an admin, who uses the smart contract to recreate its token and compare it with tokens stored in the blockchain, emitting Authenticated or NoAuthenticated events.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase in which a device sends its DID, DIP and CID to an admin, who uses the smart contract to recompute its token and compare it against stored tokens, emitting Authenticated or NoAuthenticated.&lt;SEP&gt;Research problem of verifying the legitimacy of devices so that registered devices can communicate with each other, addressed through a blockchain-based mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ethereum Test Networks">
  <data key="d0">Ethereum Test Networks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ethereum test networks that often need no faucet or mining and can reset accounts instantly with a fixed amount of fake Ether for developing and testing smart contracts.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethereum networks that need no faucet or mining. They can instantly reset accounts with a fixed amount of fake Ether for developing and testing smart contracts.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethereum test networks that need no faucet or mining. They can reset accounts instantly with a fixed amount of fake Ether for developing and testing smart contracts, which is one of the criteria for selecting Ethereum.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethereum networks that do not need a faucet or mining and can reset accounts instantly with a fixed amount of fake Ether for developing and testing smart contracts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="addDevice Function">
  <data key="d0">addDevice Function</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Smart contract function addDevice(DIP, CID, DID) that takes the device IP, cluster identifier and unique device identifier, verifies the admin's CID, checks whether the device already exists by hash comparison, and registers new devices.&lt;SEP&gt;Smart contract function addDevice(DIP, CID, DID) that verifies the admin's CID, checks for existing devices by comparing hashes with the nodes list in the blockchain, creates a keccak256 token, registers the device and triggers the DeviceAdded event.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Token">
  <data key="d0">Device Token</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Token computed as keccak256(DIP, CID, DID), stored in the blockchain and compared during authentication to verify device legitimacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Token computed as keccak256(DIP, CID, DID) that is stored in the blockchain at registration and recreated and compared during authentication to verify a device's legitimacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Token computed as keccak256(DIP, CID, DID) and stored on the blockchain when a device is registered. During authentication it is recreated and compared with the stored list of tokens to verify legitimacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Identifier">
  <data key="d0">Device Identifier</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DID; unique device identifier used together with DIP and CID to register and authenticate devices.&lt;SEP&gt;DID; unique device identifier passed to addDevice and sent in authentication requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decentralized Applications">
  <data key="d0">Decentralized Applications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DApps; applications whose construction is simplified by Ethereum; a DApp built with ReactJS enables user interaction with Ethereum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device IP">
  <data key="d0">Device IP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DIP; device address submitted with CID and DID to the addDevice function. It is used in keccak256 token generation and to look up a device's token during authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AddDevice Function">
  <data key="d0">AddDevice Function</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Smart contract function addDevice(DIP, CID, DID). It verifies that the CID corresponds to the adding admin and checks whether the device already exists by comparing hashes against the stored nodes list. It then creates a keccak256 token and registers the new device.&lt;SEP&gt;Smart contract function addDevice(DIP, CID, DID). It checks that the CID corresponds to the adding admin, checks whether the device already exists by comparing hashes with the nodes list on the blockchain, creates a keccak256 token, registers the new device and triggers the DeviceAdded event.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DeviceAdded Event">
  <data key="d0">DeviceAdded Event</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Event triggered when the smart contract accepts a device registration transaction. Its acceptance generates a new block marking successful registration of the new device.&lt;SEP&gt;Event triggered when the smart contract accepts a registration transaction, generating a new block that designates successful registration of the new device.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authenticated Event">
  <data key="d0">Authenticated Event</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Event shared when the admin finds the token corresponding to the DIP in the blockchain and successfully authenticates the device. Otherwise the NoAuthenticated event is shared.&lt;SEP&gt;Event shared when the token corresponding to the DIP exists and the admin successfully authenticates the device.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Execution Time And Power Consumption">
  <data key="d0">Execution Time And Power Consumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance aspects that the study explicitly does not evaluate, because they depend on the type of Ethereum network and the communication protocol.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance metrics that the study explicitly does not evaluate, because they depend on the type of Ethereum network, the communication protocol and the node specification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Authentication Phase">
  <data key="d0">Device Authentication Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase in which a device sends an authentication request containing its DID, DIP and CID to any admin, who uses the smart contract to recreate the device token and compare it with tokens stored in the blockchain, emitting an Authenticated or NoAuthenticated event.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Registration Phase">
  <data key="d0">Device Registration Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Phase in which an admin adds a device via the addDevice(DIP, CID, DID) function; the contract verifies the CID, checks for existing devices by hash, creates a keccak256 token, registers the device and triggers a DeviceAdded event.&lt;SEP&gt;Phase in which an admin calls addDevice(DIP, CID, DID). The CID is verified against the admin, duplicates are checked, a keccak256 token is created, and the DeviceAdded event is triggered.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Identifier (DID)">
  <data key="d0">Device Identifier (DID)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unique device identifier sent with DIP and CID in authentication requests and used as input to the addDevice(DIP, CID, DID) function and the keccak256 token computation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DIP">
  <data key="d0">DIP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Device attribute sent alongside DID and CID; the token corresponding to the DIP is checked during authentication and DIP is an input to the keccak256 token.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NoAuthenticated Event">
  <data key="d0">NoAuthenticated Event</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Event shared when the device token is not found, indicating failed authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SHA-256">
  <data key="d0">SHA-256</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Cryptographic hash algorithm used by the blockchain as proof of data integrity and authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;Hash algorithm used as cryptographic proof for data integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Hash algorithm used as cryptographic proof for data integrity in the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;Hash function whose hex-encoded digest is used as the contentHash argument in baseline scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Hash function whose 64-character hex digest of document content is stored in the contentHash field in baseline scenarios S1-S4.&lt;SEP&gt;Hash function; the payload scenarios use random hexadecimal strings instead of true SHA-256 hashes.&lt;SEP&gt;Hash function whose digest (64 hexadecimal characters) forms the baseline transaction payload representation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-033</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Node Security">
  <data key="d0">Node Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The study's evaluation focus: the mechanism's impact on the security of nodes and the network. Execution time and power consumption are not evaluated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Device Identifiers (DIP, CID, DID)">
  <data key="d0">Device Identifiers (DIP, CID, DID)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Three device attributes: the device IP (DIP), the cluster identifier (CID) and the unique device identifier (DID). They are passed to addDevice(DIP, CID, DID), hashed with keccak256 to form the device token, and sent by a device in its authentication request.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Signature">
  <data key="d0">Digital Signature</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">All transactions in the blockchain were digitally signed and validated by admin nodes in the network.&lt;SEP&gt;Signing with private keys. Nodes sign each request message, and admins sign blockchain transactions, ensuring integrity and non-repudiation.&lt;SEP&gt;Used to guarantee authenticity and integrity of certificates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
