  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ECDSA">
  <data key="d0">ECDSA</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">ECDSA (Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm) is a classical elliptic-curve digital signature scheme widely used in blockchain systems. In Ethereum-based settings, ECDSA is the supported algorithm for signing blockchain transactions with the administrator's private key, ensuring message integrity and confirming node legitimacy. Like other classical elliptic-curve schemes, ECDSA is vulnerable to large-scale quantum attacks, specifically Shor's algorithm. Migrating from ECDSA to post-quantum signatures is therefore required, although replacing it is only one part of the broader post-quantum migration of blockchain systems.

ECDSA is the native signature scheme of Hyperledger Fabric. Fabric uses it for MSP (Membership Service Provider) identities and certificates, identity management, transaction endorsement by peers and clients, TLS, transaction validation, block metadata, and ordering-service messages. In the hybrid classical/post-quantum architecture described in this work, Fabric's native ECDSA endorsement and validation pipeline remains unchanged. Peers continue to endorse transactions with ECDSA, and peer-side signature verification is unaffected. ECDSA signatures stay in transaction envelopes and endorsement metadata rather than being duplicated in the chaincode world state. ECDSA also forms the classical component of the hybrid signature scheme, where it is combined with the post-quantum algorithm ML-DSA-65.

In the experimental evaluation, ECDSA (specifically an application-layer ECDSA P-256 configuration) is the baseline against which the PQC hybrid configurations are compared. To create a latency-matched Fabric baseline, the ECDSA workload injects a synthetic 2.44 ms delay that equalizes HTTP round-trip overhead. This baseline is used across the performance comparisons, including:
- transaction-level and CreateDocument benchmarks,
- throughput experiments,
- average-latency comparisons, such as the figure comparing three signature configurations and Figure 3.

Under the ECDSA baseline, peer CPU utilization averaged 12.5% and orderer CPU utilization averaged 3.3%. The mean active-block size was 29,328 ± 640 bytes, and this value serves as the reference for computing storage ratios of the post-quantum hybrid configurations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-041</data>
