<node id="Mobile Ad Hoc Network (MANET)">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Ad Hoc Network (MANET)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Network of resource-limited mobile nodes with changing topology, the target environment of the authentication mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Network of mobile nodes such as smartphones, laptops and PDAs that communicate over a wireless medium without pre-existing infrastructure or centralized administration. Nodes act as both end systems and routers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DoS/DDoS Flooding Attacks">
  <data key="d0">DoS/DDoS Flooding Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attacks aimed at shutting down clusters; future work will integrate an intrusion detection system to detect them.&lt;SEP&gt;Flooding attacks aiming to shut down a cluster by overwhelming the admin with authentication requests; addressed in future work.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intrusion Detection System">
  <data key="d0">Intrusion Detection System</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Planned future component to detect DoS/DDoS by checking timing of authentication requests.&lt;SEP&gt;Planned future component to detect DoS/DDoS attacks by checking the timing of authentication requests sent to admins.&lt;SEP&gt;Security mechanism detecting normal and abnormal behaviors; acts as a second wall of defense after authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;Controlling tool that ad hoc networks lack, contributing to their security problems.&lt;SEP&gt;IDS used for detecting attacks in MANETs; fuzzy logic and deep learning have been applied to IDSs.&lt;SEP&gt;Mechanism using cryptography and access control to detect and prevent security attacks; types include HIDS, Application-based IDS and Network IDS.&lt;SEP&gt;Detection systems (IDSs) that AI makes more accurate at detecting adversaries in the network and categorizing attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
