<node id="Admin Nodes">
  <data key="d0">Admin Nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cluster administrator nodes that digitally sign, validate and store blockchain transactions, approve node identities, maintain the blockchain and control access by other nodes; registration and authentication times depend on their availability.&lt;SEP&gt;Cluster admins that digitally sign and validate blockchain transactions, approve node identities, hold Ethereum addresses, and share public keys with nodes for encrypting requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Real-Time Application Limitation">
  <data key="d0">Real-Time Application Limitation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Open issue: the proposed approach is not adapted to real-time applications because registration and authentication times rely on admin availability, due to limited node storage capacity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consensus Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Consensus Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Blockchain mechanism after which transactions are validated; consensus time is a critical and challenging issue in MANET due to limited power and computation resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Blockchain mechanism by which transactions are validated only after the consensus time; a critical and challenging issue in MANET because of limited power and computation resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transaction Fees">
  <data key="d0">Transaction Fees</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Open issue: high financial costs of cryptocurrency spent on blockchain transaction fees.&lt;SEP&gt;High financial costs from the cryptocurrency spent on transaction fees, identified as another problem of the blockchain-based approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
