<node id="ECC Consumes Less Power With Same Security As RSA">
  <data key="d0">ECC Consumes Less Power With Same Security As RSA</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "The ECC algorithm is suited to the MANET environment, particularly in terms of key sizes and signature times. Also, it consumes less power and has the same level of security as Rivest Shamir Adleman (RSA)[18]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ECC">
  <data key="d0">ECC</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Elliptic Curve Cryptography, used for authentication; suited to MANETs due to small key sizes, fast signatures, and low power consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RSA">
  <data key="d0">RSA</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Rivest Shamir Adleman public-key algorithm, compared with ECC in terms of security level and power consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Classical public-key mechanism whose security relies on the hardness of integer factorization. It is vulnerable to Shor's algorithm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502198</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
