  <data key="d0">Decentralized and Secure Communication Architecture for FANETs Using Blockchain</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [15]. Written by K. Khullar, Y. Malhotra and A. Kumar and published in Procedia Computer Science, vol. 173, pp. 158–170, 2020. It proposes a blockchain-based secure communication architecture for FANETs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791466843</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Parameter Training in MANET Using Artificial Neural Network">
  <data key="d0">Parameter Training in MANET Using Artificial Neural Network</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [16]. Written by B. Chatterjee and H. N. Saha and published in International Journal of Computer Network &amp; Information Security, vol. 11, no. 9, 2019. It applies artificial neural networks to parameter training in MANETs.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference 30, by B. Chatterjee and H.N. Saha. Published in the International Journal of Computer Network and Information Security 11(9) (2019).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="K-Means Based Cluster Formation and Head Selection Through Artificial Neural Network in MANET">
  <data key="d0">K-Means Based Cluster Formation and Head Selection Through Artificial Neural Network in MANET</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [17]. Written by D. Bisen, S. Mishra and P. Saurabh in 2021. It uses k-means clustering and artificial neural networks for cluster formation and cluster head selection in MANETs.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference 31, by D. Bisen, S. Mishra and P. Saurabh, 2021. It is a preprint on K-Means clustering and neural-network-based cluster head selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lightweight Security Algorithm for Low Power IoT Devices">
  <data key="d0">Lightweight Security Algorithm for Low Power IoT Devices</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [18]. Written by T. K. Goyal and V. Sahula and published at the 2016 International Conference on Advances in Computing, Communications and Informatics (ICACCI), IEEE, 2016, pp. 1725–1729. It proposes a lightweight security algorithm for low power IoT devices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
