</node>
<node id="Automatic Defect Detection">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Defect Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated inspection of appearance and surface defects in manufacturing, replacing manual visual inspection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Burrs Around Functional Assembly Hole">
  <data key="d0">Burrs Around Functional Assembly Hole</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Specific anomaly studied in This Paper; material inside the functional hole can prevent proper closure or sealing of the assembled part.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plastic Injection Molding Parts Image Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Plastic Injection Molding Parts Image Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Images manually captured from the production line of a plastic injection molding facility in northern Morocco, showing plastic boxes used to package industrial goods. The collected data comprised 2210 images of good parts and 1130 images of bad parts, focused on burrs around the functional assembly hole. Images were captured at 900x1200 pixels and resized to 256x256 for feature extraction and model testing. The dataset was split into 3000 training images (2100 good, 900 bad) and 340 testing images (110 good, 230 bad).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integration of Canny edge and CNNs for faulty part classification is scarce">
  <data key="d0">Integration of Canny edge and CNNs for faulty part classification is scarce</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "the primary gap highlighted is the scarcity of studies that integrate both the canny edge technique and convolutional neural networks (CNNs) for classifying faulty parts."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Plastic Injection Molding Facility in Northern Morocco">
  <data key="d0">Plastic Injection Molding Facility in Northern Morocco</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Industrial plastic injection molding facility in northern Morocco that produces plastic boxes for packaging industrial goods. It is the source of the images used in This Paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Neural Network Quality Prediction Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Neural Network Quality Prediction Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Neural network algorithm developed by Im et al. (2023) to predict the quality of injection molding products. Its independent variables are statistical features extracted from machine vibration data and cavity temperature and pressure sensor data. Its quality grades come from image indicators.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Vibration and Cavity Sensor Data">
  <data key="d0">Machine Vibration and Cavity Sensor Data</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Machine vibration data and temperature and pressure data from each mold cavity, gathered through infrastructure built by Im et al. (2023). The study also collected image data alongside these signals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Knowledge reuse CNN achieves about 99% defect detection accuracy with 200 images per category">
  <data key="d0">Knowledge reuse CNN achieves about 99% defect detection accuracy with 200 images per category</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Experiments on injection molding products demonstrate a detection accuracy of around 99% with only 200 images per category, outperforming traditional CNN models and support vector machine methods."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Combining DIP with MFO eliminates defects in injection molded parts">
  <data key="d0">Combining DIP with MFO eliminates defects in injection molded parts</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "This method, successfully applied to an injection molding machine, effectively eliminated defects in molded parts."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Analyzing only the first layer predicts quality of subsequent layers in MMJ">
