  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hysteresis edge tracking uses edge following or connectivity analysis">
  <data key="d0">Hysteresis edge tracking uses edge following or connectivity analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "This is typically done using techniques like edge following or connectivity analysis[18]"</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CNNs are deep learning models designed for visual data analysis">
  <data key="d0">CNNs are deep learning models designed for visual data analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "CNNs are deep learning models designed for visual data analysis[19]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MVML">
  <data key="d0">MVML</data>
  <data key="d1">venue</data>
  <data key="d2">Venue where This Paper appears, inferred from the page headers "MVML 120-4" and "MVML 120-5"; these indicate paper number 120.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Good vs. Bad Image Dataset">
  <data key="d0">Good vs. Bad Image Dataset</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Image dataset used in This Paper. Its samples are labeled Good or Bad, as shown in Fig. 4.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noise Reduction">
  <data key="d0">Noise Reduction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">First step of Canny edge detection, in which the image is smoothed to reduce noise before edges are detected, typically with Gaussian blur.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gradient Calculation">
  <data key="d0">Gradient Calculation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Second step of Canny edge detection. It computes the gradient magnitude and direction for each pixel using operators such as Sobel or Prewitt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Convolutional Layer">
  <data key="d0">Convolutional Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">CNN layer that uses learnable filters to extract features from input images, creating feature maps and hierarchical representations.&lt;SEP&gt;The study's architecture has two convolutional layers. The first has 16 filters of size 3x3 with ReLU activation. The second has 32 filters of the same size and activation. Both are used for feature extraction from input images.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pooling Layer">
  <data key="d0">Pooling Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">CNN layer that reduces the spatial dimensions of feature maps to improve computational efficiency. Common operations are max pooling and average pooling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fully Connected Layer">
  <data key="d0">Fully Connected Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">CNN layer that connects neurons across layers, enabling high-level reasoning, complex pattern recognition and high-level predictions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hierarchical Representation Learning">
  <data key="d0">Hierarchical Representation Learning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ability of CNNs to learn hierarchical representations from raw data. This ability explains their wide use in vision tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zhao, Confusion Matrix Reference [20]">
  <data key="d0">Zhao, Confusion Matrix Reference [20]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [20]; referenced for the use of the confusion matrix to evaluate the trained model in identifying quality defects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference [21] on Confusion Matrix Outcomes">
  <data key="d0">Reference [21] on Confusion Matrix Outcomes</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [21]; referenced for the definition of the outcomes represented by each cell of the confusion matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference [22] on Classification Performance Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Reference [22] on Classification Performance Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [22]; referenced for deriving performance metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, specificity and F1 score from the confusion matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max-Pooling">
  <data key="d0">Max-Pooling</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Pooling layers following convolutional layers for feature extraction from input images.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ReLU Activation">
  <data key="d0">ReLU Activation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Activation function used in both convolutional layers and the 32-neuron dense layer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dropout Regularization">
  <data key="d0">Dropout Regularization</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Regularization with a rate of 0.5 applied before the output layer to enhance generalization and prevent overfitting.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467109</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specificity">
  <data key="d0">Specificity</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Performance metric derived from the confusion matrix.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confusion matrix is used to evaluate quality defect identification">
  <data key="d0">Confusion matrix is used to evaluate quality defect identification</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "To evaluate the performance of the trained model in identifying quality defects, we utilized the confusion matrix[20]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Each confusion matrix cell represents a specific outcome">
  <data key="d0">Each confusion matrix cell represents a specific outcome</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Each cell of the confusion matrix represents a specific outcome[21]"</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Key performance metrics are derived from confusion matrix components">
  <data key="d0">Key performance metrics are derived from confusion matrix components</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "By examining these components, we can derive key performance metrics such as accuracy, precision, recall, specificity, and the F1 score[22]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference [20] on Confusion Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Reference [20] on Confusion Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [20]. The source text gives no author, title or year. It is cited for using the confusion matrix to evaluate the trained model's ability to identify quality defects. This entity replaces the earlier label "Zhao, Confusion Matrix Reference [20]", whose author name was not supported by the text.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flattening Layer">
  <data key="d0">Flattening Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A layer that converts 2D feature maps into a 1D vector before the dense layer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dense Layer">
  <data key="d0">Dense Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A densely connected layer with 32 neurons and ReLU activation that follows the flattening layer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canny Edge Detection Filter">
  <data key="d0">Canny Edge Detection Filter</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Edge detection filter applied to input images as a pre-processing step before feeding them into the CNN; helps the model focus on essential image features and reduces false positives.&lt;SEP&gt;Edge detection pre-processing filter applied before feeding images into the CNN, improving accuracy, precision and F1-Score.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edge Detection Pre-Processing">
  <data key="d0">Edge Detection Pre-Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Use of edge detection as a pre-processing step to emphasize essential and relevant image features before classification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Image Dataset (3000 Train / 470 Test)">
  <data key="d0">Image Dataset (3000 Train / 470 Test)</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Image data set used to train (3000 images) and test (470 images) both CNN configurations, ensuring a fair and consistent comparison.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canny filter improves CNN classification performance">
  <data key="d0">Canny filter improves CNN classification performance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding of the paper: the CNN with the Canny filter achieved notably higher accuracy (99.57% vs 95.31%) and precision (99.44% vs 94.24%), suggesting edge detection helps the model focus on essential features and reduce false positives.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CNN Without Canny Filter">
  <data key="d0">CNN Without Canny Filter</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuration (1): a CNN model that processes raw images with no Canny filter pre-processing. It was trained on 3000 images and tested on 470 images. Results: accuracy 95.31%, precision 94.24%, recall 100%, F1-score 97.03%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CNN With Canny Filter">
  <data key="d0">CNN With Canny Filter</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuration (2): a CNN model that receives images after Canny edge detection pre-processing. It was trained on 3000 images and tested on 470 images. Results: accuracy 99.57%, precision 99.44%, recall 100%, F1-score 99.72%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Canny filter reduces false positives">
  <data key="d0">Canny filter reduces false positives</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "The substantial increase in precision indicates that the Canny filter helps the model reduce false positives by emphasizing the most relevant features of the images."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Both models identify all positive cases">
  <data key="d0">Both models identify all positive cases</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: recall stayed at 100% for both configurations, so both models correctly identified all actual positive cases in the dataset.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lee et al. (2021)">
  <data key="d0">Lee et al. (2021)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [7]. Prior study that achieved 96.94% accuracy using a model combining Canny filters and CNN (ResNet101) with 10,000 trained images.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ha et al. (2021)">
  <data key="d0">Ha et al. (2021)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [23]. Prior study that reached around 93% accuracy using CNN and edge detection with approximately 3,800 images for injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5436254d7328f14e8f79864da9fef604-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">MVML_120 (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467113</data>
