  <data key="d2">Author of "Review in Authentication for Mobile Ad hoc Network", affiliated with Sultan Moulay Slimane University, LIMATI Laboratory.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Factor Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Factor Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication approach coupling two or more different factors, providing higher protection of devices and online services against unauthorized access.&lt;SEP&gt;MFA; mentioned as needing to react promptly when biometric fingerprint verification fails to authenticate the correct individual.&lt;SEP&gt;Authentication approach that combines multiple factors; it is surveyed for V2X applications in reference 4.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Public Key Infrastructure">
  <data key="d0">Public Key Infrastructure</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication mechanism in wired and infrastructure-based wireless networks that manages digital certificates and public key encryption; cannot be applied directly to MANETs due to dynamic topology.&lt;SEP&gt;PKI; manages digital certificates and public key encryption for legitimate nodes in wired and infrastructure wireless networks; not directly applicable to MANET.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lack of centralized management causes security problems in ad hoc networks">
  <data key="d0">Lack of centralized management causes security problems in ad hoc networks</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Lack of Centralized Management: Ad hoc networks don't have controlling tools like a server or intrusion detection system, which leads to different security problems [1].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MANET characteristics enable adversaries to attack networks or nodes">
  <data key="d0">MANET characteristics enable adversaries to attack networks or nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">These characteristics open the door to adversaries to perform an attack on a network or a particular node. They can read or modify data flowing through the network or stop a particular service, etc. [2].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authentication can be performed via something we have, know, or are">
  <data key="d0">Authentication can be performed via something we have, know, or are</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text that authentication can be executed in three general forms: something one has (certificate, one-time password generator, key fob, smart card), something one knows (password, PIN code, security question answer), and something one is (fingerprint, iris scan, voice, speech pattern). Citing sentence: "Something we are, such as a fingerprint, iris scan, voice, or speech pattern [3]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-factor authentication provides higher protection against unauthorized access">
  <data key="d0">Multi-factor authentication provides higher protection against unauthorized access</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">It provides a higher level of safety and protection of computing devices and online services from unauthorized access [4].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wireless Links">
  <data key="d0">Wireless Links</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MANET characteristic in which wireless transmission links make ad hoc networks vulnerable to attacks such as eavesdropping and traffic analysis. Attackers do not need physical access, and malicious nodes can exploit the network's lower bandwidth to prevent regular communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lack of Centralized Management">
  <data key="d0">Lack of Centralized Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MANET characteristic in which ad hoc networks lack controlling tools such as a server or intrusion detection system, which leads to security problems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Single-factor authentication does not provide adequate protection">
  <data key="d0">Single-factor authentication does not provide adequate protection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "the authentication with just a single factor does not provide adequate protection due to multiple security threats. Therefore, Multi-factor Authentication (MFA) was proposed to couple two or more different factors."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Certificate">
  <data key="d0">Digital Certificate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Credential managed by PKI and issued to legitimate nodes that have the right to access network services. Certificates are also cited as an example of the 'something we have' authentication factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sharma and Gangal [6]">
  <data key="d0">Sharma and Gangal [6]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work by Sharma and Gangal that integrates a clustering technique for MANET authentication; nodes are authenticated by an elected cluster head using the AUCRES algorithm.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Verma et al. [7]">
  <data key="d0">Verma et al. [7]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work by Verma et al. presenting a robust authentication mechanism based on certificate exchange between nodes, requiring MIN-CERTIFICATE members and using digital signatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ramkumar et al. [8]">
  <data key="d0">Ramkumar et al. [8]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work by Ramkumar et al. combining authentication and intrusion detection into a single console using static IDs and fingerprints across four levels of security.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Umair and Munam [9]">
  <data key="d0">Umair and Munam [9]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work by Umair and Munam combining authentication with confidential communication using Group-id, Group-ip and server-provided symmetric keys.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hacha et al. [10]">
  <data key="d0">Hacha et al. [10]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work by Hacha et al. suggesting an authentication scheme using smart antennas, hash chaining and a reputation-based system to protect SIP node credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [10]. Proposes an authentication scheme for SIP nodes in MANET using smart antennas, hash chaining and a reputation-based system. The scheme protects SIP node credentials, ensures authentication of registered nodes, provides security against eavesdropping, replay attacks, impersonation and selfishness, demands less calculation for authentication materials, and develops location-based services. Its drawbacks are more computation for position location and hardware changes to replace omnidirectional antennas with smart ones.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sharma">
  <data key="d0">Sharma</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-author of the clustering-based MANET authentication work cited as [6].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
