<node id="Certifying Authority">
  <data key="d0">Certifying Authority</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CA; a single node acting as certifier creates a vulnerability point in MANET and may be unreachable due to mobility, motivating decentralization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Clustering Technique">
  <data key="d0">Clustering Technique</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Algorithm dividing the network into clusters and electing the highest-weight node as cluster head, suited to MANET without TTP or CA.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique that reference [12] combines with a machine learning algorithm to predict crash injury severity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Certificate Exchange">
  <data key="d0">Certificate Exchange</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication mechanism in which a new node proves authenticity with MIN-CERTIFICATE members before joining the MANET.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fingerprint Verification">
  <data key="d0">Fingerprint Verification</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Biometric authentication with limitations such as false dismissing, false acknowledgment and inability to catch.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Symmetric Key Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Symmetric Key Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Encryption of node communication with a server-provided symmetric key, characterized by simplicity and low memory and power usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Encryption with symmetric keys, which are simple, use less memory and consume less power.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Session Initiation Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Session Initiation Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">SIP; signaling protocol used to start, modify and terminate calls or multimedia sessions over IP networks.&lt;SEP&gt;SIP; the protocol whose node credentials Hacha et al.'s scheme protects. The scheme also ensures authentication of registered SIP nodes over the IP network.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SIP Identity Theft">
  <data key="d0">SIP Identity Theft</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Example of identity credential theft or forging problem in MANET.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Antennas">
  <data key="d0">Smart Antennas</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Antennas directing power to the precise position of the destination node rather than diffusing in all directions.&lt;SEP&gt;Antennas directing power to the precise position of the destination node instead of diffusing it in all directions; used in Hacha et al.'s scheme.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hash Chaining">
  <data key="d0">Hash Chaining</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Technique used to protect SIP node credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;Technique used in Hacha et al.'s authentication scheme to protect SIP node credentials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reputation-Based System">
  <data key="d0">Reputation-Based System</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">System used alongside smart antennas and hash chaining to protect SIP credentials and authenticate registered nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;System where users select well-reputed neighbours as guarantors to confirm identity to the registrar, avoiding selfish and misbehaving nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Key distribution schemes add load and are prone to attacks">
  <data key="d0">Key distribution schemes add load and are prone to attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In addition, the key distribution schemes apply additional loads on the network and they are prone to many attacks [ 5].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confidential Communication">
  <data key="d0">Confidential Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security mechanism that Umair and Munam combine with authentication. Communication between two nodes is encrypted with a symmetric key that the server provides after successful authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MIN-CERTIFICATE">
  <data key="d0">MIN-CERTIFICATE</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The minimum number of network members with which a new node must prove its authenticity before joining the MANET in the certificate-exchange scheme. Authentication risks failing if fewer nodes than MIN-CERTIFICATE are available.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Group-id and Group-ip">
  <data key="d0">Group-id and Group-ip</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Parameters that valid nodes receive from the network admin. The server requests them when nodes try to join the ad hoc network in the Umair and Munam scheme.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Continuous Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Continuous Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combination of continuous authentication and intrusion detection, described as the significant advantage of the Ramkumar et al. system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467168</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Performance Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Network Performance Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">End-to-end delay, throughput and packet dropping, used in simulations to evaluate the certificate-exchange authentication mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Identity Credential Theft">
  <data key="d0">Identity Credential Theft</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Theft or forging of identity credentials, a major problem in MANET. It arises from the absence of encryption or hash functions in some authentication schemes, and SIP identity theft is one example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zafar and Soni [11]">
  <data key="d0">Zafar and Soni [11]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [11]. Discusses disadvantages of existing ad hoc network protocols and proposes the Biometric Stationed Authentication Protocol (BSAP), which combines iris-based biometrics, a genetic algorithm and cryptography. BSAP applies three levels of security that develop trust between ad hoc network nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zheng et al. [14]">
  <data key="d0">Zheng et al. [14]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [14]. Addresses the need for a Blockchain-based authentication system for VANETs using CA-issued pseudonyms, providing a secure, decentralized system with responsibility and confidentiality.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biometric Stationed Authentication Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Biometric Stationed Authentication Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">BSAP; authentication protocol combining iris-based biometrics, genetic algorithm and cryptography, providing three levels of security.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DES Key Generation Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">DES Key Generation Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Feistel or DES key generation algorithm used in BSAP to produce a biometric cryptographic key.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Certificate Exchange Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Certificate Exchange Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Authentication based on exchanging certificates, from [7].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Symmetric Key Cryptography">
  <data key="d0">Symmetric Key Cryptography</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Cryptographic approach used in [9]; low memory and power usage but vulnerable if the shared key is compromised.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intrusion Detection">
  <data key="d0">Intrusion Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Combined with authentication in [8] to detect and eliminate malicious intruders.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blockchain provides a decentralized and distributed framework for MANET">
  <data key="d0">Blockchain provides a decentralized and distributed framework for MANET</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">By using Blockchain technology, we can take advantage of the decentralized and distributed framework [12].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blockchain transactions are validated by nodes and visible to the whole network">
  <data key="d0">Blockchain transactions are validated by nodes and visible to the whole network</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Transmissions between network users are grouped in blocks and each one is validated by network nodes and added to the Blockchain. The transaction is then visible to the receiver as well as the entire network [13].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Iris Recognition">
  <data key="d0">Iris Recognition</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Iris connotation process used in BSAP to generate strong biometric features. The input text describes iris biometrics as resolute and unique throughout human life.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pseudonym-Based Communication">
  <data key="d0">Pseudonym-Based Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Approach in Zheng et al.'s scheme where vehicles use pseudonyms issued by a CA to communicate without revealing their real identity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Location-Based Services">
  <data key="d0">Location-Based Services</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Services in MANET that the smart antenna-based scheme of Hacha et al. develops.&lt;SEP&gt;Attractive VANET service in urban environments, listed with Internet access, automatic toll payment and traffic management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Selfish And Misbehaving Nodes">
  <data key="d0">Selfish And Misbehaving Nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Nodes that perturb network progress. The reputation-based system and Hacha et al.'s scheme protect against them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fingerprint Recognition">
  <data key="d0">Fingerprint Recognition</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Biometric technique whose limitations are the disadvantage of the authentication and intrusion detection approach in [8].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [11] Biometric Stationed Authentication Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Ref [11] Biometric Stationed Authentication Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [11]. Proposes a biometric stationed authentication protocol that uses three security levels: iris biometrics, a genetic algorithm and cryptography. Its limitations include difficulty separating the iris from the eyelid, pupil and reflections, and sensitivity to illumination.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [14] Blockchain-Based Authentication System">
  <data key="d0">Ref [14] Blockchain-Based Authentication System</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [14]. Proposes a Blockchain-based authentication system for VANETs that offers faster processing, data that is hard to delete or modify, and confidentiality and privacy. Its drawback is high energy consumption costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper (1).pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467169</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Blockchain-based authentication incurs high energy consumption costs">
  <data key="d0">Blockchain-based authentication incurs high energy consumption costs</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The high costs due to energy consumption [15]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-003</data>
