<node id="Microservices-Driven Automation in Full-Stack Development: Bridging Efficiency and Innovation with FSMicroGenerator">
  <data key="d0">Microservices-Driven Automation in Full-Stack Development: Bridging Efficiency and Innovation with FSMicroGenerator</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, accepted for publication in IEEE Access; presents FSMicroGenerator, a low-code code generation tool that uses UML class diagrams and templates to generate multilingual full-stack web applications based on a microservices architecture, supporting DevSecOps practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Samira Khalfaoui">
  <data key="d0">Samira Khalfaoui</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Corresponding author of the FSMicroGenerator paper, affiliated with the Intelligent Automation and BioMedGenomics Laboratory, Abdelmalek Essaâdi University.&lt;SEP&gt;GitHub account owner (samiraKHALFAOUI) hosting the fsmicrogenerator-evaluation repository; likely an author of the article.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of the article; State Engineering Diploma in Information Systems from ENSA Tangier (2021), Ph.D. candidate in Computer Science researching AI integration into software engineering, model-driven approaches, DevSecOps and intelligent code generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low-Code Approach">
  <data key="d0">Low-Code Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Development approach underlying FSMicroGenerator that reduces technical barriers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UML Class Diagram">
  <data key="d0">UML Class Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Modeling artifact used by FSMicroGenerator as input for code generation.&lt;SEP&gt;UML diagram type used to define the business data model, specifying entities, their attributes, and relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagram representing business entities and their relationships, serving as design-time input to the data model definition process.&lt;SEP&gt;Modeling notation used to formalize the domain model of the inventory management case study.&lt;SEP&gt;Modeling notation according to which users manually define business entities via forms in FSMicroGenerator's semi-manual package creation stage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Automatic Code Generation">
  <data key="d0">Automatic Code Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Research topic of automatically producing source code, central to the FSMicroGenerator paper.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
