  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expectations for software functionality continue to rise">
  <data key="d0">Expectations for software functionality continue to rise</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">With rapid advances in technology and the growing demand for sophisticated IT systems, the expectations for software functionality continue to rise [1].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="The amount of code to develop and maintain daily is overwhelming">
  <data key="d0">The amount of code to develop and maintain daily is overwhelming</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">However, the massive amount of code that needs to be developed and maintained daily is becoming extremely overwhelming [2].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Developers spend almost 80% of their time debugging">
  <data key="d0">Developers spend almost 80% of their time debugging</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In 2002, a study by the National Institute of Standards and Technology revealed that developers spend almost 80% of their time debugging and fixing bugs, with around 40 to 50% of this effort devoted to rework that could have been avoided [3].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model-driven paradigms position modeling as fundamental to development efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Model-driven paradigms position modeling as fundamental to development efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Early paradigms such as MDA, MDD, MDE, MBA, and MDSE have positioned modeling as a fundamental approach to improving development efficiency [4].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Development environments incorporate TBCG mechanisms such as T4 and Apache Velocity">
  <data key="d0">Development environments incorporate TBCG mechanisms such as T4 and Apache Velocity</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">To mitigate these limitations, development environments have incorporated Template-Based Code Generation (TBCG) mechanisms, such as Microsoft's Text Template Transformation Toolkit (T4) and Apache Velocity [5].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467611</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
