</node>
<node id="Full-Stack Development">
  <data key="d0">Full-Stack Development</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Development covering both frontend and backend. Most existing code generation tools focus on only one side, which makes full-stack development difficult. FSMicroGenerator targets full-stack web applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Development covering frontend and backend components with clear separation, modular and scalable architectures.&lt;SEP&gt;Development of complete web applications covering frontend and backend. FSMicroGenerator automates full-stack development from development to deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Role of developers managing both user interfaces and backend services, increasingly sought by companies.&lt;SEP&gt;Development spanning frontend and backend; FSMicroGenerator automates the generation of multilingual full-stack solutions from development to deployment with integrated monitoring and supervision.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Debt">
  <data key="d0">Technical Debt</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Consequence of shadow IT, especially when non-developers build applications without proper governance.&lt;SEP&gt;Increased by reliance on heterogeneous languages and frameworks, complicating maintenance and slowing project evolution.&lt;SEP&gt;Accumulated cost of suboptimal software design. FSMicroGenerator aims to reduce technical debt.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk assessed as part of maintainability evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;Software maintenance burden that FSMicroGenerator helps reduce by applying widely accepted development practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Software quality concern that FSMicroGenerator helps reduce.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Talent Shortage in Software Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Talent Shortage in Software Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Shortage of skilled developers that makes modern architectures harder for companies to implement. The shortage contradicts the expertise demands of modeling paradigms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multilingual Web Applications">
  <data key="d0">Multilingual Web Applications</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Web applications supporting multiple languages, as generated by FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reusable Functional Blocks Catalog">
  <data key="d0">Reusable Functional Blocks Catalog</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalog of ready-to-use functional blocks created by FSMicroGenerator. The blocks can be reused and integrated into other solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model-Driven Paradigms Depend Heavily on Modeling Expertise">
  <data key="d0">Model-Driven Paradigms Depend Heavily on Modeling Expertise</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Limitation of modeling paradigms: they face challenges of complexity, scalability and model transformation efficiency, and they are less accessible to non-technical users.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator Tool">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator Tool</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Low-code tool and unified framework proposed by the paper that generates full-stack microservices web applications from UML class diagrams and templates, integrating DevSecOps practices for security.&lt;SEP&gt;Code generation tool that produces microservice applications with a frontend, API Gateway, and microservices, built-in containerization, CI/CD pipelines, security checks, and monitoring instrumentation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467612</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="10.1109/access.2025.3589285">
  <data key="d0">10.1109/access.2025.3589285</data>
  <data key="d1">identifier</data>
  <data key="d2">10.1109/access.2025.3589285 is the Digital Object Identifier (DOI) of the article that presents and describes FSMicroGenerator. The article was accepted for publication in IEEE Access, and the DOI identifies the FSMicroGenerator paper within that journal.

In the source material, this DOI also refers to "This Paper," meaning the article being read. It appears in the article's citation information.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [14]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [14]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [14]; reference on shadow IT and technical debt from ungoverned non-developer applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Work cited as [14] for the emergence of GPT-4.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work discussing requirements of MANET routing protocols and multiple existing MANET routing protocols, with one example per routing category.&lt;SEP&gt;Proposes new ways to improve VANET performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work that improved VANET performance by detecting and removing unused and useless packets; it is evaluated by message expiration ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Template-Based Code Generation">
  <data key="d0">Template-Based Code Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">TBCG; since the 1990s simplifies code generation using predefined templates with static code and dynamic meta-code processed by a template engine; limited to specific domains like UI, CRUD and API generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Approach in which templates with placeholders such as ${entityName} and ${controllerName} are substituted with entity details to generate backend files following the pattern ${entityName}.&lt;component&gt;.js.&lt;SEP&gt;Code generation approach based on templates. It is the topic of the cited works by Uyanik and Şahin and by Shinde and Sun.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Text Template Transformation Toolkit">
  <data key="d0">Text Template Transformation Toolkit</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Microsoft's T4, a TBCG mechanism incorporated into development environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model-Driven Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Model-Driven Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MDE; relies on model-to-text transformations generating code from platform-independent models refined into platform-specific models.&lt;SEP&gt;Software engineering approach (MDE) built on models and domain-specific languages. A cited systematic review examines its use in AI software systems engineering.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low-Code/No-Code Platforms">
  <data key="d0">Low-Code/No-Code Platforms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">LCNC platforms enabling rapid creation of applications with minimal coding through graphical interfaces and predefined components; limited by vendor lock-in, customization and scalability issues.&lt;SEP&gt;LCNC development platforms that often impose restrictions on architecture and languages used, offering less flexibility than FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Citizen Developers">
  <data key="d0">Citizen Developers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Concept introduced by LCNC platforms of non-professional developers building applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shadow IT">
  <data key="d0">Shadow IT</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phenomenon where employees adopt unauthorized tools bypassing official processes, leading to technical debt.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vendor Lock-In">
  <data key="d0">Vendor Lock-In</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Limitation of LCNC solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467620</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UML Class Diagrams">
  <data key="d0">UML Class Diagrams</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Modeling notation used as input for automatic code generation tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Models used by FSMicroGenerator as input to generate applications.&lt;SEP&gt;UML diagrams used in the package creation stage to specify entities, their attributes and relationships in the business data model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TBCG Is Implemented By Tools Such As T4 And Apache Velocity">
  <data key="d0">TBCG Is Implemented By Tools Such As T4 And Apache Velocity</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">To mitigate these limitations, development environments have incorporated Template-Based Code Generation (TBCG) mechanisms, such as Microsoft's Text Template Transformation Toolkit (T4) and Apache Velocity [5].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TBCG Gained Popularity Due To Effectiveness And Ease Of Use">
  <data key="d0">TBCG Gained Popularity Due To Effectiveness And Ease Of Use</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This technique, based on the principle of 'code once, implement everywhere', has gained popularity due to its effectiveness and ease of use [6].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TBCG Limitations Reduce Accessibility For Non-Technical Users">
  <data key="d0">TBCG Limitations Reduce Accessibility For Non-Technical Users</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">These factors reduce its accessibility for non-technical users [6].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TBCG Bridges Modeling And Programming Within MDE">
  <data key="d0">TBCG Bridges Modeling And Programming Within MDE</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Although MDE relies on model-to-text transformations to generate code from platform-independent models refined into platform-specific models [7], TBCG improves automation by using predefined templates. This ensures higher abstraction and more effective bridging between modeling and programming [7].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LCNC Platforms Introduce Citizen Developers">
  <data key="d0">LCNC Platforms Introduce Citizen Developers</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">LCNC platforms enable the rapid creation of efficient and scalable applications with minimal coding effort, introducing the concept of citizen developers in application development [8].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GenAI Supports Code Generation, Completion, Translation And Defect Detection">
  <data key="d0">GenAI Supports Code Generation, Completion, Translation And Defect Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">GenAI also supports code refinement to improve readability and efficiency, code summarization that provides concise explanations of complex modules, and defect detection to identify errors and redundant code through clone detection [9]–[11].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LCNC Solutions Cause Vendor Lock-In And Scalability Issues">
  <data key="d0">LCNC Solutions Cause Vendor Lock-In And Scalability Issues</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">LCNC solutions can lead to vendor lock-in [12], limited customization, and scalability issues in high-load environments [13].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shadow IT Leads To Technical Debt">
  <data key="d0">Shadow IT Leads To Technical Debt</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This can lead to technical debt, especially when non-developers build applications without proper governance [13], [14].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GenAI Tools Are Prone To Errors And Security Risks">
  <data key="d0">GenAI Tools Are Prone To Errors And Security Risks</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Similarly, GenAI tools depend on training data quality, making them prone to errors, incomplete solutions, and security risks [15]. Ensuring compliance with coding standards remains challenging [9]</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Over-Reliance On AI Weakens Developer Problem-Solving Skills">
  <data key="d0">Over-Reliance On AI Weakens Developer Problem-Solving Skills</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Over-reliance on AI can also weaken the problem-solving skills of developers over time [16].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ensuring GenAI Compliance With Coding Standards Is Challenging">
  <data key="d0">Ensuring GenAI Compliance With Coding Standards Is Challenging</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Ensuring compliance with coding standards remains challenging [9], and Artificial Intelligence (AI) alone cannot replace human oversight in complex decision-making."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Apache">
  <data key="d0">Apache</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Organization behind Apache Velocity, a TBCG mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model-To-Text Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Model-To-Text Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Transformation that MDE relies on to generate code from platform-independent models refined into platform-specific models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467621</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Software Engineering Talent Shortage">
  <data key="d0">Software Engineering Talent Shortage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Growing shortage of skilled developers that drives demand for code generation and LCNC solutions requiring minimal technical expertise.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001</data>
