</node>
<node id="Spring">
  <data key="d0">Spring</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Backend framework used in the Livraghi tool.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AngularJS">
  <data key="d0">AngularJS</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Frontend framework used in the Livraghi tool.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ražinskas and Čeponienė [19] MDA-Based Laravel Code Generation">
  <data key="d0">Ražinskas and Čeponienė [19] MDA-Based Laravel Code Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [19]; by Mantas Ražinskas and Lina Čeponienė; proposes an MDA-based methodology for automatic generation of Laravel code from UML diagrams via PIM, model-to-model and model-to-code transformations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prasanthan et al. [2] Backend as a Service">
  <data key="d0">Prasanthan et al. [2] Backend as a Service</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [2]; study by Prasanthan et al. presenting Backend as a Service (BaaS), a tool generating preconfigured backend code with CRUD and authentication from a JSON data model, output as a Docker container.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tesoriero et al. [20] MDA Full-Stack Web Application Development">
  <data key="d0">Tesoriero et al. [20] MDA Full-Stack Web Application Development</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [20]; offers an MDA-based comprehensive solution for full-stack development of multi-layered web applications from UML class diagrams, using PHP (Propel ORM), REST APIs and Polymer, with a monolithic client-server architecture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UML">
  <data key="d0">UML</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Unified Modeling Language; UML diagrams and class diagrams serve as input models for code generation in [19] and [20].&lt;SEP&gt;Widely adopted and well-known modeling language that ensures ease of learning and reduces design time; used for defining business data models via class diagrams and for depicting the package lifecycle via a state diagram.&lt;SEP&gt;Widely adopted modeling language whose class diagrams are used to define the business data model of a package.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eclipse Acceleo">
  <data key="d0">Eclipse Acceleo</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Open-source code generation tool that transforms models into code based on MDA; used for model-to-code transformation in [19].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model-to-Model Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Model-to-Model Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Transformation generating a platform-specific model from a platform-independent model by applying transformation rules, including Laravel-specific stereotypes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model-to-Code Transformation">
  <data key="d0">Model-to-Code Transformation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Final transformation stage generating PHP files from models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backend as a Service">
  <data key="d0">Backend as a Service</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">BaaS tool that accelerates backend development by generating a preconfigured code base with CRUD functionality and authentication; improved efficiency and reduced deployment errors but limited to backend and lacks service assembly and communication features.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467633</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Propel ORM">
  <data key="d0">Propel ORM</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">PHP ORM used for the backend in the Tesoriero et al. tool.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Polymer">
  <data key="d0">Polymer</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">UI library used for UI generation in the Tesoriero et al. tool.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="REST API">
  <data key="d0">REST API</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Communication mechanism used in the Tesoriero et al. tool.&lt;SEP&gt;API provided by the backend for data handling.&lt;SEP&gt;Interface style through which microservices expose their functionality.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Papyrus">
  <data key="d0">Papyrus</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Eclipse-based modeling tool used for integration in the Tesoriero et al. tool.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Package">
  <data key="d0">Package</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Base logical unit in FSMicroGenerator containing specific, autonomous, reusable functionalities grouping tightly coupled business units.&lt;SEP&gt;Base unit containing specific, autonomous, reusable functionalities that group tightly coupled business units; the core unit of FSMicroGenerator with a lifecycle from creation to pre-integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prior Code Generation Tools Lack Microservices Integration">
  <data key="d0">Prior Code Generation Tools Lack Microservices Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement from the literature analysis: "Most tools favor monolithic architectures, despite the advantages of microservices, and those that adopt microservices often lack mechanisms for service integration and communication, making them unsuitable for distributed systems."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Claim: Ražinskas and Čeponienė's MDA approach reduces Laravel development time and errors">
  <data key="d0">Claim: Ražinskas and Čeponienė's MDA approach reduces Laravel development time and errors</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "This research aims to simplify information system development with PHP Laravel by automating UML-to-Laravel code transformation, reducing development time and errors."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BaaS improves efficiency and produces uniform, maintainable code">
  <data key="d0">BaaS improves efficiency and produces uniform, maintainable code</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text about [2]: "Results showed that BaaS improved efficiency, reduced deployment errors via Docker, and generated uniform, maintainable code."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tesoriero et al. tool is restricted to specific technologies and monolithic">
  <data key="d0">Tesoriero et al. tool is restricted to specific technologies and monolithic</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text about [20]: "However, the tool is restricted to specific technologies (e.g., MySQL for persistence) and lacks support for non-relational databases or advanced frontend frameworks. Additionally, its monolithic structure limits scalability, and customization options remain insufficient for complex applications."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XMI">
  <data key="d0">XMI</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">XML Metadata Interchange format used to export the platform-independent UML model in the Ražinskas and Čeponienė methodology [19].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platform-Independent Model">
  <data key="d0">Platform-Independent Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Model created with UML tools and exported in XMI format as the first stage of the MDA-based Laravel code generation process in [19].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platform-Specific Model">
  <data key="d0">Platform-Specific Model</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Model generated from the platform-independent model by model-to-model transformation rules, including Laravel-specific stereotypes such as 'LaravelModel', 'LaravelController' and 'LaravelBlade', in [19].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MySQL">
  <data key="d0">MySQL</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Relational database used for persistence in the Tesoriero et al. tool [20]; cited as an example of the tool's restriction to specific technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CRUD Functionality">
  <data key="d0">CRUD Functionality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Create, read, update and delete operations included in the preconfigured backend code base generated by BaaS [2].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TagML">
  <data key="d0">TagML</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">TagML-based XML processing used by the Tesoriero et al. tool [20] to ensure interoperability with third-party systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PHP">
  <data key="d0">PHP</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Programming language underlying Laravel and used for the backend (with Propel ORM) in the Tesoriero et al. tool; [19] generates PHP files.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Module">
  <data key="d0">Module</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Combination of packages or other modules collaborating to cover a larger or complete business functionality, with looser coupling than within a package.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Project">
  <data key="d0">Project</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Complete, ready-to-use application built by combining modules and packages, with weak or no coupling between entities that collaborate via clearly defined interfaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Domain-Driven Design">
  <data key="d0">Domain-Driven Design</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Design approach (DDD) leveraged to decompose systems into bounded contexts aligned with business domains.&lt;SEP&gt;Design principles structuring the case study's UML domain model into bounded contexts implemented as independent microservices.&lt;SEP&gt;Design approach whose principles were used to structure the case study domain model into bounded contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Design approach used in reference [21] to design microservice-based applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bounded Contexts">
  <data key="d0">Bounded Contexts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Decomposition units in Domain-Driven Design, corresponding to packages and modules, aligned with business domains.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Template Management">
  <data key="d0">Template Management</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Heart of FSMicroGenerator, responsible for defining, organizing and customizing predefined code models (templates) used to generate packages, modules or projects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Templates">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Templates</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Templates that generate code snapshots for individual solution components, including microservices templates and Angular frontend templates.&lt;SEP&gt;Specialized parameterized templates (e.g., using ${entityName}, ${packageName}) that the engine uses to generate API routes, Angular modules, components and core files.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Static Templates">
  <data key="d0">Static Templates</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Templates loaded to establish foundational architecture and directory structure, including API Gateway configuration, base frontend and microservices structures, and integration points for complementary microservices.&lt;SEP&gt;Templates defining the overall architecture and structure of the generated solution as a predefined skeleton, ensuring standardization and accelerating development.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Angular">
  <data key="d0">Angular</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Frontend framework for which frontend templates are tailored to create UIs interacting with microservices.&lt;SEP&gt;Frontend framework for which the engine generates package-level modules, routing files, list, add, clone and translate components, and core TypeScript files.&lt;SEP&gt;Frontend framework used for the FSMicroGenerator UI.&lt;SEP&gt;A frontend framework that delivers responsive client-side interfaces in the MEAN stack.&lt;SEP&gt;Frontend framework whose standardized components are used in generated solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Frontend framework used for the components generated by FSMicroGenerator for the digital freight exchange platform.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Generation Engine">
  <data key="d0">Code Generation Engine</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Component converting user configurations into ready-to-use source code using templates; validates data consistency, resolves dependencies, ensures schema compatibility, and is extensible.&lt;SEP&gt;Engine described in This Paper that generates backend, frontend, i18n and infrastructure files from entity configurations using dynamic and specialized templates, then organizes and pushes the complete source code to a repository.&lt;SEP&gt;Engine within FSMicroGenerator that extracts the package configuration, loads static templates and iterates over entities with dynamic templates to generate code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MVC Pattern">
  <data key="d0">MVC Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Model-View-Controller pattern followed by generated code for better readability and maintenance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Interface">
  <data key="d0">User Interface</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Main interaction point between developers and FSMicroGenerator, providing management of packages, modules, projects, users, teams, role-based access and multi-language support.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Package Lifecycle">
  <data key="d0">Package Lifecycle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lifecycle of a package in FSMicroGenerator comprising creation, validation, adaptation, and pre-integration stages, ending with the package marked 'Ready for integration'.&lt;SEP&gt;Lifecycle of a package in FSMicroGenerator from creation to pre-integration, starting with a creation stage of configuration and data modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;Lifecycle of packages in FSMicroGenerator whose creation stage currently relies on a semi-manual approach where users define business entities via forms, which can introduce errors or slow initial configuration in large-scale projects.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UML eases learning and reduces design time">
  <data key="d0">UML eases learning and reduces design time</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "UML is a widely adopted and well-known modeling language that ensures ease of learning and reduces design time [20],"</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microservices Templates">
  <data key="d0">Microservices Templates</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic templates in FSMicroGenerator that produce all files needed to build and run an independent microservice.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frontend Templates">
  <data key="d0">Frontend Templates</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Dynamic templates in FSMicroGenerator that supply files to create the UI, specifically tailored for the Angular framework to interact with generated microservices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467640</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DevSecOps">
  <data key="d0">DevSecOps</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DevSecOps is a practice and set of principles that integrates security into every stage of software development and operations. Rather than treating security as a post-deployment concern, it builds security into the delivery pipeline as a native "shift-left" step. The approach embeds automated security checks and continuous testing throughout the development lifecycle, combining automation, collaboration, and asset security to produce well-architected, secure solutions.

Within the context of FSMicroGenerator, DevSecOps plays a central role. Its principles inspired the design of the FSMicroGenerator infrastructure and were adopted by the tool to produce well-architected solutions and to support collaboration between development and operations teams. DevSecOps practices are integrated directly into the architecture that FSMicroGenerator generates, which strengthens the security of the resulting systems. FSMicroGenerator in turn makes it easier to apply DevSecOps across the development and operations lifecycle.

DevSecOps also features in Samira Khalfaoui's research, where its practices are combined with artificial intelligence (AI) and model-driven approaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Creation Stage">
  <data key="d0">Creation Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">First lifecycle stage in which the data entry team provides basic configuration (package name, database name, service port, responsible team), defines the business data model with UML class diagrams, and configures auto-generated tables and forms. Default validation rules enforce naming conventions, uniqueness and type compatibility before the package is submitted for validation.&lt;SEP&gt;First phase of the package lifecycle, in which the user provides basic configuration (package name, database name, service port, responsible data entry team) and defines the business data model using UML class diagrams.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Language Support">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Language Support</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Feature of the FSMicroGenerator user interface that removes language barriers and improves the experience for international or multicultural teams.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Role-Based Access Management">
  <data key="d0">Role-Based Access Management</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">User, team and role-based access management provided by the FSMicroGenerator user interface.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UML State Diagram">
  <data key="d0">UML State Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">UML diagram used in Figure 1 to depict the lifecycle of a package.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Validation Stage">
  <data key="d0">Validation Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lifecycle stage where a validation user familiar with UML and the business context reviews the package for consistency with functional and technical requirements, returning it for correction if errors are found.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptation Stage">
  <data key="d0">Adaptation Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lifecycle stage where the conceptual model is transformed into executable code by triggering generation, assigning the adaptation team, and performing tests and adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pre-Integration Stage">
  <data key="d0">Pre-Integration Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Final lifecycle stage that detects remaining inconsistencies and optionally validates code quality, structure, performance, resilience, and compliance before integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generation Process">
  <data key="d0">Generation Process</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Structured process used by FSMicroGenerator during adaptation: configuration extraction, skeleton setup with static templates, and backend microservices generation with dynamic templates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Microservices Templates">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Microservices Templates</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Specialized templates used to generate backend code files (model, repository, controller) for each entity following the naming pattern ${entityName}.&lt;component&gt;.js.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="API Gateway">
  <data key="d0">API Gateway</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Gateway component whose configuration is included in the predefined skeleton generated from static templates.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer handling request management and service orchestration: service registry, centralized security enforcement, routing, and load balancing; acts as the sole secure entry point managing authentication and authorization via JSON Web Token.&lt;SEP&gt;A component of the applications generated by FSMicroGenerator, deployed alongside the frontend and the microservices.&lt;SEP&gt;Component of generated applications whose service registry supplies Prometheus with a dynamic list of microservice endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Microservices architecture pattern used in generated solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Secure gateway integrating connected vehicles and user applications with the blockchain system.&lt;SEP&gt;Secure gateway connecting vehicles and user applications to the smart contracts in the proposed architecture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26549e3ff493405b55b221c1d804516e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26549e3ff493405b55b221c1d804516e-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;poster_nihad.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501149</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UML Eases Learning And Reduces Design Time">
  <data key="d0">UML Eases Learning And Reduces Design Time</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "UML is a widely adopted and well-known modeling language that ensures ease of learning and reduces design time [20], making it an ideal choice for user input."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Configuration Extraction">
  <data key="d0">Configuration Extraction</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Step 1 of the generation process. After the adaptation team validates the package definition and triggers generation, the code generation engine extracts the complete package configuration, including the data model and UI component specifications (tables, forms).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Skeleton Setup">
  <data key="d0">Skeleton Setup</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Step 2 of the generation process. The engine loads static templates to create a predefined skeleton with the API Gateway configuration, base frontend and microservices structures, and integration points for complementary microservices. The step ensures structural standardization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backend Microservices Generation">
  <data key="d0">Backend Microservices Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Step 3 of the generation process. The engine iterates through each entity and uses dynamic microservices templates to generate backend code files (model, repository, controller) for the main package microservice.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HTML Component Generation">
  <data key="d0">HTML Component Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">FSMicroGenerator feature that automatically generates fully customizable HTML tables and forms from the data model. The feature maps input types to suitable UI elements (e.g., a date field becomes a date picker) and allows real-time preview and adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model Component">
  <data key="d0">Model Component</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Generated backend file that defines the data model from entity definitions. Listing 1 presents a simplified template snapshot for generating it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frontend Application">
  <data key="d0">Frontend Application</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Base frontend application structure generated from static templates, with common utilities such as reusable components, pipes, directives and custom data validators.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joi">
  <data key="d0">Joi</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Schema description language and data validator for JavaScript, used to generate validation schemas for input validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Express.js">
  <data key="d0">Express.js</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">JavaScript web framework; a template is used to generate the Express.js router file mapping HTTP methods and paths to controller functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Node.js web framework for which the engine generates API route files via templates, including routes for getAll, add, updateState and translation endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Web framework used with Node.js to provide the REST API of FSMicroGenerator.&lt;SEP&gt;A Node.js framework that simplifies API routing in the MEAN stack.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mongoose">
  <data key="d0">Mongoose</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">MongoDB object modeling library for JavaScript; a template generates Mongoose entity schemas including attributes, references, constraints and timestamps.&lt;SEP&gt;MongoDB object modeling library used in generated model files exporting entity schemas.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Swagger">
  <data key="d0">Swagger</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">API documentation specification used to generate ${entityName}.path.js and ${entityName}.schema.js documentation files.&lt;SEP&gt;Tool providing API documentation for FSMicroGenerator services.&lt;SEP&gt;Tool used for automated API documentation, simplifying integration and developer onboarding.&lt;SEP&gt;A tool that automates API documentation and provides an interactive interface for exploring endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Tool for automated API documentation that simplifies integration and developer onboarding.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message Queues">
  <data key="d0">Message Queues</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Asynchronous communication mechanism for which code is generated to subscribe to queues and observe RPC calls, facilitating inter-service communication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CRUD Operations">
  <data key="d0">CRUD Operations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Create, read, update and delete data access logic generated in the repository layer, including handling of translatable attributes.&lt;SEP&gt;Create, read, update, delete operations foundational to data management; FSMicroGenerator automates their standardized generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Basic create, read, update and delete functionality that FSMicroGenerator generates automatically. These are marked with an asterisk in the functional coverage checklist.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unit And Integration Testing">
  <data key="d0">Unit And Integration Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Testing approach for which two test files are generated per entity: one for unit tests and one for integration tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Handlebars-Style Templating">
  <data key="d0">Handlebars-Style Templating</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Templating syntax using partials (definePartial), #each, #if and #unless blocks, used in the conceptual recursive helper that renders entity attributes, sub-attributes, references and constraints in the Mongoose model template.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Translatable Attributes">
  <data key="d0">Translatable Attributes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Entity attributes marked with a 'translatable' constraint; the repository generates translation-handling data access logic for them and the model template separates translatable from non-translatable attributes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Static Template Skeleton">
  <data key="d0">Static Template Skeleton</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Static template established in Step 2 that defines the microservices structure and provides standard functions; generated backend files are placed into their designated locations within it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Environment Configuration Files">
  <data key="d0">Environment Configuration Files</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">.env files generated for different stages (development, testing, production) as common backend infrastructure files.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Model Definition Process">
  <data key="d0">Data Model Definition Process</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Process shown in Figure 2 in which business entities, their attributes, data types, constraints and relationships (association types and participant attributes) are defined through a UI, with a UML class diagram as design-time input.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Layered Backend Components">
  <data key="d0">Layered Backend Components</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Set of generated per-entity components: model, repository, schema validator, controller, routes, communication, tests and documentation, each produced as ${entityName}.&lt;component&gt;.js.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dynamic Table Component">
  <data key="d0">Dynamic Table Component</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Reusable static Angular table component (dynamic-table.component) used by generated list components, with headers and actions configured dynamically.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Internationalization">
  <data key="d0">Internationalization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">I18n step that collects keys for enums, labels, messages and breadcrumbs during generation, extracts values from the generator database for configured languages, and generates JSON files in assets/i18n/.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-functional requirement covering dynamic label translation and user language preference management. Manual implementation scores 0/5 and FSMicroGenerator scores 5/5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Docker Compose">
  <data key="d0">Docker Compose</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Container orchestration tooling for which the engine generates development and production docker-compose files.&lt;SEP&gt;An orchestration tool. FSMicroGenerator generates two Docker Compose files, one for development and one for production, to define the full application stack.&lt;SEP&gt;Container orchestration files generated by the engine for development and production environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Multi-container orchestration tool used by FSMicroGenerator. In production, the matching Docker Compose file is pulled and executed over a remote SSH step.&lt;SEP&gt;Tool currently used by FSMicroGenerator for local microservices management.&lt;SEP&gt;Used for Docker containerization and orchestration of the system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467642</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prometheus">
  <data key="d0">Prometheus</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Prometheus is an open-source, widely adopted, cloud-native monitoring solution. It collects metrics using a pull-based model and stores them in a time-series database, which supports trend analysis, anomaly detection, and long-term performance tracking. It is commonly used for scalable monitoring of microservice architectures.

Within FSMicroGenerator, Prometheus is an integrated infrastructure service for monitoring and is included in the generated Docker Compose files. Each generated module or microservice exposes a /metrics endpoint, which Prometheus scrapes. The scrape targets come from a dynamic endpoint list supplied by the API Gateway and from a prefilled prometheus.yml configuration file. The generation engine personalizes Prometheus's static configuration templates so that monitoring is tailored to each generated system.

Prometheus has also been used in research. Abbas et al. used it as a monitoring tool when evaluating post-quantum cryptographic schemes in Hyperledger Fabric.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502213</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CI/CD Pipeline">
  <data key="d0">CI/CD Pipeline</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous integration and deployment pipeline defined by a static template file, written in the text as ".gitbal-ci.yml" and likely meaning .gitlab-ci.yml. The engine personalizes this template during infrastructure and operations setup.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Separation Of Concerns">
  <data key="d0">Separation Of Concerns</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Design principle maintained by organizing package entity components into entity-specific subfolders within a dedicated Angular module.&lt;SEP&gt;Design principle ensured by the multi-layered organization of generated solutions, facilitating maintainability and scalability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Package-Level Angular Module">
  <data key="d0">Package-Level Angular Module</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Dedicated Angular module (${packageName}-management.module.ts) with its associated routing file, generated for each package. It encapsulates components related to the package's entities and organizes them into entity-specific subfolders to improve modularity and code structure. It is placed in the components/ directory.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Angular List Component">
  <data key="d0">Angular List Component</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Generated list component (list-${entityName}.component.html/.ts) that displays entity data in an HTML table using the reusable dynamic-table component. Its headers and actions, such as delete, translate, edit, detail, clone and add, depend on the configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entity Form Components">
  <data key="d0">Entity Form Components</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Generated form-based Angular components for manipulating data: add-${entityName}.component and clone-${entityName}.component, plus translate-${entityName}.component when translatable fields exist.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Core TypeScript Files">
  <data key="d0">Core TypeScript Files</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Essential per-entity files generated by specialized templates: ${entityName}.model.ts for the data structure, ${entityName}.service.ts for API interaction logic, and ${entityName}.resolver.ts for data fetching during routing. They are organized under shared directories such as shared/models/${packageName}/.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generator Database">
  <data key="d0">Generator Database</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Database of the code generator. The I18n step extracts values for collected keys from it for each configured language.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Body Validation Middleware">
  <data key="d0">Body Validation Middleware</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Middleware (bodyValidation.middleware) that provides validateBody, validateParam and schemas. Generated Express.js routes use it to validate request bodies and id parameters, including on the translation routes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Translation Routes">
  <data key="d0">Translation Routes</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Optional Express.js routes (/translate/:id) generated when an entity has translatable fields. They expose getTranslations (GET) and translateData (PATCH) controller actions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UI Configuration Interface">
  <data key="d0">UI Configuration Interface</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">User interface for previewing and configuring tables (e.g., for a Category entity) and for previewing and adjusting forms in real time (e.g., for a Product entity). The engine generates Angular components based on this table and form configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Source Code Submission">
  <data key="d0">Source Code Submission</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Step 6 of the engine's process. The engine organizes all generated and personalized files and automatically pushes the complete source code to a repository.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infrastructure And Operations Setup">
  <data key="d0">Infrastructure And Operations Setup</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Step 5 of the engine's process. Additional templates configure the operational environment, covering container orchestration, monitoring and CI/CD.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CI/CD">
  <data key="d0">CI/CD</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Continuous integration and delivery practices; the engine personalizes a static CI/CD pipeline template (.gitlab-ci.yml), and changes are validated through automated pipelines.&lt;SEP&gt;System-wide non-functional requirement for continuous integration and deployment. Each module contributes unit tests to the CI pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Node.js">
  <data key="d0">Node.js</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Runtime on which the FSMicroGenerator backend is built.&lt;SEP&gt;A JavaScript runtime that supports asynchronous operations in the MEAN stack.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MongoDB">
  <data key="d0">MongoDB</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Database storing FSMicroGenerator project configurations and metadata.&lt;SEP&gt;A NoSQL database that provides flexible data storage and stores data in BSON, which reduces query time and server load.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical service whose management is optimized via the singleton pattern in FSMicroGenerator-generated solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GitLab">
  <data key="d0">GitLab</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Private internally hosted Git platform integrated with FSMicroGenerator for secure storage and centralized version control, with restricted access and synchronized accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Role-Based Access Control">
  <data key="d0">Role-Based Access Control</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Strict RBAC enforced in the FSMicroGenerator ecosystem and offered as a pre-configured service in generated solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multilingual Support">
  <data key="d0">Multilingual Support</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Centralized multilingual support for dynamic entities and static UI elements in generated solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature of generated solutions providing internationalization for both dynamic entities and static UI elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Git">
  <data key="d0">Git</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Version control system; generated source code is pushed to a designated Git repository and changes are tracked via Git.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Container Orchestration">
  <data key="d0">Container Orchestration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Configuration of the operational environment through generated docker-compose files for development and production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operational monitoring configured through personalized static Prometheus and Grafana templates.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-functional requirement implemented with Prometheus metrics and Grafana dashboards. Each module exposes a /metrics endpoint. Manual implementation scores 0/5 and FSMicroGenerator scores 5/5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Development Server">
  <data key="d0">Development Server</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Dedicated server within the protected local network to which the adaptation team clones generated projects for internal validation, customization and refinement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptation Team">
  <data key="d0">Adaptation Team</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Team notified when generated code is pushed; clones generated projects to the development server for testing, customization and integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Encryption at Rest">
  <data key="d0">Encryption at Rest</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Security measure in which sensitive data such as configurations and API keys are encrypted at rest.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Audit Logging">
  <data key="d0">Audit Logging</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Logging of all critical actions for traceability and audit purposes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Isolation">
  <data key="d0">Network Isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Operation of FSMicroGenerator server, GitLab and the development server within a protected local network, preventing external exposure of source code and company assets.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entity Cloning">
  <data key="d0">Entity Cloning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Advanced capability in generated solutions for variant management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Search and Filtering">
