  <data key="d2">Capability in generated solutions facilitating system integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functional Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Functional Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Modular functional architecture of generated solutions designed to meet business requirements by automating essential tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Translation System">
  <data key="d0">Translation System</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">System supporting the Angular UI of FSMicroGenerator for accessibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Layered Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Layered Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Layered organization of generated solutions (presentation, API Gateway, microservices and data layers) ensuring separation of concerns, maintainability and scalability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Presentation Layer">
  <data key="d0">Presentation Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Layer defining the user interface for efficient, ergonomic navigation with reduced cognitive load, uniform behavior, logical grouping, instant feedback, and decoupled connection via the API Gateway.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microservices Layer">
  <data key="d0">Microservices Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Layer of independent, specialized services exposing functionality via REST APIs, including a main business microservice plus Member management, Technical configuration and Taxonomy support services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Layer">
  <data key="d0">Data Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Layer responsible for data storage, management, consistency and integrity, implementing a database per service pattern and Redis caching.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Database Per Service Pattern">
  <data key="d0">Database Per Service Pattern</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Pattern isolating data for each microservice to enhance scalability and resilience by preventing data access conflicts and limiting failure impact.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Redis">
  <data key="d0">Redis</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Caching system temporarily storing frequently accessed data to reduce query latency, improve responsiveness and reduce storage load.&lt;SEP&gt;An infrastructure service included in the generated Docker Compose files.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical service whose management is optimized via the singleton pattern in FSMicroGenerator-generated solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Caching technology used for frequently accessed endpoints in the generated modules.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RBAC">
  <data key="d0">RBAC</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Role-based access control used for managing users, roles and permissions and for strict access governance in generated solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JSON Web Token">
  <data key="d0">JSON Web Token</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Token mechanism used by the API Gateway to manage authentication and authorization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Site Scripting">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Site Scripting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Common web vulnerability (XSS) mitigated through double frontend and backend data validation and managed authentication tokens.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Site Request Forgery">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Site Request Forgery</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Common web vulnerability (CSRF) against which generated solutions are protected.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distributed Denial of Service">
  <data key="d0">Distributed Denial of Service</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DDoS attacks mitigated in generated solutions through rate limiting.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rate Limiting">
  <data key="d0">Rate Limiting</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Security measure against brute-force and DDoS attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Scaling approach allowing microservices to be replicated and dynamically balanced for efficient traffic management and high availability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467649</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maintainability">
  <data key="d0">Maintainability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Property supported by the modular design, enabling updates without regression risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative metric estimating modifiability, independence of components and technical debt risk, assessed through expert review.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative criterion estimating modifiability, independence of components, and technical debt risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative evaluation criterion; the manual implementation scored 2/5 and FSMicroGenerator scored 5/5.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation criterion reflecting the cumulative impact of modularity, reusability, consistency, tests and documentation on long-term maintenance.&lt;SEP&gt;One of four architectural dimensions assessed by the qualitative evaluation rubric on a 5-point scale.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative metric assessing ease of understanding, modifying and adapting code, with clean separation of concerns at the highest level.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security And Access Governance">
  <data key="d0">Security And Access Governance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Central pillar of generated solutions, including encryption, vulnerability protection, secure inter-service communication and strict RBAC.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Member Management Service">
  <data key="d0">Member Management Service</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Essential support microservice in generated solutions handling users, roles, permissions via RBAC, and authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Configuration Service">
  <data key="d0">Technical Configuration Service</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Support microservice in generated solutions handling dynamic menus and internationalization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Taxonomy Service">
  <data key="d0">Taxonomy Service</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Support microservice in generated solutions for structuring and classifying content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Service Registry">
  <data key="d0">Service Registry</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">API Gateway function providing dynamic microservice management.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Data Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Security measure integrated in generated solutions, especially for sensitive data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Double Frontend And Backend Data Validation">
  <data key="d0">Double Frontend And Backend Data Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Security measure validating data on both frontend and backend to protect against injection, XSS and CSRF vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Injection Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Injection Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Common web vulnerability against which generated solutions are protected through double frontend and backend data validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Brute-Force Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Brute-Force Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attacks mitigated in generated solutions through rate limiting.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cognitive Load">
  <data key="d0">Cognitive Load</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mental effort that the presentation layer aims to reduce to achieve a smooth and intuitive user experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator Paper">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, accepted for publication in IEEE Access (DOI 10.1109/ACCESS.2025.3589285). It presents FSMicroGenerator, a generator of full-stack microservice applications built on the MEAN stack. FSMicroGenerator uses Swagger and PrimeNG to improve developer experience, Docker and Docker Compose for deployment, and CI/CD and DevSecOps workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, accepted for publication in IEEE Access (DOI 10.1109/ACCESS.2025.3589285); presents FSMicroGenerator, a tool that automates microservice generation, inter-service communication and infrastructure setup using a MEAN-stack-based architecture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stack Overflow 2024 Survey">
  <data key="d0">Stack Overflow 2024 Survey</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [28]; developer survey reporting that 30.7% of developers identify as full-stack, the most reported role for the third year in a row.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synchronous Communication">
  <data key="d0">Synchronous Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Request-response communication model using RPC; suited for real-time interactions but increases coupling and is sensitive to latency and failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Remote Procedure Call">
  <data key="d0">Remote Procedure Call</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">RPC model in which a service sends a request and waits for a direct response before continuing execution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asynchronous Communication">
  <data key="d0">Asynchronous Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Event-driven communication model where services publish and consume messages via a message broker; improves decoupling and fault tolerance but complicates delivery, ordering and retries.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RabbitMQ">
  <data key="d0">RabbitMQ</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">An infrastructure service included in the generated Docker Compose files.&lt;SEP&gt;Message broker that is easier to deploy and manage, suited to transactional, low-latency communication; chosen by FSMicroGenerator.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical service whose management is optimized via the singleton pattern in FSMicroGenerator-generated solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MEAN Stack">
  <data key="d0">MEAN Stack</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A homogeneous JavaScript stack made up of MongoDB, Express.js, Angular and Node.js, suited to microservices architectures. It uses JSON end-to-end, is open source and supports agile development.&lt;SEP&gt;Coherent technology stack presented as an ecosystem for unified development.&lt;SEP&gt;Technology stack used as the identical underlying stack for both the manual and the generator-based implementations.&lt;SEP&gt;JavaScript technology stack targeted by FSMicroGenerator.&lt;SEP&gt;Web application technology stack discussed for simplifying web application development.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LAMP/WAMP Stack">
  <data key="d0">LAMP/WAMP Stack</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Common stack of Linux/Windows, Apache, MySQL and PHP/Python/Perl combining heterogeneous tools and languages.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id=".NET Stack">
  <data key="d0">.NET Stack</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Common web development stack combining heterogeneous tools requiring specific expertise.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inter-Service Communication">
  <data key="d0">Inter-Service Communication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Key challenge in microservices: independent services must exchange data reliably to maintain consistency, integrity and coherence.&lt;SEP&gt;Communication between microservices, present in the FSMicroGenerator implementation and missing in the manual implementation, adding latency overhead.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monolithic and microservices are two common architectural approaches">
  <data key="d0">Monolithic and microservices are two common architectural approaches</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Two common architectural approaches are the monolithic and microservices [22].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microservices improve modularity and fault isolation">
  <data key="d0">Microservices improve modularity and fault isolation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In contrast, microservices split the application into independent services, improving modularity and fault isolation [23].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microservices enable shorter time-to-market but add complexity">
  <data key="d0">Microservices enable shorter time-to-market but add complexity</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"This enables faster deployment and adaptability to changing needs, which many companies value for shorter time-to-market [24]." and "However, microservices introduce complexity, especially for new developers... [24]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synchronous RPC increases coupling and latency sensitivity">
  <data key="d0">Synchronous RPC increases coupling and latency sensitivity</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In this model, a service sends a request and waits for a direct response before continuing execution [25]. While this is well-suited for real-time interactions, it increases coupling between services and is sensitive to latency and failures, which can delay or block execution [26].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asynchronous messaging improves decoupling but adds delivery complexity">
  <data key="d0">Asynchronous messaging improves decoupling but adds delivery complexity</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"Asynchronous communication relies on an event-driven model, where services publish and consume messages via a message broker such as RabbitMQ or Kafka [25]." and "This improves decoupling, scalability, and fault tolerance but adds complexity in managing message delivery, ordering, and retries [26]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RabbitMQ is more suitable than Kafka for transactional low-latency systems">
  <data key="d0">RabbitMQ is more suitable than Kafka for transactional low-latency systems</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In contrast, RabbitMQ is easier to deploy and manage, making it more suitable for transactional communication, low-latency systems, and applications that benefit from advanced queue management [25].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A stack is a coherent set of technologies from frontend to database">
  <data key="d0">A stack is a coherent set of technologies from frontend to database</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">A stack refers to a coherent set of technologies used to build a complete application, from the frontend to the database [27].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="30.7% of developers identify as full-stack">
  <data key="d0">30.7% of developers identify as full-stack</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">According to the Stack Overflow 2024 survey [28], 30.7% of developers identify as full-stack.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heterogeneous stacks exceed a single developer's skill set and complicate integration">
  <data key="d0">Heterogeneous stacks exceed a single developer's skill set and complicate integration</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"However, they combine heterogeneous tools and languages, each requiring specific expertise, often exceeding the skill set of a single developer [30]." and "Additionally, these technologies were not originally designed to work together, making integration and maintenance more difficult [30]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technology Stack">
  <data key="d0">Technology Stack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A coherent set of technologies, such as languages, frameworks and libraries, used to build a complete application from the frontend to the database. Technology stacks have become essential for structuring web application design efficiently.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Message Broker">
  <data key="d0">Message Broker</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Middleware through which services publish and consume messages in asynchronous, event-driven communication. RabbitMQ and Kafka are examples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stack Overflow">
  <data key="d0">Stack Overflow</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Organization that produced the Stack Overflow 2024 developer survey, cited as [28].&lt;SEP&gt;Organization that produced the 2024 Developer Survey.&lt;SEP&gt;Organization producing the 2024 Developer Survey.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microservices Complexity">
  <data key="d0">Microservices Complexity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Difficulty introduced by microservices, especially for new developers, because it requires expertise in distributed systems management, service orchestration and inter-service communication. FSMicroGenerator addresses this difficulty through automation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shortage of Specialized Developers">
  <data key="d0">Shortage of Specialized Developers</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lack of specialized developers that FSMicroGenerator helps teams cope with by reducing technical barriers and simplifying complex architectures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stack Fragmentation">
  <data key="d0">Stack Fragmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The use of heterogeneous tools and languages in traditional web stacks. Fragmentation increases development costs, team size and coordination complexity, and makes integration and maintenance more difficult.&lt;SEP&gt;Use of heterogeneous tools and languages in stacks such as LAMP/WAMP and .NET. This increases development costs, team size and coordination complexity, and makes integration and maintenance more difficult.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference [28] (Stack Overflow 2024 Survey)">
  <data key="d0">Reference [28] (Stack Overflow 2024 Survey)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work [28], the Stack Overflow 2024 developer survey. It reports that JavaScript has been the most widely used language for over a decade and that 58.7% of professional developers use Docker.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Heterogeneous stacks require expertise beyond a single developer">
  <data key="d0">Heterogeneous stacks require expertise beyond a single developer</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">However, they combine heterogeneous tools and languages, each requiring specific expertise, often exceeding the skill set of a single developer [30].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traditional stack technologies were not designed to work together">
  <data key="d0">Traditional stack technologies were not designed to work together</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Additionally, these technologies were not originally designed to work together, making integration and maintenance more difficult [30].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JavaScript has been the most widely used language for over a decade">
  <data key="d0">JavaScript has been the most widely used language for over a decade</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">As JavaScript has been the most widely used language for over a decade [28], MEAN benefits from a large support ecosystem, ensuring stability and long-term viability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Docker packages components with dependencies into isolated environments">
  <data key="d0">Docker packages components with dependencies into isolated environments</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">To address this, FSMicroGenerator adopts Docker, a containerization technology that packages each component along with its dependencies into isolated environments [31].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Docker containers are lighter and faster than virtual machines">
  <data key="d0">Docker containers are lighter and faster than virtual machines</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Unlike virtual machines, which require a full operating system per instance, Docker containers share the host system's kernel. This makes them lighter, faster, and more efficient [29].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="58.7% of professional developers use Docker">
  <data key="d0">58.7% of professional developers use Docker</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">According to the Stack Overflow 2024 survey, 58.7% of professional developers use Docker to deploy distributed systems, highlighting its adoption as a standard tool for modular deployment [28].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JavaScript">
  <data key="d0">JavaScript</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The programming language used across all layers of the MEAN stack. It is described as the most widely used language for over a decade.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PrimeNG">
  <data key="d0">PrimeNG</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">An Angular component library that provides pre-built UI elements for building responsive interfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Library of standardized Angular components used to ensure frontend consistency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CI/CD and DevSecOps">
  <data key="d0">CI/CD and DevSecOps</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DevOps and DevSecOps-driven workflows that FSMicroGenerator integrates to support fast, reliable and secure delivery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Developer Experience">
  <data key="d0">Developer Experience</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A priority of FSMicroGenerator: minimizing technical overhead so that teams can focus on business logic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Virtual Machines">
  <data key="d0">Virtual Machines</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A virtualization approach that requires a full operating system per instance. The text contrasts virtual machines with Docker containers, which share the host system's kernel and are lighter, faster and more efficient.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dockerfile">
  <data key="d0">Dockerfile</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A file that FSMicroGenerator automatically produces for each generated component. It defines the image build process, including base images and dependencies, and uses lightweight base images to optimize performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id=".dockerignore">
  <data key="d0">.dockerignore</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A file that FSMicroGenerator automatically produces for each generated component. It reduces Docker image size by excluding unnecessary files.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JSON">
  <data key="d0">JSON</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A data format that the MEAN stack uses end-to-end. Using JSON throughout removes the need for data format conversions and improves performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="BSON">
  <data key="d0">BSON</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The binary data format in which MongoDB stores data. It reduces query time and server load.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="NoSQL">
  <data key="d0">NoSQL</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A flexible, non-relational data storage paradigm offered by MongoDB.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Agile Methods">
  <data key="d0">Agile Methods</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Development methods with short development cycles. The MEAN stack aligns well with agile methods and supports rapid prototyping, such as building a minimum viable product.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Minimum Viable Product">
  <data key="d0">Minimum Viable Product</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A rapid-prototyping outcome given as an example of what the MEAN stack supports within agile development.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Open Source">
  <data key="d0">Open Source</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The licensing model of the MEAN stack. It removes licensing costs and vendor lock-in, which makes the stack scalable and cost-effective.&lt;SEP&gt;Proposed future direction of making FSMicroGenerator open source. The aim is to foster collaborative innovation, enable a worldwide community to contribute, enrich the tool's functionalities and reinforce its durability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GitLab CI/CD Pipeline">
  <data key="d0">GitLab CI/CD Pipeline</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A seven-stage pipeline (install, test, build, security, deploy, notify, cleanup) defined in .gitlab-ci.yml. It automates delivery of the frontend, API Gateway, and microservices, and pushes images to GitLab Container Registry by default.&lt;SEP&gt;GitLab pipeline covering test, build and deployment stages.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Static Application Security Testing">
  <data key="d0">Static Application Security Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Static code analysis (SAST) security check embedded in the FSMicroGenerator pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Container Image Scanning">
  <data key="d0">Container Image Scanning</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Security check performed during the CD stage of the FSMicroGenerator pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Checkov">
  <data key="d0">Checkov</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure-as-code scanning tool used to detect misconfigurations early in the pipeline.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
