<node id="Monitoring In Distributed Architectures">
  <data key="d0">Monitoring In Distributed Architectures</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Monitoring as a critical function for system performance and stability in distributed and scalable architectures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Monitoring is critical for performance and stability in distributed architectures">
  <data key="d0">Monitoring is critical for performance and stability in distributed architectures</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "In distributed and scalable architectures, monitoring is a critical function that ensures system performance and stability, especially in production environments [24], [32]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Early metric signals reveal latent issues before outages">
  <data key="d0">Early metric signals reveal latent issues before outages</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "A gradual increase in latency, rising memory usage, or a spike in HTTP 500 errors can reveal latent issues before they cause visible outages [33]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dependency Scanning">
  <data key="d0">Dependency Scanning</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated security check in the FSMicroGenerator CI pipeline that detects vulnerable dependencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secret Detection">
  <data key="d0">Secret Detection</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Automated security check in the FSMicroGenerator CI pipeline that finds exposed secrets in code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infrastructure As Code">
  <data key="d0">Infrastructure As Code</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure defined as code (IaC). In the FSMicroGenerator pipeline, Checkov scans it to detect misconfigurations early.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shift-Left Security">
  <data key="d0">Shift-Left Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Approach that treats security as a native part of the pipeline rather than a post-deployment step, reducing the risk of exposing vulnerabilities in production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DevOps">
  <data key="d0">DevOps</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Practices that FSMicroGenerator integrates alongside DevSecOps into its GitLab-based CI/CD pipeline for fast, reliable delivery.&lt;SEP&gt;Software development and operations practice whose monitoring tools are surveyed in a systematic grey literature review.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rollback Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Rollback Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanism in the FSMicroGenerator deployment process that restores the last stable version if deployment fails. Image versions are tagged by Git commit SHA.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Observability">
  <data key="d0">Observability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Comprehensive monitoring capability delivered by FSMicroGenerator's embedded monitoring stack, improving availability, predictive diagnostics and resilience.&lt;SEP&gt;Ability to detect bottlenecks, trace failures and optimize resource usage. FSMicroGenerator provides it through automated monitoring instrumentation and /metrics endpoints in every generated service.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Without robust observability, detecting bottlenecks and failures is difficult">
  <data key="d0">Without robust observability, detecting bottlenecks and failures is difficult</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Without robust observability, it becomes difficult to detect bottlenecks, trace failures, or optimize resource usage." It follows the monitoring statement supported by [24] and [32].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Prometheus uses a pull-based model to collect metrics without agents">
  <data key="d0">Prometheus uses a pull-based model to collect metrics without agents</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Prometheus, a widely adopted solution in modern cloud-native environments, uses a pull-based model that allows it to periodically collect metrics from services without requiring agents [34]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
