  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inventory Management System Case Study">
  <data key="d0">Inventory Management System Case Study</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Simplified enterprise web application case study used to compare FSMicroGenerator with a traditional manual development approach.&lt;SEP&gt;Comparative case study source code covering FSMicroGenerator-generated and manually developed inventory management systems, publicly available on GitHub.&lt;SEP&gt;Experimental case study comprising FSMicroGenerator-generated and manually developed inventory management systems, publicly available on GitHub.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traditional Manual Development">
  <data key="d0">Traditional Manual Development</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual development approach used as baseline for comparison with FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alerting">
  <data key="d0">Alerting</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Preconfigured alerting with default notification channels (including Slack) and predefined alert rules for common incidents such as high memory usage or service unavailability, accelerating setup and ensuring operational readiness from the first deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Model-Driven Approach">
  <data key="d0">Model-Driven Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Approach in which UML class models defining business entities ensure that the conceptual structure aligns with the generated software architecture; combined with security integration and standardized architecture to rapidly generate reliable microservice solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bounded Context">
  <data key="d0">Bounded Context</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distinct domain partition from Domain-Driven Design. Each bounded context in the case study is intended to be implemented as an independent microservice.&lt;SEP&gt;Domain-Driven Design notion used to decompose the inventory management system into distinct contexts, each implemented as an independent microservice.&lt;SEP&gt;Well-defined business capability boundaries represented by each FSMicroGenerator-generated microservice, with loose coupling between them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inventory Management Case Study">
  <data key="d0">Inventory Management Case Study</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Full-stack enterprise web application case study covering backend, frontend and infrastructure. Its domain model was formalized as a UML class diagram and decomposed into bounded contexts implemented as microservices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Implementation">
  <data key="d0">Manual Implementation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Baseline development effort by five developers with 2–3 years of experience. Within 8 hours it achieved 61% functional and 33% non-functional coverage.&lt;SEP&gt;Development approach performed by a team of five developers (2-3 years experience), used as the baseline compared with FSMicroGenerator.&lt;SEP&gt;Manually developed implementation used as a baseline. It produced 176 files (~26k LOC) with over 3,800 files created during development, ran 9 containers, and had incomplete functionality. It showed 15.21 ms latency, 25.44 req/sec raw throughput (5.12 req/sec normalized), 19% CPU and 642 MB RAM (normalized 96% CPU, 3189 MB RAM).&lt;SEP&gt;Manual development approach used as baseline; within 8 hours it reached 61% functional and 33% non-functional coverage, with 115 commits, 3,835 files created and 1,305 files modified.&lt;SEP&gt;Baseline manually developed system using 9 containers, built by a more experienced team. It was incomplete, received lower qualitative scores (modularity 3/5; reusability, clarity and maintainability 2/5), and its normalized resource estimates are 96% CPU and 3189 MB RAM.&lt;SEP&gt;The manually developed baseline implementation, which scored poorly (2/5) on maintainability due to moderate modularity, poor code reusability, inconsistent structure, lack of backend tests and absent documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Baseline manual development approach, implementing 17 of 28 functional features (Rf = 0.61) and fewer non-functional requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Completion-Aware Normalization">
  <data key="d0">Completion-Aware Normalization</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Normalization technique introduced to compare the two implementations fairly. It adjusts the partial manual implementation's metrics using the product of Rf and Rnfr (0.2013): scope-correlated metrics are adjusted upward, and throughput is adjusted downward.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functional Coverage Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Functional Coverage Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Rf: the number of functional features implemented relative to the total defined (Equation 1).&lt;SEP&gt;Metric (Rf) quantifying the proportion of functional features implemented relative to the total required, collected via a manual feature checklist.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric (Rf) computed from a binary checklist verifying whether each expected functional feature was implemented or missing in a solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric calculated with the binary functional coverage checklist (Table 5) to evaluate the functional features expected in the experimental case study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Functional Coverage Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Non-Functional Coverage Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Rnfr: the NFR coverage achieved relative to the total NFRs expected, counting both system-wide and module-specific NFRs (Equation 2).&lt;SEP&gt;Metric (Rnfr) quantifying the proportion of non-functional requirements implemented relative to the full specification, collected via a manual NFR checklist.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric (Rnfr) computed with a two-level strategy: module-level NFRs assessed as the ratio of modules implementing them, and system-wide NFRs such as CI/CD and Docker orchestration evaluated globally.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric Rnfr measuring the proportion of non-functional requirements covered (e.g., 17/52 = 0.33 vs 52/52 = 1.00).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Functional Requirements">
  <data key="d0">Non-Functional Requirements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">System-wide and module-specific quality requirements whose coverage was measured in the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-cutting concerns including security, data integrity, observability, deployment automation, caching, logging, internationalization, monitoring, CI/CD and user experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Module-level quality requirements evaluated in the article, including internationalization, security, input validation, caching, error handling, logging, monitoring and API documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-functional requirements (NFRs) evaluated in the article being read. They include error handling, logging, monitoring, API documentation, deployment and orchestration, and CI/CD. The text reports 17 of 52 NFRs covered by the baseline versus all 52 covered with FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Apache JMeter">
  <data key="d0">Apache JMeter</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Standardized tool used to collect quantitative performance data.&lt;SEP&gt;Standardized tool used to measure scalability under load (latency, error rate, throughput).&lt;SEP&gt;Load testing tool used to run a test with 250 concurrent virtual users, two iterations of POST, GET, and DELETE product requests, and a 60-second ramp-up, totaling 1500 requests per implementation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Git Logs">
  <data key="d0">Git Logs</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Standardized source used to collect quantitative development data.&lt;SEP&gt;Commit logs and diff inspection used to count manual interventions (manually written and modified files).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Docker Stats">
  <data key="d0">Docker Stats</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Standardized tool used to collect resource usage data.&lt;SEP&gt;Tool used to collect resource usage (CPU/RAM) metrics under simulated load.&lt;SEP&gt;Docker container statistics tool used to sample CPU utilization and memory consumption every 5 seconds per Fabric component in Scenario S6.&lt;SEP&gt;Tool used to measure CPU utilization and memory consumption of Fabric Docker containers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator achieved full requirement coverage within 8 hours">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator achieved full requirement coverage within 8 hours</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The FSMicroGenerator implementation achieved full coverage (100%) of both specified functional and non-functional requirements, while the manual implementation achieved partial coverage (61% functional, 33% non-functional)."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reusable Technical Subsystems">
  <data key="d0">Reusable Technical Subsystems</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Green-labeled packages in the case study architecture that are intended for cross-module integration. FSMicroGenerator pre-generated them, and both development efforts received them as pre-built components so that the work focused on core business logic and integration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Core Business Modules">
  <data key="d0">Core Business Modules</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">White-labeled packages in the case study architecture. The evaluation measured how effectively each approach supported developing and integrating these modules while using shared components and maintaining architectural integrity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asymmetric Team Composition">
  <data key="d0">Asymmetric Team Composition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intentional difference between the two development teams: five developers with 2–3 years of MEAN stack and microservices experience did the manual implementation, and two junior developers with 1 and 2 years of experience used FSMicroGenerator. The difference was chosen to explore the tool's impact, but it introduces factors beyond the tool itself and is discussed as a threat to validity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quantitative Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Quantitative Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Objectively measurable attributes such as code volume, system performance, time and automation. They were collected with Git logs, Apache JMeter and Docker stats, and normalized for the manual implementation where relevant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Qualitative Metrics">
  <data key="d0">Qualitative Metrics</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Metrics requiring expert judgment that assess architectural and structural properties, including modularity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modularity">
  <data key="d0">Modularity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Architectural property assessed through the qualitative metrics.&lt;SEP&gt;One of four architectural dimensions assessed by the qualitative evaluation rubric on a 5-point scale.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Threats to Validity">
  <data key="d0">Threats to Validity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Section V-E of the paper. It discusses the effects of the asymmetric team composition and the assumptions behind completion-aware normalization.&lt;SEP&gt;Considerations of the study's limitations, including participant characteristics, tool specificity, basis of comparison from single instances, and interpretation of normalized estimates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VS Code Counter Extension">
  <data key="d0">VS Code Counter Extension</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Tool used to measure lines of code (LOC) to estimate codebase size and complexity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Likert Scale">
  <data key="d0">Likert Scale</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">5-point scale used in a predefined rubric for structured manual review of qualitative metrics by two independent evaluators.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normalization Based On Functional And Non-Functional Coverage">
  <data key="d0">Normalization Based On Functional And Non-Functional Coverage</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Approach normalizing quantitative metrics of the manual implementation by functional coverage ratio (Rf) and non-functional coverage ratio (Rnfr), assuming a proportional relationship between scope and metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ISO/IEC 25010:2023">
  <data key="d0">ISO/IEC 25010:2023</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Software quality standard in accordance with which the evaluation metrics were selected.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ISO/IEC 25002:2024">
  <data key="d0">ISO/IEC 25002:2024</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Quality measurement standard in accordance with which the evaluation metrics were selected.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inventory Management System">
  <data key="d0">Inventory Management System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Case study application representing a common type of complex web application on which the findings are based.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Construct Validity">
  <data key="d0">Construct Validity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Extent to which operational measures reflect theoretical constructs such as development effort, productivity and code quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="External Validity">
  <data key="d0">External Validity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Extent to which findings might apply in different settings (generalizability).&lt;SEP&gt;Validity category on the generalizability of the study's findings. It covers application domain and project scale, participant characteristics and tool specificity, since the findings are specific to FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Architectural Modularity">
  <data key="d0">Architectural Modularity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Qualitative metric assessing separation of concerns, cohesion and service decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative evaluation criterion; the manual implementation scored 3/5 and FSMicroGenerator scored 5/5.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation criterion concerning separation of responsibilities into modules; the manual implementation showed moderate modularity while FSMicroGenerator showed strong modularity enabling independent updates and scaling.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative metric assessing separation of concerns, bounded contexts, cohesion and loose coupling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Reusability">
  <data key="d0">Code Reusability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Qualitative metric evaluating the presence of reusable components and abstraction mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative evaluation criterion; the manual implementation scored 2/5 because of duplicated logic, while FSMicroGenerator scored 5/5 thanks to its shared directory and reusable helpers.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation criterion on which the manual implementation performed poorly and the FSMicroGenerator-based implementation performed well.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative metric in the 5-point Likert rubric. It ranges from duplicated business logic with no shared components (1) to extensive reuse through abstracted, generic components with no duplication (5).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Clarity">
  <data key="d0">Code Clarity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Qualitative metric assessing structural consistency, adherence to naming conventions and architecture standards such as MVC and RESTful.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scalability Under Load">
  <data key="d0">Scalability Under Load</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Quantitative metric evaluating system performance as the number of users increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Evaluation dimension measured through latency, throughput and error rate. Error rate was 0.00% for both the manual and FSMicroGenerator implementations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lines Of Code">
  <data key="d0">Lines Of Code</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Quantitative metric (LOC) estimating codebase size and complexity, collected with the VS Code Counter extension and normalized by Rf and Rnfr.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Development Time">
  <data key="d0">Development Time</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Quantitative metric measuring productivity under a fixed time constraint, tracked via stopwatch.&lt;SEP&gt;Development effort metric under an 8-hour constraint: 8.00 hours manual raw, 39.74 normalized, 3.00 hours for FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Manual Interventions">
  <data key="d0">Manual Interventions</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Quantitative metric assessing the degree of automation by counting manually written and modified files, analyzed via commit logs and diff inspection and normalized by Rf and Rnfr.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Usage">
  <data key="d0">Resource Usage</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Quantitative metric (CPU/RAM) measuring runtime efficiency under simulated load, collected with Docker stats and normalized by Rf and Rnfr.&lt;SEP&gt;CPU and RAM consumption monitored during the JMeter load test to compare the implementations.&lt;SEP&gt;CPU and RAM usage under load: CPU 19.24% raw / 95.58% normalized manual vs 136.12% FSMicroGenerator; RAM 641.99 MB raw / 3,189.20 MB normalized manual vs 1,291.80 MB FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Expert Review">
  <data key="d0">Expert Review</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Structured manual review conducted independently by two evaluators using a predefined rubric based on a 5-point Likert scale; discrepancies greater than one point were resolved through discussion. Used to assess qualitative metrics such as modularity, clarity, reusability and maintainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Qualitative assessment used to evaluate the implementations, including maintainability and adherence to architecture standards.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Empirical Software Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Empirical Software Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Research field whose standard practices are reflected in the threats-to-validity discussion of the findings.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Web Application">
  <data key="d0">Web Application</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Application type of which the inventory management system is a common complex example; code generation of structure and boilerplate is expected to benefit a wide range of web application contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;The complex web application developed in the study. Code generation for structure and boilerplate is expected to benefit a wide range of web application contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MVC">
  <data key="d0">MVC</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Architecture standard (Model-View-Controller) against which code clarity, structural consistency and standard conformance are assessed.&lt;SEP&gt;Model-View-Controller architecture standard referenced in the qualitative evaluation criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Model-View-Controller design pattern, cited in the rubric as an example of the patterns that an excellent codebase conforms to.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RESTful">
  <data key="d0">RESTful</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Architecture standard against which code clarity, structural consistency and standard conformance are assessed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normalization">
  <data key="d0">Normalization</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Procedure that scales manual-implementation metrics by the coverage ratios Rf=0.61 and Rnfr=0.33, dividing by the normalization factor 0.2013, to estimate full-completion effort. The procedure assumes proportional effort scaling. Applied to the manual approach, it yields about 40 hours (39.74), 571 commits, 19,051 files created and 6,482 files modified, which is over 25,000 manual file interventions. The resulting figures are extrapolations to be interpreted with caution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conclusion Validity">
  <data key="d0">Conclusion Validity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Concerns the reasonableness of conclusions drawn from the data; the study notes single-instance comparison and estimate-based conclusions warrant caution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RESTful Architecture">
  <data key="d0">RESTful Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">REST architecture standard referenced in the qualitative evaluation criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;REST architectural style. The rubric cites it as an example pattern for standard conformance, and reference [27] implements a RESTful IoT service.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functional Coverage">
  <data key="d0">Functional Coverage</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Metric Rf measuring the ratio of functional requirements implemented: 0.61 manual vs 1.00 FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Functional Coverage">
  <data key="d0">Non-Functional Coverage</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Metric Rnfr measuring the ratio of non-functional requirements implemented: 0.33 manual vs 1.00 FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lines of Code">
  <data key="d0">Lines of Code</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Codebase size metric: 26,209 manual raw, 130,198 normalized, 192,050 for FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Development Effort">
  <data key="d0">Development Effort</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Effort required to implement the system, measured in hours, commits, and file interventions; the manual approach was projected to need about 40 hours, 571 commits, and over 25,000 file interventions for full scope.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric group including development time, commits, files created and modified; under an 8-hour constraint.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator substantially reduces development effort">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator substantially reduces development effort</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding reported by the paper itself, without a supporting citation: "FSMicroGenerator demonstrably automated significant portions of the setup, configuration, and boilerplate". The FSMicroGenerator implementation reached full completion in 3 hours with 11 commits. Normalized manual estimates are about 40 hours, 571 commits and over 25,000 manual file interventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Participant Characteristics">
  <data key="d0">Participant Characteristics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Threat to validity: the study involved specific developers, two junior and five with 2-3 years of experience. Outcomes might vary with other skill sets, experience levels or team dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tool Specificity">
  <data key="d0">Tool Specificity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Threat to validity: the findings are specific to FSMicroGenerator, and direct extrapolation to other code generation tools may not be appropriate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Basis of Comparison">
  <data key="d0">Basis of Comparison</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Conclusion-validity consideration: the comparison relies on single instances (one generator project and one manual project) plus qualitative assessments. Without multiple replications, broad statistical conclusions call for caution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Error Rate">
  <data key="d0">Error Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Metric recorded during the load test; both systems achieved 0%, indicating basic operational correctness.&lt;SEP&gt;Scalability-under-load metric. It was 0.00% for the manual implementation (raw and normalized) and 0.00% for FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Codebase Size">
  <data key="d0">Codebase Size</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Comparison of file counts and lines of code between the implementations, noted as a complex measure of efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Metric group covering number of files and lines of code. Number of files: 176 manual raw, 874 normalized, 904 FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Number of Commits">
  <data key="d0">Number of Commits</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Development effort metric: 115 commits manual raw, 571 normalized, 11 for FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Developers">
  <data key="d0">Developers</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Study participants: two junior developers and five developers with 2-3 years of experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Load Testing">
  <data key="d0">Load Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Experimental procedure assessing scalability and performance under load by recording latency, throughput, and error rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normalization Factor">
  <data key="d0">Normalization Factor</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Scaling factor (0.2013) used to extrapolate the partially completed manual implementation's metrics to full scope, based on the assumption of proportional effort scaling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Performance Trade-Off">
  <data key="d0">Performance Trade-Off</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding that the incomplete manual system was faster but less functional, while the complete generated system handled comparable load with higher latency due to its comprehensive feature set.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Middleware">
  <data key="d0">Middleware</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Processing layers such as authentication, rate limiting, and data validation that contribute to FSMicroGenerator's higher latency.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Churn">
  <data key="d0">Code Churn</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Significant creation, refactoring, or deletion of code during manual development, shown by over 3,800 files created versus 176 final files.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proportional Effort Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Proportional Effort Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Assumption underlying the normalized figures. The partially completed manual implementation's effort and metrics are assumed to scale proportionally to full scope. The figures are therefore extrapolations, discussed further in Section V-E.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Production-Readiness">
  <data key="d0">Production-Readiness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Goal behind FSMicroGenerator's automatic inclusion of features beyond the core requirements. Examples are entity cloning, business statistics visualization components, and database-structured documents for pre-configured entities such as menus, users and roles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microservice Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Microservice Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Architectural style with independent fine-grained services, bounded contexts and loose coupling; generated by FSMicroGenerator with separate frontend, gateway and backend microservices.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural style for building applications as independent services, discussed in references [21] and [22].&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural style addressed by cited works on predictive analytics, monitoring and DevOps.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Clarity And Structural Consistency">
  <data key="d0">Code Clarity And Structural Consistency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Qualitative evaluation criterion covering code clarity, structure and standard conformance; the manual implementation scored 2/5 and FSMicroGenerator scored 5/5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Usage Normalization">
  <data key="d0">Resource Usage Normalization</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Procedure that estimates the resource usage of the manual implementation if it were fully implemented, yielding 96% CPU and 3189 MB RAM. The resulting figures are acknowledged as speculative.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Likert-Scale Qualitative Evaluation">
  <data key="d0">Likert-Scale Qualitative Evaluation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Rubric-based assessment (Appendix C, Table 7) in which two independent reviewers assigned 1–5 scores, resolving significant discrepancies through discussion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator enables junior teams to deliver complete systems with less effort">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator enables junior teams to deliver complete systems with less effort</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "These findings indicate that FSMicroGenerator can help less experienced teams deliver complete, production-ready systems within shorter timeframes, with reduced effort, lower risk of structural errors, and more consistent resource usage under realistic conditions."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generated system trades higher latency for greater functional depth">
  <data key="d0">Generated system trades higher latency for greater functional depth</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "Performance analysis highlights a trade-off between the raw speed of the incomplete manual system and the higher latency but greater functional depth of the complete generated system."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generated system uses fewer resources per unit of functionality">
  <data key="d0">Generated system uses fewer resources per unit of functionality</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "Resource usage patterns follow a similar trend, with the auto-generated system consuming more in absolute terms but potentially less per unit of functionality compared to the normalized estimates for the manual approach."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generator architecture facilitates independent scaling of components">
  <data key="d0">Generator architecture facilitates independent scaling of components</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "While the normalized figures for the manual implementation are speculative, they highlight that the generator's architecture inherently facilitates better independent scaling and optimization of components, leading to more efficient resource use per unit of functionality."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator produces a larger, more feature-rich codebase">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator produces a larger, more feature-rich codebase</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "FSMicroGenerator produced a larger, more feature-rich codebase."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Loose Coupling">
  <data key="d0">Loose Coupling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Design property of the FSMicroGenerator-generated microservices, each of which represents a well-defined bounded context with loose coupling to the others.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Separation Of Responsibilities">
  <data key="d0">Separation Of Responsibilities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Design principle that the manual implementation was criticized for violating, because data definitions, business logic and the communication layer were potentially mixed within single files.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Redundancy">
  <data key="d0">Code Redundancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Duplication of logic across components. It was observed frequently in the manual implementation and reduced in FSMicroGenerator through uniform service structure, reusable helper functions and middleware.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Independent Scaling">
  <data key="d0">Independent Scaling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ability to scale and optimize system components independently. The generator's granular, container-distributed architecture inherently facilitates it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Consistency">
  <data key="d0">Code Consistency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Evaluation criterion concerning uniform directory structures and naming conventions for folders, files, functions and variables across the codebase.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Qualitative Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Qualitative Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Evaluation procedure in which two reviewers independently scored implementations on criteria such as consistency and maintainability, with a discussion procedure for resolving discrepancies; both reviewers assigned identical scores.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Automation Technologies">
  <data key="d0">Smart Automation Technologies</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A Moroccan startup that used FSMicroGenerator in the development of several real projects, including Smart DLSP.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart DLSP">
  <data key="d0">Smart DLSP</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Smart Digital Logistic Services Providers, a national initiative under the Al Khawarizmi program aimed at modernizing freight and logistics operations through intelligent, AI-powered solutions; FSMicroGenerator generated its digital freight exchange platform architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Smart Digital Logistic Services Provider; a research project registered in Morocco's Al Khawarizmi program (May 2019) aiming to develop a collaborative Logistics 4.0 solution and give freight vehicles more intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;Smart digital logistics service platform whose main challenge is building a supportive ecosystem capable of solving global logistics problems.&lt;SEP&gt;System whose vehicles circulate in the studied VANET environments. The text does not give its full name or further details.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Al Khawarizmi Program">
  <data key="d0">Al Khawarizmi Program</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Moroccan national program under which the Smart DLSP initiative (Smart Digital Logistic Services Providers) was carried out, aimed at modernizing freight and logistics operations through intelligent and AI-powered solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Program launched in Morocco in May 2019 under which the Smart DLSP project is registered.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AI Agents">
  <data key="d0">AI Agents</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intelligent agents planned for future integration into the Smart DLSP platform to automate decision-making processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Digital Freight Exchange Platform">
  <data key="d0">Digital Freight Exchange Platform</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A platform developed within Smart DLSP whose full-stack architecture, including modular backend microservices and Angular-based frontend components, was automatically generated by FSMicroGenerator. Its development proceeded in two stages: a functional, scalable base system for real-time logistics flow management, then future integration of AI agents.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Backend Test Suites">
  <data key="d0">Backend Test Suites</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Test suites generated within each microservice by FSMicroGenerator; reviewers noted they significantly reduced modification risks and enabled early detection of regressions. Backend tests were absent from the manual implementation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generated Documentation">
  <data key="d0">Generated Documentation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Comprehensive system documentation generated by FSMicroGenerator, easing developer onboarding and facilitating rapid contribution from new team members; documentation was absent from the manual implementation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator Enforces Architectural Best Practices">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator Enforces Architectural Best Practices</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding stated in the text: "FSMicroGenerator appears effective in enforcing architectural best practices, consistency, and generating supporting elements (e.g., tests, documentation) that positively impact maintainability."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OMG Standards">
  <data key="d0">OMG Standards</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Object Management Group standards adopted by FSMicroGenerator to ensure standardization and quality of generated code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RESTful Best Practices">
  <data key="d0">RESTful Best Practices</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">API design best practices adopted by FSMicroGenerator for homogeneous generated solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Generative AI Code Tools">
  <data key="d0">Generative AI Code Tools</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">GenAI-based tools that mainly produce portions of code rather than complete solutions; effective as assistance tools but with limitations in security and compliance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Traditional Development">
  <data key="d0">Traditional Development</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Manual, often tedious and error-prone software development process contrasted with FSMicroGenerator's automated approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Standardization">
  <data key="d0">Code Standardization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Homogeneity and quality of generated code, a key benefit of FSMicroGenerator, though potentially inducing dependency on generated models.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Talent Shortage">
  <data key="d0">Talent Shortage</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Setting in which FSMicroGenerator is particularly suitable, helping teams produce well-structured architectures without impacting timelines or costs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator generates complete architectures unlike GenAI tools">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator generates complete architectures unlike GenAI tools</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "Unlike tools based on generative AI, which mainly produce portions of code without providing a complete solution, FSMicroGenerator is designed to generate entire architectures tailored to the specific needs of a project."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator is suitable for automating complex microservice architecture development">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator is suitable for automating complex microservice architecture development</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Conclusion in the text: "The results suggest that FSMicroGenerator is suitable for automating the development of complex microservice architectures. It can reduce implementation times, improve interoperability, and support system maintainability."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JavaScript-Based Stack">
  <data key="d0">JavaScript-Based Stack</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Technology stack used by FSMicroGenerator that reduces context-switching between frontend and backend technologies, allowing developers to focus on business logic rather than infrastructure concerns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Design Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Design Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Software design patterns used by FSMicroGenerator, together with generic functions and reusable components, to improve application maintainability and scalability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reusable Components">
  <data key="d0">Reusable Components</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Generic functions and reusable components employed by FSMicroGenerator that contribute to improved maintainability and scalability of generated applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Package And Module Catalog">
  <data key="d0">Package And Module Catalog</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">FSMicroGenerator capability to build a catalog of packages and modules to feed projects, promoting extensibility, reusability and potentially faster delivery of IT solutions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Other Code Generators">
  <data key="d0">Other Code Generators</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Code generation tools discussed in Section II of the article and compared with FSMicroGenerator in Table 4; FSMicroGenerator differs from them through its modular approach, microservices orientation, native integration of best practices, and coverage beyond CRUD generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CRUD Generation">
  <data key="d0">CRUD Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Generation of create-read-update-delete functionality; FSMicroGenerator is not limited to CRUD generation but covers the entire application development cycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Infrastructure Automation">
  <data key="d0">Infrastructure Automation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Automation of deployment environment preparation, infrastructure configuration, and service monitoring performed by FSMicroGenerator; FSMicroGenerator helps teams less experienced with infrastructure automation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Advanced Customization">
  <data key="d0">Advanced Customization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Challenge identified for FSMicroGenerator: some use cases such as complex business functionality and advanced user interface customization require manual adjustments after initial generation during the adaptation phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AI Integration">
  <data key="d0">AI Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Technical context in which FSMicroGenerator's adoption in large-scale projects demonstrated flexibility and adaptability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator may induce dependency on generated models">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator may induce dependency on generated models</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Limitation stated in the text: "Finally, although the tool ensures effective standardization, it might induce a certain dependency on the generated models, which could make the integration of new technologies or frameworks not supported by the generator a little trickier." The constraint is offset by the modularity and modifiability of produced code.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
