<node id="Most existing code generation tools are monolithic and lack monitoring">
  <data key="d0">Most existing code generation tools are monolithic and lack monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding drawn from Table 4, "Comparative analysis of FSMicroGenerator and existing code generation tools": six of seven compared tools use a monolithic architecture. None of the compared tools provide monitoring (logging, performance tracking, system health), and only Prasanthan et al. [2] supports containerized deployment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FSMicroGenerator offers superior scalability, security and multilingual support compared to existing tools">
  <data key="d0">FSMicroGenerator offers superior scalability, security and multilingual support compared to existing tools</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding drawn from Table 4: FSMicroGenerator is rated High for scalability, Very high for security and Very good for user experience. It is also rated Easy for interoperability, supports containerized deployment, multilingual support and monitoring, and offers CRUD, translation and clone business operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="System Monitoring">
  <data key="d0">System Monitoring</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Logging, performance tracking and system health supervision. FSMicroGenerator integrates system monitoring, while none of the compared tools provide it.&lt;SEP&gt;Monitoring of software systems and microservices, discussed as a means of enhancing reliability and scalability, including via Prometheus, Grafana and DevOps monitoring tools.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mobile Adaptability">
  <data key="d0">Mobile Adaptability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Proposed future direction of integrating architectures adapted to mobile applications. The aim is to create scalable, high-performance mobile solutions without sacrificing backend quality.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Qualitative Evaluation Rubric">
  <data key="d0">Qualitative Evaluation Rubric</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Standardized rubric rating modularity, reusability, clarity, and maintainability on a 5-point scale to reduce reviewer subjectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
