</node>
<node id="Two-Level Evaluation Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Two-Level Evaluation Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Strategy for computing Rnfr. Module-level NFRs such as security, error handling, caching, logging, internationalization and monitoring are scored as the ratio of modules implementing them. System-wide NFRs such as CI/CD and Docker-based orchestration are scored with a global binary check.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Docker-Based Orchestration">
  <data key="d0">Docker-Based Orchestration</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">System-wide non-functional requirement for container orchestration. Each module defines its deployment parameters in the orchestration configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467650</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
