<node id="Code Generation">
  <data key="d0">Code Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Code Generation refers to the automated production of software code and related artifacts. Its techniques are attracting growing interest because they can automate and speed up software development. In its broader sense, Code Generation covers the automatic creation of source code and configuration, as well as supporting elements such as tests and documentation. It often works from models or specifications, including the transformation of user-defined conceptual models into executable code and user interface (UI) components.

A key benefit of Code Generation is the automatic creation of application structure and boilerplate code. This is expected to bring advantages across a wide range of web application contexts. However, existing code generation tools are often tightly coupled to specific programming languages and require complex configuration, which limits their flexibility and ease of use.

Code Generation is the research topic in which FSMicroGenerator is situated, and it is the core function of that tool. FSMicroGenerator automatically generates source code, configuration, tests, and documentation. The field also includes the various tools compared against FSMicroGenerator and is the subject of several cited works on generating code from models or specifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
