<node id="Functional Coverage Ratio (Rf)">
  <data key="d0">Functional Coverage Ratio (Rf)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Metric measuring the proportion of required functional features implemented, used to compare manual implementation and FSMicroGenerator.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Swagger/OpenAPI">
  <data key="d0">Swagger/OpenAPI</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">API documentation standard generated for all endpoints per module.&lt;SEP&gt;API documentation generated for all endpoints per module.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reference [18] (2020, Computers)">
  <data key="d0">Reference [18] (2020, Computers)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [18]. A 2020 paper whose bibliography entry is truncated in the text; only its year and DOI 10.3390/computers9030056 are visible.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UML Diagrams">
  <data key="d0">UML Diagrams</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Unified Modeling Language diagrams used as input models for Laravel code generation in reference [19].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Laravel Framework">
  <data key="d0">Laravel Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Web application framework that is the target of code generation from UML diagrams in reference [19].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Functional Requirements Checklist">
  <data key="d0">Functional Requirements Checklist</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 5 of the article. It lists functional requirements for each module, such as product, category, inventory movement, transaction, transaction line, supplier and customer management, plus external integration. The checklist is used to compute the functional coverage ratio Rf. Manual implementation covers 17 of 28 features, and FSMicroGenerator covers all 28.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Access Control Security">
  <data key="d0">Access Control Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-functional security requirement covering authentication, authorization and rate limiting. Manual implementation scores 0/5 and FSMicroGenerator scores 5/5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Input Validation">
  <data key="d0">Input Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-functional requirement covering client-side validation (manual 5/5, FSMicroGenerator 5/5) and server-side validation of payloads and parameters (manual 1/5, FSMicroGenerator 5/5).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Caching">
  <data key="d0">Caching</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-functional requirement implemented with Redis caching for frequently accessed endpoints. Manual implementation scores 0/5 and FSMicroGenerator scores 5/5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Logging and Error Handling">
  <data key="d0">Logging and Error Handling</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-functional requirements covering standard HTTP status codes, structured error messages, and centralized, structured, persisted logs. Both manual implementation and FSMicroGenerator score 5/5.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="External API Integration">
  <data key="d0">External API Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Functional module integrating a taxonomy API for classification references, a currency API for multi-currency pricing and exchange-rate conversion, and an account package for authentication and role-based access. FSMicroGenerator generates these integrations automatically; manual implementation does not cover them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-024</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="5-Point Likert Scale Rubric">
  <data key="d0">5-Point Likert Scale Rubric</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Structured rubric for qualitative metrics (architectural modularity, code reusability, code clarity/consistency/conformance, maintainability) scored from Very poor (1) to Excellent (5).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
