  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Clarity, Structural Consistency, and Standard Conformance">
  <data key="d0">Code Clarity, Structural Consistency, and Standard Conformance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Qualitative metric in the 5-point Likert rubric. It ranges from unreadable code with disorganized folders and no naming conventions (1) to a fully consistent, well-structured codebase that strongly conforms to patterns such as MVC and RESTful (5).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structured Error Handling">
  <data key="d0">Structured Error Handling</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Error-handling feature that uses standard HTTP status codes and structured error messages. FSMicroGenerator generates this feature automatically, and both compared systems score 5/5 on it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791467655</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centralized Logging">
  <data key="d0">Centralized Logging</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Centralized error and request logging with structured, persisted logs. FSMicroGenerator generates this feature automatically, and both compared systems score 5/5 on it.</data>
