<node id="Docker">
  <data key="d0">Docker</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Docker is a containerization technology that packages software components together with their dependencies into isolated environments. Docker containers share the host operating system's kernel, which makes them lightweight compared with full virtualization. Docker supports scalable, reproducible deployments, reduces deployment errors, and makes it easier to integrate microservices.

Within the FSMicroGenerator system, Docker is integrated to enable fast, reproducible, and modular deployments. A Dockerfile is generated for each microservice so that it can be containerized individually. The entire FSMicroGenerator system is also containerized, and docker-compose files are generated for both development and production environments. This allows system-level deployment of the generated modules, with orchestration handled through Docker Compose. Similarly, BaaS produces a Docker container as its output, which reduces deployment errors and simplifies integration into microservices architectures.

Beyond code-generation contexts, Docker is used in cloud application architectures for smart manufacturing. There, it serves as the container technology underlying machine-learning-based container management.&lt;SEP&gt;Container platform (Docker Engine 24.0.7) on which all Fabric components run on a single host over a bridge network.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a4aa31c8531fdbc66868e8d96c0e0d18-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Microservices-Driven_Automation_in_Full-Stack_Deve.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
