  <data key="d5">1791500933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [18]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [18]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work ([18]) on the effectiveness of retrieval augmentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Previous work of the authors presenting a survey on various distinct MANET authentication mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited work defining a Bayesian network as a pair (G, O) with a directed acyclic graph encoding a joint probability distribution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ref [19]">
  <data key="d0">Ref [19]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited work ([19]) on the synergy between LLMs and RAG systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Work combining authentication with confidentiality, encrypting data with a symmetric key after successful node authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;Paper cited as [19] for the three principal steps of implementing Fuzzy Logic.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Paper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hallucination">
  <data key="d0">Hallucination</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phenomenon in which LLMs generate statements that seem plausible but are factually incorrect.&lt;SEP&gt;Limitation of LLMs that RAG overcomes by anchoring generated content on reliable external sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Issue in large language models used for chatbots that can lead to incorrect or inadequate information.&lt;SEP&gt;Generation of incorrect or non-compliant information by standalone LLMs, avoided by leveraging relevant legal data.&lt;SEP&gt;Generation of unsupported or false content by conversational models; reference [16] shows retrieval augmentation reduces it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791500933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vector Database">
  <data key="d0">Vector Database</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Database of relevant information that RAG systems integrate with LLMs for retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;Database storing embeddings with pointers to text chunks, enabling efficient similarity-based search and retrieval.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791500933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Legal Assistance Chatbot">
  <data key="d0">Legal Assistance Chatbot</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Chatbot proposed by the paper. It gives basic legal advice on contract law, relies on verified data, and can be adapted to different jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791500933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chatbot">
  <data key="d0">Chatbot</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Software, also called a conversational agent or dialogue system, that simulates human conversation through text or voice.&lt;SEP&gt;Cited as [22]. K. B. Prakash, A. J. S. Kumar and G. R. Kanagachidambaresan, 2021. A book chapter on chatbots.&lt;SEP&gt;Conversational software agents; the topic of references [5] through [12], covering development tools, applications in commerce, education and consumer settings, and design trends.&lt;SEP&gt;Conversational agents, covered in the cited works on children's legal rights guidance and on smart contract specification and code generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791500933</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Natural Language Understanding">
  <data key="d0">Natural Language Understanding</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">NLU: chatbot component for interpreting user messages, identifying intent, and extracting information.&lt;SEP&gt;NLU; interpreting user messages by identifying intent, extracting information and understanding conversation context.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-caa1a23d50101616a42f59c788898ea5-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_113-Accurate_AI_Assistance_in_Contract_Law1.pdf</data>
