<node id="Security Improvements of Artificial Intelligence in MANET">
  <data key="d0">Security Improvements of Artificial Intelligence in MANET</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, by H. Khalfaoui et al.; discusses attacks in Mobile Ad Hoc Networks (MANETs), their classification, and existing MANET security algorithms including routing protection and data security schemes.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, by H. Khalfaoui et al. It surveys AI-based security methods in Mobile Ad Hoc Networks (MANETs), including deep learning, neural networks and fuzzy logic. It also discusses their limitations and the advantages of AI for MANET security.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, by H. Khalfaoui et al.; surveys MANET security challenges and artificial intelligence approaches (machine learning, deep learning) for securing MANETs.&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, identified from the running page header. Its reference list covers security, attacks, authentication and routing in mobile ad hoc networks (MANETs).&lt;SEP&gt;The article being read, by H. Khalfaoui et al. It reviews existing security solutions in Mobile Ad hoc Networks (MANETs) and the advantages of AI-based approaches: better IDSs, faster response time and massive data management. It summarizes existing AI-based security methods in a table and concludes that most current approaches have limitations. Future work will integrate AI with blockchain technology to strengthen MANET protection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
