<node id="Flooding Attack">
  <data key="d0">Flooding Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DoS attack in which malicious nodes broadcast fake packets to absorb resources and disrupt network operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Attack in MANETs, including data flooding and UDP flooding. Intrusion detection systems by Luong et al. and by Sbai and El Boukhari target this attack.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Route Discovery Frequency Vector">
  <data key="d0">Route Discovery Frequency Vector</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">RDFV; represents each node's route discovery history to distinguish normal from abnormal behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flooding Attack Detection Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Flooding Attack Detection Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">FADA; used with RDFV and AODV to prevent flooding attacks; achieves a misbehavior detection ratio over 99%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CICDDoS2019">
  <data key="d0">CICDDoS2019</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">A dataset dedicated to DDoS attacks with a large number of network transaction records.&lt;SEP&gt;Dataset used by Sbai and El Boukhari to build a deep learning IDS for UDP flooding attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Key Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Key Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MANET security challenge caused by the lack of a centralized control unit; commonly addressed using clusters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Packet Overhead">
  <data key="d0">Packet Overhead</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Extra packets generated to detect unauthorized nodes, increasing congestion, collisions, packet loss, processing time and energy use.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Many security-routing methods make choosing an optimal solution difficult">
  <data key="d0">Many security-routing methods make choosing an optimal solution difficult</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Moreover, numerous methods have been developed to combine security data with routing protocols, making it difficult to determine the most optimal and efficient solution that can be applied in different situations [22].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Existing MANET security approaches face several challenges">
  <data key="d0">Existing MANET security approaches face several challenges</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">We present below a general idea about some challenges of existing MANET security approaches in the literature [9, 23]</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Forecasting and database processing are representative examples of AI">
  <data key="d0">Forecasting and database processing are representative examples of AI</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Forecasting activities such as weather and natural environment forecasts, design and management work, and database construction and processing are representative examples of AI [25].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AI can transform network nodes into smart nodes">
  <data key="d0">AI can transform network nodes into smart nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This technology has been explored to transform network nodes into smart nodes that can make brilliant decisions on their own, much like humans [26].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep learning uses multiple layers each interpreting data distinctly">
  <data key="d0">Deep learning uses multiple layers each interpreting data distinctly</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Still, there are multiple layers in deep learning, each of which provides a distinct interpretation of the data it feeds on [28].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Processing Time">
  <data key="d0">Processing Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MANET security challenge: the time each technique needs to discover dangerous nodes and secure the network; dynamic topology forces rerouting, lengthening processing and reducing MANET flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cooperative Malicious Nodes">
  <data key="d0">Cooperative Malicious Nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MANET security challenge where defeating approaches cannot discover cooperating malicious nodes together but locate them one by one across executions, which takes a long time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Frequency Knowledge">
  <data key="d0">Frequency Knowledge</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">MANET security challenge requiring each node to know the transmission frequency, made difficult because nodes freely join and leave the network.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Application-Based IDS">
  <data key="d0">Application-Based IDS</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of Intrusion Detection System highlighted in the work cited as [21].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AI is a system's ability to interpret data, learn and adapt to achieve goals">
  <data key="d0">AI is a system's ability to interpret data, learn and adapt to achieve goals</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">As cited in [24], AI is defined as 'a system's ability to interpret external data correctly, to learn from such data and to use those learnings to achieve specific goals and tasks through flexible adaptation.'</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Several AI branches have been used to secure MANETs">
  <data key="d0">Several AI branches have been used to secure MANETs</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">According to different studies, e.g. [13], involving the security approaches of AI in the MANET, the populated branches that have been reported to be utilized for securing network system are briefly discussed as follow:</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FADA achieves over 99% misbehavior detection ratio">
  <data key="d0">FADA achieves over 99% misbehavior detection ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"Simulation results reveal that FADA achieves a higher misbehavior detection ratio (over 99 %)." Attributed to Luong et al. [27].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Routing Overhead">
  <data key="d0">Routing Overhead</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Network performance metric that is reduced by the FADA-based approach compared to standard AODV.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Denial Of Service Attack">
  <data key="d0">Denial Of Service Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DoS attack class of which the flooding attack is a type.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sbai and El Boukhari [29] (Deep Learning IDS for UDP Flooding in MANETs)">
  <data key="d0">Sbai and El Boukhari [29] (Deep Learning IDS for UDP Flooding in MANETs)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [29]. The work proposes a deep-learning-based intrusion detection system for data flooding or UDP flooding attacks in MANETs, using the CICDDoS2019 dataset. It reports strong Accuracy, Precision, Recall and F1-score.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chatterjee and Saha [30] (ANN-Based Clustering Protocol)">
  <data key="d0">Chatterjee and Saha [30] (ANN-Based Clustering Protocol)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [30]. The work improves the authors' previous protocol with an ANN-based clustering algorithm that selects cluster heads using weight-based parameters. The inputs are mobility, packet drop, energy and the number of neighbor nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kaushik [32] (ANN and Firefly-Based Black Hole Detection)">
  <data key="d0">Kaushik [32] (ANN and Firefly-Based Black Hole Detection)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [32]. The work uses ANNs to identify black hole nodes, AODV for path selection, and the Firefly Algorithm fitness function to determine node features. It reports higher throughput and lower energy consumption, packet loss rate and delay.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hiremath et al. [33] (Adaptive FIS Against Cooperative Black Hole Attack)">
  <data key="d0">Hiremath et al. [33] (Adaptive FIS Against Cooperative Black Hole Attack)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [33]. The work develops a method for detecting and preventing cooperative black hole attacks on MANETs using an adaptive fuzzy inference system with fuzzy rule bases. It also explains how black hole attacks drop packets and lower network performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ghasemnezhad and Ghaffari [35] (FRRP)">
  <data key="d0">Ghasemnezhad and Ghaffari [35] (FRRP)</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Cited as [35]. The work creates the Fuzzy Logic-Based Reliable Routing Protocol (FRRP), which treats nodes as intelligent agents. It considers bandwidth, battery energy, hop count and mobility when selecting routes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chatterjee">
  <data key="d0">Chatterjee</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-author of work [30] on ANN-based clustering in MANETs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Saha">
  <data key="d0">Saha</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-author of work [30] on ANN-based clustering in MANETs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kaushik">
  <data key="d0">Kaushik</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Author of work [32] on ANN-based black hole node detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hiremath">
  <data key="d0">Hiremath</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">First author of work [33] on an adaptive FIS against cooperative black hole attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ghasemnezhad">
  <data key="d0">Ghasemnezhad</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-author of work [35] proposing FRRP.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ghaffari">
  <data key="d0">Ghaffari</data>
  <data key="d1">author</data>
  <data key="d2">Co-author of work [35] proposing FRRP.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Firefly Algorithm">
  <data key="d0">Firefly Algorithm</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">A metaheuristic for finding the best path, inspired by firefly flashing behavior and bioluminescent communication. Its fitness function is used to determine node features.&lt;SEP&gt;Optimization algorithm combined with an ANN and AODV for black hole attack detection.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy Logic-Based Reliable Routing Protocol">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy Logic-Based Reliable Routing Protocol</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">FRRP, a fuzzy-logic routing protocol that regards nodes as intelligent agents. It shows higher stability and efficiency than AODV.&lt;SEP&gt;FRRP, a fuzzy logic routing protocol that minimizes cost and network resource consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adaptive Fuzzy Inference System">
  <data key="d0">Adaptive Fuzzy Inference System</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">An adaptive FIS using fuzzy rule bases that lets nodes reason over imprecise information about neighbors to detect and prevent attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="UDP Flooding Attack">
  <data key="d0">UDP Flooding Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A data flooding attack in MANETs, addressed with a deep learning IDS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deep learning layers each provide a distinct interpretation of the data">
  <data key="d0">Deep learning layers each provide a distinct interpretation of the data</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "...multiple layers in deep learning, each of which provides a distinct interpretation of the data it feeds on [28]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ANNs are inspired by biological neural networks of human brains">
  <data key="d0">ANNs are inspired by biological neural networks of human brains</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "ANNs are computing systems that are inspired by the biological neural networks that constitute human brains [31]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Black hole attacks drop data packets and lower network performance">
  <data key="d0">Black hole attacks drop data packets and lower network performance</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "As a result, data packets are dropped in the network, lowering its performance [33]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy logic brings a more human way of thinking to computer programming">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy logic brings a more human way of thinking to computer programming</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "These values like fairly tall and swift are defined mathematically and prepared by PCs, aiming to use a more human way of thinking in PC programming [34]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AI makes systems more resilient as they learn from experience">
  <data key="d0">AI makes systems more resilient as they learn from experience</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement in the text: "Second, when a system learns from experience, AI will make the system more resilient day by day [36]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accuracy, Precision and Recall">
  <data key="d0">Accuracy, Precision and Recall</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Evaluation metrics used to assess the performance of the deep learning IDS proposed by Sbai and El Boukhari in MANET environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DDoS Attack">
  <data key="d0">DDoS Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Distributed Denial of Service attacks, to which the CICDDoS2019 dataset is purely dedicated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="AI-Based Networking">
  <data key="d0">AI-Based Networking</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A self-manageable network administration paradigm in which machines manage networks in place of humans, requiring very little human intervention.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Limitations of AI-Based MANET Security Approaches">
  <data key="d0">Limitations of AI-Based MANET Security Approaches</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The surveyed approaches have high time cost and memory resource consumption for predictions. They detect only intrusion types learned during the training phase, so detection becomes less reliable when traffic changes and the algorithm must be reset.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Node Legitimacy">
  <data key="d0">Network Node Legitimacy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Information about whether nodes are legitimate, which the AODV protocol lacks. Kaushik addresses this gap with the Firefly Algorithm fitness function.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sbai and El Boukhari [29]">
  <data key="d0">Sbai and El Boukhari [29]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as [29]. It uses deep learning for intrusion detection of data flooding or UDP flooding attacks. It achieves high accuracy, precision, recall and F1-score, but it is only resistant to flooding attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chatterjee and Saha [30]">
  <data key="d0">Chatterjee and Saha [30]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as [30]. It uses Artificial Neural Networks for clustering, creating a model to predict the weights needed to select cluster heads. It requires large storage and processing time.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kaushik [32]">
  <data key="d0">Kaushik [32]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as [32]. It addresses intrusion detection of black hole attacks using an Artificial Neural Network and the Firefly Algorithm with AODV. It reduces packet loss rate, delay and energy consumption, but it is only resistant to black hole attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ghasemnezhad and Ghaffari [35]">
  <data key="d0">Ghasemnezhad and Ghaffari [35]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as [35]. It proposes the Fuzzy Logic-Based Reliable Routing Protocol (FRRP), which minimizes cost and network resource consumption. The work covers only a single unicast routing protocol.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hiremath et al. [33]">
  <data key="d0">Hiremath et al. [33]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as [33]. It uses a Fuzzy Inference System to detect and prevent cooperative black hole attacks. It detects only black hole attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1e0beceeffe2b62352afd4291e0fd937-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501031</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
