<node id="Enhancing Predictive Analysis of Vehicle Accident Risk: A Fuzzy-Bayesian Approach">
  <data key="d0">Enhancing Predictive Analysis of Vehicle Accident Risk: A Fuzzy-Bayesian Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, published in IJACSA Vol. 15, No. 7, 2024. It develops a fuzzy-Bayesian approach that combines Bayesian networks and fuzzy logic to anticipate vehicle accident risks through predictive analysis. Results show a strong correlation between fatal injuries and factors related to driver and vehicle conditions, and the model is validated through three axioms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road Traffic Injuries">
  <data key="d0">Road Traffic Injuries</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Road traffic injuries (RTIs), a major cause of death claiming nearly 1.3 million lives each year.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
