</node>
<node id="Driver Condition">
  <data key="d0">Driver Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian network node 11 with linguistic values Good, Medium, Bad.&lt;SEP&gt;Node of the Bayesian network modeling road accident risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Parent node of Driver reaction time in the Bayesian Network.&lt;SEP&gt;Input variable describing the driver's condition (e.g., medium) used to condition the probability of driver fatigue.&lt;SEP&gt;Parent node of Driver Reaction-Time with linguistic values Bad, Medium and Good.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
