</node>
<node id="The three-axiom BN validation approach is widely adopted by researchers">
  <data key="d0">The three-axiom BN validation approach is widely adopted by researchers</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The axioms in question were originally proposed by [100] and widely adopted by several researchers such as [8], [88], [101], [102], [103], [104], [105]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Probabilistic Inference Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Probabilistic Inference Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">BN inference mechanism that, once the BN is given the input node states of a scenario, propagates probabilities across intermediate effects and final outcomes to assess the likelihood of an accident occurrence.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road and Traffic Parameters">
  <data key="d0">Road and Traffic Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BN input parameters covering road lighting, road cleaning after accident, speed limited, road design, road surface condition and traffic flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Driver Parameters">
  <data key="d0">Driver Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BN input parameters covering reaction time, driver style, driver condition, hard acceleration, speed limits respects, safety distance respect and hard breaking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delivery Planning Parameters">
  <data key="d0">Delivery Planning Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BN input parameters covering kilometers to be covered, number of exchanges, delivery period and truck fill rate; summarized as planning overload (minimum or maximum) in Table VI.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vehicle Condition Parameters">
  <data key="d0">Vehicle Condition Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">BN input parameters covering physical vehicle condition and stopping distance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario S1">
  <data key="d0">Scenario S1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario in which all parameters (road, traffic, driver, planning and vehicle condition) are favourable; yields 98% no accident, 1% possible injury and 1% fatal injury (Table VII).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario S2">
  <data key="d0">Scenario S2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario with favourable road, traffic and vehicle condition but unfavourable driver and planning parameters (e.g. too long reaction time, bad driver style, maximum overload); yields 98% fatal injury, 1% no accident and 1% possible injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario S3">
  <data key="d0">Scenario S3</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario with unfavourable road and traffic parameters (obscurity, wet surface, dangerous design, stop-and-go traffic) and favourable driver, planning and vehicle condition; yields 92.30% no accident, 3.85% possible injury and 3.85% fatal injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scenario S4">
  <data key="d0">Scenario S4</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario with favourable road, traffic, driver and planning parameters but unfavourable vehicle condition (bad physical condition, long stopping distance); yields 88.20% possible injury, 5.90% no accident and 5.90% fatal injury.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Driver and planning conditions drive the highest fatal accident risk">
  <data key="d0">Driver and planning conditions drive the highest fatal accident risk</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding of the study based on Table VII: unfavourable driver and planning parameters (S2) result in a 98% probability of fatal injury, whereas unfavourable road and traffic (S3) still yield 92.30% no accident.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Poor vehicle condition leads mainly to possible injury">
  <data key="d0">Poor vehicle condition leads mainly to possible injury</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding of the study based on Table VII: with unfavourable vehicle condition (S4), the probability of possible injury reaches 88.20%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axiom Verification">
  <data key="d0">Axiom Verification</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation procedure applied to every node in the network to confirm adherence to three axioms through sensitivity analysis of parent-node probability changes (increases of 10% and 20%, decreases of 5% and 10%).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Driver's Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Driver's Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Child node in the network influenced by parent nodes Driver's condition and Visibility; its probability rose from 52.3% to 65% when Driver's condition increased by 20%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Driver's Condition">
  <data key="d0">Driver's Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Parent node of Driver's reaction in the Bayesian network. In the Axiom 1 verification (Table VIII), raising Driver's condition from its 50% prior to 70% raised Driver's reaction from 52.3% to 65%, and lowering it to 40% reduced Driver's reaction to 50.1%. In the Axiom 3 verification (Table X), raising it alone to 100% changed driver reaction time by only 0.8%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delivery Planning">
  <data key="d0">Delivery Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factor, alongside driver behavior, with significant impact on accidents; optimized delivery schedules and smart routing are recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vehicle Condition">
  <data key="d0">Vehicle Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factor with considerable effect on accident occurrence; regular vehicle maintenance recommended.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road Safety">
  <data key="d0">Road Safety</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Overall research topic: recognizing and preventing risk elements to reduce road accidents and traffic injuries.&lt;SEP&gt;The application domain the model aims to improve; integrating the model with other predictive technologies is intended to further enhance road safety measures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Logistics Delivery Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Logistics Delivery Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Expected to increase through use of the proposed fuzzy Bayesian Network approach.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Computational Cost Of Inference">
  <data key="d0">Computational Cost Of Inference</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Challenge of computational expense of inference in fuzzy Bayesian networks, especially large or multistate networks; target of future work.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Driver behavior and delivery planning influence accidents more than road and traffic conditions">
  <data key="d0">Driver behavior and delivery planning influence accidents more than road and traffic conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding: "driver behaviors, delivery planning, and vehicle condition have a considerable effect on the occurrence of accidents compared to parameters related to road and traffic conditions."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Road accidents result from interplay of multiple causal factors">
  <data key="d0">Road accidents result from interplay of multiple causal factors</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">According to bibliographical research and expert perspectives, road accidents are not caused by a single factor but by a complex interplay of multiple factors connected by causal interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Distracted">
  <data key="d0">Distracted</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Parent node of the driver reaction-time node in the Axiom 3 verification (Table X). Raising Distracted alone from 34% to 100% produced the largest single-parent change in driver reaction time: 26.9%, from 50.5% to 77.4%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axiom 3 Verification">
  <data key="d0">Axiom 3 Verification</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Validation test (Table X) showing that raising all parent nodes of Driver's reaction to 100% gives a larger increase than raising any single parent. Raising all parents changed driver reaction time by 29.5%, to 80.0%, which is consistent with axiom 3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raising all parent nodes produces a larger increase than raising a single parent">
  <data key="d0">Raising all parent nodes produces a larger increase than raising a single parent</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">a more substantial increase results when all parent elements of the 'Driver's reaction' node are elevated to 100%, compared to the increase observed when only a single parent element is separately enhanced. This observation aligns well with the principles of axiom 3.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Driver Training">
  <data key="d0">Driver Training</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Measure recommended by the findings to substantially reduce accident risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vehicle Maintenance">
  <data key="d0">Vehicle Maintenance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Regular vehicle maintenance is recommended by the findings to reduce accident risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">Paper_101-Enhancing_Predictive_Analysis_of_Vehicle_Accident_Risk.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501134</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Smart Routing Planning">
  <data key="d0">Smart Routing Planning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing planning designs recommended, together with monitoring driver behaviors, to avoid road accidents.</data>
