  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Freight Vehicles">
  <data key="d0">Freight Vehicles</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vehicles that Smart DLSP is intended to give more intelligence in the service of logistics on a global scale.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vehicular Ad Hoc Network (VANET)">
  <data key="d0">Vehicular Ad Hoc Network (VANET)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Wireless vehicular communication technology characterized by high mobility, no centralized control unit, scalability issues, hidden node issue, insecure medium and limited resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fuzzy–Bayesian Approach">
  <data key="d0">Fuzzy–Bayesian Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Model combining Bayesian networks and fuzzy logic to build conditional probability tables and predict QoS risks in VANETs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthetic QoS Risk Database">
  <data key="d0">Synthetic QoS Risk Database</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">Synthetic database created by the paper predicting risks associated with QoS in VANETs during transport, containing combinations of possible risk situations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VANET Applications Require Best-Effort QoS">
  <data key="d0">VANET Applications Require Best-Effort QoS</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In a VANET, many applications are sensitive to latency and bandwidth constraints and have an epsilon tolerance for network interruptions. As a result, it must provide the best effort in terms of quality of service (QoS) to guarantee its performance [5].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="QoS Provides Priorities to Applications Under Service Constraints">
  <data key="d0">QoS Provides Priorities to Applications Under Service Constraints</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In other words, it is the ability to provide different priorities to various applications that can satisfy a set of predetermined service constraints in terms of time, available bandwidth, packet loss, security, etc. [6].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Comparative Studies of Routing Protocols Improve QoS Parameters">
  <data key="d0">Comparative Studies of Routing Protocols Improve QoS Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"On the one hand, some authors [7–9] chose to conduct comparative studies of existing routing protocols and algorithms." They aimed to select efficient protocols improving delay, jitter, throughput and packet loss ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CBQoS-Vanet">
  <data key="d0">CBQoS-Vanet</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing protocol using clustering schemes with cluster heads and an artificial bee colony to find routes satisfying mobility and QoS metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GeoQoE-Vanet">
  <data key="d0">GeoQoE-Vanet</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Geographic video streaming protocol using a correlated QoE and QoS formula; outperformed GPSR and GPSR-2P in urban simulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artificial Bee Colony">
  <data key="d0">Artificial Bee Colony</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Optimization algorithm used by CBQoS-Vanet to find optimized routes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Greedy Perimeter Stateless Routing (GPSR)">
  <data key="d0">Greedy Perimeter Stateless Routing (GPSR)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing protocol outperformed by GeoQoE-Vanet in urban simulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPSR-2P">
  <data key="d0">GPSR-2P</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Routing protocol outperformed by GeoQoE-Vanet in urban simulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dijkstra's Dedicated Short-Range Communication Protocol (DDSRC)">
  <data key="d0">Dijkstra's Dedicated Short-Range Communication Protocol (DDSRC)</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Algorithm that determines the shortest route to the destination based on the cost of each transmission path, used with roadside units.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Roadside Units (RSUs)">
  <data key="d0">Roadside Units (RSUs)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure units used to collect and transmit traffic data in VANETs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quality of Experience (QoE)">
  <data key="d0">Quality of Experience (QoE)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Factor correlated with QoS in GeoQoE-Vanet to achieve high quality in relaying vehicles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Artificial Intelligence (AI)">
  <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence (AI)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An information technology that Ecodid integrates. The paper combines two AI approaches, Bayesian networks and fuzzy logic, to quantify QoS in a VANET.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VANET Routing">
  <data key="d0">VANET Routing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The routing aspect of VANETs. The text states that most authors in the literature have focused on it when treating QoS improvement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501518</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="New VANET Protocols Were Developed to Improve QoS">
  <data key="d0">New VANET Protocols Were Developed to Improve QoS</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Others developed new protocols, such as QMM-VANET [10], CBQoS-Vanet [11], and GeoQoE-Vanet [12].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
