<node id="FL implementation consists of fuzzification, inference and defuzzification">
  <data key="d0">FL implementation consists of fuzzification, inference and defuzzification</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "The implementation of FL for generating CPs was done in three principal steps [19,20]".</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mamdani uses defuzzification while Sugeno uses weighted average">
  <data key="d0">Mamdani uses defuzzification while Sugeno uses weighted average</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Mamdani employs the defuzzification phase for fuzzy outputs, whereas Sugeno computes the result values by using a weighted average [21]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Internet mode fails in special conditions such as isolated sites and disaster areas">
  <data key="d0">Normal Internet mode fails in special conditions such as isolated sites and disaster areas</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "However, it can not fulfill the communication needs under some special conditions, such as at isolated sites and in areas after floods and tremors [22]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RSUs can provide Internet connectivity via base stations">
  <data key="d0">RSUs can provide Internet connectivity via base stations</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "They can even provide Internet connectivity to road users via their connection to base stations [23]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VANETs enable applications such as traffic management, platooning and vehicle tracking">
  <data key="d0">VANETs enable applications such as traffic management, platooning and vehicle tracking</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Benefiting from many applications, such as traffic control and management, platooning, vehicle tracking, comfort applications, and different notification services [24]."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weighted Average">
  <data key="d0">Weighted Average</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Computation the Sugeno inference method uses to obtain result values from fuzzy inputs, instead of a defuzzification phase.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ad Hoc Mode">
  <data key="d0">Ad Hoc Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Communication mode of the Smart DLSP that is used when there are problems with the Internet; it relies on a VANET.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Mode">
  <data key="d0">Normal Mode</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Communication mode of the Smart DLSP that is used when an Internet connection exists. It offers increased capacity, large coverage and existing infrastructure, but fails under special conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501545</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ETL">
  <data key="d0">ETL</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Extract–transform–load platform that aggregates, transforms and structures data streamed from message brokers. Apache Storm is one example.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Lake">
  <data key="d0">Data Lake</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage where the streaming data are kept, accessible later to different users and vehicles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Base Stations">
  <data key="d0">Base Stations</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Infrastructure through which RSUs can provide Internet connectivity to road users.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sugeno method is preferred for its faster processing time">
  <data key="d0">Sugeno method is preferred for its faster processing time</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "This study prefers the method of Sugeno because it has a faster processing time. As a result, the generation of CPs is achieved with just the two first steps."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FB Approach">
  <data key="d0">FB Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Proposed approach combining a Bayesian Network and Fuzzy Logic to compute the QoS in a VANET for scenario examples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="False Data Injection Attacks">
  <data key="d0">False Data Injection Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attacks in which hackers alter a target's data to influence the behavior of other nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Byzantine Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Byzantine Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attacks gaining access to the wireless network and selectively or totally dropping received packets, such as gray hole and black hole attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Security problem used as an input node in the BN scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flooding Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Flooding Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attack variable (few, medium, many) that acts as a parent of congestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Denial-of-service attacks that flood the network with false RREQ packets, causing congestion and packet drops.&lt;SEP&gt;Security problem used as an input node in the BN scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Input variable (few, medium, many) influencing congestion in the BN.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Selfish Behavior">
  <data key="d0">Selfish Behavior</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Node misbehavior variable (few, medium, many) that degrades network performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Selfish nodes not participating in network activities to save resources, degrading network performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Security problem used as an input node in the BN.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VANETs enable many logistics applications">
  <data key="d0">VANETs enable many logistics applications</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Benefiting from many applications, such as traffic control and management, platooning, vehicle tracking, comfort applications, and different notification services [24].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Adverse weather causes signal attenuation">
  <data key="d0">Adverse weather causes signal attenuation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Precipitation with various forms, including rain, clouds, snow, and fog, absorbs and disperses electromagnetic energy, resulting in signal attenuation [25].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VANET mobility varies with authorized road speed">
  <data key="d0">VANET mobility varies with authorized road speed</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In a VANET, the mobility of vehicles varies according to the speed authorized on each type of road (highways, urban areas, residential, rural, etc.) [15].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VANET density varies by region">
  <data key="d0">VANET density varies by region</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">For example, it is very high in congested city situations and is deficient in rural areas due to the low traffic [26].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FDI attacks alter target data to influence nodes">
  <data key="d0">FDI attacks alter target data to influence nodes</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This variable represents false data injection attacks, in which hackers attempt to make changes in a target's data to influence the behavior of other nodes [28].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Byzantine attacks drop received packets">
  <data key="d0">Byzantine attacks drop received packets</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">This variable represents all attacks that gain access to the wireless network and drop selectively or totally received packets, such as gray hole [29] and black hole attacks [30].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Flooding attacks degrade network performance">
  <data key="d0">Flooding attacks degrade network performance</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finally, they degrade the network performance in terms of battery power, available bandwidth, and computational ability [31].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gray Hole Attack">
  <data key="d0">Gray Hole Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Type of Byzantine attack in which a malicious node gains access to the wireless network and selectively drops received packets; cited with reference [29].&lt;SEP&gt;Packet-dropping attack in vehicular networks. Addressed by Ali Alheeti et al. and by Krishnan and Kumar.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Denial-of-Service Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Denial-of-Service Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">DoS attacks that disrupt the normal operation of a network. Flooding attacks are a form of DoS that degrade battery power, available bandwidth and computational ability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Signal Attenuation">
  <data key="d0">Signal Attenuation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Weakening of wireless signals caused by precipitation such as rain, clouds, snow and fog, and by reflection and attenuation from obstacles such as trees, buildings, walls and hilly terrain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vehicle Mobility">
  <data key="d0">Vehicle Mobility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Input variable of the Bayesian model. Vehicle mobility in a VANET varies with the speed authorized on each road type, such as highways, urban, residential and rural roads.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Inputs">
  <data key="d0">Data Inputs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian network variable for all data collected from sensors, uploaded from the Internet, or received from other vehicles and RSUs. Its linguistic values are few, medium, and many.&lt;SEP&gt;Input variable of the Bayesian model representing data collected from sensors, uploaded from the Internet, or received from other vehicles and RSUs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edge Components">
  <data key="d0">Edge Components</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian network variable for the saturation of an edge box's resources (processor, RAM, storage), which affects the performance of data processing. Its linguistic values are saturated, medium, and normal.&lt;SEP&gt;Input variable of the Bayesian model representing saturation of edge box resources (processor, RAM, storage), which affects data processing performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Platooning">
  <data key="d0">Platooning</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">VANET application cited among the benefits for logistics operations, together with traffic control, vehicle tracking, comfort applications and notification services.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Selfish nodes degrade network performance in battery power, bandwidth and computation">
  <data key="d0">Selfish nodes degrade network performance in battery power, bandwidth and computation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Statement made in the text: "Finally, they degrade the network performance in terms of battery power, available bandwidth, and computational ability [31]." The excerpt does not explicitly name the subject "they"; it appears in the description of a misbehavior variable (likely selfish behavior) that also causes congestion and packet drops.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sugeno's Method">
  <data key="d0">Sugeno's Method</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Fuzzy inference method implemented with FisPro to create the FL inference system.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edge Box">
  <data key="d0">Edge Box</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Vehicle edge computing box with processor, RAM, and storage. Saturation of its resources affects data processing, and the vehicle battery charges it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Battery Energy">
  <data key="d0">Battery Energy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian network variable for the battery charge of a vehicle that charges an edge box, even when the vehicle is stopped. Its linguistic values are discharged, medium, and charged.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Drops Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Drops Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Packet-drop attack variable in the Bayesian network, with linguistic values few, medium, and many.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="FDI Attacks">
  <data key="d0">FDI Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">False data injection attacks, a security problem used as an input node in the BN.&lt;SEP&gt;False data injection (FDI) attack variable in the Bayesian network, with linguistic values few, medium, and many.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Signal Strength">
  <data key="d0">Signal Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian network variable with linguistic values low, medium, and high.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="E2ED">
  <data key="d0">E2ED</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">End-to-end delay variable in the Bayesian network, with linguistic values short, medium, and long.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quantity Of Data">
  <data key="d0">Quantity Of Data</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bayesian network variable with linguistic values few, medium, and many.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Universe Of Discourse">
  <data key="d0">Universe Of Discourse</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Component U of a linguistic variable's quadruplet, associated with the variable X. For congestion it is the range [0, 100] in percent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Roadside Unit">
  <data key="d0">Roadside Unit</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Roadside units (RSUs) in a VANET, which send data that vehicles receive as data inputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Open Markov">
  <data key="d0">Open Markov</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Software used to build the Bayesian Network and feed it with conditional probabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vehicle Density">
  <data key="d0">Vehicle Density</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Road condition input variable (low, medium, high) influencing congestion and connectivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urban Environment">
  <data key="d0">Urban Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario 1: high density, low mobility, obstacles causing disconnections, prone to attacks, many services causing bandwidth congestion.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rural Environment">
  <data key="d0">Rural Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario 2: low density and poor infrastructure, large inter-vehicle spacing, very low attack percentage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Highway Environment">
  <data key="d0">Highway Environment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Scenario 3: adequate communication but short link lifetimes due to speeds over 100 km/h, with many selfish nodes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urban VANET connectivity is affected by obstacles causing frequent disconnections">
  <data key="d0">Urban VANET connectivity is affected by obstacles causing frequent disconnections</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">However, this connectivity can be affected by obstacles such as tall buildings or vehicles that are not connected, which leads to frequent disconnection problems between edges [32].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urban VANETs offer many attractive services including location-based services">
  <data key="d0">Urban VANETs offer many attractive services including location-based services</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">On the other hand, there are enumerable attractive services, such as Internet access, automatic toll payment, traffic management, location-based services [33], and increased road events, such as accidents and criminal activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rural VANETs have very low attack rates and data exchange causes no vehicle problems">
  <data key="d0">Rural VANETs have very low attack rates and data exchange causes no vehicle problems</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In this scenario, the percentage of attacks was assumed to be very low, and the data exchanged did not cause any vehicle problems [34].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Many highway VANET nodes are selfish and refuse to participate in routing">
  <data key="d0">Many highway VANET nodes are selfish and refuse to participate in routing</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">In this scenario, a significant number of nodes are assumed to be selfish and deny participation in routing to save their own resources [35].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Max Aggregation of Rule Conclusions">
  <data key="d0">Max Aggregation of Rule Conclusions</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Aggregation step in which the conclusion for a state is the maximum over the applicable rules, e.g. congestion (high) = max(0.135, 0.044, 0.607) = 0.607.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bandwidth Congestion">
  <data key="d0">Bandwidth Congestion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Saturation of bandwidth, edge components and battery energy caused by the exponential increase of data exchange in urban VANETs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Network Disconnection">
  <data key="d0">Network Disconnection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Frequent disconnection between edges in urban VANETs caused by obstacles such as tall buildings or non-connected vehicles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Link Lifetime">
  <data key="d0">Link Lifetime</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Duration of links between vehicles. It is very short on highways because vehicle speeds exceed 100 km/h.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Tree Analysis Reference [36]">
  <data key="d0">Event Tree Analysis Reference [36]</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work cited as [36] that describes event tree analysis, including initial events and intermediate events that represent controlled incidents.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Connection Loss">
  <data key="d0">Connection Loss</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Loss of connection in a VANET. Its rate ranges from 43.271% when all security systems fail to 0.006% when they all function.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authentication Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Authentication Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Security mechanism used as an intermediate event in the event tree.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Integrity Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Integrity Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Security mechanism used as an intermediate event in the event tree.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cryptographic Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Cryptographic Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Security mechanism used as an intermediate event in the event tree.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intrusion Detection and Prevention Systems">
  <data key="d0">Intrusion Detection and Prevention Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">IDSs and IPSs, which serve as security mechanisms and intermediate events in the event tree.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event tree analysis models sequences of events via initial and intermediate events">
  <data key="d0">Event tree analysis models sequences of events via initial and intermediate events</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Then, it is followed by intermediate events, which present controlled incidents with the aim of avoiding further danger [36].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Security barriers limit effects of low QoS in VANET">
  <data key="d0">Security barriers limit effects of low QoS in VANET</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding of the paper: the connection loss rate is at its maximum (43.271%) if all security systems fail and at its minimum (0.006%) otherwise, which shows the importance of security barriers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Event Tree">
  <data key="d0">Event Tree</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Tree structure (ET) built chronologically from an initial event, "low QoS in the VANET" for the urban case, followed by intermediate security-mechanism events and consequences. Branch probabilities are quantified as P(R) = ∏ P(Bi) over the branches leading to outcome R.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Low QoS in VANET">
  <data key="d0">Low QoS in VANET</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Initial event in the paper's event tree. It is responsible for the critical situation of the system in the urban environment case and can lead to supply chain connection loss.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Urban Areas">
  <data key="d0">Urban Areas</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environment where QoS in VANET is found to be more prone to weaknesses and vulnerabilities, due to high accessibility, congestion, and increased traffic and delivery flows in cities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three Scenarios">
  <data key="d0">Three Scenarios</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Three scenarios defined by the potentials of BN input nodes (Table 7) for road condition (density, mobility, obstacles, weather), security problems (selfish behavior, flooding, Byzantine and FDI attacks) and vehicle resources (data inputs, battery energy, edge components). They are used to compute the probability distribution of QoS in VANET.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="QoS in urban VANET is more prone to vulnerabilities">
  <data key="d0">QoS in urban VANET is more prone to vulnerabilities</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Finding of the paper: "it was concluded that the QoS in VANET in urban areas is more prone to weaknesses and vulnerabilities due to the high accessibility and congestion emanating from the increased traffic and delivery flows in cities."</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Connection Loss Prediction">
  <data key="d0">Connection Loss Prediction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Prediction of connection loss in a VANET in the presence of security mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Symbiotic_Combination_of_a_Bayesian_Network_and_Fu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
