</node>
<node id="Villaizán-Vallelado et al., 2025">
  <data key="d0">Villaizán-Vallelado et al., 2025</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Diffusion Models for Tabular Data Imputation &amp; Generation (2025). It introduces a model that combines transformer-based conditioning and dynamic masking for both missing data imputation and synthetic data generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shi et al., 2024">
  <data key="d0">Shi et al., 2024</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Work by Shi et al. (2024) that proposes TabDiff, a joint diffusion framework with feature-wise learnable diffusion processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Z. Li et al., 2025">
  <data key="d0">Z. Li et al., 2025</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">Survey (2025) detailing progress, challenges and future directions of diffusion approaches for tabular data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TabDDPM">
  <data key="d0">TabDDPM</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Diffusion model for mixed-type tabular data. It outperforms many GAN- and VAE-based generators in fidelity and diversity, and better handles structural correlations while reducing privacy risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffusion-model-based approach for modelling tabular data, introduced by Kotelnikov et al. (2022).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TabDiff">
  <data key="d0">TabDiff</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Joint diffusion framework that models continuous and categorical features. It improves preservation of pairwise correlations and outperforms numerous baselines.&lt;SEP&gt;Joint diffusion framework modeling continuous and categorical features with feature-wise learnable diffusion processes; improves preservation of pairwise correlations and outperforms numerous baselines.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixed-type diffusion model for tabular data generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Copulas">
  <data key="d0">Copulas</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Classical probabilistic approach used to model joint distributions for synthetic data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diffusion Models">
  <data key="d0">Diffusion Models</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Generative models, successful in image and signal domains, that are being adapted for tabular data generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Generative models applied to tabular and time-series synthetic data generation.&lt;SEP&gt;Generative models applied to tabular data (TabDDPM, Li et al. 2025) and to text-conditioned synthetic sensor data generation (Mora-de-León et al. 2025).&lt;SEP&gt;Generative models applied to tabular data generation, tabular data imputation and synthetic financial time series.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Synthetic Tabular Data Generation">
  <data key="d0">Synthetic Tabular Data Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Research problem of generating synthetic tabular datasets that preserve target proportions, adhere to defined intervals, and exclude invalid combinations.&lt;SEP&gt;Mature research area focused on creating artificial datasets that preserve the statistical properties, constraints and inter-column dependencies of real data.&lt;SEP&gt;Research topic of generating synthetic structured/tabular data.&lt;SEP&gt;Generation of synthetic tabular data that is statistically coherent with the intended distributions and logically consistent with domain-specific constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;Research problem of generating artificial tabular data that reproduces target marginal distributions and adheres to logical constraints.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Predictive Privacy">
  <data key="d0">Predictive Privacy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Notion introduced by Mühlhoff (2023): privacy violations can arise when models infer sensitive traits about individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Concept of collective data protection in the context of AI and big data, discussed by Mühlhoff (2023).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GDPR">
  <data key="d0">GDPR</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">European data protection regulation. Its principles, such as data minimization and purpose limitation, conflict with centralized architectures and with AI systems' use of inferred data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Noisy or imbalanced data complicates training of reliable predictive maintenance models">
  <data key="d0">Noisy or imbalanced data complicates training of reliable predictive maintenance models</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">These difficulties are further compounded when available data is noisy or imbalanced, complicating the training of reliable models (Bansal et al., 2022).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centralized architectures pose privacy risks and GDPR non-compliance">
  <data key="d0">Centralized architectures pose privacy risks and GDPR non-compliance</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Traditional centralized architectures pose significant risks due to the concentration of sensitive operational data in cloud environments, increasing exposure to breaches and non-compliance with regulations such as the GDPR (Chen &amp; Zhao, 2012; Zhang, 2018).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Privacy-enhancing techniques protect federated model updates from inference attacks">
  <data key="d0">Privacy-enhancing techniques protect federated model updates from inference attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Privacy-enhancing techniques such as homomorphic encryption, differential privacy, and secure multi-party computation (SMPC) have been integrated to further protect model updates from inference attacks (Hosni, 2025).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CTGAN is a strong baseline in tabular data benchmarks">
  <data key="d0">CTGAN is a strong baseline in tabular data benchmarks</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Later works have extended or adapted CTGAN for domain-specific uses (Parise et al., 2025), and comparative benchmarking studies frequently place CTGAN as a strong baseline (Pathare et al., 2023).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Probabilistic methods learn and sample joint distributions">
  <data key="d0">Probabilistic methods learn and sample joint distributions</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Earlier probabilistic approaches relied on Bayesian networks (Gogoshin et al., 2021) and copulas (Kamthe et al., 2021) to learn and sample joint distributions over variables (Xu et al., 2019).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Privacy and Security">
  <data key="d0">Data Privacy and Security</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A critical concern for predictive maintenance systems that rely on large-scale data from IT and industrial infrastructures. Centralized cloud architectures increase exposure to breaches.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Homomorphic Encryption">
  <data key="d0">Homomorphic Encryption</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Privacy-enhancing technique integrated with federated learning to protect model updates from inference attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secure Multi-Party Computation">
  <data key="d0">Secure Multi-Party Computation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Privacy-enhancing technique (SMPC) integrated with federated learning to protect model updates from inference attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inference Attacks">
  <data key="d0">Inference Attacks</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Attacks on model updates that privacy-enhancing techniques in federated learning aim to prevent.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variational Autoencoders">
  <data key="d0">Variational Autoencoders</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Deep generative models (VAEs) used as baselines for tabular data generation. CTGAN, TabDDPM and the Villaizán-Vallelado et al. model are compared against them.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Conditional Sampling">
  <data key="d0">Conditional Sampling</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Technique introduced in CTGAN to account for rare categories in tabular data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mode-Specific Normalization">
  <data key="d0">Mode-Specific Normalization</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Technique used by CTGAN for continuous variables, enabling joint learning of numeric and categorical columns.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Missing Data Imputation">
  <data key="d0">Missing Data Imputation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Task of filling in missing values. The model of Villaizán-Vallelado et al. (2025) handles it jointly with synthetic data generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transformer-Based Conditioning with Dynamic Masking">
  <data key="d0">Transformer-Based Conditioning with Dynamic Masking</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Diffusion model introduced by Villaizán-Vallelado et al. (2025) that combines transformer-based conditioning and dynamic masking to jointly perform imputation and synthetic tabular data generation. It compares favorably with GANs and VAEs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CTGAN outperforms Bayesian baselines and earlier GAN/VAEs">
  <data key="d0">CTGAN outperforms Bayesian baselines and earlier GAN/VAEs</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">"CTGAN showed strong performance against Bayesian baseline methods and earlier GAN/VAEs in multiple benchmark datasets." Attributed to Xu et al. (2019).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TabDDPM outperforms GAN- and VAE-based generators in fidelity and diversity">
  <data key="d0">TabDDPM outperforms GAN- and VAE-based generators in fidelity and diversity</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">TabDDPM (Kotelnikov et al., 2022): A diffusion model for mixed-type tabular data that outperforms many GAN- and VAE-based synthetic generators, particularly in terms of fidelity and diversity. It is shown to better handle structural correlations and reduce privacy risk compared to interpolation methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="TabDiff improves preservation of pairwise correlations">
  <data key="d0">TabDiff improves preservation of pairwise correlations</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">TabDiff (Shi et al., 2024): Proposes a joint diffusion framework to model both continuous and categorical features with feature-wise learnable diffusion processes, improving preservation of pairwise correlations and outperforming numerous baselines across multiple metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Diffusion-based imputation model compares favorably with GANs and VAEs">
  <data key="d0">Diffusion-based imputation model compares favorably with GANs and VAEs</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Diffusion Models for Tabular Data Imputation &amp; Generation (Villaizán-Vallelado et al., 2025): Introduces a model combining transformer-based conditioning and dynamic masking to jointly handle missing data imputation and synthetic data generation, comparing favorably with GANs and VAEs over benchmarks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
