<node id="TabDiff improves pairwise correlation preservation">
  <data key="d0">TabDiff improves pairwise correlation preservation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">TabDiff (Shi et al., 2024): Proposes a joint diffusion framework ... improving preservation of pairwise correlations and outperforming numerous baselines across multiple metrics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid autoencoder-diffusion models capture tabular correlations">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid autoencoder-diffusion models capture tabular correlations</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid models combining autoencoders and diffusion also demonstrate efficacy in capturing correlations in tabular data (Suh et al., 2023).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zero-shot LLMs can match or surpass CTGAN">
  <data key="d0">Zero-shot LLMs can match or surpass CTGAN</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">The comparative study (Barr et al., 2025) explores zero-shot generation using GPT-4o versus CTGAN, showing that LLMs ... can sometimes match or surpass CTGAN in preserving means, correlations, and privacy under some datasets.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LLMs provide semantic scaffolding while CTGAN ensures statistical coherence">
  <data key="d0">LLMs provide semantic scaffolding while CTGAN ensures statistical coherence</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">(Khalil et al., 2025) explores blending CTGAN and LLMs to generate educational tabular data, demonstrating how LLMs can provide semantic scaffolding while CTGAN ensures statistical coherence.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-GPU GAN training achieves near-linear speed-up">
  <data key="d0">Multi-GPU GAN training achieves near-linear speed-up</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">(Cardoso et al., 2021) explored multi-GPU and TPU parallelization of GAN training ... achieving near-linear speed-up in training time while maintaining the quality of generated data comparable to Monte Carlo simulations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPU-enabled diffusion sampling is feasible for real-time augmentation">
  <data key="d0">GPU-enabled diffusion sampling is feasible for real-time augmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Their results show that GPU-enabled diffusion sampling is feasible for real-time synthetic data augmentation and that the synthetic samples maintain high fidelity in downstream tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Accelerated diffusion models offer favorable quality-diversity trade-off">
  <data key="d0">Accelerated diffusion models offer favorable quality-diversity trade-off</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">(Takahashi &amp; Mizuno, 2025) ... report that diffusion models-when accelerated-offer a favorable trade-off between quality and diversity versus other generative methods like GANs and VAEs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPU-accelerated DDP significantly reduces execution time">
  <data key="d0">GPU-accelerated DDP significantly reduces execution time</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">Their experiments demonstrate that employing GPU-accelerated DDP reduces execution times significantly (a proposed DDP-GPU scheduling approach led to 95.3% improvements in efficiency over conventional single-GPU execution...).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPU parallelism suits high-throughput ML and DL workloads">
  <data key="d0">GPU parallelism suits high-throughput ML and DL workloads</data>
  <data key="d1">claim</data>
  <data key="d2">They emphasize that the massive parallelism of GPUs allows complex computational problems to be decomposed into smaller, more efficient tasks, making them particularly suitable for high-throughput workloads in ML and DL.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501852</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
