<node id="Biased Distributions">
  <data key="d0">Biased Distributions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">System-level risk where generated data distributions are biased because parameters do not accurately represent real-world data or domain-specific characteristics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501853</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User Misconfiguration">
  <data key="d0">User Misconfiguration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Risk where user configuration errors result in invalid data or failure to enforce intended constraints.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501853</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPU Debugging Difficulties">
  <data key="d0">GPU Debugging Difficulties</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Practical difficulties in developing the parallel method: CUDA kernels lack interactive step-by-step inspection, making defects such as infinite loops or incorrect termination conditions harder to detect, and type inconsistencies in indices, counters or probability values can cause silent failures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501853</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Large-Scale Stress Testing">
  <data key="d0">Large-Scale Stress Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">IT infrastructure application enabled by the framework, using synthetic data with controlled distributions and dependencies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791501853</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
