<node id="Toward Quantum-Safe Permissioned Blockchains: Evaluating Hybrid ML-DSA-65/ECDSA Signatures on Hyperledger Fabric">
  <data key="d0">Toward Quantum-Safe Permissioned Blockchains: Evaluating Hybrid ML-DSA-65/ECDSA Signatures on Hyperledger Fabric</data>
  <data key="d1">paper</data>
  <data key="d2">The article being read, accepted for publication in IEEE Access. It presents a controlled empirical evaluation of a hybrid ML-DSA-65/ECDSA signature architecture for Hyperledger Fabric. The architecture integrates ML-DSA-65 at the application layer through an external post-quantum signing microservice and preserves Fabric's native ECDSA infrastructure. The paper finds no statistically significant transaction-level degradation and blocks about 1.43x larger.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502182</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
