  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ML-DSA-65">
  <data key="d0">ML-DSA-65</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">ML-DSA-65 is a post-quantum digital signature parameter set of the ML-DSA module-lattice signature standard specified in FIPS 204. It is the NIST-standardized successor of CRYSTALS-Dilithium 3 and provides post-quantum authentication at NIST security category 3. It is regarded as a strong candidate for long-term transaction authentication in blockchain systems. The study uses ML-DSA-65 in place of pre-standardization Dilithium variants. It serves as the primary configuration and as the post-quantum component of a hybrid signature scheme that combines it with ECDSA on Hyperledger Fabric. The paper compares ML-DSA-65 with ECDSA and evaluates it both alone and in hybrid configurations within a Fabric-oriented transaction workflow, including a primary six-scenario benchmark evaluation.

ML-DSA-65 is integrated at the application layer rather than in Fabric's native identity layer. Signatures are produced by an external PQC signing microservice built with FastAPI/uvicorn on liboqs-python, using signing-service instances with round-robin request distribution. Public keys are registered per MSP organization and bound to MSP identities. Signatures are generated over document content hashes, so signing time does not depend on payload size. The signatures are recorded by chaincode, for example through SignDocument transactions, as application-level cryptographic evidence. Verification is not done in chaincode; it is performed off-chain by clients, auditors, or relying parties using the registered public key. Across 417 monitoring samples, the signing microservice used an average of 0.10% CPU and 64.7 MB of memory.

**Artifact sizes and storage:**
- An ML-DSA-65 signature is 3,309 bytes, about 47 times larger than an ECDSA DER-encoded signature.
- The public key is 1,952 bytes.
- Both are Base64-encoded in the chaincode and stored on-ledger. This adds about 4,412 signature characters and 2,604 public-key characters, or 7,016 characters per transaction or signing event.
- Combined, the signature and public-key material is about 20.9 times larger than ECDSA P-256 artifacts. This makes PQC hybrid blocks 1.48 times larger than ECDSA blocks.
- Across 478 analyzed blocks, the measured mean active-block size was 43,551 bytes. A model estimate of 43,360 bytes differed by about 0.4%. Estimated storage is about 21,776 bytes per transaction.

**Performance (optimized liboqs implementation, 1,000 iterations):**
- Signing averaged 0.226 ms, roughly 4,425 single-thread operations per second, which is negligible relative to Fabric transaction latency.
- Isolated verification averaged 0.087 ms.
- System throughput in the ML-DSA-65 configuration was 14.42 ± 3.11 TPS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-041</data>
