<node id="Dilithium">
  <data key="d0">Dilithium</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Post-quantum digital signature scheme evaluated by Abbas et al. and used in hybrid form with ECDSA by Alsubai et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Post-quantum digital signature scheme, referred to together with ML-DSA as ML-DSA/Dilithium.&lt;SEP&gt;Pre-standardization post-quantum signature variants. The paper chose not to use them in favor of ML-DSA-65.&lt;SEP&gt;Post-quantum digital signature scheme on which a blockchain transaction model [23] is based.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502202</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Discrete Event Simulation">
  <data key="d0">Discrete Event Simulation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Simulation technique used by Zhukabayeva et al. to evaluate a Fabric-based healthcare framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulation approach used by Zhukabayeva et al. instead of a real Fabric deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulation method used to evaluate Hyperledger Fabric-based post-quantum cryptography for healthcare [27].</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-040</data>
  <data key="d4">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
