<node id="Open Quantum Safe Project">
  <data key="d0">Open Quantum Safe Project</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Project for post-quantum key exchange on the internet, described by Stebila and Mosca (SAC 2016).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Signing-Service High Availability">
  <data key="d0">Signing-Service High Availability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Resilience of the signing-service tier under partial infrastructure failures. Proposed future work covers automatic failover after instance loss, health-aware load balancing, shared-storage failure and service restart/recovery behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Six-Scenario Benchmark Suite">
  <data key="d0">Six-Scenario Benchmark Suite</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Benchmark suite used for the primary ML-DSA-65 evaluation. It covers stress, payload variation, resource consumption and storage conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Signature Aggregation">
  <data key="d0">Signature Aggregation</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage optimization strategy proposed for future work to reduce ledger growth, alongside compact encoding and selective audit trails.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Off-Chain Storage With On-Chain Commitments">
  <data key="d0">Off-Chain Storage With On-Chain Commitments</data>
  <data key="d1">methodology</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage optimization strategy proposed for future work to reduce ledger growth while preserving post-quantum auditability.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Post-Quantum Auditability">
  <data key="d0">Post-Quantum Auditability</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ability to audit ledger records with post-quantum security guarantees. Storage optimization strategies must preserve it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-038</data>
  <data key="d4">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791502219</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
