<edge source="Machine Learning for Industrial Manufacturing: A Case Study" target="Ref [8] Multi-Agent System and AHP for Machine Selection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">In [8], researchers used a multi-agent system and Analytical Hierarchy Process (AHP) to select the best machine for manufacturing orders based on factors like quality, time, and cost.</data>
  <data key="d9">cites,related work</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">978-3-031-75329-9_31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791420960</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Machine Learning for Industrial Manufacturing: A Case Study" target="Ref [9] Fuzzy TOPSIS Machine Selection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ref [9] applied Fuzzy TOPSIS to select among 14 electrical molding machines, incorporating factors like rate of return, risk investment, and environmental impact.</data>
  <data key="d9">cites,related work</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">978-3-031-75329-9_31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791420960</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Machine Learning for Industrial Manufacturing: A Case Study" target="Ref [10] Taguchi and FAHP with TOPSIS">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Ref [10] used Taguchi and fuzzy analytic hierarchy process (FAHP) with TOPSIS to determine the best moldability index and alternatives for injected parts in injection molding.</data>
  <data key="d9">cites,related work</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-5f0352d149ce07cb8b4fdf8db0076c7d-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">978-3-031-75329-9_31.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791420960</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Machine Learning for Industrial Manufacturing: A Case Study" target="Ref [11] Classical Machine Selection Methods">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Firstly, existing approaches primarily rely on classical methods like TOPSIS, AHP, and others for decision-making in machine selection [11].</data>
  <data key="d9">cites,literature gap</data>
