<edge source="TOPSIS" target="Euclidean Distance">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">TOPSIS uses Euclidean distance for normalization and for the distances to the ideal solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The first step in the TOPSIS method involves normalizing the decision matrix presented in Table5, utilizing the Euclidean distance as shown in (21).&lt;SEP&gt;TOPSIS computes the Euclidean distance between each alternative and both the ideal and anti-ideal solutions.</data>
