<edge source="F1-Score" target="This Paper">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between F1-Score and This Paper describes the paper's use of the F1-score as a core performance metric for evaluating and comparing its models. The F1-score is computed alongside accuracy, precision, and recall to assess the classification models, and it serves as a key basis for the paper's performance comparison.

In one context, the paper reports F1-scores per class for each model, specifically measuring how well the models identify churn and non-churn customers. This per-class reporting allows a more detailed assessment of performance on each customer category, which matters in churn prediction, where the two classes may be imbalanced.

In another context, the F1-score is used to quantify the effect of applying a Canny filter: the F1-score rose from 97.03% to 99.72% when the filter was applied. This indicates that the Canny edge-detection preprocessing substantially improved classification performance.

The churn-prediction and Canny-filter findings belong to different application domains, customer analytics and image-based classification. They may therefore come from distinct works that are each referred to as "This Paper," although in every case the F1-score serves as a principal evaluation metric.</data>
