<edge source="Machine Selection" target="This Paper">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Machine Selection and This Paper is that machine selection is the central problem the paper (also called the article) sets out to solve. The work focuses on selecting the best, or optimal, machine from a set of competing alternatives. The specific candidates it evaluates are the ARB250T, ARB200T and HAIT320T machines.

Methodologically, the paper treats machine selection as a multi-criteria classification problem. It applies weighted criteria to judge which machine is best, using these weights to both rank the machine alternatives and select the optimal one. The ranking organizes the alternatives in order of suitability, which supports a clear and justified final selection.

The paper also places the machine selection problem in a practical industrial setting, with the goal of identifying the optimal machine for production schedules. The selection outcome is therefore intended to support operational planning and production efficiency, not just to serve as a theoretical exercise.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,multi-criteria decision</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-467b87e0a1eaa0377cb70477245debc3-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d11">document.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791426515</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
