<edge source="Bayesian Network" target="This Paper">
  <data key="d7">18.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Bayesian Network and This Paper describes how "This Paper" uses Bayesian Networks (BNs) as its central method for modeling, analysis, and prediction. The BN is a core component of the proposed model and is integrated into the paper's system model as an expert-driven network. The descriptions appear to refer to several distinct works that share the generic label "This Paper," each applying Bayesian Networks to a different domain.

In the context of Vehicular Ad Hoc Networks (VANET), the paper builds a Bayesian Network to model risk analysis of Quality of Service (QoS) and to predict QoS. The BN is used to predict problems that disturb network functioning, and the study defines the causal architecture of the Bayesian model for QoS risks. Building on this model, the paper proposes a series of steps for analyzing QoS in VANET. It also applies a BN inference system across three scenarios to evaluate network behavior under different conditions.

In the context of road safety, the paper uses Bayesian networks for risk prediction, modeling the risk of road accident occurrence and forecasting its likelihood. It constructs a three-level Bayesian Network architecture for accident occurrence and defines the states of the network's nodes using linguistic values, presented in Table III. The network graph's conditional probabilities are calculated with Fuzzy Logic, and these fuzzy-generated probabilities are used to assess the likelihood of accidents.

In a separate context, the paper builds Bayesian networks to model employee burnout. This shows that the methodology is also applied to occupational and human-factor risks.

Across these applications, This Paper consistently constructs a Bayesian network architecture as its core analytical tool. It often grounds the network in expert knowledge and fuzzy reasoning to capture causal dependencies and estimate the probability of adverse outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d9">QoS analysis,QoS prediction,accident causal model,accident probability modeling,graph model,proposes,risk modeling,risk modelling,risk prediction,road accident risk,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db5423cfc6b0239a805a929baa02d1e9-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bed29169806bd2571a0eff67abe0e549-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a503621d914a716d7d3a5232c23b6bc6-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7716e61d153c4d281900275dc536a626-chunk-008</data>
