<edge source="Scalability" target="This Paper">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Scalability and This Paper concerns how the paper treats scalability as both an open research problem and a central evaluation criterion. The paper identifies blockchain scalability as an unresolved issue that limits the practical adoption of blockchain technologies. In response, it investigates scalability challenges in Hyperledger Fabric, focusing on how system behavior changes as the number of peers in the network grows.

To evaluate scalability, the study varies the number of peers per organization and measures the effect on performance. It finds that Hyperledger Fabric handles up to 4 peers per organization without significant degradation, but that scaling beyond 4 peers introduces substantial latency. These results give the paper practical insight into Fabric's scalability limits and into strategies for optimizing its performance. The paper also states that its proposed architecture is designed to support scalability.

The paper further assesses scalability at the level of its proposed framework. It conducts additional case studies across different application domains to test the framework's scalability and general applicability. The results reported in Table 7 confirm that the framework remains scalable and efficient across multiple domains and varying levels of complexity.

These descriptions may come from more than one study sharing the label "This Paper": one focused on peer-level scalability in Hyperledger Fabric, and another on cross-domain framework evaluation. Taken together, they show scalability treated both as a known limitation of blockchain systems and as a property the proposed approach is shown to address.</data>
  <data key="d9">additional case studies,addresses,blockchain scalability,efficiency,open issue,peer scaling</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26549e3ff493405b55b221c1d804516e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8a68f6918fb713b374b6980cb85c4169-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d11">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;poster_nihad.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Vol.13.No.7.13.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791501904</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
