<edge source="International Journal of Advanced Computer Science and Applications" target="This Paper">
  <data key="d7">19.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between the International Journal of Advanced Computer Science and Applications (IJACSA) and This Paper is one of publication: the journal is the venue in which the paper or article appears. The descriptions give two different publication details. Because "This Paper" is a generic label, these most likely refer to two distinct articles from different source documents, not conflicting accounts of one work.

In the first case, This Paper is published in IJACSA Volume 16, Issue No. 2, released in 2025. Several descriptions confirm this placement, referring to the work as "the paper," "the article," or "the article being read."

In the second case, This Paper appears in IJACSA Volume 15, Issue No. 7, released in 2024. One description calls this work "the citing article," which suggests it cites other research within its own source document.

In both cases, IJACSA is the peer-reviewed journal through which the respective work was made available to the academic community.</data>
  <data key="d9">published_in</data>
