<edge source="This Paper" target="Scopus">
  <data key="d7">15.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Scopus and This Paper is that Scopus is the bibliographic database from which the study's data were drawn. Because "This Paper" is a generic label, the descriptions appear to refer to several different studies that used Scopus in different ways. This explains the differences in document counts, time spans, and whether other databases were also used.

In several cases, Scopus was the sole data source. The authors used only the Scopus database, extracting their dataset exclusively from it. They justified this choice by Scopus's broader coverage and by the wish to avoid duplicated data that could arise from merging multiple databases. The retrieved records were exported and saved in CSV format for further processing and analysis.

The descriptions report different dataset sizes and time spans. In one instance, This Paper retrieved 2,088 documents from Scopus. Another analysis is based on 4,015 documents published in the Scopus database over a 35-year period. A further study collected 132 articles from Scopus covering 2019 to 2023. Scopus was also used to examine yearly publication trends on Explainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI), and specifically XAI in e-commerce, from 2018 to 2023.

Other descriptions present Scopus as one of several sources rather than the only one. In one case, the bibliometric data supporting the study's findings came from both Scopus and Web of Science. In another, the study merged data from Scopus, Web of Science (WoS), and PubMed. These accounts contrast with the statements that only Scopus was used, which supports the view that they describe separate studies with different data collection strategies. In all of them, Scopus remains a central data source for the research.&lt;SEP&gt;Scopus is one of the four databases selected.&lt;SEP&gt;The systematic review analyzes papers published across Scopus.&lt;SEP&gt;Scopus was one of the four databases used to collect the 30 analyzed papers.&lt;SEP&gt;Relevant papers were drawn from Scopus.</data>
  <data key="d9">bibliometric analysis,bibliometric data,data source,database selection,literature source,related_to,uses_dataset</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3b6de35b4fc6654223999680ef1082ec-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d11">25293-55764-1-PB.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_AIapplicationinmarketanalysis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791425922</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
