<edge source="This Paper" target="Feature Selection">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">This Paper performs a comprehensive bibliometric analysis of the feature selection literature spanning the past decade.&lt;SEP&gt;Feature selection is a key step of This Paper's methodology.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper performs feature selection on each dataset.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper investigates the impact of feature selection on Random Forest classifier performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The study investigated the impact of feature selection on the performance of Random Forest classifiers.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper underscores the importance of appropriate feature selection for optimal model performance.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,bibliometric study,impact study,performance impact</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d11">A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423777</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="This Paper" target="Bibliometric Analysis">
  <data key="d7">13.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Bibliometric Analysis and This Paper is mainly that the paper uses bibliometric analysis (BA) as its core method to map the intellectual structure of its research field. The paper also sets out the BA methodology and its process, illustrated in Fig. 1, and explains what BA is and how and why it is done, illustrated in Fig. 2. Its analysis has both quantitative and qualitative parts and covers a corpus of 1,296 papers.

In most descriptions, the paper's bibliometric analysis is about where Human Resource Management (HRM) meets Artificial Intelligence (AI) and other new technologies. The analysis covers 2019 to 2023 and aims to visualize how the HRM and AI literature has developed. It looks at research output by country, citation patterns, collaboration networks, and the main themes in HR and AI research.

One description gives a different focus: a comprehensive bibliometric analysis of AI in oncology over the past five years. This most likely refers to a separate paper, also labeled "This Paper," that applies the same method to a different field. In that case, bibliometric analysis is again the main tool for mapping a body of AI-related research, here in cancer medicine rather than HRM.&lt;SEP&gt;The study is a bibliometric analysis of papers on AI and market analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The study presents the results of a bibliometric analysis of the publications.&lt;SEP&gt;This Paper conducts a bibliometric analysis of AI in market analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper uses bibliometric analysis of affiliations, countries and authors.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper conducts a bibliometric study of AI applications in market analysis.</data>
  <data key="d9">research methodology,review methodology,scientometrics,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7f659f89172b81a0adff01963801bdcb-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d11">A_bibliometric_analysis_of_feature_selection_techn.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;ACS_10_THEPOTENTIALOFARTIFICIALINTELLIGENCEINHUMANRESOURCEMANAGEMENT.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_25_66701.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_AIapplicationinmarketanalysis.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423342</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="This Paper" target="Web of Science">
  <data key="d7">10.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between This Paper and Web of Science (WoS) describes how Web of Science figures in the data collection methods of one or more studies all labeled "This Paper." The descriptions conflict: some say WoS was actively used and others say it was deliberately excluded. This most likely means several distinct studies share the generic name "This Paper," so each usage is summarized separately below.

In several instances, This Paper used Web of Science as a primary data source for bibliometric analysis. One study retrieved 1,328 documents from Web of Science and exported the records as plain text. Another bibliometric study based its findings on data from both the Scopus and Web of Science databases. A further study combined WoS with Scopus and PubMed into a single merged dataset. More generally, Web of Science is described as a data source for the study.

In the context of a systematic review, Web of Science was one of four databases selected for the literature search. This review analyzed papers published across these databases, and Web of Science contributed to the collection of the 30 papers ultimately analyzed.

In contrast, at least one instance of This Paper considered Web of Science but chose not to use it, opting for Scopus instead. The authors justified this choice by citing Scopus's broader coverage and the need to avoid duplicated data across databases. This relationship was clarified to correct an earlier "compares_with" label, because no benchmarking or formal comparison between the two databases took place; Web of Science was simply weighed as an option and set aside.

Taken together, Web of Science serves as an important scholarly database for literature retrieval in these works, either as a direct source of records or as a considered alternative to Scopus.</data>
  <data key="d9">bibliometric data,data source,database selection,excluded database,literature source,related_to,uses_dataset</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7b9912ddab6105f96b8cd8cb51d46ee9-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-860e34bf4e631717387a6fc6684e1154-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010</data>
