<edge source="This Paper" target="Sensitivity Analysis">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Sensitivity Analysis and This Paper describes how the paper uses sensitivity analysis to test the robustness of its methodology and the rankings it produces. Together with a comparison against other methods, sensitivity analysis forms the final phase of the study's approach. Its purpose is to confirm that the rankings are stable and reliable.

The paper focuses on how the results respond to changes in the highly weighted criteria. Specifically, it evaluates the effect of altering the values of these dominant criteria on the outcomes. To do this, it builds three scenarios that vary the scrap rate and the breakdown rate. These scenarios serve as the sensitivity analysis used to validate the rankings. One description refers to the second varied criterion as "cost breakdown" rather than "breakdown rate," but this most likely refers to the same breakdown-related criterion.

The paper also acknowledges that its sensitivity analysis is limited to scrap rate and breakdown. It proposes extending the analysis to other criteria in future work to further strengthen the robustness assessment.</data>
  <data key="d9">robustness,scenarios,uses_method,validation</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d11">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf&lt;SEP&gt;IJE_Volume38_Issue2_Pages488-502_Versionfinale.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791426494</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="This Paper" target="Online Retail Supplier Evaluation Criteria">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The research introduces a new set of evaluation criteria designed for the online retail sector, focusing on financial stability, service quality and operational efficiency.</data>
