<edge source="This Paper" target="DeepLabV3+">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between DeepLabV3+ and This Paper centers on the paper's use of DeepLabV3+ as the core semantic segmentation model for extracting road networks from satellite imagery. The study uses DeepLabV3+ to perform pixel-level segmentation that identifies road pixels, which allows the road network structures in the images to be delineated.

In the paper's implementation, DeepLabV3+ is configured with a ResNet-50 (ResNet50) backbone that serves as the encoder for feature extraction. The architecture includes Atrous Spatial Pyramid Pooling (ASPP), which captures multi-scale contextual information, and the model is trained with Dice Loss, a loss function well suited to segmentation tasks with class imbalance, such as thin road structures against large background areas.

Within the paper's overall methodology, DeepLabV3+ makes up the segmentation stage of a multi-step pipeline. It runs after an initial classification step, and only the image tiles kept by that classification are passed to DeepLabV3+ for road segmentation. This two-stage design lets the segmentation model concentrate on relevant regions of the satellite imagery.</data>
  <data key="d9">road segmentation,segmentation,semantic segmentation,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d11">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791422810</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
