<edge source="This Paper" target="VGG16">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between This Paper and VGG16 centers on the paper's use of the VGG16 convolutional neural network for image-level road-presence classification in satellite imagery. The study applies transfer learning, taking a VGG16 model pre-trained on ImageNet and fine-tuning it for binary classification: determining whether a satellite image or tile contains a road.

Within the paper's workflow, VGG16 serves as a filtering stage. It identifies road-positive tiles and screens out non-road images, so that only relevant satellite images proceed to later analysis.

The paper also evaluates VGG16 against alternative architectures, notably VGG19. VGG16 outperformed VGG19 and proved superior at identifying roads, which establishes it as the preferred model for the road-presence classification task in this research.</data>
  <data key="d9">classification,fine-tuning,image classification,road presence classification,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d11">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791422825</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
