<edge source="This Paper" target="Generative Adversarial Networks">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) and This Paper is central, as GANs are the primary subject of the review. The paper places GANs among the modern deep learning strategies that frame its work. It reviews both theoretical and empirical studies on GANs, giving a broad view of their foundations and practical performance. It also cites the foundational GAN work by Goodfellow et al. (2014), which appears as reference 5 in its reference list.

A major part of the paper is its survey of GAN variants and their applications, including an overview of 16 important GAN variants. It focuses on financial data, systematically reviewing GAN architectures designed for financial applications. This covers how GANs have been used in financial markets, in financial modeling, and specifically in financial data generation and market modeling. The paper therefore serves as a structured synthesis of GAN methods, both in general and as applied to finance.</data>
  <data key="d9">GAN variants,addresses,cites,overview of variants,reference list,related work,related_to,review subject,survey,systematic review</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4e26e4b19a21a1bf5f3daec0bcb0830c-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ed200d7fb9035c5336533a6730c8671b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d11">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;acs_AIapplicationinmarketanalysis.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;GANsinsyntheticfinancialdata_donalsonwilson_versionpublie.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791425884</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="This Paper" target="Reference (23)">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">VGG16 is particularly well-suited for tasks with constrained computational resources, yet it maintains a high level of accuracy in image classification tasks (23).&lt;SEP&gt;Nowadays, there is no theoretical framework to identify these parameters to obtain a specific performance of the model; hence, it requires iterative training and parameter adjustment to minimize the chosen quality metric until an optimal model is identified (23).</data>
  <data key="d9">VGG16,cites,hyperparameter selection</data>
