  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">By systematically altering the orientation, perspective, and scale of the input images, these augmentations expose the model to a diverse range of transformations, mirroring real-world variations in satellite imagery (29).&lt;SEP&gt;CEGEN (Conditional Euler Generator) is identified as the best-performing GAN, excelling in replicating marginals, correlations, and consistency across datasets, while TGAN (Time Series Generative Adversarial Network) (29) offers more generality.</data>
