<edge source="This Paper" target="LSTM">
  <data key="d7">14.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) and This Paper centers on the paper's use of the LSTM neural network for daily sales forecasting. The paper describes the LSTM architecture and applies it to model sales time series. The specific configuration has three hidden layers of 50 neurons each.

LSTM plays a dual role in the study. First, it is a core component of the paper's proposed hybrid model, where it captures complex patterns in the sales data. Within this hybrid framework, LSTM is applied first to model the sales time series. Its predictions are then used to derive a residuals series, which the other parts of the hybrid model process further.

Second, the paper uses LSTM as a standalone model for comparison. It serves as a standard baseline forecasting model and is evaluated alongside other time series models. This lets the study measure the performance of the hybrid approach against LSTM on its own.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper describes the LSTM cell's gates and equations.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper uses an LSTM model to model the injection molding function and predict the Melt Cushion parameter.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper uses an LSTM network to predict the next Melt Cushion value.</data>
  <data key="d9">baseline,comparative analysis,prediction,recurrent network,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b861a9335e2f8bb52dad6132b0acac1d-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d11">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;CIST_171Edited_FV.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423777</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="This Paper" target="SARIMA">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between SARIMA and This Paper centers on the paper's extensive use of the Box-Jenkins Seasonal Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average (SARIMA) model, which serves two roles in the study. The paper describes the SARIMA methodology and applies it to daily sales forecasting, using it chiefly to capture linear trends and seasonal patterns in the data.

First, SARIMA is a core component of the paper's hybrid forecasting model. Within this framework, SARIMA is applied to the residuals of the LSTM model, modeling the residual errors that the neural network leaves behind. To support this approach, the paper fits SARIMA models to both the original sales series and the residuals series.

Second, the paper uses SARIMA as a standalone standard baseline forecasting model. In this role, it serves as a benchmark among the time series models compared in the study, against which the performance of the hybrid model and other approaches is evaluated.</data>
  <data key="d9">baseline,comparative analysis,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d11">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423613</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="This Paper" target="Holt-Winters Exponential Smoothing">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The paper uses Holt-Winters within the hybrid model and also as a standalone comparison model.</data>
  <data key="d9">baseline,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-001</data>
