<edge source="This Paper" target="Ref. 7">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">After verifying stationarity, the determination of model parameters proceeds by examining the Auto-Correlation Function (ACF)... and the Partial Auto-Correlation Function (PACF)... (7). For optimal predictive accuracy, model selection can be automated by identifying its hyperparameters (p, d, q, P, D, Q) that minimize statistical criteria (7), such as the Akaike Information Criterion (AIC) or the Bayesian Information Criterion (BIC).</data>
  <data key="d9">cites,model selection,parameter identification</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-285b07b80137f799fd1205a24fb418c4-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d11">AHybridApproachforSalesForecastingCombiningDeepLearningandTimeSeries.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423618</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="This Paper" target="Ref. 29">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Exponential smoothing serves as a prediction method for univariate time series data, focusing on forecasting future values by giving more significance to recent observations through exponentially diminishing weights on older data (29, 30).</data>
