<edge source="This Paper" target="Endorsement Policy">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Campaign C1 compares the OR and AND endorsement policies under a baseline configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;This Paper investigates how endorsement policies interact with other parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;This Paper identifies endorsement policy as driving a large share of overhead on the critical path.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper studies how the choice of endorsement policy affects latency and throughput at scale.&lt;SEP&gt;This Paper finds endorsement policy to be a dominant driver of performance.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper finds endorsement policy to be a dominant driver of performance across all baseline conditions.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,campaign C1,configuration parameter,critical path overhead,dominant performance driver,performance driver,performance impact</data>
