<edge source="This Paper" target="Block Size">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Block Size and This Paper centers on the paper's systematic study of how block size affects system performance. This Paper examines block size as a key configuration parameter and evaluates its impact on latency and throughput. The experiments, along with the associated figure data, measure performance at three block sizes: 50, 100 and 200 transactions per block.

These block-size experiments are organized as Campaign C2. In this campaign, the block size is varied across the three values while the other settings stay fixed: 4 peers per organization and the OR endorsement policy. The paper also analyzes performance across combinations of block size and timeout settings, which places the block-size results within a broader parameter study.

Based on this evaluation, This Paper finds that a block size of 100 transactions gives the best performance among the tested settings. It quantifies the effect of block size on performance and recommends 100 transactions per block.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,campaign C2,configuration parameter,configuration tuning,evaluation,experimental parameter,ordering configuration,ordering layer,parameter study,parameter tuning,performance tuning</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d11">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791425250</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
