<edge source="This Paper" target="OR Endorsement Policy">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between the OR Endorsement Policy and This Paper centers on the paper's experimental evaluation and eventual recommendation of the policy. This Paper evaluates the OR endorsement policy and uses it in campaign C2 of its experiments. Scalability tests were conducted under this policy. Latency and throughput were measured for each peer configuration to assess how performance changes as the number of peers varies.

Based on these evaluations, This Paper finds that the OR endorsement policy outperforms the AND endorsement policy, offering lower latency and higher throughput. The paper therefore recommends using an OR policy whenever the application logic allows it, and it includes the OR endorsement policy as part of its recommended default configuration.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,endorsement policy,evaluation,experimental condition,performance evaluation,recommendation,recommended configuration,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d11">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791425268</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="This Paper" target="AND Endorsement Policy">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between the AND Endorsement Policy and This Paper is one of performance evaluation. This Paper examines the AND endorsement policy as the stricter baseline configuration and measures its latency and throughput.

The evaluation includes scalability tests that vary the number of peers per organization, testing configurations of 4, 6, and 8 peers. Latency and throughput are measured for each peer configuration, which shows how the policy behaves as the network grows.

Based on these results, This Paper concludes that the AND endorsement policy is less suited for larger networks. Its strict endorsement requirements make it harder to scale as the number of peers increases.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,endorsement policy,evaluation,experimental condition,performance evaluation,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d11">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791425276</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
