<edge source="This Paper" target="P95 Latency">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between P95 Latency and This Paper reflects the paper's use of 95th-percentile latency as a core performance metric throughout its experimental evaluation. The paper measures and reports P95 latency, expressed in milliseconds, for each evaluated configuration, including every combination of block size and timeout setting examined in the study.

P95 latency is used alongside P50 and P99 latency to assess the performance of different configurations and the scalability of the system under study. Beyond reporting absolute values, the paper also tracks P95 latency degradation across configurations to show how performance changes as parameters vary.

These results appear in several parts of the paper. P95 latency is presented in its experimental figures, notably the Sensitivity and Performance Degradation Analysis figure, which reports both P95 latency and P95 degradation. The metric is also reported in Table 5.</data>
  <data key="d9">evaluation metric,metric,performance evaluation,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d11">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791425308</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
