<edge source="This Paper" target="AHP-TOPSIS">
  <data key="d7">3.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The proposed methodology is founded on a fusion of AHP and TOPSIS, segmented into five steps.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper discusses the advantages of the combined AHP-TOPSIS method for minimizing decision errors and uncertainties.&lt;SEP&gt;It presents a model that combines the Analytic Hierarchy Process to assess the weights of five main criteria and eleven sub criteria, which are subsequently utilized in the Technique for Order of Preference by Similarity to Ideal Solution method to select the best option among the three presented machines.</data>
  <data key="d9">decision model,hybrid MCDM,machine selection,proposes,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-690b1785f1cbb35b37a4dcdbae1984e4-chunk-013</data>
