<edge source="This Paper" target="Smart Contract">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between the Smart Contract and This Paper is central: the mechanism the paper proposes is implemented as an Ethereum smart contract. The smart contract is the core component through which the paper's device registration and authentication scheme operates, and the mechanism depends on it for both initialization and registration.

Within this design, the smart contract carries out several key functions. It handles system initialization, creates admins and verifies admin status. It also computes and creates the access tokens used in the scheme, verifies and validates device registrations, and manages the authentication process. It also emits events that record or signal relevant actions within the system.

For development and evaluation, the paper's smart contracts were compiled and deployed using the Remix IDE and Hardhat, and tested on Ganache-CLI, a local Ethereum blockchain environment. This toolchain allowed the authors to implement and validate the proposed registration and authentication mechanism in a controlled blockchain setting.</data>
  <data key="d9">access tokens,addresses,implementation,proposes,registration and authentication logic,registration logic,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d11">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791466880</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
