<edge source="This Paper" target="Ref [13]">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">This fusion of retrieval and generation delivers results that are inaccessible by either component in isolation, positioning RAG as a major advancement in generative models [13], [30].&lt;SEP&gt;Although they are designed for tasks such as machine translation, summarization, and conversational interactions, RAG models can also be used for information retrieval [13].&lt;SEP&gt;Some authors [13] used roadside units (RSUs) to collect and transmit traffic data via Dijkstra's dedicated short-range communication protocol (DDSRC).</data>
  <data key="d9">RAG,cites,information retrieval,related work</data>
