  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">This concept was later adapted by Shannon in 1948 [7], to measure uncertainty in information sources, becoming known as information entropy [24].&lt;SEP&gt;"The entropy weight method assesses a criterion's significance and weight by calculating its information entropy, which is based on the variation of the initial data matrix, through several steps [24], [42]." Reference [24] is also cited for information entropy and for combining AHP/FAHP with entropy (equation 20).</data>
