<edge source="Reference [8]" target="Comprehensive Framework for Supplier Selection">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The supplier selection process generally consists of two main phases: first, assigning weights to criteria to establish their importance, which can be achieved through subjective approaches such as Decision-Making Trial and Evaluation Laboratory (DEMATEL)[4], Simple Multi-Attribute Rating Technique (SMART) [5], and Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) [6], to quantify their relevance using judgments and experts' opinions, or objective methods like entropy [7], and Criteria Importance Through Inter-criteria Correlation (CRITIC) [8], to determine weights based on data variability without relying on subjective judgments.</data>
  <data key="d9">cites,objective weighting</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-54e26c32a6c6377d00b93d14e0ea3092-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d11">A_Comprehensive_Framework_for_Supplier_Selection_Using_Subjective_Objective_and_Hybrid_Multi-Criteria_Decision-Making_Techniques_With_Sensitivity_Analysis_F (1).pdf</data>
