<edge source="VGG19" target="VGG16">
  <data key="d7">9.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between VGG16 and VGG19 is a comparison of two closely related convolutional neural network architectures evaluated on insect classification. The two models share the same foundational design. VGG19 extends VGG16 by adding three supplementary convolutional layers, and this added depth is the primary architectural difference between them. The extra depth lets VGG19 capture finer details than VGG16, but it also demands more computation and longer training times.

Despite its greater depth, VGG19 did not outperform VGG16 in this study. VGG16 consistently achieved better accuracy and lower loss on both the training and validation sets. It reached 99.29% training accuracy and 99.09% validation accuracy (0.9909), while VGG19 reached a validation accuracy of 0.9136.

Overall, the results suggest that the added depth and representational capacity of VGG19 brought no performance advantage for this insect classification task. The shallower and computationally lighter VGG16 proved to be the more effective model.</data>
  <data key="d9">accuracy,architectural depth,classification accuracy,classification performance,compares_with,computational cost,deeper architecture,extends</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a32e5ba6e7447add4fce7dbb90abe96-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d11">A_Deep_Learning_Pipeline_for_Accurate_Road_Detecti.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791422786</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
