<edge source="Feature Selection and Classification Performance: A Multi-Dataset Comparative Analysis Using Boruta Algorithm and Random Forest" target="Kursa et al. [14] (Boruta)">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Boruta algorithm is particularly effective for feature selection [8], [9], [10], [11], [12], [13]. Developed by Miron B. Kursa et al in [14], Boruta uses a wrapper method to assess feature importance by comparing them to random noise features [22].</data>
  <data key="d9">algorithm origin,cites</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423768</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Feature Selection and Classification Performance: A Multi-Dataset Comparative Analysis Using Boruta Algorithm and Random Forest" target="Dataset 1">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The paper evaluates Dataset 1 with full and reduced feature sets; feature selection improved accuracy by 1.06% and F1-score by 3.36%.</data>
  <data key="d9">evaluation,uses_dataset</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423768</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Feature Selection and Classification Performance: A Multi-Dataset Comparative Analysis Using Boruta Algorithm and Random Forest" target="Dataset 2">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The paper evaluates Dataset 2 with full and reduced feature sets; feature selection improved accuracy by 0.46% and F1-score by 5.42%.</data>
  <data key="d9">evaluation,uses_dataset</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423768</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Feature Selection and Classification Performance: A Multi-Dataset Comparative Analysis Using Boruta Algorithm and Random Forest" target="Dataset 3">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The paper evaluates Dataset 3, which showed no significant change with feature selection.</data>
  <data key="d9">evaluation,uses_dataset</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423768</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Feature Selection and Classification Performance: A Multi-Dataset Comparative Analysis Using Boruta Algorithm and Random Forest" target="Boruta enhances classification performance when irrelevant features are present">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The paper's results confirm that Boruta enhances classification performance, especially when irrelevant features are present, with minimal benefit when all features are relevant.</data>
  <data key="d9">main finding,proposes</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-ed5a32c2476eb625d3377722542a5d95-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">CIST_174.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791423768</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
