<edge source="Hyperledger Fabric" target="ECDSA">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fabric relies extensively on ECDSA to authenticate clients, endorse proposals, validate identities, and secure channels.&lt;SEP&gt;Fabric endorsers sign execution results with their own ECDSA keys.&lt;SEP&gt;ECDSA is the native signature scheme of Hyperledger Fabric.&lt;SEP&gt;Fabric uses ECDSA for identity management, endorsement signing, and transaction validation.&lt;SEP&gt;Fabric's endorsement and validation pipeline operates with ECDSA.&lt;SEP&gt;Fabric's native endorsements use ECDSA, which remains classical.</data>
  <data key="d9">dependency,endorsement signing,endorsement validation,native cryptography,native endorsements,native signature,related_to,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-034</data>
  <data key="d11">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791502235</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hyperledger Fabric" target="PQFabric">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">PQFabric integrates hybrid post-quantum mechanisms into Fabric's cryptographic stack.&lt;SEP&gt;PQFabric modifies Fabric cryptographic components to support post-quantum mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Integrates PQC into Fabric by modifying its cryptographic layer.&lt;SEP&gt;PQFabric integrates post-quantum mechanisms into Fabric's cryptographic and credential-processing stack. This requires compatible cryptographic software and credential changes.</data>
