<edge source="Blockchain" target="Decentralized Authentication Mechanism">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The mechanism is built on blockchain technology.&lt;SEP&gt;The proposed decentralized authentication mechanism is built on the blockchain concept.&lt;SEP&gt;The mechanism stores device tokens on the blockchain, and admin nodes validate its transactions.&lt;SEP&gt;The mechanism relies on the distributed nature and cryptographic characteristics of blockchain.</data>
  <data key="d9">based on,built on,decentralization,related_to,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d11">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791466863</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blockchain" target="Decentralized Authentication Mechanism for Mobile Ad hoc Networks">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The mechanism is based on the concept of the blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper proposes and evaluates a blockchain-based authentication mechanism for MANET nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;The article reviews blockchain technology as a basis for decentralized authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;The proposed mechanism is a distributed authentication mechanism based on blockchain.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper uses a blockchain to store device tokens and validate transactions, with SHA-256 and ECC as cryptographic proof for data integrity and authentication.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,decentralized authentication,decentralized ledger,distributed authentication,proposes,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d11">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791466863</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blockchain" target="Access Control">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Blockchain is described as well suited for MANET authentication and access control services.&lt;SEP&gt;Blockchain is well suited for MANET access control services because of its decentralization and cryptographic features.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d11">InfocomJ_2022_3_4_Khalfaoui.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791466863</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Blockchain" target="Mobile Ad Hoc Network">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Security experts concentrate on blockchain to improve MANET authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;Blockchain lets MANET avoid dependence on a central trusted authority that is a single point of failure.</data>
  <data key="d9">decentralization,related_to,security solution</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-aaf2c8f641e35f769c72ec556a34ec4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ccc87fb659a572e9c9db17272d2f6955-chunk-002</data>
