<edge source="OR Endorsement Policy" target="AND Endorsement Policy">
  <data key="d7">11.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between the AND Endorsement Policy and the OR Endorsement Policy is a comparison of how each policy affects transaction latency and throughput. The two policies are evaluated side by side in Figures 2 and 3 and Table 2. They are also compared in the scalability analysis, where Figure 10 shows latency and throughput as the number of peers per organization varies.

Across all evaluations, the OR Endorsement Policy outperforms the AND Endorsement Policy on both metrics. OR achieves lower latency and roughly double the throughput, at about 1.8 transactions per second versus 0.9 for AND. Compared with OR, the AND policy increases latency by about 105% at the 50th percentile (P50), 148% at P95, and 151% at P99.

The performance gap comes from structural differences between the two policies. Under AND, all peers must endorse and validate transactions, which increases coordination and validation work and lowers throughput. The OR policy requires a smaller endorsement set, which reduces this overhead. As a result, it consistently lowers latency and raises throughput relative to AND across the tested configurations.</data>
  <data key="d9">campaign C1,compares_with,latency,performance comparison,policy comparison,scalability,throughput</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-020</data>
  <data key="d11">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791425216</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="OR Endorsement Policy" target="Latency">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The OR policy achieved roughly half the latency of the AND policy, with a P50 of 518 ms versus 1062 ms.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 8 measures latency against the number of peers per organization under the OR endorsement policy.&lt;SEP&gt;The OR policy consistently lowers latency.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 10(a) plots P50 latency for the OR policy across 4, 6 and 8 peers per organization.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,latency reduction,measured performance,performance measurement,performance result,related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d11">Configuration_Driven_Performance_Analysis_of_Hyper.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791425268</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="AND Endorsement Policy" target="Latency">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">AND adds coordination time and validation work on the critical path, which increases latency.&lt;SEP&gt;The AND policy makes the latency increase worse. With 6 peers per organization, P50 latency is 1141 ms and P99 latency is 2163 ms.&lt;SEP&gt;Panel (b) of Figure 8 reports latency in milliseconds (up to 3000 ms) at the P50, P95 and P99 percentiles under the AND endorsement policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 10(a) plots P50 latency for the AND policy across 4, 6 and 8 peers per organization.</data>
  <data key="d9">coordination overhead,full consensus delay,measured performance,performance measurement,related_to</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dfeceae54500e0aef047f46e66c1451b-chunk-018</data>
