<edge source="ECDSA" target="Hybrid Post-Quantum Signatures for Hyperledger Fabric">
  <data key="d7">17.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relationship between ECDSA and Hybrid Post-Quantum Signatures for Hyperledger Fabric centers on ECDSA's dual role in the work: it is the classical component of the hybrid signature scheme and the primary baseline for evaluation. As the signature scheme native to Hyperledger Fabric, ECDSA is the established classical reference against which the post-quantum enhancements are measured.

Within the hybrid architecture, ECDSA is combined with the post-quantum algorithm ML-DSA-65. The design deliberately preserves Fabric's existing cryptographic infrastructure. Fabric's endorsement and validation pipeline continues to run on ECDSA, and the hybrid design relies on ECDSA-based endorsements produced by Fabric peers. Fabric-native ECDSA signatures stay in transaction envelopes and endorsement metadata, so the native endorsements remain classical while the post-quantum layer is added alongside them.

For performance evaluation, the paper compares ECDSA with both ML-DSA and the hybrid signature configuration. The central benchmark is a latency-matched ECDSA baseline, which incorporates a synthetic delay of 2.44 ms so that it aligns with the overhead of the PQC hybrid setup. This baseline was evaluated under identical host conditions, allowing a controlled comparison that isolates the effects of the post-quantum hybrid configuration relative to the classical ECDSA-only approach.</data>
  <data key="d9">baseline,classical baseline,classical endorsements,classical signature,classical signatures,compares_with,hybrid signature,native signatures,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d11">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791502254</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
