<edge source="ECDSA" target="ML-DSA-65">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Post-quantum signatures such as ML-DSA are substantially larger than ECDSA signatures.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper compares ECDSA and ML-DSA-65 signature schemes.&lt;SEP&gt;ML-DSA-65 is compared against the ECDSA baseline.&lt;SEP&gt;PQC blocks average 43,551 bytes versus 29,328 bytes for ECDSA blocks.&lt;SEP&gt;ML-DSA-65 active-block size is ~1.48× the original ECDSA baseline of 29,328 bytes.</data>
  <data key="d9">compares_with,signature schemes,signature size,storage overhead</data>
