  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Toward Quantum-Safe Permissioned Blockchains: Evaluating Hybrid ML-DSA-65/ECDSA Signatures on Hyperledger Fabric" target="Ref [1] Hyperledger Fabric">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Among these platforms, Hyperledger Fabric is widely adopted because of its modular architecture, membership-based identity model, configurable endorsement policies, and separation between transaction execution, ordering, and validation [1].</data>
  <data key="d9">cites,platform background</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791502234</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Toward Quantum-Safe Permissioned Blockchains: Evaluating Hybrid ML-DSA-65/ECDSA Signatures on Hyperledger Fabric" target="Ref [2] Shor's Algorithm">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">While these mechanisms are efficient and mature, they are vulnerable to large-scale quantum attacks based on Shor's algorithm [2], [3].</data>
  <data key="d9">cites,quantum threat</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791502234</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Toward Quantum-Safe Permissioned Blockchains: Evaluating Hybrid ML-DSA-65/ECDSA Signatures on Hyperledger Fabric" target="Ref [3] Quantum Attacks">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">While these mechanisms are efficient and mature, they are vulnerable to large-scale quantum attacks based on Shor's algorithm [2], [3].</data>
  <data key="d9">cites,quantum threat</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d11">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
