<edge source="Ledger Storage Overhead" target="Hybrid Post-Quantum Signatures for Hyperledger Fabric">
  <data key="d7">2.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The paper identifies ledger storage growth (blocks 1.48x larger) as the only practically and statistically significant difference.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper reports about 20.9x larger cryptographic artifacts but only about 1.43x larger complete blocks relative to the functionally equivalent ECDSA baseline. It also reports a 1.48x measured ratio for the SignDocument workload and finds that ledger growth depends on the workload.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,block size,storage analysis</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d11">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791502266</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Ledger Storage Overhead" target="SignDocument">
  <data key="d7">1.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The 1.48x block-size ratio is specific to the signing-intensive SignDocument workload.</data>
  <data key="d9">related_to,workload dependence</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-030</data>
  <data key="d11">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791502266</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
