<edge source="ML-DSA-65" target="Hybrid Post-Quantum Signatures for Hyperledger Fabric">
  <data key="d7">24.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The relation between Hybrid Post-Quantum Signatures for Hyperledger Fabric and ML-DSA-65 centers on the paper's use of ML-DSA-65, standardized in FIPS 204, as the post-quantum component of its hybrid signature scheme. The work pairs ML-DSA-65 with classical ECDSA to form hybrid ML-DSA-65/ECDSA signatures. These are applied to hybrid post-quantum document signing and provide application-level post-quantum signature evidence within Hyperledger Fabric.

Architecturally, the paper integrates ML-DSA-65 keys and signatures at the application layer rather than modifying Fabric's native cryptographic stack. Signatures are generated by an external application-layer signing service, implemented as a PQC microservice. In the PQC hybrid configuration, the ML-DSA-65 signature and public-key artifacts are stored on-ledger, while verification is performed off-chain. ML-DSA-65 signing is also used in the paper's evaluation of the PQC microservice and of a two-instance signing-service setup.

ML-DSA-65 serves as the primary parameter set and configuration throughout the study. It was chosen and retained because it occupies the intermediate NIST security category 3 position, which offers a balanced trade-off between security strength and storage overhead. The paper evaluates ML-DSA-65 signatures in Hyperledger Fabric across six scenarios to assess the practicality of adding post-quantum security to the platform.</data>
  <data key="d9">PQC signing,hybrid signature,post-quantum signature,post-quantum signatures,post-quantum signing,primary configuration,primary parameter set,signature algorithm,uses_method</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-041</data>
