  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The article defines the SignDocument chaincode function.&lt;SEP&gt;SignDocument workloads are evaluated under PQC and ECDSA configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;The primary SignDocument metrics show no significant difference in throughput (p = 0.620) or average latency (p = 0.997) between ECDSA and the PQC hybrid configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress-test throughput was measured for SignDocument at 10 TPS and 50 TPS submission rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Five independent SignDocument runs were executed per parameter set at 20 TPS with five workers and 500 transactions per run.&lt;SEP&gt;The proposed chaincode's SignDocument function persists ML-DSA-65 artifacts.&lt;SEP&gt;The paper implements a SignDocument chaincode function that enforces the MSP-authenticated ML-DSA-65 key binding.</data>
  <data key="d9">addresses,chaincode,chaincode function,primary workload,proposes,signing transaction,stress test,uses_method,workload</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3cdf7983d59d3aabda65b170e48426b0-chunk-034</data>
  <data key="d11">Toward_Quantum-Safe_Permissioned_Blockchains_Evalu.pdf</data>
  <data key="d12">1791502266</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
